(E'dd029360-b954-4bfd-b154-401fb9f4d592', E'2025-04-25T13:08:51.383512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the glasses into the case', E'Policy A was slightly more precise when grabbing the glasses, it made a grasp attempt very close to the glasses but did not successfully pick them up. In contrast, policy B approached the glasses and got somewhat close but never actually made a grasp attempt. Neither policy was able to successfully pick them up or put them in the case.'),
(E'600c89fc-e9a4-41f8-93cb-019444541a6d', E'2025-04-25T13:23:55.191216Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the red cup and put it in the blue bowl', E'The actions of policy A were more progressive, albeit a bit jittery. Policy B did not execute any noticeable actions.'),
(E'b88d85aa-9dc4-4742-b94e-3680f1aa05f8', E'2025-04-25T13:25:17.032287Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'close the black and pink glasses case', E'Policy A was not able to close the case, but it could identify the case, approach it, and manipulate it in a way that could have led to it being closed. In contrast, policy B did not seem to recognize the case at all and made no progress towards interacting with it.'),
(E'1ee6d898-1876-4232-8250-e15f3ce6cac9', E'2025-04-25T13:42:03.498532Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the yellow bottle of mustard onto the shelf', E'Policy A was able to successfully grasp the mustard and move it toward the shelf, although it did not actually put it on the shelf. Policy B showed some indication of preference toward the mustard, but was not actually able to pick it up or move it to the target'),
(E'8680082e-0dc2-4ed4-8609-dd1044c51d10', E'2025-04-25T13:58:40.780472Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the red box onto the shelf', E'Both policies moved toward the red box, but neither was able to grasp it or put it onto the shelf. Policy A pushed the box around a little bit, but did not know where to grasp it. Policy B made a grasp attempt, but it was completely off from where it should have been'),
(E'f1326bd2-884b-4c9d-a649-a08f84d1c7f0', E'2025-04-25T13:59:26.468581Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'erase the board', E'Policy A failed to move in any direction. On the other hand, policy B gradually solved the task with multiple attempts although it seems to struggle due to the low height of the table.'),
(E'00e1796c-c4d0-4017-8925-93d763f90f72', E'2025-04-25T14:34:37.406413Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'erase the board', E'Both policy A and policy B were hesistant but policy A showed more redundant and repetitive actions. Policy  B seems to take smoother actions than policy A.'),
(E'967bb1ee-9933-487d-a705-60bd61c5f91c', E'2025-04-25T14:51:15.255077Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the eraser in the dustpan', E'Policy B takes smoother and faster actions than policy A. Both policy A and policy B failed to solve the task.'),
(E'dab90390-74ef-428a-8001-1742cca1e5f0', E'2025-04-25T16:37:12.047873Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'fold the blue towel', E'Policy B is faster than policy A and also policy B solves the task more confidently. Meanwhile, policy A shows some sluggish movements.'),
(E'51378b69-075e-4953-bbe2-baa28f648dd7', E'2025-04-25T16:39:09.952912Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick the lid off of the black kettle.', E'A was able to grasp the lid but did not lift it. B moved towards the kettle and attempted a grasp but was unsuccessful.'),
(E'7ccd5be8-c1d6-4917-871d-905015915744', E'2025-04-25T16:44:47.116017Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the red cola can', E'Both A and B almost do nothing, A early stop at origin, B go forward 20cm and early stops;'),
(E'c4645961-8cc6-4b89-b564-5ccbf482134e', E'2025-04-25T16:49:32.905891Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Stir the pot.', E'A was much more hesitant than B. Both eventually made motions towards the pot but did not grasp the spoon.'),
(E'852444f5-77f0-4dc7-b10c-f7beb712715d', E'2025-04-25T16:50:51.058267Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the tape on the blue towel', E'Policy A succeeded at the task after some number of attempts. On the other hand, policy B seems to be not confident enough and makes more conservative actions.'),
(E'9a012fc0-dacb-4d8b-93eb-8a6dbc1b518f', E'2025-04-25T17:05:54.278499Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the pen in the cup', E'Policy B follows a smoother trajectory compared to policy A. Policy B shows an impressive corrective behavior.'),
(E'8f69bf33-8a4e-4cbd-a7be-14b0c839bc82', E'2025-04-25T17:09:11.630129Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the black plate with the wooden cup and place it on the table.', E'A put its gripper in the right spot but did not fully close, then it moved away. B was faster in approach, but only managed to grab the cup.'),
(E'ed20036f-b36a-4a7a-8eb8-3f1ba55432a2', E'2025-04-25T17:19:36.753138Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Rotate the kettle 90 degrees clockwise.', E'A got confused and went to the pot instead of the kettle. B was able to identify the correct grasp point on the kettle, but kept opening and closing the gripper instead of rotating.'),
(E'f33bc806-72ad-4ffc-88dc-000e6cee5c3c', E'2025-04-25T17:26:03.516329Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the blue pen on the dish', E'Policy B demonstrates better performance compared to policy A in both speed and accuracy. Policy B efficiently reaches the target position with minimal jittery movements. In contrast, policy A exhibits slower execution, lacking precision.'),
(E'70cf47f5-38b0-4c00-9870-fcc790900e1a', E'2025-04-25T17:30:21.480250Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Unstack the objects.', E'A did mot move. B failed to get a grasp initially but then picked up two of the objects from the table, it hesitated in the air after until time ran out.'),
(E'dfce518e-7eb6-4fa4-947e-4e86dc8ab042', E'2025-04-25T17:32:43.129250Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the pen on cloth', E'Policy A is better since it approached the blue pen at first and constantly grasping it on the air without moving any further to the pen. Policy B tend to shift toward the blue marker and froze'),
(E'76dd111d-a054-4436-a219-3819ae36ecf4', E'2025-04-25T17:47:59.357463Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the stuffed animal in the white box', E'Only policy A was able to completely solve the task. Policy B seems to be affected by the distractors.'),
(E'deb6c64d-6645-49e8-8d2f-6023b1cc0387', E'2025-04-25T17:49:27.991827Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the cloth on white bowl', E'Both policies are very good at identifying the location of the cloth but going further, none can perform the grasp movement on it'),
(E'b7a5c346-219a-4274-97be-58d50530004c', E'2025-04-25T17:59:23.304013Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue water bottle onto the red box', E'both policies identified the blue water bottle and moved towards it, and both policies attempted to form a grasp. A attempted the grasp and closed the gripper, but it was off base to actually pick the bottle up. B did not close the gripper, but the grasp it formed was better, and if it had closed the gripper, it would have llikely succeeded. Neither policy put the bottle on the red box'),
(E'21ea4f2e-c7a2-4e57-a190-f589dccd7d53', E'2025-04-25T18:04:43.607357Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the deck of card on the lounge', E'Both policies were consistent grabbing the deck of card but failed to lift it since the card''s length is wider than the gripper span. It would be better if theey change the direction to better fit with the narrower side'),
(E'cf1a67d0-887e-4ce8-b50d-e600c4f1dfb5', E'2025-04-25T18:06:13.703199Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the carrot and place it on the yellow dish', E'Policy B exhibits faster motions but confuses objects of the same color. Policy A barely moves at all, showing no progress toward the target.'),
(E'84940a1d-d93a-44db-adc9-8b8cf69eb69a', E'2025-04-25T18:15:15.598799Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue cup onto the red box', E'both policies attempted one grasp on the object, which should be relatively simple to grasp. The robot did not attempt a second grasp after the first one failed. Policy B adjusted a little bit to improve the closure before grasping, but still failed.'),
(E'f52d9695-adab-4e87-9598-933f547c8c8a', E'2025-04-25T18:25:01.465839Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the black sponge on chair', E'Policy A and B both reached for the orange cloth, which is the wrong object specified here.'),
(E'2bed5443-cc21-4cf4-951d-457563f78924', E'2025-04-25T18:29:06.496882Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the cable in the basket', E'Although both policy A and policy B failed to succeed at the task, policy B exhibited smoother trajectory with more reasonable corrective behaviors.'),
(E'739165f0-2b54-4776-91b8-1530a4148feb', E'2025-04-25T18:32:09.472107Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the cups, then put the ball in the green cup', E'Policy A approached the blue cup and formed a grasp pose, but failed to actually execute it. It then placed the green cup on top of the blue cup, which is not what the instructions were. Policy B formed a grasp around each cup, but did not execute on either of them.'),
(E'f5d9ce11-f550-43e6-ae06-531f91cfbb37', E'2025-04-25T18:50:35.490401Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the black plate on the white plate. Then place the cup on the black plate.', E'A picked up the wrong object first. B moved to the correct object but did not successfully pick it up. B wins because it chose the correct object.'),
(E'ef79622f-b6bf-450f-9a82-139040609f52', E'2025-04-25T18:55:01.021449Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'move the deck of card to notebook', E'Both policies did poorly since they both attempted to reach to the notebook without bringing anything over, which in this  required bringing the deck of card. Policy A also grabbed part of the notebook page at the end,'),
(E'3f8a023f-ad3c-4194-bfe2-eeffd92bb6ab', E'2025-04-25T18:57:47.820411Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Open the drawer', E'Policy A did not attempt the task. Policy B started to approach the cabinet and rotating its gripper. The arm was a bit too far to the left of the cabinet, to the point where the wrist camera would not see the cabinet. Policy B did collide with the cabinet a bit, but it did not warrant an early stop.'),
(E'a1878b1c-5355-4e08-96ca-53700dffcf17', E'2025-04-25T19:10:16.182267Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Find the bread.', E'A got confused, B started looking outside the scene (ignoring the container in front of it).'),
(E'15df57dc-0daf-4556-bc67-f38a4c4f2d6d', E'2025-04-25T19:11:45.587333Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the blue cup and place it in the yellow bowl', E'Policy A remained stalled, while policy B was able to reach the target with some number of attempts.'),
(E'd8e99781-e40e-44f8-a31e-fcbed325baf0', E'2025-04-25T19:13:11.729219Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'place spoon into the bowl', E'Policy A finished the task very feasibly while policy B struggled to wander around the spoon but failed to pick it up'),
(E'18182cfd-23ee-410b-ba40-77e37e9b4eef', E'2025-04-25T19:21:28.118631Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Balance the spatula on the bowl.', E'A picked up the spatula but dropped it in the wrong spot, B was very sporatic picking and dropping the spatula many times.'),
(E'1910d9d3-813c-4b1b-ab94-0401000ad25c', E'2025-04-25T19:28:38.802772Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'clean the table', E'Policy A did not attempt the task. Policy B grabbed the cloth and started wiping the coffee beans. At some point the policy did drop the cloth and regrasped it. Maybe it was to adjust?'),
(E'97d965fe-7c4c-4b7d-b26d-833c8b2e3fc1', E'2025-04-25T19:31:45.930621Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Flip over the cup.', E'A got into the correct position but pulled back, almost as if it was not confident. B explored more randomly but also did not grab the cup.'),
(E'c3d4f82d-cf43-4d6c-83df-70405087178a', E'2025-04-25T19:41:27.406918Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Rotate the bread 90 degrees counter clockwise.', E'B executed the task perfectly and with confidence. A rotated in the wrong direction and moved the bread off of the plate.'),
(E'ac84c580-bba5-442d-b810-8c951614edec', E'2025-04-25T19:52:07.774440Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put the cup on the plate.', E'A was unable to pick up the cup reliably. B placed the object on the plate but did not orient it to be standing. This was not stictly part of the language statement.'),
(E'f54d18c5-2290-4a02-97ed-a08bb2b3101b', E'2025-04-25T21:03:39.862852Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'pick up the dish brush', E'policy A actually attempted to pick up the brush but it failed to grip and let go. Policy B didn''t even go for the brush but moved around the tray.'),
(E'eedec128-c537-4054-9168-d34ad3905e1c', E'2025-04-25T21:13:54.752400Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'take the block out of the box and then close the box', E'Policy A was able to grasp the block, but did not lift it high enough out of the box initially to take it out, leading to it dragging the box along with the block. After placing the block down, Policy A did not attempt to close the box. Policy B was better at taking the block out of the box (did not clip the sides). Is first attempt to close the lid of the box, it approaches the wrong side and attempted to grasp the side. It then realized the lid is on the other side, but missed the grasp.'),
(E'fc5d4180-2ada-4092-b894-006621c31694', E'2025-04-25T21:14:33.146028Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'check if there utensils to put away from the dish rack. If there are, put them away into the sink', E'both policies failed to clear utensils and failed to grasp the objects to even put them away'),
(E'4051a633-a978-4d8e-85d5-ab8d70e60c8c', E'2025-04-25T21:21:41.918894Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put away the silver utensils into the sink', E'both policies recognized the utensiles and attempted to pick it up. Policy B was better because it actually picked up the fork in the air but dropped it on its second attempt. Policy A had trouble picking up the utensil when it attempted (utensil slipped out). I don''t see a way where both policies can do the task end-to-end successfullgrasp the object'),
(E'64524de6-3682-44c5-ba19-03f550ba36fc', E'2025-04-25T21:31:38.848382Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Take the block out of the box', E'Both policies failed to open the box. Both policies approached the box, but policy A made a better attempt at opening. Policy A tried to grasp the edge of the box while policy B pushed the gripper into the middle of the lid.'),
(E'c76acf8c-6df7-42cc-bcf2-5ac45df2ae22', E'2025-04-25T21:31:46.658249Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'please please drop all the utensils into the sink~ don''t touch the white dish brush', E'policy B actually picked up the spoon but dropped it. both policies failed to follow my instructions to not touch the brush. They both carelessly went for the utensil without considering the proximity of the brush'),
(E'60047c46-a615-45c2-aedd-8021277c6152', E'2025-04-25T21:42:00.888486Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'do not touch the spoon. pick up the dish scrub instead and drop it in the sink. no matter what do not touch the spoon as if your life depends on it pleaseeeee', E'both policies went straight for the spoon when I really emphasized not to touch the spoon twice'),
(E'2b63766e-3fe0-4198-bfdd-cf7c4cb23b7b', E'2025-04-25T21:49:55.201420Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'stir the pan with the spoon', E'Both policies identified the spoon and attempted to grasp it. Both policies struggled with picking up the handle, but policy A was making better attempts by not retracting its arm after each attempt like policy B.')
INSERT INTO sessions (id, occurred_at, site_id, instruction, notes) VALUES
(E'376267da-36e5-4ba5-b062-42a63af2e2e7', E'2025-04-25T21:54:02.000489Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'there are two dish brushes. pick up the yellow gray one and not the white one.', E'both policies were terrible. policy A didn''t do anything. Policy B just ignored my instructions and went for the wrong dish brush'),
(E'31e52219-98d4-4941-89b6-94276b5df5b3', E'2025-04-25T22:13:31.841009Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'stir the pan with the spoon', E'Policy A was able to grab and lift the spoon. Policy B correctly moved towards the spoon but did not make an attempt to grasp. After the first approach, policy B retracted and froze for the rest of the rollout.'),
(E'88823fcb-c494-4544-86a1-c3b50604592f', E'2025-04-25T22:27:08.255664Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'put the carrot in the red bowl', E'Both policies were able to put the carrot in the task but policy A was more confident, made a better grasp, and policy B dropped the carrot once'),
(E'f845aa64-4376-485c-b58a-ca33718ea83a', E'2025-04-25T22:29:38.175954Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Open the water bottle.', E'Policy A moved to the correct position to grasp the lid, and successfully grasp it. But could not rotate the gripper to open the bottle, moved back and tried again but failed. Policy B moved more agressively to the bottle but failed to grasp it, instead policy B pushed the bottle. And, after moved randomly.'),
(E'ce6fee70-3a71-4530-b72f-888fb7b2ab6b', E'2025-04-25T22:42:27.237714Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Open the bottom drawer, pickup the carrot, and put the carrot in the drawer.', E'Both policies A and B failed to open the drawer, which a very difficult first stage of the task. However, Policy A just kept trying to open the drawer, while policy B actually went and did the next step of the task (picking up a carrot). So, I prefer policy B.'),
(E'5ddbf16e-2d8b-46f6-b155-1645f2772419', E'2025-04-25T22:52:43.504789Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the red mug near the yellow rubber duck on top of the brown paper towel roll.', E'Policy A did not move. Policy B tried to pick up the correct red mug couple of times but failed.'),
(E'e7ec66ae-95c0-4601-b044-a9313914dfca', E'2025-04-25T22:59:25.118570Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the carrot in the bottom drawer.', E'Both policy A and policy B were able to put the carrot in the open drawer. However, policy A was much smoother when doing so. Policy B collided with the side of the drawer. Both policies tried opening the other drawers after completing the task.'),
(E'ecc071f2-5dfe-48b4-83b1-c0623826803b', E'2025-04-25T23:15:47.299987Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the white lego brick on top of the blue lego brick that is in between the red mugs.', E'Policy A picked up the yellow rubber duck instead of white lego brick, and put the yellow duck on top of the correct blue brick. But the task was to put the white brick on top of blue lego brick between the mugs. Therefore, it was not successfull. Policy B, picked up the white lego brick and put it on top of the correct blue lego brick. But the rotation was off, so the white brick was not fully on top of the blue brick.'),
(E'18d95f1f-0c8f-4746-b2f5-aa1c5edfcfd0', E'2025-04-25T23:16:32.346722Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Close the drawer.', E'Both policies were able to close the drawer most of the way. However, policy A went straight for the drawer and didn''t stop until it was closed. On the other hand, policy B got distracted by the plastic food items halfway through (although it did eventually remember to go back and close the drawer). I put the food items there on purpose to see if the models would get distracted by them.'),
(E'e2a260e2-02e0-4ad0-996f-90a59fec01cb', E'2025-04-25T23:32:03.687663Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Close the drawer.', E'Policy A got distracted by the objects in the left of the scene and completely ignored its task of closing the drawer. Policy B went straight to the drawer and closed it (mostly).'),
(E'47e76d78-578a-44a2-bd7c-bcc84616ee1e', E'2025-04-25T23:37:16.576411Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the marker in the pink bowl', E'Policy B did better than Policy A. Policy did not complete the task as it picked up the green cylinder and put that into the pink bowl instead of the requested marker. Policy B did pick up the marker and was about to drop it into the pink bowl but ran out of time. However, it is important to note that Policy B before picking up the marker went to approach the green cylinder just like Policy but midway during the evaluation, it went to the marker instead.'),
(E'06df62e9-1e4e-434b-8a6f-45448ca5c87f', E'2025-04-25T23:44:11.782140Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Fold the cloth', E'Policy A was able to grab the edge of the cloth and pick it up. Policy B just moved around near the cloth''s surface for a while and poked at it.'),
(E'c5e62dc1-3a58-423c-9f66-0a02f126b78f', E'2025-04-25T23:51:06.742029Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the green cylinder into the blue bowl', E'Policy A did not approach the green cylinder at all and went to other object. Thus, failing on the task requested. Policy B approached the green cylinder and after some time was able to pick it up but was unable to put it in the bowl in time.'),
(E'9e74b344-c280-456c-afb5-2c367ffeed4f', E'2025-04-25T23:55:56.682144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Fold the cloth.', E'Policy A got distracted by the red bowl and completely ignored its task of folding the cloth. Policy B did a great job folding the cloth.'),
(E'33564d71-15cb-4032-a29b-d4d6c4225ccc', E'2025-04-26T00:08:24.778041Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the ball into the black box.', E'Policy A first picked up the wrong object (rubber duck) and put it into the correct object (black box). Then after a while, policy A picked up the ball and moved towards the black box. But, the execution finished. Policy B did not move.'),
(E'2ef1cf78-7903-4629-95d1-a1d7183216b9', E'2025-04-26T00:09:28.897237Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Fold the blue cloth.', E'Both policies moved towards the correct colored cloth, but were not able to fold it.'),
(E'b8b4ce87-d34f-4b63-9966-6e8bbe9d8570', E'2025-04-26T00:13:27.298551Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the blue square into the blue bowl', E'Policy A was able to pick up the square and put it int the blue bowl. Policy B did pick it up the square and was approaching to put it in the blue bowl but intially struggled to pick up the square. Whereas, Policy A was much more smooth and efficent in picking the square and putting it in the blue bowl.'),
(E'aa72d063-11df-4b33-a556-88347cd0067a', E'2025-04-26T00:25:24.523995Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Fold the blue cloth.', E'Both policies did well at identifying and grasping the blue cloth. I put 10 instead of 100 for policy B. Policy B looked more natural than A and made a nice neat fold.'),
(E'8c0f3584-ef5d-46da-82e1-c9cbda4921eb', E'2025-04-26T00:28:35.003954Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the egg in the pink bowl', E'Policy B was able to pick up the egg but wasn''t able to carry it all the way into the pink bowl. Policy A did worse due to it attempting to picking the egg and failing which led the egg to roll of the table.'),
(E'1e2a967e-5ac2-45b0-a2ac-0002a43f10a9', E'2025-04-26T00:38:39.024458Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the ducky in the trash.', E'Neither policy did very well. Policy A grabbed the wrong item. Policy B failed to move at all.'),
(E'90051b4c-d2dc-469f-abb0-df823449b64e', E'2025-04-26T00:40:09.752816Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Fold the green cloth.', E'Both policies moved towards the empty corner. But could not pick the cloth. So, they both failed.'),
(E'101e7a98-a724-475e-ba69-4aab2ff76d41', E'2025-04-26T00:40:53.027732Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the marker in the pink bowl', E'Policy B was able to pick up the marker but put it in the blue bowl instead of the requested pink bowl. Policy A froze and was still for most of the evaluation until the end where it slightly apporoached the marker but was unable to pick up the marker.'),
(E'145cd70e-59b9-4c53-83cc-6962733e734d', E'2025-04-26T00:54:05.301291Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the ducky in the box.', E'Policy A completed the task without any issues. Policy B did not move at all.'),
(E'6a33c6dd-c9d7-4e06-9b42-983719494e30', E'2025-04-26T01:01:01.575330Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the yellow rubber duck into the red mug.', E'Policy A did not move. Policy B successfully picked up the correct rubber duck and put it into correct mug. Policy B''s actions were smooth and it was fast.'),
(E'cea7f6f7-cfa8-48f3-93ff-7d00071b07d8', E'2025-04-26T01:05:04.431886Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Pick up the marker from the blue bowl to the pink bowl', E'Both polices were unable to pick up the marker. They both approached but got distracted by the green cylinder.'),
(E'9f6ad7f4-1c71-4075-85dd-84213767ce85', E'2025-04-26T01:08:27.284992Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Drape the cloth over the box.', E'Policy A was able to pick up the cloth and move towards the box (a bit). Policy B moved towards the cloth but got stuck trying to pick it up.'),
(E'66ba3e74-9991-432e-8186-87ebed27fd47', E'2025-04-26T01:17:18.197709Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the rubber ducks into the red mugs the ducks are in front of.', E'Policy A was able to put one of the ducks in to the correct mug. And then moved towards the other duck. Policy A quickly picked up the first duck and put it into correct mug, but slowed down during picking up the second duck. Policy B picked up the first duck, but then droped it and moved randomly. Therefore, policy A was more successful.'),
(E'2bfd8160-596a-4ea8-8aab-61995be0f37b', E'2025-04-26T01:23:09.247445Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Drape the cloth over the box.', E'Both policies succeeded. Policy B really emphasized the "draping" movement though of dragging the cloth across the box before dropping it. Policy A instead just put the tip of the cloth over the box and dropped.'),
(E'9b70548e-b1c6-4c3d-8364-fba34a77949b', E'2025-04-26T01:34:52.078553Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the red mug upside down.', E'Policy A moved back and forth but did not grasp the mug. Policy B grasped the mug couple of times but it could not rotate it, due to weak grasps. Overall, policy B was the better policy.'),
(E'a6fdbff4-b300-4110-b680-df8a33b97a04', E'2025-04-26T01:40:15.599586Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Drape the cloth over the box then put the red bowl in the silver bowl.', E'Policy A picked up the cloth (the very first step), but then put it in the silver bowl instead of draping it over the box. Policy B failed to pickup the cloth at all.'),
(E'8b205c5a-e5d3-4a46-a79f-937780babf4b', E'2025-04-26T02:00:12.114319Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the red bowl in the silver bowl then drape the cloth over the box.', E'Both policies failed the first step of the task: to pickup the red bowl.'),
(E'65482c84-6eae-405c-9230-6909f05cd1ec', E'2025-04-26T02:13:40.896565Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the red bowl and the ducky in the silver bowl.', E'Policy A stopped for a long time at the start. Policy A also didn''t manage to drop the ducky in the bowl. Policy B was able to pickup the ducky and drop it in the silver bowl, but then it tried picking up the croissant (a distractor) instead of the red bowl.'),
(E'0104e304-97be-4f8b-a0af-064a27dcf596', E'2025-04-26T02:29:35.142804Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the lid on top of the grey pot.', E'Both policies were successful. But policy A was faster to complete the task, while policy B slowed down after it put the lid on top of the pot. Also, policy B did not let go the lid, that is why policy A was better.'),
(E'bac53018-e08d-4a5d-a6be-c31ca65e32ce', E'2025-04-26T02:30:47.741874Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the ducky and the red bowl in the silver bowl.', E'Policy A managed to complete the entire task (put the ducky and the red bowl in the silver bowl). Policy B put the ducky in the red bowl then seemed to get confused since it also accidentally grabbed a corner of the cloth underneath everything while it was grabbing the ducky.'),
(E'68fe1184-6439-44a6-8b01-0750ebac0abf', E'2025-04-26T02:47:20.949882Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the carrot into the grey pot and put the lid on top.', E'Policy A moved towards the carrot, but could not grasp it. Policy B was able to put carrot into the pot. It also put the rubber duck into the pot, which was not part of the task. Then policy B moved towards the lid, and nearly grasped it, but the execution finished. Since policy B was able to put the carrot into the pot, it was more successful.'),
(E'8bb5fa58-3a5d-4416-af38-9f9c47189680', E'2025-04-26T12:06:49.492187Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the red tape', E'A completely failed to do anything. B immediately picked up the tape, and started moving it (reasonable because I did not specify any kind of end destination'),
(E'2eb8d874-df32-4944-87e0-0b26cb7b43f9', E'2025-04-26T12:15:42.840196Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'stack the three rolls of tape', E'Policy A was able to pick up the one roll off to the side, and brought it near the other two rolls, but did not actually place it onto the other rolls to form a stack. Policy B picked up one of the two rolls (which would not have been the optimal way to stack) and then hesitated to actually do anything with it. Policy A went off to the right side at first, where there were no rolls, but then returned and picked up a roll.'),
(E'9e23d3ea-642c-415a-801c-b5ee315771c6', E'2025-04-26T12:33:54.827014Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the mouse into the white cup', E'Policy A picked up the mouse quickly but did not recognize the cup at first, trying to put it on the shelf instead. Eventually, it went over to the cup and held the mouse above it, but did not drop it in. When the robot reset and relaxed the gripper after the episode, the mouse fell into the cup. The second policy also picked up the mouse, but then hesitated for the remainder of the episode.'),
(E'e1786245-6ef7-4a68-900b-70e04138764c', E'2025-04-26T12:47:24.586812Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'stack the blocks into the white cup', E'policy A was able to pick up one block and place it into the cup, but did not stack any more. Policy B was not able to pick up the block properly and became confused, moving towards the cup anyway.'),
(E'e64e1439-2919-4986-bc1d-7d6baeea460d', E'2025-04-26T13:09:57.670408Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the fish onto the center of the wooden tray', E'policy A moved to the center of the wooden tray, but did not bring the fish. Policy B did not respond at all.'),
(E'433ca5cd-4cc1-4b81-a65f-51d08d84a7bf', E'2025-04-26T13:24:03.704511Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'push the blocks together to make a square', E'A moved toward the blocks, but then moved to the back of the scene, the cardboard boards, and did not make any more progress. B moved toward the blocks, but then got stuck and did not make any more progress'),
(E'150591df-2cfb-4dae-a826-87a5e8824c62', E'2025-04-26T13:42:37.178220Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the apple into the square', E'Policy A picked up the apple and moved it toward the square, but then it began to hesitate and move it around the area. There were several moments where it could have completed the task if it opened the gripper, but it never did. Policy B moved toward the apple but never picked it up, and simply hesitated and moved around the area of the apple'),
(E'6c306de9-b155-4842-9732-07b35cc99287', E'2025-04-26T13:57:35.807413Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'remove the wrench from the beaker', E'policy A did nothing. Policy B attempted to move around the scene and explore for the target, then tried to grasp the mouse but failed. This is a difficult task because the wrench is so small in the camera view, but B at least tried to make progress'),
(E'c5695e64-1672-4c4b-84f3-ccd6cbede39b', E'2025-04-26T20:46:48.186878Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the fork and put it on the white dish', E'Policy A''s actions are faster and contain minimal jerkiness. However, policy B, although it is slower and seems to lag a bit, exhibits more cautious behaviors leading to enhanced precision.'),
(E'f6bd95dd-7c4f-4623-8f18-bb88e1ae4c8d', E'2025-04-26T21:13:21.596481Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'stack the blue cup on the green cup', E'Policy A successfully completed the task while policy B failed to do the final movement. Also, policy A is better at making small movements that can enhance the precision.'),
(E'fd94c503-9938-4d11-a0cc-059b825ae7aa', E'2025-04-26T21:28:28.994043Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the toothpaste on the towel', E'Policy A makes longer trajectory each step than policy B. Policy A seems to be slightly aggressive yet faster in its actions compared to policy B.'),
(E'd2b59c33-3a4e-489b-bb20-9fbe5795e1bd', E'2025-04-26T21:57:28.430242Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cup right side up on the plate.', E'A successfully picked up the cup that was fallen and quickly put it right side up on the plate. Policy B went off into the distance seemingly without reason. It is worth noting the scene is dark in this case which may be affecting B (but clearly did not effect A).'),
(E'f42e832a-ff53-4fec-93f2-b14bb94c344c', E'2025-04-26T22:03:23.899969Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the purple cup and place it in the sink', E'Policy B almost succeeded at the task with rapid movements together with impressive corrective behaviors. Policy A failed in the middle of the task and showed redundant motion patterns.'),
(E'07fbba6f-3409-48b5-964a-614b72cc0cac', E'2025-04-26T22:07:05.372272Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the fork to the right of the plate.', E'A missed grabbing at first but then came back and picked up the fork. A then moved the fork to the right but ran out of time before it could let go. B was confused and then tried to pick up the knife (but failed to do so).'),
(E'8c045222-b8fd-4d1d-ae84-56caffd221d8', E'2025-04-26T22:16:18.308180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put the food on the plate.', E'Policy A grabbed the fork and put it on the plate before puttin a food item on. It then went off the table. Policy B quickly took one food item and put it on the plate, but ignored the second food item that was not on the plate.'),
(E'd4cc364e-1e96-4d22-8e08-8cb935759528', E'2025-04-26T22:20:49.300551Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'fold the blue towel', E'Both policy A and policy B almost solved the task completely. However, policy A displayed more decisive motions with less corrective behaviors while policy B solved the task by chance after multiple attempts.'),
(E'cdf647a1-a766-42a8-b7ee-f1364793848c', E'2025-04-26T22:26:29.982475Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pour the contents of the kettle into the cup.', E'A did not move. B identified the kettle but was unable to find a grasp. Then it got confused and went to go pick up the bread.'),
(E'457cce2e-a944-4c63-858e-3b9ee2fc0446', E'2025-04-26T22:35:31.664074Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the blue pen in the box', E'Only policy A managed to solve the task halfway through. Policy B remained stalled from the beginning of the episode.'),
(E'934888cd-305e-4281-9d33-b34da4f4ba04', E'2025-04-26T22:38:13.783876Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the plate into the cup.', E'A did not move. B moved its end effector into the plate but got confused, picking up the plate instead of pushing it.'),
(E'da27727a-83e9-4424-9ef8-a75e94308817', E'2025-04-26T22:47:43.716926Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the stuffed animal and place it in the box', E'Policy B takes its actions with more confidence while policy A tends to repeat the same trajectories it has made before, slowing down the progress.'),
(E'6c4e72b0-850f-4bd1-8d19-691db2f23349', E'2025-04-26T22:49:04.679859Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Point at the kettle.', E'A explored acting somewhat confused until it put the kettle in the middle of its end effector camera and closed its end effector. B seemed to be trying to interact with objects on the opposite sides of the scene from the kettle.'),
(E'b126c698-34d9-4fd9-b6bf-43d04d42fcb5', E'2025-04-26T22:49:39.072811Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'empty the bowl', E'While both did take the object out of the bowl, which qualifies for 100, but B placed the object on the table area next to the bowl. This is the more natural thing to do.'),
(E'1537083d-55dd-421b-89e4-dcc48846928a', E'2025-04-26T22:57:31.835365Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the cup off of the black bowl.', E'Both A and B picked up the cup instead of pushing, and both then placed in on the table. After letting go A returned to a starting pose while B kept repeatedly grabbing the cup, which is sub optimal.'),
(E'3872d194-627d-47c4-bc64-d31085727f0c', E'2025-04-26T23:01:43.440468Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'move the objects with similar color together', E'Neither policy was able to release the object. Once it grabs the first object, it never releases it.'),
(E'fd94ab62-98d7-473c-9944-1df05d42fdcd', E'2025-04-26T23:08:00.272464Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Fold the rag.', E'Policy B grabbed both sides of the rag and made a motion to fold but quit part of the way through. A did not successfully grasp the rag at all.'),
(E'fda392f6-41ed-4146-bb32-dcf771c518ae', E'2025-04-26T23:10:35.831224Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the screwdriver in the plastic bag', E'Policy A nearly reached the final goal while policy B struggled from the beginning. Policy A was faster than policy B.'),
(E'0db114b3-8ba7-4d2f-8926-50065343338f', E'2025-04-26T23:16:17.968908Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'push over the blocks', E'Both A and B moved the gripper close to the blocks, but did not perform any significant pushing motion.'),
(E'9a0f599b-2831-44b8-be25-ba3fc606c320', E'2025-04-26T23:23:16.452553Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Open the middle drawer.', E'B did not move. A moved to the base of the drawer rack and seemed to get stuck there, confused as to what to do.'),
(E'ee24b4b2-b87a-4e62-8b8e-22a6ec3975df', E'2025-04-26T23:28:24.175957Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick the screwdriver and place it in the silver bowl', E'Policy B initially hesitated to move long distance but later transitioned to effective and rapid movements. Meanwhile, policy A also succeeded at the task, but it exhibited more sluggish movements.'),
(E'bcc8c9c6-e4dd-401b-9225-7bfc247a53d1', E'2025-04-26T23:29:29.550895Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Push over the stacked blocks on the table.', E'B tried to get close to the blocks, while A reached for a place far away from the blocks.'),
(E'4723472f-e712-4599-8576-3ef055f2d912', E'2025-04-26T23:35:26.602022Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Flip the bread with the spatula.', E'A picked up the spatula then dropped it. B ignored the spatula and opted to pick up and drop the bread itself.'),
(E'17635a7c-5bb8-455f-984b-f0869926ff18', E'2025-04-26T23:37:03.847938Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the one with different color', E'A did not pick up anything, B picked up a object that is not of a different color than others.'),
(E'68ace831-7a29-42be-a6c3-dfa432534614', E'2025-04-26T23:42:06.994799Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'upright the cup', E'Both policy A and policy B were confused during their first attempt. Later on, policy A showed better performance in terms of speed and accuracy.'),
(E'cea4a5f4-7cb7-4513-8590-dd646cec97ad', E'2025-04-26T23:43:39.113958Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Open the drawer with blue handle.', E'A tried to open a drawer, but not the one with blue handle and did succeed in doing that. B reached for the shelf and had unnatural pose.'),
(E'cb3a637a-bea7-45f2-84dc-50fda57dd912', E'2025-04-26T23:57:45.068308Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put everything in the pot.', E'A did not seem to move. B struggled to find a grasp but eventually picked up the cup. B did not make any dstinct moves to put the cup in the pot.'),
(E'22a1ce25-b099-4e0d-abae-2d798695e39f', E'2025-04-27T00:03:59.976149Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the tape on the plate', E'Policy A didn''t take any action throughout the rollout, remaining still in its initial position. Policy B tackled the task with confidence although some of its actions were misleading.'),
(E'ac6ab3e0-4c01-443f-bf27-a8480517bb54', E'2025-04-27T00:07:41.852750Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take everything out of the pot.', E'B did not move. A took out the cup (but knocked over the measuring tape in the process). Now that the measuring tape was knocked over A was not able to pick it up.'),
(E'fc4c7448-d940-4620-8841-8472bd1368ed', E'2025-04-27T00:20:47.311138Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'stack the bowls', E'Policy B reached closer to the target goal. Also, policy B exhibited impressive corrective behaviors that led to better performance. Meanwhile, policy A is slower and failed to perform fine-grained actions.'),
(E'82843e97-5e96-4a34-a888-06820b70bd4b', E'2025-04-27T00:21:25.874252Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Uncross the knife and fork.', E'A did not move. B repeatedly grasped and released both the knife and fork, clearly confused as to what to do.'),
(E'03919d42-23d1-4dd7-b03c-e066de78103d', E'2025-04-27T00:32:01.892462Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the bread with the knife.', E'A was unable to get a grasp on the knife, and spent much of its time moving near the knife. B was also hesitant, but right as time ran out it got a grasp on the knife.'),
(E'43b0190d-e747-4f92-b8d4-072bc727a220', E'2025-04-27T00:35:15.486018Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Move the computer mouse to the left', E'Both policies completed the entire task but policy B did it on the first try. After the first grasp and lift, it feels like policy A dropped the mouse prematurely. It then picked it up again and moved it further.'),
(E'57e27cdb-ddd6-48fc-a05d-4fcbd519bfb7', E'2025-04-27T00:46:09.873713Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the lid on the pot.', E'A placed the lid on the pot somewhat misaligned, it also spent a significant amount of time with the lid on the pot before letting go of it. B placed the lid in a somewhat better configuration but never let go.'),
(E'5afb8f69-fc7a-4404-b3eb-c395da53b3a1', E'2025-04-27T00:46:49.547882Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pull out the tissue', E'Policy A was more aggressive and achieved further in terms of task progression. On the other hand, policy B took repetitive actions moving the same trajectory back and forth.'),
(E'4050abe7-2f99-4582-9688-26c92a10e8da', E'2025-04-27T00:53:26.392349Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Move the computer mouse to the left', E'Policy A moved towards the mouse, but when it got close it started backing away. After that it froze for a while and then started moving towards the mouse again, but never attempted a grasp. Policy B moved confidently with large movements and completed the task swiftly.'),
(E'db1d1cb7-8aa5-42b5-93fe-0b6ceb14a623', E'2025-04-27T00:56:17.211744Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take the bread out of the pot and place it on the cutting board.', E'A and B both got the lid off the pot. A struggled but eventualy was able to grasp the bread, while B never went low enough to grab the bread. To the credit of B, it was faster and more decisive than A.'),
(E'0d2a3df8-3ad4-4047-96d0-8732cec02c39', E'2025-04-27T01:05:37.622622Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread in the pot.', E'A placed the bread on top of lid that covered the pot. B did the same thing, then realized that it needed to remove the lid. B struggled and failed to find a valid grasp on the lid to take it off.'),
(E'd185ddd4-a856-4217-85df-e73686cdbefa', E'2025-04-27T01:14:37.379422Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove the lid and place the bread in the pot.', E'A did not move, B picked up the bread and moved it to the top of the pot (without removing the lid first).'),
(E'db2e3274-4a50-4095-879d-41608dc97180', E'2025-04-27T01:17:45.433241Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the block in the silver bowl', E'Policy B was more confident in its grasp and did not have to regrasp like policy A had to. Policy A put the block in the wrong bowl.'),
(E'1e1ddded-c37d-432f-b5c0-838e38fce94a', E'2025-04-27T01:29:55.911458Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the block in the silver bowl', E'Policy A correctly places the block in the silver bowl where policy B places it into the red bowl. Policy A did clip the bowl a bit as it moved the block over.'),
(E'018316ac-98d8-4d40-b973-cc6704e4ff70', E'2025-04-27T01:44:58.145750Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Pour the water from the mug into the silver bowl', E'Both policies incorrectly tried to pour the mug into the red bowl instead of the silver bowl. Both policies were not accurate in the pouring and would have missed the red bowl. Policy B grabbed the mug by the handle instead of side which is preferable.'),
(E'45c5df4a-1bdd-437c-83ad-3ae2485e0e03', E'2025-04-27T01:57:48.204185Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'pick up the green cup force it back on the table', E'Policy A picked up a cup  albiet the wrong one (the white cup instead of the green cup) and it  it held the cup up for a while but not quite 3 seconds. It was also pretty quick interms of picking up the cup in the first place. However, policy B was flailing around for most of the time, picked up the wrong color cup, and never kept it back on the table.'),
(E'eeaaf64b-fdf7-43b2-8b29-f4618902800c', E'2025-04-27T02:01:19.538227Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Drape the white cloth over the chair', E'Policy A did not attempt the task. Policy B grabbed the cloth and placed it on the chair''s seat. While I meant for it to drape it over the chair''s back, I did not specify that explicitly, so I give it 100.'),
(E'5f1333ff-0c7d-4666-af30-57dfeb3f6da0', E'2025-04-27T02:15:40.797347Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the white cloth in the box', E'Policy A did not attempt the task. Policy B tried picking up the cloth from the chair but was grasping it too far down, so it was grasping on the chair as well. After lifting the cloth slipped due to a bad grasp.'),
(E'02f67afc-8eb7-429b-ba93-c021fd5f709a', E'2025-04-27T10:24:08.231772Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the book and then put it down', E'policy A did nothing. Policy B moved toward the book and placed its gripper near the spine, but did not actually pick it up. It moved its gripper around several times while near the spine.'),
(E'12af69f7-abf6-4102-a861-4530e7f78f92', E'2025-04-27T10:42:52.377387Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'put the cable onto the tape roll', E'Policy A focused on the top of the cabinet in the background, and did not move toward the cable or the tape roll at all. Policy B moved toward the tape roll, but did not pick up the cable or put it onto the roll'),
(E'841e76f6-31ed-4e4b-9f16-163f78b0fe34', E'2025-04-27T11:04:28.837360Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the orange into the cone', E'Policy A picked up the orange confidently, and moved it toward the cone, but it knocked the cone over and failed to actually put it in. Policy B grabbed the orange, but it was a weak grasp. It picked up the orange, and then waited a while before moving it towards the target. I''m not sure if policy B could have put it in if it had more time.'),
(E'5465afef-ae76-46d8-9260-0348b6cdfa48', E'2025-04-27T11:17:56.688185Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the book', E'Policy A went for the white box of sugar instead of the book, and tried to grab it, knocking the book over in the process. Policy B moved toward the red box a little bit, but just moved around and stayed confused.'),
(E'fb50d71b-c015-4e6c-9fb4-3a8133c738f2', E'2025-04-27T11:29:01.822437Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue block next to the green block', E'Policy A attempted to grasp the blue block, but failed. It then became stuck and didn''t do very much. Policy B went for the green block instead, knocking it off the stand, and then the policy got stuck as well.'),
(E'2ee119b4-52ca-42e9-baec-cfd475e1e455', E'2025-04-27T11:43:20.977711Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the pineapple next to the apple', E'Policy A grabbed the pineapple, but it was very slow and jerky. It moved the pineapple near the apple, but did not put it down. Policy B grabbed the pineapple mmore quickly, and moved it very close to the apple, but did not put it down and instead pushed the apple backwards. Neither policy put the pineapple into the second roll of tape'),
(E'9e8c12d7-29d2-4148-ae08-b99e88c1f3a9', E'2025-04-27T11:58:20.090151Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the water bottle into the blue tray', E'Policy A took a step back to see more of the scene, then moved toward the water bottle, but it just moved around the bottle from various views and did not actually try to pick it up. It also pushed the newspaper a little bit. Policy B did not go towards the water bottle at all and moved towards the shelf in the back of the scene.'),
(E'2d584672-de34-40f4-9993-59f47d40942b', E'2025-04-27T12:11:27.543313Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the pineapple into the blue tray', E'Policy A picked up the pineapple and brought it to the target, but it got stuck on the edge, and it did not actually drop it in. It then brought it back near its original position. Policy B brought it to the target, but did not drop it in.Policy B was a little bit slow bringing it over'),
(E'e0b4e16c-a195-4ba0-96a5-77f718caa814', E'2025-04-27T12:33:30.423171Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue tray into the white tray', E'Policy A was able to pick up the blue tray, and pushed it toward the white tray, but did not lift it high enough to clear the side of the white tray. It kept trying for the remainder of the rollout, but if it had lifted it higher it probably could have succeded. Policy B initially couldn''t lift it high enough, but then it lifted it higher and placed it into the white tray, bbut it did not relax its grip'),
(E'755f0be9-8a74-441c-8aae-79e2381c84f8', E'2025-04-27T12:49:30.917546Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the sprinkles into the black pan', E'Policy A moved toward the sprinkles, but then moved behind them and then to the side. It waited for a bit and then moved towards the sprinkles again, then back again. Policy B picked up the sprinkles but pushed them back towards the cabinet.'),
(E'a3664ef3-4e80-4c5b-87f9-33e0acdb1af6', E'2025-04-27T13:02:22.794227Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the duck into the black pan', E'Policy A picked up the duck and brought it to the pan, but failed to actually put it in. It did not lift it high enough to clear the side of the pan. Policy B hesitated a little bit grabbing the duck, but did succeed eventually, and placed it into the pan, but did not relax its grip.'),
(E'6e5f337d-853d-4f0e-a3fa-cc3b7f230d73', E'2025-04-27T13:19:46.689638Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the duck into the teal pan', E'Policy A simply looked around at the scene and did not do anything. Policy B went towards the duck and grasped it, but at a very poor and unstable position. It then dragged the duck towards the teal pan very slowly.'),
(E'fa4842c0-c42c-450d-864a-39302db16720', E'2025-04-27T13:33:03.231513Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the red tape into the wooden tray', E'Policy A moved toward the red tape, but just pushed up against it and did not attempt to grasp it. When it realized that this wasn''t working, it moved back and looked around more. Policy B also moved toward the tape and pushed against it more, without making progress towards grasping it or getting it off the hook.'),
(E'5bb5f19c-c68a-40e7-b7a8-2121ca281bf9', E'2025-04-27T14:31:39.757930Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'put the red box into the white tray', E'Policy A moved toward the red box and knocked it over, but did not pick it up. It then tried to move it more for a little while. It also knocked over the occluder. Policy B picked up the red box after one failed grasp attempt. It then placed the box into the tray, knocking over the occluder, but did not release its grasp'),
(E'd9fa7b45-9aa3-4c0b-959d-4af301a1a5f7', E'2025-04-27T14:45:09.600775Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the apple into the wooden tray', E'Policy A picked up the pineapple, not the apple, and did not move it toward the tray. It moved it around a little bit to various places and seemed hesitant. Policy B also picked up the pineapple, and moved it around behind the sugar.'),
(E'56e7be98-e728-4c15-a83d-dce27f505f43', E'2025-04-27T15:04:59.535052Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the bottle of mustard into the wooden tray', E'Policy A moved around a little bit and did not show any particular preference for any object. Policy B moved in a jerky way at first toward the mustard, then confidently grasped it and tried to put it onto the shelf, but pushed against one of the shelves. Then, it moved it to the wooden tray but did not release it.'),
(E'61efb4c7-1dc6-43aa-a9ad-183fd5759ff4', E'2025-04-27T15:18:30.129174Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the white ball into the wooden tray', E'Neither policy went for the white ball, each went for the apple instead. Policy A picked up the apple pretty quickly and confidently and brought it to the wooden tray but did not release it. Policy B hesitated and spent a long time decidding whether or not to pick up the apple. It eventually picked it up and brought it close to the wooden tray slowly.'),
(E'3dbfbe39-1081-4185-b6bb-e1d558ef72e9', E'2025-04-27T15:32:22.539280Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the red roll of tape into the wooden tray', E'Policy A moved towards the two red objects, but could not decide to focus on the tape. It moved a little bit between a few different positions until the end of the rollout. Policy B picked up the tape with a little hesitation and moved it towards the other side of the scene. Eventually, it focused on the wooden tray and put it into the tray, but did not release its gripper.'),
