(E'09836787-40cc-4c82-bc26-f6cf64956336', E'2025-04-29T18:32:51.893315Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the corn inside the drawer', E'Policy A successfully pick up the corn while policy B just move toward the corn'),
(E'05a417df-0ea1-4e50-8eec-c900b6494747', E'2025-04-29T18:43:34.824970Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'close the left door on the top compartment of the cabinet', E'Both policies closed the door but policy A had more style, it looked like understanding the goal more'),
(E'c6ae4d03-9c1e-42b5-b267-c7368c669cc3', E'2025-04-29T18:44:50.485129Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Take the duckie out of the drawer and then close the drawer', E'Both policies reach into the drawer for the duckie but fail to grasp it as they push the gripper way too far down.'),
(E'5f6ef83e-7a22-46ff-8702-bc9e2050f781', E'2025-04-29T18:51:26.867999Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'wipe the table', E'Policy A complete the task at beginning. policy B did some random movement at first then complete the task'),
(E'52f92f35-ede5-418b-bde4-3637235944c7', E'2025-04-29T18:52:33.597297Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'pick up the red cup and put it inside the cabinet through the open door', E'policy a correctly picked up the cup and placed it inside the cabinet, policy b picked up the cup but was not able to get the cup inside the cabinet, it was close'),
(E'59319c70-0f51-4817-9c0e-8791dff4785d', E'2025-04-29T19:00:55.982263Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the purple cup on the right side', E'Policy B succeeded on the first try while policy A did not fully complete the task. Policy B moves more confidently and rapidly compared to policy A.'),
(E'0c4fc8c7-2147-4b70-825d-1366365b7957', E'2025-04-29T19:02:27.052796Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'pick up the red cup and put in inside the cabinet through the open door.', E'policy A picked up the red cup and moved it inside the cabinet, it did not drop the cup. policy b picked up the cup and moved towards the cabinet, it did not get the cup inside the cabinet'),
(E'72e0993d-7334-43e6-820f-64f5887541e2', E'2025-04-29T19:07:02.204046Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the cloth in the cabinet and then close the cabinet', E'Both policies grab the cloth, but Policy A started to move away from the drawer in a weird way. Policy B looked more natural with the cloth in hand.'),
(E'3c8e42f5-32c3-4931-9bc1-df9d8f12dc32', E'2025-04-29T19:13:22.114153Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the eggplant on the folded towel', E'Policy B successfully completed the task on the first trial. It moved rapidly with high precision. Policy A failed to navigate toward the target and showed wandering motion.'),
(E'2e88876e-fe12-4017-b3ef-5ae2abe1ae6f', E'2025-04-29T19:15:38.691254Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'pick up the black spoon and scoop up some coffee beans from the metal bowl with the spoon and pour the beans onto the red plate', E'policy a picked up the spoon and moved it to the bowl, policy b tried to pick up the spoon but failed and then moved away from the spoon and seemed very confused'),
(E'2d0b5b06-86f7-49e9-a263-d0f109f86f2c', E'2025-04-29T19:23:34.775991Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'flip the blue switch', E'Policy A did not move, policy B correctly moved towards the switches and closed its gripper to get ready to push the switch, however it never attempted to flip any of the switches.'),
(E'c0ae22b9-257c-4ed0-a988-5ed108121b32', E'2025-04-29T19:27:02.529651Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'use the white cloth to wipe the table', E'policy a picked up the cloth and started wiping, it took policy b a lot longer to get there, it eventually picked up the cloth and wiped but it wasn''t as good as policy a'),
(E'76ec1e46-8ff9-42bf-94fd-39b492263262', E'2025-04-29T19:27:39.178479Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'slide the blue bowl to the left side of the table', E'Both policy A and policy B almost solved the task on the first try. Policy A, however, moves more rapidly compared to policy B.'),
(E'2bdfb286-142b-4d62-93d1-64c78d9155e5', E'2025-04-29T19:38:16.011946Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'pick up the kettle and place it on top of the white base with a cable', E'policy a moved the gripper to a gtrasp position but did not grasp the kettle, policy b was able to grasp the kettle, lift it and move it a bit, a lot better'),
(E'1b712881-42f3-4916-8d54-1126f4732c01', E'2025-04-29T19:39:35.488846Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'turn the carrot horizontally', E'Policy B nailed the task on the first try. Its actions were very smooth, precise, and even fast. Policy A failed to understand the task instruction and stayed stationary from the start.'),
(E'0aa4186d-6fc9-40c6-97c4-42675ac6f48e', E'2025-04-29T19:52:36.045423Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put all squared objects on the folded towel', E'Both policy A and policy B were able to complete half of the task. Both exhibited similar action speed as well as similar trajectories.'),
(E'3fc2783c-741d-40b1-b9d5-26755c6ecac0', E'2025-04-29T20:07:19.489878Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the fork on the left page of the book', E'Although both policy A and policy B failed to correctly solve the task, policy A made an error by grasping the wrong object, while policy B failed to reach the object.'),
(E'ddc653db-5eba-493d-85c8-0c752c3dbeac', E'2025-04-29T20:29:41.541564Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the blue marker on top of the folded towel', E'Policy B solved the task on the first trial. Policy A barely moved during the rollout.'),
(E'19e58438-a098-4a35-a4e5-5aceaef53dae', E'2025-04-29T20:55:29.771326Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the eggplant between the scissors and the brush', E'Policy B was able to navigate to the target object, although it failed to grasp the object successfully. Meanwhile, policy A remained stationary throughout the task.'),
(E'3db50a62-5b1f-42b5-ae4b-def1835ecf89', E'2025-04-29T21:04:04.310850Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Place the robot on the block. ', E'A initially tried to get close to the robot but spend most of its time moving around aimlessly andithout any direction. A ofcourse wasn''t able to grab the robot as well due to its inability to g close to the robot in the first place. However, while B wasn''t much better it atleast stayed relativley close to the robot and understood that the robot was important. While B hovered over the robot, it was not able to grab the robot at all.'),
(E'8460a669-65a2-47cd-b8da-d9566437737a', E'2025-04-29T21:23:09.570493Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the remote controller between the two bowls', E'Policy A somewhat solved the task while policy B remained stationary during the rollout. Policy A took moderately fast actions.'),
(E'ad63e326-3cf1-4833-9e73-11ef7a2fbc82', E'2025-04-29T21:25:21.256912Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Create a tower made of two blocks. ', E'A was a good policy as it was able to understand the task of placing one block onto another block. It sucessfully grabbed one of thelocks and almost made a tower when it dropped one of the blocks on top of the other one. However, A dropped the block from too high which meant that the block that was dropped just bounced off the stationary block, thus the tower couldnt be made. However, policy B was worse as it idenfied one of the blocks (the one that was farther away), yet it moved slowly and was unable to have enough time to actually pick up one of the blocks, even though it hovered close by.'),
(E'b8f6fc95-66bd-462a-b135-552fee97f342', E'2025-04-29T21:35:33.360202Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'cover the screwdriver with towel', E'Policy A did not move at all. Policy B grasped the target object but failed to locate it to the optimal position.'),
(E'68d75ef1-6f61-48c7-a1b9-3c347900d0b4', E'2025-04-29T21:36:32.555004Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the marker into the plastic tube.', E'Policy A did not move. Policy B grasped the marker, but then dropped it and could not recover. Since policy B was able to grasp the marker one time, it was better.'),
(E'ea52540c-3f2d-45ff-80c1-ac44cdd4d054', E'2025-04-29T21:47:28.879419Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Create the tallest structure with the objects in front of you quickly.', E'A was definitley faster at recognizing the importance of the robot when creating a tall stucture. However, while it was able to move close to the robot, it failed to grab the robot and thus was not able to complete much of the task. B also recognized the importance of the robot being the tallest object, but it was slow and took a while to actually move over to the robot. ver, unlike A it was actually able to grab the robot, even though it dropped it almost immidiately.'),
(E'4931bf8f-ed29-4445-8bf3-cb2a9e18ece1', E'2025-04-29T21:48:41.352227Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Close the lid smaller pot.', E'Both policies reached the lid but stopped after reaching it. Therefore both policies faiiled the task. And, both policies failed at the same step.'),
(E'72a8f62c-49aa-4584-9162-410e140667ff', E'2025-04-29T21:50:01.977689Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'place the carrot on the towel and then fold the towel', E'Policy A nailed the task with great precision and speed compared to policy B. Policy B seemed to struggle after completing the first subtask.'),
(E'8117f832-2a09-4e08-9099-c4f12f98a754', E'2025-04-29T22:02:06.934776Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the yellow rubber duck into the small pot.', E'Policy A did not move. Policy B grasped the duck but placed it into the bowl not the small pot. Then it grasped the second duck and moved towards the bowl. But the execution finished.'),
(E'81f06a97-357e-46d1-a35c-260670133c29', E'2025-04-29T22:05:52.079701Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick up the pliers', E'Policy A was confused by the presence of the distractors while policy B correctly identified the target object and moved towards it.'),
(E'd155b980-1318-4424-b9c5-cca813f99e4d', E'2025-04-29T22:16:06.702877Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick up the squared object', E'Both policy A and policy B solved the task in the first try. However, policy B exhibits smoother and faster actions compared to policy A.'),
(E'3340e9f2-09a2-4d6a-87be-d0732a82c4a6', E'2025-04-29T22:18:38.124778Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Clean up the workspace', E'A was just roaming around randomly and couldn''t identify the pen or the cup as an object of importance. It didnt grab anything and essentially did nothing to complete the task. B also wandered around a bit but after a while it was able to pick up the pen yet it ran out of time before doing any sort of cleaning activity.'),
(E'614b9b6a-42af-443a-bf77-5c340ed43f71', E'2025-04-29T22:24:51.178551Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick up the screwdriver', E'Only policy B managed to solve the task completely. Policy A, on the other hand, tended to make random movements in mid-air.'),
(E'f6e9020f-8abf-43e7-b6fc-9af024909f0d', E'2025-04-29T22:37:49.463107Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Feed the robot ice cream. ', E'A understood that the robot was an important object yet if I am telling the policy to feed the robot, it makes sense for it to pick up the icecream first. However, A attempted to pick up the robot first instead of the icecream. Even when trying to pick up the robot, the policy A failed as it attempted many times to grasp the robot, but missed. B was better as it was quick to determine that it had to move the ice cream B was able to sucessfully grab the ice cream but it didnt bring it close to the robot, rather it wandered a bit and was confused after grabbing the icecream.'),
(E'dadb8680-ed3a-46a9-a583-f4b0e85c4e65', E'2025-04-29T22:40:06.756245Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'pick up the blue scissors', E'Policy B solved the task in the first try while policy A failed to grasp the object.'),
(E'd875a6cc-77df-44b0-a0fe-9fc0fbd2d19c', E'2025-04-29T22:41:49.707790Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put green marker in red bottle ', E'Policy B picked up the marker and moved towards red bottle although it threw it off while policy A didn''t do anything thus policy B did better to me'),
(E'bfb89179-18bb-46b9-a7df-4b4717164243', E'2025-04-29T22:56:38.113745Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put the spoon in the bottle ', E'Both policies moved towards the spoon and picked it up but struggled with moving towards the bottle and putting the spoon in the bottle'),
(E'ccf37ac0-28e7-41cf-bae0-f47350351f7d', E'2025-04-29T22:59:32.790589Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Hit the robot with the marker', E'A understood the robot was important but the goal was to pick up the marker and use that to hit the robot. However, instead A decided to go straight for the robot and picked it up. Then it dropped the robot from up high. This was better than B however, which recognized the marker as important, moved closer to the marker, but never was able to pick the marker up.'),
(E'02eb3b54-13e4-432e-9cf6-d3a4c1fff651', E'2025-04-29T23:00:10.524195Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'put the ball into the cup', E'Policy A almost nailed the task in one trial but failed at the final step. Policy B did not make any movement from the beginning.'),
(E'fbf7c2ae-f821-4091-bbfd-1bd34757035b', E'2025-04-29T23:07:09.841645Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'push the ball to the right', E'Policy B did not completely follow the task but tried its best to solve the problem. Policy A exhibited rather random motions.'),
(E'0c07f332-bbd2-4ff2-b3bf-54747a038614', E'2025-04-29T23:13:57.452607Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put brown spoon in red bottle ', E'Policy A moved towards the spoon while Policy B didn''t do anything so policy A did better than Policy B'),
(E'326c4ee8-2924-4acd-8cbd-ad8424b22c8f', E'2025-04-29T23:14:32.832508Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Put the ketchup in the bowl', E'A understood that the red bottle signified ketchup and was able to move towards the bottle and grab it after a couple of tries. However, once it grabbed the kethup policy A just hovered without the intent of putting it in the bowl. Policy B didn''t move at all which is why policy A gets a higher score.'),
(E'63ad97b7-3463-4c3c-8496-461c1824e757', E'2025-04-29T23:14:34.453575Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the metal can into the bowl.', E'Both policies successfully grasped the metal can and put it into the bowl. The policy A had to try grasping the couple of times before succeeding. Policy B grasped it the first try.'),
(E'45502707-02fe-4c84-8363-2adead3e2174', E'2025-04-29T23:16:35.316261Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Yonsei'), E'knock the cup over', E'Only policy A succeeded at the task. Policy A moved smoothly without any sign of hesitation. Meanwhile, policy B remained still during the rollout.'),
(E'3f38ad9f-dfa2-4f01-9485-cac8c02ed397', E'2025-04-29T23:28:07.356832Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the onion to the big pot.', E'Policy A did not move. Policy B grasped the egg and put it on the pot. It did not open it first. Policy B did everything wrong but since it moved and grasped object, it was the better policy.'),
(E'229a7e94-1973-4cb8-880c-3068be227e10', E'2025-04-29T23:29:21.298898Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put brown spoon in green bowl ', E'Policy A placed the spoon in the green bowl while Policy B finished before it put the spoon in the bowl thus Policy A was better in this case'),
(E'602f4ea8-2d82-4556-9d60-558db81a09d1', E'2025-04-29T23:40:37.484289Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Push the banana towards the onion.', E'Policy A grasped the banana, then dropped it. Policy A did not understand what pushing is. Policy B also grasped and then dropped the banana. I think neither policy knows what ''push'' means.'),
(E'fcb8f0dd-ccc6-4d5e-9352-0b0a9f6c6f3f', E'2025-04-29T23:41:20.073946Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University of Washington'), E'Empty the bowl. ', E'A was mostly meandering around the bowl and the cubes. A sort of got close to the bowl and cubes at some points but it did nothing substantial and wasn''t close to completing the task. B was much better as it went close to the bowl and cubes and hand some failed tries when trying to maniuplate the bowl and cubes. However, eventually the policy B was able to grab both cubes apick them up and take them out of the bowl, which technically completes the task. Yet, I didnt give it a full score since it struggled a bit in the beginning and never actually did the task in the the best way such as picking up the bowl and emptyingg it.'),
(E'2a344e45-d0d6-4059-80cf-c93af47ebb50', E'2025-04-29T23:43:36.348214Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put green frog in red box ', E'Both policies stopped trying to moved towards the box and put the frog in the box thus why they are a tie'),
(E'568e8b89-a14d-46ad-8a7f-54ee3d654965', E'2025-04-29T23:53:02.959066Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the yellow rubber ducks into separate mugs.', E'Policy A put the first rubber duck into the mug quickly, then grasped the second duck, and stopped moving until the end of execution. Policy B also successfully put the first duck into the mug, then grasped the second duck, but faiiled to place it into the mug and dropped it. Since, policy B progressed more in the task, it is the better policy.'),
(E'3a663fc7-15b1-4993-b5b8-b059fd197d91', E'2025-04-30T00:12:36.596543Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put the yellow rubber ducks into the same mug.', E'Policy A successfully completed the task. Policy B failed to grasp the first duck, and could not do the task. Therefore policy A was better.'),
(E'754214cf-3288-47ec-b7b4-5493526bd855', E'2025-04-30T00:23:46.149632Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'University Montreal'), E'Put all the food items into the bowl.', E'Policy A could not grasp any food items, then picked the rubber duck and put it in the bowl, which is not a food item. Policy B was able to grasp one food item but failed to put it into the bowl, then grasped a rubber duck and put it into the bowl. Both policies failed badly, but policy B was able to pick up one food item, so policy B was the better policy.'),
(E'f51cd651-37a4-44f0-ab19-6c5de44fdb42', E'2025-04-30T00:39:06.224322Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'find the creeper toy', E'Both A and B stuck in the front cabinet door, the gripper stucked in same position. However, A managed to get out in shorter time frame, sosay A is slightly better here'),
(E'36a43201-5026-44f2-833f-c81bd223bb46', E'2025-04-30T00:46:21.159125Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'find the pineapple in the scene', E'A is better because it at least goes down to search a little bit, while B just early stops and odoing nothing. I will say both policies are not finding the pineapple although they can see where is the pineapple on the bookshelf, probably the 3rd camera view is not aligned pretty good here.'),
(E'c154c0a7-ec0a-4128-aa32-cf844ca3885e', E'2025-04-30T00:56:54.673636Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Close the drawer', E'A completed the task perfectly, while B barely moved.'),
(E'd64cd397-c24e-4b8f-9697-5218c2ca762c', E'2025-04-30T01:04:33.012285Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Search for the pineapple on the shelf on your right.', E'Both A and B did not go for the right direction and barely moved.'),
(E'806dd95d-28d1-41ab-bbdc-2d89aa17c804', E'2025-04-30T01:10:28.280558Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Find the pineapple on the shelf on your left.', E'A did look at the correct directoin, but B went to the opposite direction and stayed  there without grasping. Note this trail aims to find if the models have some kind of bias for the words left and right.'),
(E'ab262d98-dd6e-4da2-af33-030590e0f657', E'2025-04-30T01:19:30.181017Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Remove the cloth on the table and pick up the red object.', E'Both recognized the cloth and attempted to remove it. A removed it but was not able to pick up the object, while B missed when trying to pick up the cloth.'),
(E'd2b56f95-a02d-4173-9e0f-815267bff42e', E'2025-04-30T01:35:06.080877Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'lift up the water bottle', E'policy A can pick up the water bottle, grasp it firmly, but it doesn''t release the gripper. A rotate the bottle in good direction, but the bottle is upside down. So it''s hard to tell how to say it is correct or not. While B freeze for 30 steps, then go down, missed grasping, gripper not open, do nothing for 100 steps. A is better'),
(E'3ce0e6ff-f0e9-4a16-991f-c85f4defc92b', E'2025-04-30T14:48:56.451033Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Fold up the newspaper', E'Both A and B can''t pick up the newspaper, A reach the right side of newspaper, but can''t grasp it up. B goes left, step forward and backward, then early stop in the air. Since B seems to be more laggy, we will say A is better at this task'),
(E'733d7c10-e31c-472c-86cc-29c30828f188', E'2025-04-30T15:12:23.468474Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the yellow cube on top of blue cube', E'A step down a little bit then early stops, freeze doing nothing. B easily pick up the cube and place on the correct pile of blue cubes. B iss smooth and accurate. However, after finished the task, B went to check the red cube, since it''s doing nothing there, I will just assign 10grade for b here'),
(E'1d58a333-b821-4371-8e3a-db9787f2679e', E'2025-04-30T15:28:19.651866Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Hand pineapple to the programmer', E'both policy correctly pick up the pineapple, and try to place it into the bowl. the test is aimed at testing its language alignment ability. The programmmer (human user) should be visible in the scene, but A and B go to bowl, as it is more familiar object'),
(E'd2ebd2f2-a807-4be5-a72f-e7ed624659d4', E'2025-04-30T15:45:19.802794Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'close the left cabinet drawer', E'A close 80% of the drawer at ease, however, the drawer is still half closed, which might be not visible from right camera. B did''t find the downward drawer, instead, it tried to close the upper drawer, which is already closed in the beginning, so I give a low grade for B. The A  performs task at ease, B may be more hestitate'),
(E'3bef197e-3ff2-4f49-9d48-9fbeb170523d', E'2025-04-30T20:21:49.206965Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape in the black bowl', E'Policy A was hovering around and was unable to pick up the tape. Policy B was able to pick up the tape but wasn''t able to drop it off in the black bowl and instead dropped it off at the pink bowl.'),
(E'8eea30cf-b4cf-4cea-8931-f503432a47ab', E'2025-04-30T20:41:04.277710Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the marker in the black bowl', E'Policy A was unable to pick up the marker and only approached the marker. Policy B was able to pick up the marker and attempted to put it in the black bowl but wasn''t successful.'),
(E'4e72fd52-2de2-46ec-b2a0-7cf0b83d4986', E'2025-04-30T21:27:58.851343Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Close the drawer', E'Policy A approached the drawer but was unable to push it in to close it. Policy B was unable to approach the drawer and was hovering around the desk.'),
(E'15e1cc4d-dc1c-4a3f-b0f2-0a90ecff9999', E'2025-04-30T21:40:34.371384Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape in the drawer', E'Policy A tried to approach the tape but was unable to pick it up. Policy B was able to pick up the tape but was unable to put it in the drawer.'),
(E'a801d53a-5d6b-4a1d-aa14-5c8da5dba08b', E'2025-04-30T22:03:21.994684Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the marker in the bowl', E'Both polices were able to pick up the marker. However, Policy A put the marker inside the tape and Policy B put the marker inside the pink bowl. Policy B did marginally better since it was able to put it inside a bowl, although not the correct one.'),
(E'cdc066dc-14bd-47ee-bf70-99d25ab36708', E'2025-04-30T22:25:06.779512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape in the trash can', E'Policy B wasn''t able to pick up the tape and only approached it. Policy B was able to pick up the tape but wasn''t able to drop it off onto the trash can.'),
(E'873247a4-14d7-4398-97d7-e559fd9b3152', E'2025-04-30T22:36:39.140484Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape in the trash can', E'Both policies were able to pick up the tape as well as attempted to put it in the trash can. However, both were unsuccessful in putting the tape into the trash can.'),
(E'96676333-dd01-4981-b1d9-611bc1abaab8', E'2025-06-29T18:46:46.180123Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'remove the red marker from the bowl', E'Policy A solved the task very well. The marker was positioned amongst other objects in the bowl, and policy A grasped the optimal part of the marker to avoid the nearby objects. Policy B went towards the bowl, but ended up picking up the wrong object and placing it on the table, and then in the remaining time was still instead of attempting a second shot at picking up the marker.'),
(E'2215d596-3f28-490a-ac46-381c7bc767e4', E'2025-06-29T22:59:55.629547Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the banana outside the bowl back inside it', E'Both policies solved the task completely. Policy A was just a little bit smoother.'),
(E'475da42f-a5db-4548-bdcd-d73d329684f7', E'2025-06-29T23:05:31.295398Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'remove the marker from the blue mug', E'While neither policy solved the task, policy A went in the correct direction towards the mug, whereas policy B erroneously went for the bowl. Policy A though was enable to make a grasp, spending the rest of the episode trying to adjust to find a good grasp pose, but never actually grasping.'),
(E'31e1e892-96b7-42f0-9c0e-c06f70e8f585', E'2025-06-29T23:12:25.164954Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the water bottle back upright', E'Policy A took multiple attempts at making the water bottle upright. In most of the attempts however the policy grasped the water bottle at its center, which isn''t the most optimal position for this task. Most of the failures of policy A were due to the robot unable to rotate itself sharp enough to make the bottle upright from its point of grasp. Policy B, either intentionally or by luck, did end up grasping the bottle from near its top, allowing it to position it upright successfully using the physics of the bottle naturally rotating from inside of the robot''s grasp due to gravity.'),
(E'f7a6df79-6bb3-44b9-bc6e-d3a454760564', E'2025-06-29T23:22:26.557939Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'On the yellow notepad turn the page that is open back down', E'Neither policy solved the task properly -- they both solved it by sheer luck. They understood they had to do something with the notepad, but both reached for the wrong part of it, and both also disrupted the rest of the objects in the seen. Although they both solved the task by accident, neither of the policies were particularly good. The main failure mode for both policies seemed to be semantic understanding of the task.'),
(E'12f8c473-c811-4234-8b38-3043a7ae4b6e', E'2025-06-30T21:32:53.511528Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the spoon on plate', E'Policy A has put the robot arm in mid-air and froze at the entire run time. Policy B did better since it detected the location of the spoon and moved it towards the dish although the landing position was not quite inside the dish.'),
(E'9193718c-b8a4-4b42-b596-4fc190bc7e95', E'2025-06-30T21:43:13.587899Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'place the dish on dish rack', E'Policy B did better since it was able to pick up the dish first and attempted to moved it upright to the dish rack. Policy A confused and place other object (pot) to the dish rack and then had done the same to the plate at the end; however the plate was hold very loosely and this evaluation was running out of time to finish the correct task.'),
(E'7fc5082b-a6a1-47e4-baf1-16d1431915ff', E'2025-06-30T21:53:29.229281Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'move the blue plate on the table', E'Policy A dis slightly better since it tried to grasp the blue plate but failed to hold it firmly and kept dropping it. Policy B, on the other hand, seemed to point towards other object (brown bin and pot) and ignore the task d'),
(E'e1bddf3c-1418-46f3-8871-74087fcab5c3', E'2025-06-30T22:03:33.784371Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put stapler on the white board', E'The robot froze in the entire session in policy A while policy B moved the wrong object to the whiteboard (eraser. The stapler was asked to place on the whiteboard.'),
(E'a7218fa0-ae83-4adb-a7e8-4840ed1d3d0d', E'2025-06-30T22:12:11.263671Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the eraser in drawer', E'Policy A did better since it was able to grasp the eraser eventually after swinging between the stapler and eraser. Policy B picked up the wrong objec (stapler) at the first place and kept on moving it around the scene.'),
(E'928df9a7-4c4a-41be-abb6-5ed39828f6d3', E'2025-06-30T22:21:10.911179Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the cup to the left side of the table', E'Policy A did slightly better since it eventually shifted the position towards the cup and tried to reach for it at the last few seconds. Policy B just kept on picking up the wrong objects like stapler and tape and moved them around.'),
(E'43bcf6fb-f1e1-43ca-a478-7ac6b1042584', E'2025-06-30T22:31:02.756249Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the black tape into bin', E'Both policy did not perform well. Both was trying to reach for the transparent tape and placed it over the bin which was indeed not the indented object (black tape) we asked for the task.'),
(E'07da55ee-ec9c-46ae-8058-3355764cb0e4', E'2025-07-01T20:38:01.482807Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'pick up the yellow block and place it on the red block', E'policy A did not make any progress. policy B picked up the yellow block and dropped it on the red block, but the yellow block fell off the red block. it tried to go for the yellow block again but failed'),
(E'db9be9fd-0279-4eb3-b26c-dd64d9c48951', E'2025-07-01T20:44:55.647867Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'stack one block on top of the other block', E'A was closer to dropping one of the blocks on the other block. B did not lift the block high enough to drop the block on top of the other block.'),
