(E'c64aaacc-99f5-4411-9052-f887849f735e', E'2025-08-08T17:11:04.954613Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the pen.', E'Both policies opted for the marker and were able to successfully pick it up. It is worth mentioning that policy A moved around a lot more after picking up the marker while policy B stayed in the same spot and didn''t lift the marker very high either.'),
(E'b379247f-c6c9-4b7a-a71a-07c5e245c7a3', E'2025-08-08T17:17:34.545036Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'pick up the marker and place it next to the spatula.', E'policy B was able to completly execute the task while policy A just sat in place.'),
(E'7015bcad-640e-4e62-82ef-16fb01c96ab9', E'2025-08-08T17:23:32.477634Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object that you would use to screw in a screw.', E'policy A had opted for the spatula and was successfully able to grab at it. I chose policy B because, even though it didn''t succesfully grab the screwdirver, it had correctly identified that it was the object it needed to go for. It is worth mentioning that policy B might have found it difficult to grasp the screw driver due to the cluttered nature of the environment. It had enough space to grab the screwdriver, but it''s perception might have been confused or something similar to that.'),
(E'd10d1bde-30ef-4426-a330-f5856663e9a0', E'2025-08-08T17:32:04.886333Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object best for eating.', E'policy A had grabbed the screwdriver for some reason. It is worth mentioning that the screwdriver is close to the bread, so it is possible that the robot had begun reaching for the bread and had for some reason changed course to the screwdriver. policy B had correctly idenfitied that it should grab the bread but was not able to grab it. That being said, policy B was very close to grabbing the bread and given some more time, I believe it coud.'),
(E'bcba23f6-fa26-43d8-8bdd-f17a567733c1', E'2025-08-08T17:38:51.912740Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object that you could use as material to build a wood house.', E'policy A was able to identify that it should go for the wooden block, but was unable to grab it. policy B had identified and grabbed the bread whicmight be because it had confused the bread for wood or because it was the easiest, most visible object to grab.'),
(E'b38dc9b3-655a-404f-ae6c-458e2349d58f', E'2025-08-08T17:46:03.626399Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object that you would use to draw with.', E'policy A had started by attempting to grab the screwdriver but then it''s movement began drifting towards the pencil. It is worth mentionting that the pencil is on the far left of the scene, so if the policy is more prone to look right in the center, it might explain why policy A had gone for the screwdriver and then began to drift towards the pencil. It is also worth mentioning that the pencil and screwdriver look somewhat similar. policy B didn''t do anything.'),
(E'9e843f9a-8f82-48fc-ac21-b238abd63025', E'2025-08-08T17:52:55.975175Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object best used for stirring a pot full of soup.', E'both policies were unable to reach the spatula. It is worth mentioning that the spatula is on the edge of the scene and in a cluttered space. Both policies seemed confused at which object to grab at some point in the episode. policy A was confident in the beginning, picking up the wooden block, but then drifted towards the spatula. policy B was less confident and started by moving towards the screwdriver and then moved back and forth also drifting towards the spatula. I am not sure if either policy had actually identified the spatula and was moving towards it, or if they just tended right when re-adjusting itself.'),
(E'91fcd78c-a02c-4cc4-a269-34a5d492fa2a', E'2025-08-08T18:08:31.869810Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the black tape that is attached to the wooden block.', E'Both policies grabbed the block but not the tape on the block. policy A might have gone for the tape in the beginning but that is mostly speculation. Both polices mostly grabbed the block. I believe that policy A was more agressive than policy B.'),
(E'98d38572-82da-4399-9925-c74d4ea976fe', E'2025-08-08T18:14:58.740849Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Press the space bar on the keyboard.', E'policy B was able to quickly able to press the space bar with so much extra time it seemed as though it was going to try it again. policy A was able to press the keyboard, but was not able to press the space bar. It is worth mentioning that policy A pressed very close to the space bar, but also didn''t seem to really progress towards it. Once policy A started pressing on the keyboard, it continued to press the same group of buttons until it was time to stop.'),
(E'4f5ac30d-ccf6-4c92-82df-b0d83a0a8624', E'2025-08-08T18:38:14.359526Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put chicken wing on plate', E'B completed the task while A only moved the wing towards the plate'),
(E'955155d7-463b-4b69-8438-294993ac9023', E'2025-08-08T18:44:35.489218Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put chicken wing on plate ', E'A couldn''t pick up the wing while B completed the task'),
(E'e2f191ac-bf5e-4975-879c-6e6c3fc35fc5', E'2025-08-08T18:50:16.090012Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put chicken wing on plate ', E'B completed the task while A did nothing'),
(E'31233f4b-4a37-40b0-ab20-43bbcc355155', E'2025-08-08T18:55:46.336393Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put chicken wing on plate ', E'Both policies tried to pick up chicken wing but didn''t manage to'),
(E'0ce424f5-2118-4ab3-84b7-b34ca99d6c93', E'2025-08-08T19:03:29.393290Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'Put chicken wing in plate ', E'A wasn''t able to pick up wing but B completed the task'),
(E'ca2f008e-d0c6-4b5e-baa5-1337c70851cf', E'2025-08-08T19:11:14.588614Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'Put chicken wing on plate ', E'B completed the task while A only managed to pick the chicken'),
(E'ae818621-845e-4bc7-8f68-c459e48759ea', E'2025-08-08T19:20:10.425277Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'put chicken wing on plate ', E'A put the chicken wing on plate while B only moved toward the wing'),
(E'f7b0fd22-4dbb-4bed-8907-d87d1bb405b1', E'2025-08-08T19:40:47.821796Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Stanford'), E'Put bread on plate ', E'B tried to pick up the bread but A moved in random directions'),
(E'55f32db2-39fb-4daa-982f-9a1ef3198727', E'2025-08-11T19:30:25.873198Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Flip the cup over.', E'I liked policy A more than policy B because policy A actually made contact with the cup. While policy A wasn''t even able to get the cup on it''s side, let alone upside down, policy B did not even grab the cup. Perhaps this relates to a difference in agressivness between policies where policy A is more aggressive than policy B.'),
(E'dfc35399-6c39-44d6-b39f-0d7e0e44473e', E'2025-08-11T19:37:38.211661Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Knock over the cup. But when you do knock over the cup, make sure that your gripper is closed.', E'Both policies were unable to knock over the cup. policy A actually picked up the cup but otherwise the policies were very similar. For some reason, both polciies seemed to grab the cup, maybe interpreting that as what it needed to do when I asked it to make sure the gripper was closed when it knocked over the cup. In any case, both policies seemed pre-occupied with grabbing the object as it''s means of interaction and failed to consider other means of interacting with the object, failing to complete the task as a result.'),
(E'6619469c-f2f9-42d8-b345-2b1a7c37de70', E'2025-08-11T19:47:19.288250Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Please pick up the screw driver', E'Neither policies were able to change their gripper position from a mostly up right position which would have helped grab the screw driver. Both policies began searching for something away from the screwdriver maybe on the ground somewhere. Both policies managed to touch the screwdriver seemingly running into it, policy B even getting to a place where if it had squeeze it''s gripper, it would have been successful in grabbing the screwdriver. Unfortunately the screwdriver has been unmoved.'),
(E'd3c30092-6885-4996-846d-690c2ade411d', E'2025-08-11T19:58:28.411300Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the screwdriver.', E'I had placed the screwdriver at a diagonal in hoping that the difficulty of more horizonal positions for the gripper might be mititgated. Unfortunatley neither policy was able to overcome this. Policy A was able to actually grab the foam that the screwdriver is resting in, but did not actually grab the screw driver.'),
(E'2f065157-4c5e-4fda-8c06-7b4d0bd4b49b', E'2025-08-11T20:11:03.133999Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'grab the screwdriver', E'Policy A was able to rotate it''s gripper and grab the screwdriver. The screw driver was placed so that it would stick out horizontally, making it easier to grab. That being said, the robot gripper still had to rotate about the z axis, something which policy B seemed to struggle with. policy B for some reason did not even approach the screwdriver but instead seemed to look at the space behind the foam block instead.'),
(E'1e334acf-e458-4c1d-9354-9093833c4565', E'2025-08-11T20:30:26.731339Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove the sponge from the table.', E'policy A was not able to move the block off the table or much at all, but at the end it was able to eventually grab the block. policy A was very intent on grabbing it from the top even though other locations on the block might have been better, or simply knocking it off the table would have worked as well. I wonder if this might be because policy A has a tendency to approach tasks by grabbing at things. policy B did nothing at all, it did not even move.'),
(E'98a64110-2248-48ac-8930-16e80134a4c3', E'2025-08-11T20:44:00.190063Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Please knock the sponge off the table. DO NOT grab the sponge.', E'Neither policy was able to knock the block off, but policy A did start moving the block and did not try grabbing the block at all. policy B on the other hand seemed incredibly confused on how to do the task and had actually begun to grab the block before stopping itself. After stopping itself from grabbing the block, policy B spent the rest of it''s time above the block seemingly trying to figure out what to do.'),
(E'6bd49cb6-c0df-4f0b-9d5d-419d30fb1e88', E'2025-08-11T20:52:29.171260Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Press the blue lego ontop of the brown lego.', E'policy A was able to grab a lego, but it grabbed the wrong one. policy B had instead opted to press the brown lego and not grab anything at all. I realize now that I might have been able to elaborate more on my instruction so that policy B might have realized that in order to press on the brown lego it would need to pick up the blue one first. In any case, I wanted to bring attention to the fact that policy B''s actions might have actually been intentional and perhaps even more correct than policy A''s, but since neiher policy approached the blue lego and make meaningful progress, I would consider this a tie.'),
(E'3bbd92ba-34a9-4df1-bf33-70d8bc066801', E'2025-08-11T21:05:10.662221Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'first grab the phone and then press a button.', E'policy B was able to smash it''s gripper into where the buttons are indicating that it had "pressed a button", but it did this before attempting to grab the phone and I am not sure if it meaningfully did y to grab the phone. That being said, since policy A did nothing, I chose policy B.'),
(E'276baae6-6b9f-469b-abf3-369834275f97', E'2025-08-11T21:12:01.007806Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the phone.', E'Neither policy was able to grab the phone. policy A seemed to struggle to actually locate/identify the pose in order to grab the phone. It seemed to smash itself hopeing to grab at something but to no avail. Other policies seemed to have difficulty with this as well, it might be because the black phone mixes with the black phone holder, making it hard for whatever vision model to differentiate the phone in order to effectivley grab it.'),
(E'9f3e970c-4859-40eb-a16e-2a0b7c2fa030', E'2025-08-11T21:17:03.001129Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'pick the edible object', E'Both policies did  well since they were able to detect the edible thing (watermelon) and grasp it eventually. A encountered some difficultties on the gripper picking up at first but completed grasping it nicely. B seemed to react a little bit better since it just grasped and go without any retry.'),
(E'46bcbeb6-71d0-40de-b10d-473196044e1a', E'2025-08-11T21:22:45.721050Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Call the number 1.', E'While no policy realized that to call 1, they would have to press 1 before grabbing the phone, I chose policy A because it was able to effectivley grab the phone while policy B had only been able to grab and let go of the phone in place without moving it at all.'),
(E'25747da9-24e2-4c2b-af7e-d83c4c4d7ab7', E'2025-08-11T21:27:02.224409Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape into bowl', E'B completely went off track since it headed towards the marker and tried to waved it over the right. A at least located where the tape was at but had difficulty grasping it. A just kept pushing the tape further and further away.'),
(E'f35673cf-c20e-44ba-a86f-4a88adf597ef', E'2025-08-11T21:35:47.953214Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the bowls with the pink bowl on the bottom', E'A and B both understands they have to perform stacking task but both did not completely do as required. A tried to reach the pink bowl first (which is not the right order of task) and placed it on the tape; it then realized the bowls must be stacked onto each so it reached for the pink bowl again and tried to grasped it but the time did not allow to do so. B completed the stacking job but the order was not correct; the pink bowl must be on the bottom while here it was placed on top'),
(E'8969aed7-b152-448c-98d8-b7f2f68f8f0a', E'2025-08-11T21:49:49.642443Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape in drawer', E'A did not response to the task while B just halfway finished it since it was able to grasp the tape but then had to left it mid air due to time constraint'),
(E'229afa83-86c9-46e8-95fc-12d19a02ebc2', E'2025-08-11T22:03:15.476926Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkley'), E'put the cube inside the tape', E'BOth policies did not do so well. A tended to reach for the middle of the scene and B it tried to grasp the waterbottle on the left.'),
(E'd9a311c8-3972-4a42-8aae-34afc84f9252', E'2025-08-11T22:22:42.485161Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the eraser on top of the drawer', E'both policies completely ignored the eraser located in the center of the scene and just reached for the waterbottle which kinda looked similar in shape'),
(E'7a9539d8-9c56-4519-ad61-6e05d7d21928', E'2025-08-11T22:38:14.727879Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move teh waterbottle on drawer', E'Both policies did not grasp the waterbottle in place. It instead tried to grasp things around it such as tape and drawer'),
(E'd981102e-0028-4dbd-ad05-c8a1c6ac253d', E'2025-08-11T22:48:32.100507Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put one of the bread on bowl', E'Both policies has reached the point that they were able to point towards where the bread and grasped it fromthe toaster; however, both failed to remove it from the toaster'),
(E'40a0960d-04ca-4712-b3ee-2e6d28d84ff1', E'2025-08-11T23:06:18.219648Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'serve the other slice of bread in the toaster', E'Both policies has stopped when they were attempting to grasp the grasp the bread from the bowl but the gripper did not lower horizontally to align well with how the bread was placed'),
(E'29298d1f-4665-4d67-bcc7-e3744ccf61f3', E'2025-08-12T08:09:29.879517Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the apples on the plate on top of the cabinet.', E'Policy A does not have a moving robotic arm. Policy B quickly finds the target and attempts to grasp it.'),
(E'305b4bf9-20ba-4c67-a3d2-3a5c5897768a', E'2025-08-12T08:17:28.231429Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the bananas in the plate on top of the cabinet.', E'Policy A completed the grabbing task, but didn''t know where the cabinet was. Policy B completed the task quickly, but knocked over the bottle.'),
(E'd357b0b9-d041-4c44-ad46-b126685b82c8', E'2025-08-12T08:22:23.013747Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Find the cabinet and open the top drawer.', E'Policy A quickly tried to open the drawer of the cabinet, but unfortunately pushed the cabinet over due to excessive force. Policy B didn''t carry out the task but picked up the items in the cabinet and fidgeted with them.'),
(E'cdc047e8-c2fc-4def-b343-eaa986f54045', E'2025-08-12T08:29:31.179393Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Find the cabinet and carefully open the top drawer.', E'Policy A attempted the actions more correctly, although it failed. Policy B didn''t find a proper way to open the drawer.'),
(E'19e9bbf3-fc55-48c2-9ea0-1c88e94bc0c8', E'2025-08-12T08:36:51.145262Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the open drawer.', E'Policy A completed the task quickly and smoothly. Policy B is still a little short of completion and its actions are slow.'),
(E'05fd8588-7fce-4e7f-9c5d-539ec6eec1fc', E'2025-08-12T08:43:43.602659Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take out the bananas from the drawer and put them in the bowl.', E'Policy A completed the task quickly and smoothly. Policy B completed the task slowly and rather roughly.'),
(E'1e89e56a-4362-4aee-b3ec-668778ff9186', E'2025-08-12T08:50:58.452328Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the bananas in the bowl into the open drawer and then close the drawer.', E'It failed to put both in the drawer.'),
(E'46021c04-0a4b-4f26-8050-138de071ebbe', E'2025-08-12T09:01:20.616631Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the building blocks on the cabinet into the open drawer and close the drawer.', E'Policy A completed the grasping and placement quickly and smoothly, but performed an additional grasping and placement of the wrong target. Policy B grasped the wrong object and the placement action also failed.'),
(E'b99c802a-d785-402c-802d-83b140883634', E'2025-08-12T09:10:33.967831Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Open the top drawer, take out the building blocks inside, and put them into the cup.', E'Policy A executed the task quickly but without success. Policy B didn''t understand the task and was trying to grab the cup.'),
(E'7cd0e2af-6991-4742-a5da-0d75022c678b', E'2025-08-12T09:19:16.761852Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Open and then close the middle drawer of the cabinet in front.', E'Policy A is fast but rough in action, and it fails to find a proper way to open the drawer. Policy B tries to open the drawer in a more correct way, though it also fails.'),
(E'dd233925-8004-4a9c-9f53-1baa16bc0ab8', E'2025-08-12T09:27:49.739803Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put all the fruits into the black box.', E'Policy A quickly achieved a goal, but there was another one at the edge of the field of vision that it didn''t notice. Policy B didn''t put the fruits into the box.'),
(E'3be96aa2-6afd-483a-9f27-5dae63e4973a', E'2025-08-12T09:37:44.254902Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take out the grapes from the top drawer and put them into the black box.', E'Policy A failed to find the target. Policy B quickly found the target and attempted to grab it.'),
(E'0dedc76e-1416-4823-9822-8a733dbdb535', E'2025-08-12T09:46:48.910607Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Only put bananas on the plate. Put other fruits in the black box.', E'Both Policy A and Policy B wrongly put the bananas in the box, but Policy A cleaned up the original grapes on the plate, which is relatively better.'),
(E'93165e50-bbef-4853-8d12-8ba82ef20488', E'2025-08-12T10:42:31.295567Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There is a pack of blue facial tissues on the cabinet. Take out a tissue and wipe the plate.', E'Policy A made some attempts, although the goal was incorrect. Policy B did not move.'),
(E'cb992378-dfe5-4192-8d0f-34a8eff1f2d8', E'2025-08-12T10:50:42.817123Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There are many fruits in the black box. Find the grapes and put them on the plate.', E'Policy A has been acting aimlessly, and Policy B is a bit better.'),
(E'a2729a74-fc55-4e78-8daf-f7ab8a27b769', E'2025-08-12T11:59:08.562460Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take the drawer out of the cabinet.', E'Some attempts have been made for the tasks, but the methods are wrong.'),
(E'da9b2725-cd1b-4702-8d71-bccf9c708eb7', E'2025-08-12T12:06:56.988817Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put only the red building blocks in the left box, and put the ones in other colors in the right box.', E'Policy A checks the situation of the box and then prepares to grab it, but it doesn''t control the gripper very well. Policy B just stands there idly.'),
(E'9e1e5342-3c73-45c1-827e-aa0244ee6d15', E'2025-08-12T12:14:45.181425Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put one building block in the box on the left, and put another one in the box above the cabinet.', E'Policy A didn''t find the building blocks and is grabbing the tablecloth. Policy B has completed half of the task.'),
(E'b8d42b65-3c35-447e-9aae-3c65173ce91a', E'2025-08-12T12:26:45.872213Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Try to let as many building blocks as possible fall into the box.', E'Policy A shows no sign of action, while Policy B has made a slight attempt.'),
(E'4ebd2fca-8e58-44db-be10-b0fb6a2032b4', E'2025-08-12T12:35:48.369425Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Knock down all the building blocks.', E'There are only two blocks left to be knocked down for Policy A, and there are still six blocks left for Policy B.'),
(E'd27ce4d7-554b-4bfc-8e6f-c7a9cfa3c65d', E'2025-08-12T12:45:13.243831Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the smallest fruit on the plate.', E'Policy A is in a daze. Policy B tries to find the smallest fruit.'),
(E'b41d2156-8290-4186-9a30-883bc2fe5a51', E'2025-08-12T12:53:32.465856Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the darkest-colored fruits on the plate.', E'Policy A was in a daze, and Policy B made some attempts.'),
(E'0429bca9-3139-4c50-8560-269f39a6e380', E'2025-08-12T20:46:42.688724Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the sponge.', E'policy A was able to determine that it needed a tool to cut the sponge, but it grabbed the pencil instead of the knife. While grabbing the pencil, policy A also accidentally grabbed onto the tarp which impeeded it''s progress to the point where it wasn''t able to successfully transport the pencil either. policy B did nothing at all.'),
(E'ae0b1402-08d3-41f3-9e19-af2643d9978a', E'2025-08-12T20:56:59.377470Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the baguette.', E'policy B was able to identify which of the breads was the baguette but was unable to approach it fast enough to grab it. policy A was quick to grab a round bun, but didn''t ever attempt to grab the baguette. Because this is a mostly semantic task, I decided that policy B did better than policy A even though policy B arguably did less than policy A.'),
(E'76318a61-d76e-4b30-bce0-fb914773a15c', E'2025-08-12T21:04:48.499005Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the bun with sesame seeds.', E'Neither policy moved much. None of the bread was touched and the hand stayed relativley close to it''s starting position for both policies. It was hard to tell if the policies were actually executing the task or if they were just stuck.'),
(E'e57fdd4d-f994-4cca-b93e-6ad0d422291e', E'2025-08-12T22:21:14.290334Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the bread with sesame seeds.', E'Neither policy was able to identify the bread with sesame seeds. The seeds might have been too small, or sesame seeds might have been too obscure. Both policies grabbed the bread that was closest to it, but policy B also grabbed a bun. I chose policy B because it was able to do twice the work of policy A and I would argue that the bread that it got the second time was closer to the correct bread than the bread policy A selected for it''s only bread.'),
(E'401a0b6f-d064-4536-b2fa-e3e4b5be7709', E'2025-08-12T22:29:23.028267Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the bread that is the smallest.', E'Neither policy was able to identify the smallest bread and instead opted for arguably the biggest bread. It is worth mentioning that there were 4 different breads on the table and that the smallest was on the far right of the table. The complexity of the setup might have lead the policies to choose the closest bread it could grab. It is also worth mentioning that policy A was much quicker at grabbing the bread, but I gave it a tie because they had done pretty much the same thing.'),
(E'bf1d5b1d-e64e-4aed-b5fb-bbfae8ae159b', E'2025-08-12T22:40:08.339670Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the smallest bread.', E'policy A was able to complete the task while policy B could not. policy B was fixated on the middle bread. I don''t know if policy B chose the middle bread because it was the most accessible, because it was similar to the actual smallest bread, or some other reason. Both policies were similarly dynamic but policy A extended itself by an unusual amount, causing itself to rotate it''s gripper, something that most policies don''t do even when asked. The hyper-extending could also be seen in how policy A overshot the bread a couple times before eventually settling on the bread.'),
(E'3fb7ebc3-ea06-4e6d-b843-c8b3afa8c899', E'2025-08-12T23:00:37.082622Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the longest bread.', E'Both policies opted for the bread that was closest to them-the smallest bread. Policy A did a somewhat better job at picking up the smallest bread but both policies struggled.'),
(E'737012ff-b181-485f-a71a-745447e20a55', E'2025-08-12T23:08:53.732399Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the red part of the xylophone.', E'Neither policy was able to touch the xylopohone. Both policies paced back and forth above the xylophone, getting close, even closing it''s grippers in anticipation to touch, but eventually pulling back as if to double check. The behavior of the policies were actually very similar, with the ony difference to note being that policy A might have been learning more heavily towards the blue tiles than policy B. It is also worth mentioning that there is a pink tile on the far left side of the xylophone near the blues which might explain why policy A was leaning towards the blue tiles.'),
(E'9da03489-9099-4e38-9d16-d9da08648073', E'2025-08-12T23:18:25.919572Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Play music.', E'I chose policy B because it had done a better job at touching the xylophone. That being said, neither policies grabbed the stick in order to play the xylophone and it isn''t super obviowere approaching the xylophone because they were attempting to play music or simply because they knew that the xyolophone could play music. It is worth mentioning that both policies knew that the xylophone could produce music, and I would also like to mention that policy B decided to actually grab the xylophone for some reason.'),
(E'24da2ad2-2100-46c0-89b2-97d313cb96d0', E'2025-08-12T23:32:16.553512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object you would use to draw on something.', E'Policy A was able to complete the task and had gotten very close to completing it multiple times. Policy B had instead opted for the bread. it is also worth mentioning that policy B for some reason had moved it''s gripper very close to itself in a somewhat uncomfortable seeming position and it did it very quickly. I am not sure if it was trying to get a better view of the scene, but this was an action I had not seen before.'),
(E'19c42130-4549-4b00-ba35-4e47190200cc', E'2025-08-13T02:32:01.980208Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Stack three small white plates on top of each other.', E'Due to the solid-color background, it has become difficult for both models to grasp the objects. Policy A has been trying to grasp the small dish, while Policy B lost the target during continuous attempts and then turned to grasp the plate.'),
(E'ee46c953-aeea-4be9-8456-14373ad3e816', E'2025-08-13T02:57:35.042959Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the fruits on the plate into the small white dish.', E'After grabbing the fruit, Policy A kept hesitating between the plate and the small dish, and finally decided to put it in the small dish, but the fruit fell on the table. After grabbing the fruit, Policy B just put it on the table and didn''t find the small dish.'),
(E'973b93e8-853b-45bc-a3ec-150c8778989a', E'2025-08-13T03:06:27.271468Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Pour the building blocks from the cup onto the plate.', E'Policy A performs actions more smoothly. Policy B acts more slowly and fails to grasp. Both models are not yet familiar with the pouring action.'),
(E'430800d5-3e8a-46d5-8b6c-0745e23355c1', E'2025-08-13T03:22:31.869577Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Grab the screws in the plate and put them into the cup.', E'Policy A grabbed the screw for the first time but then released it, and failed to grab it successfully afterwards. Policy B didn''t take any action and stayed in place.'),
(E'5efd2419-fa79-4872-905c-58eb39e5b11e', E'2025-08-13T03:30:34.262475Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There are many screws in the plate. Grab some and put them into the cup.', E'Policy A has been repeatedly trying to grab the screw and seems unable to determine whether it has successfully grabbed it. Policy B completed a task successfully by putting a screw into the cup. However, there were redundant actions during the whole process, and it hit the cabinet twice, so some points were deducted.'),
(E'418b6b00-cf72-4ef4-97e2-5c2bbad06fb7', E'2025-08-13T06:06:44.088750Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the bagged screws in the box on the plate.', E'Policy A failed to find the target and instead attempted to open the drawer. Policy B failed to place the target after grasping it and only put it on the edge of the plate.'),
(E'73415e97-924a-4ce1-8956-495e917b1238', E'2025-08-13T07:18:10.885739Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the lid of the paper box.', E'Policy A failed to find a suitable way to close the lid. Policy B found the lid of the paper box and attempted to close it, but the action was too simple to handle complex scenarios.'),
(E'a9e6d4ea-8521-4374-a1e5-9a2ffd7292ab', E'2025-08-13T07:30:53.585780Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the lid of the paper box.', E'Policy A is trying to handle the lid. Although it pushed the box out of the field, it''s relatively better. Policy B hasn''t found a way to start and has been adjusting the perspective.'),
(E'd88b5f19-528f-47a1-9f6e-0ffe183cb35e', E'2025-08-13T07:41:15.837837Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the building blocks into the hole above the paper box.', E'The grasping stage of Policy A is relatively fast and accurate. The grasping performance of Policy B is a bit worse. However, neither of them found the cardboard box with holes.'),
(E'17f8acf0-273f-422a-8eec-1fc36c7427ed', E'2025-08-13T07:48:07.797154Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the building blocks into the hole above the paper box.', E'Policy A was relatively fast and accurate during the grasping phase and used appropriate actions to place the building blocks. Unfortunately, the placement position was not the target position. Policy B failed to grasp the building blocks.'),
(E'9e56de9a-7d04-4a3d-b400-52398e068fbf', E'2025-08-13T07:57:39.367001Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the lid of the paper box.', E'Policy A completed the task in the right way. Policy B lost its current state and made ineffective actions.'),
(E'7cdf0c46-a6ad-4a5f-b2f4-bb16700f74a4', E'2025-08-13T08:05:17.802145Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Draw a circle on the lid of the paper box with a pen.', E'Policy A quickly picked up the pen on the plate and moved it to the position of the box, but the second half of the task was not accomplished. Policy B didn''t find the pen and instead grabbed the tablecloth.'),
(E'89ad2092-2dee-4e6f-b400-516a424862e8', E'2025-08-13T08:15:18.851943Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Draw a circle on the paper box with the pen in the plate.', E'Policy A quickly picked up the pen on the plate and completed part of the task. Policy B failed to grab the item.'),
(E'b5334599-4d12-4821-8fab-ddb11e73f0e7', E'2025-08-13T08:22:39.004875Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Assume that the gripper is a pen and use it to draw a circle on the box.', E'Policy A understood the task and quickly pressed on the paper box to try to draw a circle. However, the force was too large, resulting in only very slight postural movements. Policy B did not understand the task and did nothing.'),
(E'c0848a28-24d2-4f65-b741-afff60da3fd6', E'2025-08-13T08:30:03.278008Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the book.', E'Policy A started in the right way, but after pushing down half of the standing part, the task became difficult. Policy B chose the wrong way to close the book and also failed.'),
(E'dbc78599-3c29-497e-8825-8c8239e3bceb', E'2025-08-13T08:41:38.163354Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Push the red toy car and move it closer to the cup.', E'Policy A slightly moved the small car by clamping and releasing. Policy B tried to push it by closing the gripper, but the effect was not ideal, causing the small car to spin in place. The difference between the two is not significant, and I prefer Policy A.'),
(E'324be993-9a55-4d6c-8187-b7bbc1942005', E'2025-08-13T08:56:07.388734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Grab the white cable and put it into the white storage box.', E'Policy A completes the task accurately and quickly. Policy B fails to find the storage box and places the item on the edge of the table after two attempts.'),
(E'054d9c0f-75b4-4365-9303-21df962ab9b8', E'2025-08-13T09:02:52.560811Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put all the messy white cables into the black box.', E'Policy A tried to put the cable into the box, but it fell out. Policy B doesn''t know how to grab the cable yet.'),
(E'de124d8f-3e32-4346-8a63-3941189beefb', E'2025-08-13T19:52:19.854355Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object used for drinking.', E'policy B approached the marker and hovered over it, grabbing and letting it go for the entire duration of the episode. policy A seemed to approach the xylophone and the orange juice, eventually drifting towards the orange juice. policy A was not able to fully lift the orange juice as it could not fully commit to a grasp. After attempting to grasp the orange juice policy A also tried grabbing the xylophone. I chose policy A because it was able to identify that one drinks from the juice, hoewever, both policies seemed to have misconceptions on what object I was referring to at some point.'),
(E'f2a5a5ec-4dcb-40c2-8708-09f72857b214', E'2025-08-13T20:02:55.373619Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'please grab the object you would eat and place it next to the xylophone.', E'I chose to give these policies a tie because both policies were unable to identify the bread instead opted for the marker. I am not sure why both policies decided that the marker was the correct object, but there are some things to note: 1. the cameras are in a somewhat odd position, being very close to the robot and elevated the robot might have had a hard time even seeing the bread which was very close to the robot. 2. there were 4 objects in total. This might have added to the complexity to the problem to the point where the model was not able to descern the correct object. 3. the prompt didn''t explicity encode the sequence that was expected using words like ''first'', ''then'', etc. I bring this up in particular because policy A actually seemed to approach the xylophone before returning to the marker.'),
(E'544f7f8b-5191-4977-b151-0f123f882c04', E'2025-08-13T20:14:54.314079Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'First pick up the edible object and then place the edible object next to the xylophone.', E'I chose policy A because it was able to quickly identify the bread and then begin moving it. Unfortunatley, policy A was not able to identify the xylophone and instead delivered the bread to the marker instead. policy B simply had a tough time actually grabbing the bread, reaching for it, pullling back, and trying again. The closest policy B was able to get to achieving the task was grabbing the bread, but failing to lift the bread. It is worth mentioning that After moving the bread closer, removing an object from the table, and referring to the bread as "edible object" instead of "object that you would eat" both policies were at least able to identify the bread. This is something that I had tried before but neither policy was able to identify the bread, leading me to believe either one of the aformentioned changes or the new policies were the cause.'),
(E'd29a8d60-037c-4611-b239-50f9e7413925', E'2025-08-13T20:37:24.498442Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the object that I would drink out of.', E'Neither policy had identified the water cup as what you would drink out of, but I chose policy B because it went for the spray bottle which is arguably closer. policy A had tried grabbing the bread early on but then retreated to an elevated position almost to think until finally grabbing the bread one last time at the end. policy B had started going for the bread, even grabbing it, but then moved towards the spray bottle to grab it. The point of this test is to see how many items can be in a space before policies can confidently grab the correct object. The number of objects in the scene this evaluation was 6.'),
(E'7dc2dda8-add4-4f81-b73c-8f8210d4128c', E'2025-08-13T20:51:14.520956Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the watermelon into bowl', E'B is indeed more efficient compared to the idle reaction of policy A as it simply does not move after receiving the command. B almost completes the task but the hand was getting loooseright after it touched the bowl and made the objects dropped out of the seen'),
(E'9bae4168-6ede-411c-9c65-cc3e8e75f988', E'2025-08-13T20:58:23.899556Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the bowl from the plate', E'both policies sufficently did well as it removed the bowl in a single turn'),
(E'3b0d9eea-10fa-4c44-81d8-cd16042c1276', E'2025-08-13T21:06:46.285476Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the cube into drawer', E'A did not quite align with the move since it reached for the bowl all the time. B did a little relevant task since it approached the object next to the cube itself but did not quite grasp the cube'),
(E'53919760-07fd-495b-a184-6b8c16f5f867', E'2025-08-13T21:15:59.085387Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the drawer which contains the spoon', E'Both policies did extremely well in recognizing which drawer contains the spoon which is the top one and close it smoothly . Policy B quite pushed the drawer away after completing the closure task'),
(E'05e67db7-1281-4f29-a93d-a0257e977538', E'2025-08-13T21:25:59.075919Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'swipe the table and put the cloth into bin', E'A just headed towards the cloth without attempting to perform any orientation surrounding it. B did a slight improvement since it did the swiping motion for a few turns and then the cloth was lifted up the table. The trial was terminated when the cloth was placed mis-air'),
(E'7d919ea3-bf12-4c71-bd85-4b6aab2c31fb', E'2025-08-13T21:38:57.198834Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the waterbottle onto notebook', E'A did slightly bit better as it slowly moved towards the waterbottle but then shifted to the bin afterwards. B just freeze the entire time'),
(E'c34e3e16-38df-47a6-9344-c535eb35c1a2', E'2025-08-13T21:50:57.765541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the spoon in the drawer', E'both polcies tended to not detect where the spoon is while it both tried in disrupt the seen ( in A) or just pushed the drawer off table'),
(E'd3e2d9a9-45e7-48e7-bd6a-9f9feff67139', E'2025-08-13T21:53:58.942832Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the edible object.', E'The comparison for these policies were somewhat difficult because they were close to completing the objective in different ways. policy A was able to successfully pick up the water cup which you could argue contains something edible and is close to picking up the edible object. policy B was somewhat random in the beginning, attempting to pick up the white block and grab at the ground, only getting close to the bread towards the very end. The reason I chose policy B is purley because of how close it was to the bread, having actually touched it(albiet on the outside of it''s gripper).'),
(E'77e7432b-e8e4-4489-85da-b85e3bcc9601', E'2025-08-13T22:02:03.449132Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the edible object.', E'The point of this test was to see how well policies could identify a object via a description with multiple other objects to confuse the policies. Currently there are 4 objects on the field. Both policies acted pretty similar, acting somewhat confused and then grabbing the marker. policy B was also able to grab the white block, but otherwise they were pretty similar.'),
(E'165694c3-a92a-4350-844c-0172e421eb68', E'2025-08-13T22:10:01.449155Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the edible object.', E'For some reason both policies deemed the marker to be the edible object. For some reason after running similar evaluations where I ask the policies to pick up the edible object, they have been consistently been going for the marker!! This might be because the marker is closer/easier for the arm to grab or contrasts more with the floor making it an easier target. In any case, I am not sure why this has been happening.'),
(E'cbddf2de-05f1-41cd-8306-578506171e6c', E'2025-08-13T22:10:29.283989Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkelehy'), E'move the spoon into bowl', E'A did terribly off-point since it tried to grasp the entire drawer up air then thus disrupted everything stayed within the drawer. B on the other hand did indeed moved the spoon into destinated placed but the bowl was not aligned nicely on the table'),
(E'7e075c60-9baa-4e10-8be5-4f23721e10fa', E'2025-08-13T22:20:39.470366Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the orange into drawer', E'A did better since it placed the orange inside the drawer but B tried to close the drawer and thus move the orange on top of the drawer'),
(E'9d39ab48-684b-491a-9044-649d4b42bf06', E'2025-08-13T22:28:09.766535Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the edible object.', E'policy A was able to grab the bread pretty quickly after an attempt or two. policy B started by knocking off the black spray bottle and then grabbing the cup. It is worth mentionting that this task has been given before except the bread was placed farther away. In that evaluation, the bread was nevery approached leading me to think that the proximity of the object to the robot can prime it''s perception of what qualities fit each obect or at least can prime the robot''s thoughts about what the ''correct'' object to grab is.'),
(E'bd2da354-795b-4d76-b9fd-058e56bace9d', E'2025-08-13T22:31:04.586953Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the cloth and put it on the table', E'A and B both scored 0 but A somewhat moved around the cloth while B just remained froze'),
(E'a18aaf27-7ef5-4e10-95c6-a7e4a7719c96', E'2025-08-13T22:44:35.872393Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the waterbottle to the left', E'both policies just got the point it has to do something with the waterbottle but in both cases, the hand failed to grasp it properly despite many attempts done')
INSERT INTO sessions (id, occurred_at, site_id, instruction, notes) VALUES
(E'1d8fc321-c151-4a71-978a-9567acac3b73', E'2025-08-14T08:10:50.809939Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the tallest cup on the bookshelf to the left of the plate.', E'Policy A completely finished the entire task, but the cup it grabbed was not the tallest one. Policy B also grabbed a cup that was not the tallest, and when placing the cup, instead of putting it on the left side of the plate, it placed it at the upper left edge of the plate, causing the cup to collide with the plate and fall off the table. Overall, Policy A is better.'),
(E'f2fe142e-d45d-4691-a8ca-e0c5ea313e3b', E'2025-08-14T08:24:41.689230Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Store the cups in the place on the bookshelf where the cups are.', E'Policy A doesn''t take any action and remains stationary all the time. Policy B quickly grabs the cup, but when placing the cup on the bookshelf, it fails to find the original position of the cup on the bookshelf and tries to place it in other positions on the bookshelf. Affected by spatial interference, the cup is finally placed beside the bookshelf. Generally speaking, Policy B is better.'),
(E'591eb964-c7ae-4564-bee8-0dfacfb485ab', E'2025-08-14T08:42:31.837222Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Separate the stacked cups and put them on the bookshelf.', E'Policy A slowly attempts to grab the topmost cup but fails to take it out. Policy B makes several quick attempts and then successfully takes out the stacked cups. Finally, it places the cups on the table but doesn''t find the bookshelf. Overall, Policy B is better.'),
(E'06345422-d8f3-4f49-8d24-6b616a9618f1', E'2025-08-14T08:57:48.291351Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the books on the bookshelf on top of the cabinet.', E'Policy A quickly locates the book on the bookshelf, but grabs it in the wrong way, causing the bookshelf to be knocked over and ultimately failing to grab the book. Policy B fails to find the location of the book and instead tries to open the drawer of the cabinet, deviating from the task objective. Overall, Policy A is better.'),
(E'489532be-d180-4aae-95c9-ecb779712a39', E'2025-08-14T10:02:19.567510Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Place the knives from the bookshelf on the right side of the plates.', E'Policy A didn''t find the knife. It just kept ramming into the bookshelf after finding it, and the task failed. Policy B also didn''t find the knife but tried to grab the books on the cabinet. Overall, Policy A is slightly better.'),
(E'a7a5dbe0-536e-4c65-9596-3537c3b48acb', E'2025-08-14T10:10:32.035328Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Place the blue block above the yellow block.', E'Policy A quickly grabbed the blue blocks but failed to locate the yellow blocks. It didn''t actively adjust its field of view to search for them and just put the blocks down randomly. Policy B also grabbed the blocks quickly and kept holding the blocks while looking for the yellow blocks. Although it didn''t find the yellow blocks in the end, the whole process was a bit more active. Overall, Policy B is better.'),
(E'8109cb78-a2a4-4672-9097-134ff85f8143', E'2025-08-14T10:21:46.304524Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take out the yellow building blocks in the drawer, put them above the book, and then close the opened drawer.', E'Policy A found the yellow building block and attempted to grab it. After failing to grab it, it lost its target and moved around aimlessly. Policy B never found the yellow building block and was moving around everywhere. During this time, it even bumped into the bookshelf. Overall, Policy A is better.'),
(E'afae0c8b-4cf1-4b85-bc13-1358fd70e64f', E'2025-08-14T10:34:37.420412Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the opened drawer and place the plates in the middle of the table.', E'Policy A only tried to grab the plate, but failed. Policy B grabbed the plate and then used it to close the drawer, which might be an unexpected result. Moreover, it kept trying to place the plate beside the cabinet. Strictly speaking, that position is not the middle of the table. Overall, Policy B is close to completing the task.'),
(E'be500151-9ead-4d13-bcb8-0dc76e62664f', E'2025-08-14T10:47:01.628883Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take out the plates from the drawer.', E'Policy A failed to find the correct target and instead tried to grab the cup on the bookshelf. Policy B didn''t take any action. Overall, the results are the same, but their strategies are different. One is aggressive and the other is conservative.'),
(E'865f6e38-6539-4bf7-9f16-ffc60e7f587c', E'2025-08-14T11:02:00.923135Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the fruits in the plate into the box beside the cabinet.', E'After Policy A grabbed the fruits but couldn''t find a box, it put them on the table. However, it then performed a very strange action: it grabbed the plate and moved it around. Policy B didn''t perform any operations. Overall, Policy A is a bit better.'),
(E'd65eaa6f-cf4e-43e1-b0ce-a92af4f12c32', E'2025-08-14T11:23:01.854627Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There are two green cups on the right bookshelf. Take one and put it on the right side of the plate.', E'In terms of the task, the cup is placed at a relatively high position, so the grasping strategy needs to be adjusted. Policy A found the cup but didn''t adjust the grasping method, resulting in being unable to reach it. Policy B wrongly grasped a blue building block and placed it on the right side of the plate, and then knocked down the bookshelf. Overall, Policy A is a bit better.'),
(E'ab6e48d5-bd72-4b3b-8cae-3933c38831d8', E'2025-08-14T11:34:13.715245Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take out the fork from the cup and put it on the plate.', E'There is a fork in one cup and a wrench in the other. They look very similar, and one needs to be able to distinguish the objects. Policy A aims for the cup with the wrench but keeps trying to grab the cup. Policy B also aims for the cup with the wrench, successfully takes it out and puts it on the plate, and then continues to try to grab the fork. Overall, Policy B has a better completion rate.'),
(E'a27677e9-1efa-4e11-9032-0b8b9de10ed8', E'2025-08-14T11:41:15.541829Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the yellow building blocks on the cabinet into the open drawer and then close the drawer.', E'Policy A didn''t grab the building blocks but instead grabbed the cup and then stared blankly. Policy B grabbed the wrong building block, but the entire task process was completed. Overall, Policy B had a better completion rate.'),
(E'8ab6abcc-d139-49b8-abd0-06bb4d2d2cd2', E'2025-08-14T12:01:01.680764Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the white box on the bookshelf into the open drawer, and then close the drawer.', E'Policy A failed to find the white box and instead mistakenly grabbed the fruits in the plate. Policy B also failed to find it, but it kept expanding its field of vision to search for the target. Overall, the strategy of Policy B is a bit better.'),
(E'35eaf45b-7941-4d40-a5fc-e2c4c384236e', E'2025-08-14T12:08:08.495235Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the white box into the open drawer, and then close the drawer.', E'Policy A attempts to place the box under the drawer after grabbing it. Policy B does not take any action. Overall, Policy A is better.'),
(E'53f98add-b0d6-4463-83a0-414feab6a2bb', E'2025-08-14T12:23:14.396998Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the white box into the wooden box on the left.', E'The task requires putting items into a box with limited space. Policy A made some attempts. Policy B adjusted the grasping posture and tried to grasp the items. Overall, Policy B is a bit better.'),
(E'31317701-5f5e-4f97-8136-3391668ff6bd', E'2025-08-14T12:43:06.980923Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the fruits into the wooden box.', E'Policy A didn''t take any action. Policy B quickly completed a task, but when grabbing the second fruit, it unexpectedly tried to put it on the bookshelf.'),
(E'f0e839f6-1be8-4a12-889f-ccad9d4fe243', E'2025-08-14T12:52:16.320689Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Find the building blocks with the same shape on the desktop and stack them up.', E'Policy A first found the correct target and adjusted its position slightly, then went to look for other targets without completing the task. Policy B didn''t take any action.'),
(E'd53b2dcd-9a8b-4b48-bd17-2e7b2de0f6f5', E'2025-08-14T17:17:39.582516Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread to the right of the cup and to the left of the spray bottle.', E'policy A was able to grab the bread and even began moving it to the correct place (in between the spray bottle and the cup), but unfortunately it put it in the wrong spot. After putting it in the wrong spot it kind of just hovered and contorted over the bread for the remaining time. policy B had gone for the spray bottle and started moving that towards the center of the table.'),
(E'0938b90c-f0ac-46fa-bfdb-4caf72099ded', E'2025-08-14T17:35:04.260452Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread to the right of the block.', E'Neither policies did anything...'),
(E'82b89f37-dc3b-4b62-a34f-0de4b4e81a23', E'2025-08-14T17:40:56.576904Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread on the right side of the wooden block.', E'Both policies were able to complete the task. The reason I chose policy A was because it did it much faster with a greater sense of dexterity. policy B would crane it''s gripper for no reason when grabbing the bread and took 2 attempts to do so. policy A also took a much shorter time and placed the bread farther to the right than policy B.'),
(E'3e98b506-47b9-4feb-8aa3-060b8255fee1', E'2025-08-14T17:47:25.020063Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Rotate the bread 90 degrees.', E'policy A was able to grab the bread and that was it. policy A approahced the bread somewhat slowly, took a little whhie to grab the bread and then had difficulty commanding the bread while it was in it''s grasp. policy B did nothing.'),
(E'ab037d3f-9ad1-469a-b61c-0aa3b2a0d89d', E'2025-08-14T17:54:56.753046Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Rotate the bread 90 degrees.', E'policy B was able to complete the entire task. The only issue with policy B was that it had difficulty getting the 90 degrees as a result of the policy opting to move it''s entire arm to rotate the bread instead of just using it''s wrist. policy A did not do anything.'),
(E'0cfa5ee5-4c54-42e3-b910-3416f24e303c', E'2025-08-14T18:04:02.513585Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Rotate the wooden block 90 degrees.', E'policy A was able to start by approaching the block and almost grabbing it. Unfotunatley policy A was not able to pick up the block and had even began approaching the bread. policy B did nothing.'),
(E'54bbf7fc-864f-4081-908c-90700bc0c1a9', E'2025-08-14T18:20:43.449669Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Switch the places of the block and the bread.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to approach the bread and even grab it while policy A did nothing. while policy B was able to grab the bread, for some reason it would pinch the endges or tips of the bread instead of grabbing the base of the bread. policy B would also pick up and then immediatley drop the bread, barley moving it from it''s starting place.'),
(E'a60d40f9-73aa-41f9-b163-3d1bb9430bb0', E'2025-08-14T18:34:55.443229Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the bread with the wooden block.', E'I chose to tie because both policies had grabbed the bread and nothing more. the main difference is that policy B had moved the bread farther away from the wooden block than policy A, but other than that they did very similarly.'),
(E'6f91bd7d-0000-4b1c-9da6-4d0aa47d6a45', E'2025-08-14T18:43:20.544780Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'First pick up the wooden block and then pick up the bread.', E'Both policies had gone exclusivley for the bread, repeatedly grabbing and dropping the bread until the episode finished. It is worth mentioning that the wooden block was on the far end of the stage so the policies might have been less inclined to go for it.'),
(E'15f2dd4c-37ff-4dcb-98bf-8854fbb05979', E'2025-08-14T18:50:13.600932Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'First pick up the wooden block and then pick up the bread.', E'Both policies were only able to pick up the wooden block and did not try to pick up the bread.'),
(E'85afcec3-d2fa-4784-a1d8-894d4462d176', E'2025-08-16T01:56:39.051479Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the cup into the white storage box.', E'Policy A tries to grab two cups and then puts them both down, and then tries to right the fallen cup. Policy B first tries to grab the building blocks, then correctly grabs the cup and approaches the white storage box. If more time is provided, it may be able to complete the task.'),
(E'dd8763d5-490a-4a03-b7b0-4f5489ed233d', E'2025-08-16T02:53:56.579963Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the cup into the white storage box.', E'we prefer policy A, both policy manage to pick up the cup, but policy B hit some other staff along the way. Both policy didnt find the white storage box hence both failed.'),
(E'29c32627-ca35-41c5-9a5a-8948a827052a', E'2025-08-16T03:04:49.768961Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'take red apple into white storage box', E'we prefer policy A, as it manage to grab the apple, policy B didnt even take the apple up. Although policy A drop the apple in the end, it still better then B'),
(E'5b1ff9d3-84ae-429c-9109-7613f5b334ee', E'2025-08-18T01:33:25.063313Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the apples in the white storage box.', E'Policy A carefully attempted to grasp the edge of the apple. Since the apple is spherical, it failed to grasp it all the time, and finally the time ran out. Policy B first pressed the gripper against the apple and then kept hesitating and adjusting the grasping position, but it never executed the grasping action. In comparison, Policy A is more rapid in action and dares to take risks.'),
(E'4a62e504-04d7-48eb-a10c-5e00e822c54a', E'2025-08-18T01:42:00.179638Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Stack the cups on the right into the cups on the left.', E'policy Policy A acted quickly. After a moment of hesitation, it stacked the cup it grabbed from the left side onto the right side and even attempted to further stack the blue building blocks. Policy B also quickly stacked the cup it grabbed from the left side onto the right side. Both of them got the left and right mixed up. In comparison, Policy B was faster in its actions and had no unnecessary extra movements.'),
(E'c6ad516c-e4fd-42df-96a5-75eb3e893825', E'2025-08-18T01:49:54.269662Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the pen on the cabinet to the right of the book.', E'There are quite a lot of sundries at the scene. Policy A searched everywhere on the desktop for the target and finally grabbed a yellow building block for a placement, completely deviating from the task. Policy B also failed to find the positions of the cabinet and the pen. It tried to grab a fork similar in shape to the pen and place it in the upper right corner of the book. I prefer Policy B because the placed fork is closer in shape to the pen and the whole action is relatively smooth.'),
(E'6b4a8575-ae65-4a50-bc0b-f407fb9fcdbc', E'2025-08-18T01:59:33.902649Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There is a wooden cabinet in front of the desk. There is a pen on top of it. Find the pen and put it into the white storage box.', E'Policy A failed to find the cabinet and the pen according to the prompt words, but instead tried to grab the books. Policy B grabbed the building blocks and placed them in the white storage box, completing some tasks, although the items grabbed were incorrect. Therefore, Policy B is better.'),
(E'78416c76-3332-4446-8fbd-857460e986bd', E'2025-08-18T02:07:08.222348Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There is a wooden cabinet in front of the desk. There is a pen on top of it. Find the pen and put it into the white storage box.', E'Most of the interference items have been removed from the on - site environment. Policy A directly tried to find items in the bookshelf but ended up with nothing. Policy B also rummaged through the bookshelf, knocked it over, and found nothing. Therefore, Policy A is better.'),
(E'4f0194c6-7802-42fa-a7de-a228739de065', E'2025-08-18T02:13:45.234180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There is a white pen on the cabinet. Put it in the white storage box.', E'The on-site environment is arranged very simply. Policy A quickly found the target, but failed to grasp it multiple times. Policy B tried to grasp the item in the air and didn''t find the position of the pen. So Policy A is better.'),
(E'6d1ebf0b-2437-4e8c-a4df-09d8bd51d0a0', E'2025-08-18T02:20:14.924595Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the white pen on the plate.', E'Policy A is adjusting the perspective of the plate until the time runs out. Policy B quickly looks up to search for the pen but is attracted by the white cabinet and the white box. Finally, it tries to grab the building blocks in the box. In comparison, Policy B is better as it knows to try to adjust the field of view to search for the target.'),
(E'5182d13f-283c-41bd-a4b6-e021e02a1560', E'2025-08-18T02:28:03.199730Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Draw in the book with a pen.', E'Policy A repeatedly picked up the pen and put it down, and finally held the pen above the book, adjusted the pen tip and tried to make a writing motion. Policy B put the pen into the book more smoothly and quickly, but was unfamiliar with drawing and didn''t take further actions. In comparison, Policy A is better and more in line with the task objective.'),
(E'b0f6dcd3-ba53-470f-9800-b7e4b2d67684', E'2025-08-18T02:37:45.155734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Right the inverted cup.', E'Policy A only touched the cup and did not adjust the state of the cup. Policy B tried to adjust the inverted cup but failed to place it upright, leaving the cup in a toppled state. In comparison, Policy B is better and more in line with the task objective.'),
(E'62a25b65-d27e-4ec8-9983-e68ce35cd6ec', E'2025-08-18T03:24:13.926775Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Take a book from the bookshelf and put it on the table.', E'Policy A tried to find the item from a strange perspective but got nothing. Policy B searched around the bookshelf and tried to grab what was on the bookshelf. Both of them failed equally.'),
(E'1a8508e9-0ca5-435a-9da0-cbab239d7767', E'2025-08-18T03:36:10.538384Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Cover the box.', E'Policy A remains still without any action. Policy B moves outside the desktop and grabs at the air. Both have failed equally.'),
(E'ecab1938-96a3-444b-9751-7dbeb4b9e136', E'2025-08-18T03:43:39.669325Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'There is an open paper box on the desktop. Close the lid.', E'Policy A grabs the edge of the lid and tries to close it, but fails. Policy B slowly observes the box and then tries to grab the lid, but the time is up. Policy A is better.'),
(E'25f46779-aea1-4c76-a8a4-994d141c7b66', E'2025-08-18T03:51:15.041438Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the lid of the paper box.', E'Policy A didn''t carefully observe the situation of the paper box and quickly adopted the strategy of grabbing and then closing the lid, but failed to complete the task smoothly. Policy B, on the other hand, carefully observed the situation of the paper box and chose the strategy of using the gripper to hold the lid and close it, perfectly completing the task. The only fly in the ointment is that it made some redundant movements after closing the lid, so it didn''t get a full score of 100.'),
(E'031524cc-f73f-408f-ba26-0c884290ff65', E'2025-08-18T06:06:06.292746Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the fruits that are the same color as the building blocks on the bookshelf.', E'Policy A remains completely still. Policy B attempts to grab the red fruit and makes a slight adjustment to its position but fails to complete the task. The correct action should be to grab the banana, which has the same color as the yellow block, and place it on the bookshelf. Relatively speaking, Policy B has at least taken some actions, so it is slightly better.'),
(E'8e5232d1-5681-499e-82f0-adb0de23874f', E'2025-08-18T06:33:16.580907Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the banana on top of the yellow building block.', E'Policy A originally completed the task smoothly, but then strangely picked up the building blocks and placed them in other positions, leaving the banana behind. Policy B slowly grabbed the banana and placed it on the edge of the table when putting it down, causing the banana to fall. Generally speaking, Policy A has completed the task completely and is better.'),
(E'ea597420-f03e-4eaf-be0c-8ccca6cfaeca', E'2025-08-18T07:05:19.304210Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Pour out the items in the white box.', E'Policy A remains completely still. Policy B quickly grabs the box and makes a dumping motion. However, since it needs to tilt the box by an angle of over 90 degrees, which is a bit difficult for the robotic arm, no items fall out in the end. Overall, Policy B is better.'),
(E'cee72e0d-9e60-4e3c-8900-b9e555c70bed', E'2025-08-18T07:17:01.121594Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Press the largest button on the air conditioner remote control without using too much force.', E'Policy A first oddly approached the cabinet, then returned above the remote control. After closing the grippers, it gently pressed the buttons on the remote control. The first time, it slightly pressed the largest button, and the second time, it pressed the button next to it. Policy B adjusted the grippers and pressed several times, all on the area without buttons. Generally speaking, Policy A is better.'),
(E'541dd906-96ff-4718-8578-3d36157a0445', E'2025-08-18T07:25:50.406051Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the small bottle on the plate.', E'After the execution of Policy A, the location of the plate was not found. Policy B faced difficulties in grasping and lost the target after knocking over the bottle. Generally speaking, Policy A is better.'),
(E'5161bfc1-1c61-4fe6-b74a-6ab9376607ed', E'2025-08-18T07:31:58.394541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the small circuit board into the plate.', E'Policy A remains completely still. After grasping the target, Policy B put it down once during the process but still successfully completed a task. Generally speaking, Policy B is better.'),
(E'ec2bea5e-5503-462d-bfdb-9b102662b75c', E'2025-08-18T07:39:56.011065Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Arrange the small circuit boards neatly.', E'After successfully grasping the object several times, Policy A put it down without properly handling the placement issue. After grasping an object, Policy B would re - position the object''s orientation. However, after completing one operation, instead of looking for other targets to organize and place, it repeated the placement action. Generally speaking, Policy B is better.'),
(E'5f149628-d099-4346-b097-ccb1db575cf3', E'2025-08-18T07:49:46.338000Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Arrange the building blocks to form a letter C.', E'Policy A quickly grabs a building block and keeps adjusting its placement position and angle, but seems to have no idea what to do. Eventually, the time is up. Policy B quickly grabs the building block and places it on top of another block. Generally speaking, both make active attempts, but neither achieves the task.'),
(E'1117934b-02fe-405d-b6b2-7f2e072d3b59', E'2025-08-18T07:58:09.550170Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Help me shake the water in the bottle.', E'Policy A knocked over the water bottle and attempted to adjust its position. Policy B is still stuck on the grasping issue. I think Policy A is better.'),
(E'4845f5f2-a273-418d-8d4e-b46f352ffc75', E'2025-08-18T08:04:59.970879Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Put the bread on the plate. Don''t use too much force to avoid squashing the bread.', E'Policy A attempted to grab something once but failed, and then it moved around aimlessly. Policy B remained completely still. I think Policy A is better.'),
(E'bc181c1b-18ab-4229-8a29-10c2be181b24', E'2025-08-18T08:13:13.012365Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Pour the items in the white saucer onto the plate.', E'Policy A moved around in an exaggerated manner but still couldn''t find the location of the small disc. Policy B steadily found the small disc, picked it up and then put it down after a successful grab, but didn''t complete the subsequent tasks. I think Policy B is better.'),
(E'f58db858-3fb2-461a-8028-40e183852c93', E'2025-08-18T20:28:48.895492Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the red bottle on top of the blue plate. Align it vertically', E'Policy A remained freeze the entire session while B has just shifted from the direction where other object (cable) sit into the red bottle in the last second. It tried to grasp it but was running out of time'),
(E'5ee6c0f6-9168-4b16-9609-ae86f8872acb', E'2025-08-18T20:37:04.741773Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the carrot in bowl', E'Both policies only completed the very first order of the task.  Both reached for the carot and got tangled within the cable where the object hide in. Policy A lifted the carot but then drop it instantly and remained idle or got stuck somewhere along the way. B also grasp it and moved it over the left side but was not quite the exact location of the bowl, which also was on the left'),
(E'28d9cf55-8cc7-47c7-adc0-82367749f7da', E'2025-08-18T20:47:09.819403Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'cover the bowl with the plate', E'Both A and B at least were able to locate and grasp the plate but they behaved differently hereafter. A tried to pull the plate onward while B pushed the plate over the bowl and kicked it out of the seen without having placed it on top'),
(E'ca946473-098a-4267-a124-63c2e704ba7b', E'2025-08-18T20:56:30.178979Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the spoon to the plate', E'A is indeed better since it accomplished the task within a few orientation while B had a very good starting point but then it was going off to the edge of the bowl, which was where the spoon placed on and grasped nothing in the air'),
(E'939d8a99-37da-4ded-9027-9db2f2f36ffc', E'2025-08-18T21:06:12.106495Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the orange ball inside the tape', E'B was slightly better. A entirely focused on the red bottle which was irrelevant to the intended object. B grasped the entire bowl where the ball was contained and moved it over the left. It then also grasped the carrot at last.'),
(E'261caf9a-f122-419e-a2f4-c25b8fece438', E'2025-08-18T21:17:28.084336Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the tape to where the red bottle placed on', E'Both policies only stopped at grasp the tape from its initial position to the very vertically place where was indeed not the plate contained the red bottle'),
(E'e9e8da9c-1589-4cf2-a28c-57082bf75afd', E'2025-08-18T21:33:41.493446Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the marker next to the red bottle', E'B just remained freeze mid-air while A just moved the red bottle  out of the plate then shifted to the marker at the very end. It realized the core of the task and started the initial set up when the time was alsmost up'),
(E'0f17863b-e323-49ba-8f39-4695c9a9f14a', E'2025-08-18T21:45:49.460620Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the other bowl to the blue bowl', E'B at least has found the bowl and started grasp it first but then hover in the air and searched for something on the ground. A was completely off since it moved the marker from the plate to somewhere on the bowl which is not required'),
(E'da89223c-cb41-46f5-9c59-a1c796c3d82a', E'2025-08-18T21:59:13.167924Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the marker on the center of the whiteboard', E'A and B were just able to grasp the marker out of the plate but then it failed to realize the whiteboard placing right next to it on the right. It struggled to grasp it since it kept picking up and dropping it eventually'),
(E'cbac67c1-06ba-4135-9cfe-2b65b32a1760', E'2025-08-18T22:13:07.321476Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the tape over the words on the whiteboard', E'A and B were able to locate and grasp the tape in place but again, the whiteboard was eventually not the final destination of the robot arm since it just lifted the tape up and dropped it'),
(E'ea7ded57-96c7-42ae-aadd-105bf314d289', E'2025-08-18T22:26:33.279790Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'cover the letter on the whiteboard using the plate', E'B did not move from its initial position while A at least attempted to grasp the plate but seem to not be certain on where the next movement should be so it just hovered in the air'),
(E'aef852ce-3e05-4d13-9e9b-56532771420f', E'2025-08-18T22:38:05.343385Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'find the marker and place it on the edge of the whiteboard', E'A was slightly better since it was attempting to find and grasp the marker in place; however, the arm was confused on what to do next as it hovered in the air with the marker in hand. B did not sufficiently performed any movement towards the marker'),
(E'4e7bc4c5-9c6b-4d37-9bd5-95fc5c5b895d', E'2025-08-18T22:47:53.204520Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkele'), E'move the red bottle next to the spoon', E'A did not respond at all to the command and B went further a bit from moving towards the marker but B did not make ay progress onto grasping it and the gripper waas just hovering'),
(E'67936e32-e813-434c-9ff6-43cda08de9f6', E'2025-08-19T02:18:06.509491Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'scrab the small disc into the big disc', E'policy A is better than policy B. Policy A has tried to pick up the disc, but policy B has not done any action.'),
