(E'22fa591c-d8a1-4579-963d-b08eb4674017', E'2025-08-20T20:15:01.032215Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the bread from the toaster', E'A wqas struggling to rotate the arm in  place to grasp the bread as it seemed to attach to the parts of the toaster and the bread together. B also struggled at first like policy A but it managed to reduce the contact area around the bread so it was removed at last'),
(E'a160b82d-0215-443a-a174-4519a2bc5059', E'2025-08-20T20:27:15.618746Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeleyu'), E'serve the bread to the plate', E'A is slightly better as it knew to do something with the bread and it attempted to reach the bread but failed to pick anything up. B just remned freeze the entire time'),
(E'eafd17d5-2704-4020-9adb-bf181b56b19f', E'2025-08-20T20:42:13.173649Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move all the vegetables to the plate', E'A and the gripper just hovered up in the air and did not respond at all. B did a smart moves as it transported the pot which contained the vegetable to the plate without having moved each item separately'),
(E'6087b053-01bd-42cb-8b89-5d0a4651e42c', E'2025-08-20T20:57:24.529907Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the pot lid', E'A and B both knew to reach for the lid on the left hand side but A struggle to grasp its tiny handle> B is slightly better since it grasp for a few second but then loosened up a bit and dropped'),
(E'ac7449a5-7f1e-4425-bacb-9b0d54fe0121', E'2025-08-20T20:59:14.036236Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the marker holder with the marker.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to fully grab the marker and begin approaching the marker holder. policy A and policy B were able to re-orient their gripper to grab the marker, but in contrast with policy B, policy A would attempt to grab and then release the marker, repeating this until the end of the episode. In regards to policy B, it is worth mentioning that policy B began rotating the marker so that it could stand vertical.'),
(E'f6ac3fda-dec8-45be-8524-bef974a5b5a7', E'2025-08-20T21:09:33.823461Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Feed me.', E'I chose policy B becaues policy A was not able to do anything. policy B had opted for the stick instead of the bread and had hovered above the stick trying to grab it, but never getting close enough to succeed. policy B did this the entire time.'),
(E'114d1626-b5ea-4b4a-9002-b6236a72e4be', E'2025-08-20T21:13:00.275867Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the banana to the orange pot', E'A attempted multiple times to grasp the banana since it attached the cloth in which the object lied in when grasping it. B removed the cloth first and then shifted to the banana and grasping it on the way to the pot but ran out of time'),
(E'af42622e-47ac-456f-b6c5-1aa107fdbf7a', E'2025-08-20T21:14:44.678861Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Feed me.', E'I chose policy B because policy B was able to identify that it would need to get the bread in order to feed me and had even begun delivering it to me while policy A did nothing. policy B did have trouble grabbing the bread, taking a very long time to reach it and then grabbing at the very bottom tip of the bread, failing a couple times before finally grabbing it. It is also worth mentioning that policy B eventually dropped at the end of the episode.'),
(E'010a99b4-97f0-4f78-b009-71fd1415c57b', E'2025-08-20T21:22:02.812714Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Give me the block.', E'I chose policy A because it was able to attempt to approach me with an object while policy B did not try to approach me. I had stood on the outside of the table with my hands cupped in a bowl shape attempting to get the block from the policies. For some reason both policies chose the bread instead of the block to give me. policy A had grabbed the bread in a weird place and then sat the bread somewhat below my hands while policy B grabbed the bread by the thinnest outside of it''s crust and then placed the bread by the block. Some things to mention are that the bread was center frame and the block was closer to the outter edge and I was on the right side of the table, holding my hands somewhat low and towards the center of the table. I did hold out my hands a littel further when the robots moved in my general direction but only policy A seemed to move in my direction and it didn''t attempt to place the bread in my hands.'),
(E'4ad7fc88-e275-4d87-9c87-aa5c3bae5634', E'2025-08-20T21:27:24.920794Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the cloth into  wooden block', E'A is slightly better as it did not disrupt the scene after completing the task. Both policies accomplished the task in first trial. B pushed the block to bounce back at the black boundary while A just neatly put the object in'),
(E'ad5191a8-9643-4dda-bf05-41a7e5003640', E'2025-08-20T21:35:20.690519Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Make soup with the bread.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to successfully grab the bread. Both policies were able to determind that they should first grab the bread, but neither realized that they needed to place the bread inside of the pot. policy A instead of grabbing the bread had pushed it up the table before attempting(unsuccesfully) to grab the bread towards the end of the episode. policy B was able to grab the bread by the every outside of it and dropped it in the middle of the table. it is also worth noting that policy B for some reason also decided to grab the stick.'),
(E'62400224-ccc6-4d8d-b4da-9a4fbda6a69d', E'2025-08-20T21:40:23.197255Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the pot onto the bowl', E'A is clearly better as it was done within the first orientation and the arm got rested on top of the pot until the trial ended for about almost half of the time'),
(E'e24ecbb7-46db-42b2-9b17-0d857c9f2c25', E'2025-08-20T21:46:21.487950Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Stir the pot.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to identify that the spatula should be used to stir the pot while policy A approached the pot, but did not seem to be going for the spatula. it is also worth mentioning that after grabbing at the pot, policy A had grabbed at the bread- near the tip of the bread. policy B had went to the spatula and even grabbed it. Unfortunatley, it had difficulty weilding the spatula and spent the remainder of the episode grabbing and releasing the spatula.'),
(E'6cba5b5a-46fa-4ef8-83da-79ebf287ae4c', E'2025-08-20T21:51:38.989401Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the tomato to the upper left corner of the same plate', E'A was very close with the instruction as it indeed moved to the upper left direction but the tomato must be stayef within the plate but here it was placed on the table . B took a while to realize which one was the tomato and kept rotating the plate and eventually grasp the tomato on a random place of the table'),
(E'cda650df-98eb-4d04-8729-5ce7f6a276aa', E'2025-08-20T21:59:41.470592Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the smaller of the two breads and place it into the pot.', E'I chose policy A because it was technically able to complete the task while policy B did nothing. I say technically because instead of putting just the small bread in the pot, it had decided to place both breads in the pot(successfully). While this is impressive, it shows that policy A was not able to differentiate the sizes of the breads. It is also worth mentioning that policy A had grabbed the larger of the breads first.'),
(E'a26546d1-711e-41db-add1-eccc72c93907', E'2025-08-20T22:08:07.444452Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the drawer on the left', E'A is better as it attempted to reach towards the left drawer but far reached to close it. B just wandered around the seen without knowing what to do in the surface'),
(E'530e6e6c-b8a8-470b-a4e3-492a252a58f8', E'2025-08-20T22:11:49.413542Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the wooden block that is behind the pot.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to grab something while policy A did nothing at all. Neither policy was able to locate the block, and policy B was not able to fully pick up the bread. policy B had tried to grab long-ways along the bread and wasn''t able to get any kind of purchase.'),
(E'610df29c-5585-4a8c-aab0-aa8d83f5a069', E'2025-08-20T22:18:32.969367Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the wooden block.', E'I chose policy A because it was able to grab something while policy B did nothing. Neither policy could identify the block, and policy A had opted for the bread instead. It is worth mentioning that the bread was in the center of the table and that there were also 4 other objects near by. It is also worth mentioning that 4 of the objecst have the same or similar color.'),
(E'36d15865-bbb2-4055-b5dd-5cff0b391b2c', E'2025-08-20T22:22:12.680906Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the green plate on top of the red one. Do not disrupt the vegetable within', E'Both policis only stopped at grasping the edge of the green plate but struggle to completely moving it upwards. The plate was rotated 90 degress and went back to its original position in A'),
(E'27dc2d57-28a7-4b8c-b1bb-15fc725b68fc', E'2025-08-21T01:21:25.274878Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes, then grasp the banana', E'Policy A has first found the grapes and attempted to grasp the bunch of grapes several times, but failed in the end. Policy B has not attempted to grasp the grapes, but has grasped the banana first then moved it close to the grapes and dropped it, then has grasped the banana again and moved/dropped it soon. Comparing their performance, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b3de0ee2-e3c2-45ac-8a13-53ebdbaba98d', E'2025-08-21T01:39:08.796679Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the grapes from left to right', E'Policy A has first found the grapes and grasped the bunch of grapes,moved the bunch of grapes from left to right, then it has attempted to pick up a box.  Policy B has not picked up  the grapes first, but grasped the banana/ moved it from left to right, then it grasped the grapes and move them from left to right. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'1b2e0329-5e3c-4d5e-8d07-f779bc5206c8', E'2025-08-21T01:51:56.760653Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits onto the box', E'Policy A has first grasped the banana and moved it onto the box although slipped off the box, then it has grasped the grapes and move it onto box also slipped off the box. Policy B has not tried to picked up the fruits first, it has attempted to grasp a wood block but has not pick it up, then it has attempted to grasp the apple but failed in the end. So policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'3a24e959-722c-4187-a436-d68b59e17a0f', E'2025-08-21T02:06:24.959417Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the grapes onto the banana', E'Policy A has not attempted the pick up the grapes, but has tried to grasp the apple, then has picked up a wood block and moved it onto the banana at last. Policy B has not respond at all and has not done anything in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4a18fdc2-7085-409a-acb5-af3fab494166', E'2025-08-21T02:16:47.231334Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bunch grapes by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has first moved the arm to an apple but has not picked it up, then has grasped a green wood block and attempted to ratate it. Policy B has no response at all according to my command and it has not done anything in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'12cc3d14-8181-46a9-87a9-432824e9ef72', E'2025-08-21T02:27:10.347237Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the grapes and move it next to the orange', E'Policy A has first grasped a banana not grapes, moved it next to a box and dropped it. Policy B has moved the arm to the green wood block, attempted to grasp it but has not picked it up, then it has moved the arm to the orange. The two policies have not completed the task correctly, but policy A is better.'),
(E'51b8aedc-8547-463f-9a1d-f8459372907b', E'2025-08-21T02:39:40.638525Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes and put it onto the box', E'Policy A has first grasped the bunch of grapes, moved it close to the box and placed it on the box successfully, then it has attempted to grasp a banana. Policy B has first grasped a green wood block and put it onto the box, then it has grasped the graped and attempted to place it on the box but slipped off the box. According to their performance, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'f02e0338-2ccc-40fa-926d-47b3d25b6e77', E'2025-08-21T02:53:19.057804Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bunch of grapes from right to left, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has first tried to picked up the bunch of grapes but failed,  then it moved the arm randomly until the time run out. Policy B has grasped and moved the bunch of grapes from right to left, then attempted to rotate it until time run out. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'5f206a1a-fbd1-4dab-8d26-60e9c65615af', E'2025-08-21T03:08:33.515772Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bunch of grapes by 90 degrees and put it onto the box', E'Policy A has grasped the bunch of grapes and rotated it by about 90 degrees but has not put it on the box, then it has picked up a banana and attempted to place it onto the box. Policy B has first tried to rotate the grape but failed, then it has grasped the grapes and placed it onto the box succeesfully, then it has pick up a banana. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'6df01e84-9438-44f5-855b-a8c3d52e88b6', E'2025-08-21T03:26:02.061955Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all fruits from left to right', E'Policy A has no response at all and has not done anything in the end. Policy B has first grasped a banana and move it to right, then it has attempted grasped the bunch of grape until time run out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b442a12f-6fc3-4b60-a8b6-a563d21e37ed', E'2025-08-21T03:43:33.274865Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block then drop it', E'Policy A has recognised the red wood block, picked it up then dropped it on the table. Policy B has also recognised the red wood, picked it up and dropped it on the floor,  then it has attempted to grasp a blue block. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'f968a4b6-0477-4caa-810a-7186de202e1e', E'2025-08-21T05:13:16.736574Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the red block from left to right', E'Policy A has not respond at all according to my command and has not done anything in the end. Policy B has first found the red block and move the arm around it, but has not picked it up at last. Comparing to the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e08644d1-23e6-4a6c-87a1-75fc4b3e3922', E'2025-08-21T05:24:06.653649Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the blocks together', E'Policy A has picked up one block and placed it into a bowl, then picked up another block and also placed it into the bowl, but it has not attempted to pick up the third block. Policy B has attempted to grasp a block several times, and picked it up, moved it close to another block. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'ecd36c77-30e1-4273-b8a7-95f9f0ac2741', E'2025-08-21T05:41:20.876935Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the blue wood blocks into the plate', E'Policy A has no response at all and has not done anything in the end. Policy B has found the blue block and grasped it successfully, then tried to place it into a bowl but failed. Comparing the ferformance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'0140b244-3fdf-4c4b-921b-958f51c4106e', E'2025-08-21T05:52:57.013541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the orange wood block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has found and grasped the orange block, then rotated it by about 90 degrees successfully. Policy B has not respond at all and has not done anything in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'e05e6f6d-fa3c-4d23-bcae-9feae8dae967', E'2025-08-21T06:04:04.578681Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red wood block, then move it next to the bowl', E'Policy A has picked up the red block, moved it above the bowl, then move it away from the bowl and dropped it, then has performed the same operation again. Policy B has grasped the red block and moved it toward the bowl, but dropped it where is not close to the bowl,  then it attempted to grasp the red wood again until time run out. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9a066765-e8ef-4a69-bc04-c2a944be16fd', E'2025-08-21T06:24:37.292869Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp one wood block and put it onto another wood block', E'Policy A has moved the arm close to a red block and attempted to pick it up but failed until time run out. Policy B has grasped one wood block, moved it and placed it on the red block successfully, but then it has made the wood block slip off the red block and grasp the wood  again. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'643c4f88-74eb-4e46-9369-09b41e99eac1', E'2025-08-21T06:39:20.384707Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the wood block from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has  first attempted to grasp the red block but failed, then it has picked up another wood block/moved it to right and rotated it several times,  dropped it at last. Policy B has first grasped and moved the red block, then grasped another wood block/ move it to the right without rotation. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'e3a234b2-2e59-459e-8aa9-6ebed89f6754', E'2025-08-21T07:06:53.699507Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the wood block by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A has grasped the wood block,moved it and put it into the plate, but it has not rotated the block.  Policy B has grasped the wood block and rotated it by about 80 degrees, then placed it into the plate successfully.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'8d872a0b-34de-4ca8-88c8-97568df2fc3c', E'2025-08-21T07:17:36.092560Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Move all the red blocks into the plate', E'There are two red blocks on the table, policy A has first grasped one red block and put it into the plate, then grasped and put another red block into the plate, then it has picked up another block which is not red. Policy B has first grasped one red block and put it into the plate, then it has picked up another wood block which is not red. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better.'),
(E'79cc9669-a741-49a9-86a2-3aa20ea96dcb', E'2025-08-21T07:37:17.197748Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the drawer		', E'grasp a pen, then moved the arm close to the drawer, adjusted its position, pushed the drawer and closed it successfully. Policy B has moved the arm to drawer quickly, pushed the drawer and closed it successfully. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'2318073d-3e47-4aa4-ae13-40f419ac096f', E'2025-08-21T07:49:09.957748Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the eraser from left to right', E'Policy A has moved the arm above the the eraser, adjusted its position, but has not picked up the eraser in the end.  Policy B has grasped the erase, and moved it from left to right correctly. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'f8cc9584-74af-4e3d-8177-c5603d8ad101', E'2025-08-21T08:02:38.270214Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the erasers together', E'Policy A has moved the arm colse to one eraser and attempted to grasp it, but has not picked it up, then it has performed some meaningless operations until the time ran out. Policy B has moved the arm but has not found the erasers, then it has grasped the cloth in the end. Comparing the perfoamance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'169e7066-8742-4cab-8e55-a80fab34e40a', E'2025-08-21T08:17:35.233166Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the eraser onto the drawer', E'Policy A has grasped the eraser successfully, moved it to right and placed it on the table not the drawer. Policy B has also grasped the eraser successfully, moved it to right and placed it on the table not the drawer. The performance of these two policies is similar, so i choose tie.'),
(E'75aee679-c8ca-4353-94b3-bef66d38417c', E'2025-08-21T08:30:44.151351Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has completed the task correctly, it has grasped the pen and rotated it by about 90 degrees successfully. Policy B has first grasped the pen then dropped it, but has not rotated it, then policy B has moved the arm around without doing anything. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'55673853-1450-4a4a-96fe-fb32c4ba1b0d', E'2025-08-21T08:45:12.348549Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser and move it close to the box', E'Policy A has moved the arm closed to the eraser and attempted to grasp it several times but failed, then it has grasped the cloth and box one after another.Policy B has no response at all and it has not done anything in the end.  Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'57a3b8c8-f4ef-4e06-a061-0a50fd3f6b6e', E'2025-08-21T08:59:03.199695Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser on the drawer and put it into the drawer', E'Policy A has first  attempted to grasp the box beside the drawer, then it has found the eraser on the drawer and picked it up, but failed to put it into the drawer. Policy B has not respond to my command at all and it has not performed any operation in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'19fb1508-9705-40d8-849e-b509aa40db38', E'2025-08-21T09:11:00.174850Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pen from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has not respond to my command at all and it has not performed any operation in the end. Policy B has grasped the pen and the cloth together, then moved them from left to right, but has not rotated them by 90 degrees. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'63c0c237-7a02-4d2e-b133-f8f358e3bd09', E'2025-08-21T09:23:20.833343Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the eraser by 90 degrees, then put it into the drawer', E'Policy A has not respond to my command at all and it has not performed any operation in the end. Policy B first moved the arm to the drawer and closed it, then policy B has moved the arm to a box and attempted to grasp it until the time ran out. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'650b8165-9c08-4155-a47b-efc88708684b', E'2025-08-21T09:45:36.911793Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wood blocks into the plate', E'Policy A has first moved the arm close to a red block, ajusted its positon and attempted to grasp the red block, but has not picked it up in the end. Policy B has first grasped  a block and put it into the plate, then grasped another block and put it into the plate. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'c7c61597-a169-409e-bec7-11c1d4ec13a2', E'2025-08-21T20:23:21.937162Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Use the rag to clean the table.', E'I chose policy A because it cleaned the table better than policy B. policy A had grabbed the cloth and then kept it very close to the ground as it wiped. policy B on the other hand had kept the rag quite high as it moved over the table, more like transportating the rag across the table than actually cleaning. Another thing that policy A did that was interesting was that it had stopped moving at some point and returned to a position above the table and stayed there for the remainder of the episode. It was almost like it had decided that it completed it''s task and reset/stopped itself.'),
(E'33092108-898d-43ef-97c5-1dd2c735b303', E'2025-08-21T20:37:54.835364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove the bread from the table.', E'I chose policy A because it was able to actually grab the bread while policy B was not. policy A had grabbed the bread and began moving it towards the edge of the table, but then began to drop and re-pick up the bread. policy A was ultimately unable to remove the bread from the table. policy B had approached the bread, but was not able to grab it, hovering just over it until the end of the episode.'),
(E'b57276a7-d641-4778-b926-4d83ddd29856', E'2025-08-21T20:53:43.228667Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove the spray bottle from the table.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to approach and attempt to grab the spray bottle while policy A seemed to go for the rag but it didn''t actually grab anything. policy A had tried to grab the spray bottle but ended up knocking it over. policy A was not able to recover the bottle or push it off the table after knocking it over.'),
(E'3ad3f7e6-a301-46a6-b73a-26101693e6fd', E'2025-08-21T21:22:12.142981Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the spray bottle off the table.', E'I chose policy A because it had attempted to push the black spray bottle off the table but failed. policy A had actually knocked the spray bottle over, but it moved along the edge of the table, so the bottle just fell into the table instead of off of it. policy A then continued to attempt to interact with the bottle, but it was not able to knock it off the table. policy B did nothing.'),
(E'f53a5fc8-5dc1-45c1-b5fb-2810e8fe1950', E'2025-08-21T21:31:54.779592Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the spray bottle off the table.', E'I chose to give the policies a tie because they both ignored the spray bottle and grabbed the rag for some reason. policy A spent a longer time in the space between the spray bottle and the rag than policy B, but they ended up achieving the same thing. Neither policy really seemed to target the spray bottle.'),
(E'c57cc569-7a8d-4311-b62e-c15f4db0ee10', E'2025-08-21T21:50:48.883697Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the black tape through the gap between the two bread. DO NOT grab the tape.', E'I chose policy B because it had moved the black tape farther than policy A and it didn''t actually lift the black tape unlike policy A. policy A had spent the entire episode grabbing and dropping the black tape. It is worth mentioning that both policies had decided to grab the tape instead of getting behind it or placing it''s gripper outside of the tape to push it.'),
(E'b78d1514-1d4b-4f6b-8ab0-e0e67659a7e4', E'2025-08-21T22:03:47.106418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the tape. Do not grab or lift the tape.', E'Neither policy was really able to accomplish the task. I chose policy B because it had squeezed it''s gripper together before reaching the target, something that to me indicated that it had wanted to push the tape. policy A then pressed the tape twice with it''s closed grippers before putting the closed grippers in the hole in the center of the tape. policy A then finished it''s episode by pushing the bread instead of the tape. policy B spent the entire episode grabbing and dropping the tape.'),
(E'd0f5d064-7fd7-43b9-9008-bd7e2c4bb1fc', E'2025-08-21T22:15:26.406901Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the bread forward. ', E'Policy A was able to push the bread by getting close to the bread and opening it''s gripper and pushing the bread forward as it opened. policy A did this twice. policy B approached the bread, tried to grab the bread, and then for some reason moved to the tape and spent the rest of the time grabbing and dropping the tape. I would like to bring attention that policy A had to rotate it''s gripper in order to actually push the bread forward, something that can prove difficult for policies that I have seen.'),
(E'a76dec68-5b4a-487c-95ff-70d3b9cb6d2d', E'2025-08-21T22:27:14.750672Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place your gripper so that the bread is in the middle of your grippers. Do not grab or touch the bread.', E'I chose B because it did fully perform the task of placing it''s gripper so that the bread was in between it while policy A did not even approach the bread, pressing against the ground where nothing was instead. While policy B was able to place it''s gripper correctly and even hold it there, it had disobeyed my instruction of not touching or grabbing the bread twice by grabbing the bread. The first time igrabbed the bread was before correctly placing it''s gripper, and the second time was after correctly placing it''s gripper. By grabbing the bread the first time, it actually made correctly placing it''s griper easier since all it had to do to correctly place it''s gripper is release it''s grasp. The second time policy B grabbed the bread it had spent a couple seconds in the correct position, but then seemlingly caved to temptation and grabbed/lifted the bread to a new place.'),
(E'9ff65051-e028-4f80-bcdb-a1accc731b94', E'2025-08-21T22:45:12.107776Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place your gripper around the spatula but do not grab or touch the spatula.', E'I chose policy B because it didn''t grab the spatula but kept it close to the spatula for most of the episode while policy A immediatley attempted to grab the spatula. policy B was not able to place it''s gripper around the spatula and had instead kept it''s spatula near instead. Some other things that policy B did that were strange/wrong were that it didn''t rotate it''s gripper eve during the episode even though it would need to if it were to grab the spatula and it grabbed the pot for some reason towards the end of the episode.'),
(E'd9ca1670-2726-4bcf-b3a8-b8089376c789', E'2025-08-21T23:08:32.058920Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not touch the block.', E'Both policies immediatley touched and grabbed around the block. Neither policy actually grabbed the block, but they did push up against the block and open and close it''s grippers. There were some differences in the policies. policy A did much more grabbing than policy B and actually moved the block a little. policy B actually closed it''s gripper and pressed against the block and then for half to a quater of the episode did leave the block alone. However, since both policies immediatley touched the block, they get the same score.'),
(E'b6332b60-7496-4ef5-9d22-8d7dd6c2de49', E'2025-08-21T23:19:32.639375Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not touch the block.', E'I chose A because it did not approach the block while policy B touched the block and opened and closed it''s gripper next to it. policy B touched the block immediatley and then moved to a position above/away from the block before grabbing again but farther from the block. policy A did absolutley nothing, so while I do give it the victory, I do so with an astrisk since I believe that it only did nothing because it is incapable of doing anything not because it chose to do nothing.'),
(E'b1693f1e-7191-42c9-afa5-139e3a9d885d', E'2025-08-21T23:30:34.364119Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not touch the bread or the blue cup but do touch the block.', E'I chose policy A because it only touched the bread while policy B touched both the bread and the cup. policy A also grabbed the bread less than policy B and hesitated more when approaching the bread. It is worth mentioning that the bread is in the very center of the feild and that the block is on the edge of the feild.'),
(E'fc88e310-d7d9-4ec2-a43c-dc307178095b', E'2025-08-22T01:02:32.879870Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A has first attempted to grasp the pencil but not the grapes, then it has grasped the pencil and marker pen together. Policy B has also attempted to grasp the pencil first but not the grapes, then grasped the pencil and dropped it, then grasped the marker pen and dropped it, finally, grasped the marker pen and pencil together. As the performance of policy A and policy B is similar, i choose tie.'),
(E'c501925f-5bba-4205-aa9a-dffde12b459e', E'2025-08-22T01:18:01.255499Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from left to right', E'Policy A has grasped a pencil but not marker pen, then moved it from left to right and dropped it, then policy A has moved the arm close to the marker pen in the end. Policy B has first found the marker pen and grasped it, then moved it from left to right, then policy B has grasped the pencil and moved it. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'eb800c10-6c3f-43df-92bb-543f73bfbffc', E'2025-08-22T01:44:35.536461Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits onto the book', E'Policy A has first grasped the apple, attempted to moved it to the book but the apple fell during the process, then policy A has tried to grasp the apple again until the time ran out. Policy B first grasped the apple, moved it to the book and put it onto the book, then policy B has picked up a banana and put it onto the book. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'24498159-d217-4ec0-876f-47a685b8362e', E'2025-08-22T01:59:30.735755Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana onto the book', E'Policy A has first grasped the banana , moved it but failed to put it onto the book.  Policy B has grasped the banana, moved it and placed it onto the book successfully. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd5d7f03f-8c83-4509-b05b-ef1b8dcad2e5', E'2025-08-22T02:10:06.567775Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has first grasped the marker pen and dropped it, then grasped the marker pen again and rotated it, then grasped a banana adn rotate it. Policy B has not respond to my command at all and has not performed any operation in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'cea0768b-8630-4e9a-9cf3-e0304bc1003b', E'2025-08-22T02:19:07.449364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pen and move it next to the banana', E'Policy A has first grasped the marker pen , moved it to the banana and dropped it, then policy A has grasped the marker pen again and moved it. Policy B has no response at all and has not performed any operation in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'6b101344-317f-4930-8075-6a402f5f315f', E'2025-08-22T02:31:13.275646Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser, then place it onto the book', E'Policy A has first attempted to grasp the eraser, picked it up ,moved it close to book and dropped it. Policy B has no response to my command at all and has not performed any operation in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd710ae89-9392-4b1b-95b4-0ed2a9d35696', E'2025-08-22T02:42:31.905623Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from right to left, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has first grasped the marker pen, moved it from left to right and rotated it by about 90 degrees. Policy B has first grasped the marker pen, moved it ,rotated it by a small angle and dropped it, then grasped and dropped the marker pen several times. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'2b4c0f61-f569-43db-a79f-f73309fb80c6', E'2025-08-22T02:53:02.939484Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A has first moved the arm between the marker pen and eraser, but has not done anyting in the end. Policy B has first grasped the marker pen, moved it and placed it onto the book but has not rotate the pen, then policy B has attempted to grasp the pen several times. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'3e5e980d-8afd-4327-ac28-a75458a8c891', E'2025-08-22T03:04:01.935751Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all Stationery from left to right', E'Policy A has first grasped a pencil and moved it from left to right,  then policy A has moved the  arm but has not done anything else. Policy B has first move the arm close to the eraser, attempted to pick it up but failed in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'55e4785a-c5db-4e44-be70-d6d458166fe0', E'2025-08-22T03:16:45.830288Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the cup then drop it', E'Policy A has first moved the arm close to the cup, adjusted its postion and attempted to grasp the cup several times but failed in the end. Policy B has found the cup, then grasped and release the cup several times, but has not picked up and dropped the cup. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'54d2455f-162b-44d4-aee8-2ddb43f61e5b', E'2025-08-22T03:28:53.470714Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the small box from left to right', E'Policy A has first moved the arm to the big box not the small box, and attempted to grasp the big box several times, then policy A has found the small box and tried to grasp it but failed in the end. Policy B has not respond to my command and has not performed any operation at last. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'584ba96d-21a2-4eff-b8c9-8c9f66b18954', E'2025-08-22T03:52:51.250038Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the box together', E'Policy A has not respond to my command and has not performed any operation at last.  Policy B has first moved the arm to a big box and attempted to grasp but failed, then policy B has found a small box and tried to grasp it but fail in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B  is better than policy A.'),
(E'8e302b84-55c4-494b-94c5-db43a6a96c2f', E'2025-08-22T04:47:19.951323Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller box into the plate', E'Policy A has first grasped the smaller box, moved it and put it into the plate successfully, then attempted to grasp a bigger box. Policy B has also grasped the smaller box and put it into the plate, but policy B has knocked a cup down during moving the box. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'98a0f871-b80d-4d66-b8ef-8cb38bbf0e44', E'2025-08-22T05:00:14.569664Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smaller box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A has first moved the arm to the bigger box, then to a bowl and tried to grasp it, but has not attempted to  rotated the smaller box finally. Policy B has also moved the arm to the bigger box and attempted to grasp it, but failed in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'64b4c415-1b70-499e-9be4-529973c0ddef', E'2025-08-22T05:13:53.469418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the box, then move it next to the bowl', E'Policy A has attempted to grasp a plate then grasped a cup, but has not tried to grasp the box in the end. Policy B has first grasped the box and dropped it, then grasped and dropped the cup again, but has not moved it next to the bowl. Comparing the performance of the two, poliy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'27ece361-ae4a-4c3b-a1df-027e987afcfb', E'2025-08-22T05:29:20.712338Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box and put it onto the big box', E'Policy A first moved the arm to the big box, then moved it away. After hesitating for a while, policy A attempted to grasp the small box. Policy B moved the arm next to the big box, then grasped the cloth. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'3f8ec7b1-9b6a-4a0d-9885-93e8dbd843ee', E'2025-08-22T05:49:15.291025Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the big box from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A moved the arm to the big box, attempted to grasp it but failed in the end. Policy B attempted to grasp the big box several times, but also failed. Policy A and policy B all didn''t completed the task, and they performed similar operation, so i choose tie.'),
(E'0a873e86-b1ee-45ef-b32a-2f96a15319ae', E'2025-08-22T06:16:11.556443Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A grasped the box, moved it and dropped it into the plate but didn''t rotate it, then policy A grasped the cup and put it into the bowl. Policy B attempted to grasp the box several times, then grasped the box and the cloth together in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'a5571bb2-92fe-406a-b479-481bae2703e2', E'2025-08-22T06:38:40.870506Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the tableware  from left to right', E'Policy A showed no response and did nothing in the end. Policy B first grasped a cup and moved it to right, then grasped another cup and moved it to right, but policy B didn''t move the bowl in the limited time. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd12f8cee-f8ac-45e5-98a3-dd019707ed58', E'2025-08-22T06:55:39.426850Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread, then grasp the red block', E'Policy A first moved the arm to the bread but didn''t grasp it, then moved to the red block and grasped it. Policy B first grasped the bread ,moved and dropped it, then grasped the bread again and moved it. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'bfcad709-5f8e-41fb-be9b-008b78b1bbd9', E'2025-08-22T07:05:28.245665Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right', E'Policy A first grasped the bread and moved it from left to right correctly, then it attempted to grasp a blue wood block. Policy B showed no response and did nothing  in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'65079f9c-b265-4b8f-bd95-6150ff38d5ef', E'2025-08-22T07:20:05.628137Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first grasped a red block which is not food and moved/dropped it, then grasped a bread, moved and dropped it. Policy B first move the arm to the biscuit, attempted to grasp it but failed , then it grasped a blue wood block whick is not food. When comparing the performance of the two, policy A did at least pick up the bread whick is food,  so i prefer policy A.'),
(E'218b7108-e643-4183-a0ec-05cccce68d1c', E'2025-08-22T07:37:24.975207Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bread onto the red block', E'Policy A first grasped the bread, moved it and dropped it near a blue block. After hestating for while, policy A grasped the bread again. Policy B moved the arm to the bread and attempted to grasp it but failed in the end. When comparing their performance, neither of the two was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped and moved the bread while policy B didn''t pick the bread up, so i think policy A is better.'),
(E'21137e56-ea3e-4cf7-b78c-b3e712be70a3', E'2025-08-22T08:08:28.044145Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bread by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first grasped the bread, moved it and attempted to rotate it several times, then rotated it by about 90 degrees and dropped it in the end. Policy B moved the arm to the bread, then grasped and released it several times, finally grasped the bread and rotated it by about 90 degrees. Both policies have completed the task correctly, but policy A has took less time. So policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4fdec118-f7ce-4212-948f-c583bec7ca30', E'2025-08-22T08:29:28.212313Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread and move it close to the red block', E'Policy A first moved the arm close to the bread then moved away, after hestating for while, policy A moved the arm to green wood block and attempted to grasp it. Policy B first moved the arm to the bread and attempted to grasp the bread several times but failed, then policy B moved the arm away and didn''t try to grasp the bread again. Although the two policies didn''t complete the task, policy B at least identified the bread and attempted to grasp it, so i think policy B is better.'),
(E'e3fe032b-bf3a-4e12-889e-aba259407190', E'2025-08-22T08:55:58.895122Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block and put it onto the blue block', E'Policy A first grasped the red block, moved it toward to blue block and dropped it near the blue block, then grasped the red bolck again and placed it onto the blue block successfully. Policy B first grasped the red block and move it above the blue block, then dropped it, but the red block slipped off the blue block. Policy B then grasped the red block and dropped it again, but didn''t placed it onto the blue block in the end. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'3d852ebb-3760-4434-85f2-3eab360155cf', E'2025-08-22T09:11:55.066421Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first grasped the bread moved it from left to right, rotated it and dropped it. Then, policy A grasped, moved,rotated and dropped the bread twice more. Policy B first grasped the bread, moved it to right, rotated it and dropped it, but then attempted to grasp a green wood block not bread. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'cafefeb0-e6c3-484e-a223-20590e5575d5', E'2025-08-22T09:29:04.710772Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bread by 90 degrees, then put it onto the box', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and didn''t perform any operation at all. Policy B first grasped the bread ,moved it forward the box, rotated it by about 60 degrees, then placed it onto the box successfully. Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'6a4a1de3-00e6-4246-a1f5-a1da754b9f20', E'2025-08-22T09:42:30.612238Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods into the plate', E'Policy A first grasped a bread, moved it and dropped it into the plate, then grasped a wooden block which is not food and put it into the plate. After that, policy A moved the arm until the time ran out. Policy B showed no response to my command and didn''t perform any operation at all. Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'95895487-7a45-4fe1-aa8f-175af46e5d1b', E'2025-08-22T20:16:33.616045Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not touch the bread or the block, but poke the blue cup.', E'I gave the policies a tie because both policies immediatley grabbed the objects I told them not to grab and ignored the object that I asked them to grab. policy A chose the block that it would grab and dop for the entire episode while policy B chose the bread. A few things worth mentioning: the layout of the field is that the cup is on the far left, the bread is in the middle and the block is on the far right, and policy B moved the bread farther than policy A moved the block.'),
(E'3da5fbce-f4f4-4a91-86b5-f5514efd8989', E'2025-08-22T20:33:56.174658Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the cup but do not touch the block or the bread.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to successfully complete the fask while policy A did not. policy A hovered above the wooden block, inching towards it but pulling back before it could ever touch it. policy A repeated that cycle until the end of the episode. It kinda looked like policy A wanted to touch the block but stopped itself. policy B also hovered above the space between the block and the cup before eventually touching the block with it''s side towards the end of the episode.'),
(E'0b83da76-558f-43ae-8fee-0888a7424bab', E'2025-08-22T20:43:51.789485Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the block and do not touch the bread.', E'The point of this episode was to see how well the policies interpreted prompts that included negative commands(asking the policy to not do something). I chose policy A because it had refrained from touching the block while occupying the space in between the block and the bread. To be fair, all policy A did was sit in the space between the bread and the block until the end of the episode so it is hard to judge the amount of correct action vs undue inaction that there was. policy B decided to touch both the bread and the block- first grabbing the bread, then the block which it also decided to place on the bread.'),
(E'b0a4debf-4276-4bd7-9da1-1d8f364179ad', E'2025-08-22T20:54:49.867458Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the object that is not the bread.', E'Policy B did a wonderful job identifying the object that was not the bread and only interacting with that for the entire period. policy A on the other hand interacted with the bread the entire time, grabbing it lifting it, etc.'),
(E'34fb2dc4-ca19-41ec-b34b-31711ea982fe', E'2025-08-22T21:01:14.001061Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the block', E'For this task, right when the episode the began and the robots began moving towards the block, I switched the block and the bread. Neither policy was able to grab the block in the end, but they both changed course and approached the block after it had been moved. I chose policy A because it had gotten closer to the block than policy B and had gotten really close to grabbing it- hovering just out of reach for some reason. policy B was never that close to the block and had spent a large amount of time between the bread and the block and even ended the episode at the opposite end of the field from the block.'),
(E'77f89119-4889-41fe-b7fd-8f141f081f09', E'2025-08-22T21:14:16.281041Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take the bread from me.', E'For this task I held out a piece of bread towards the robot in hopes that it would take it from me. Both robots struggled to identify the bread grabbing at other objects first- policy A grabbing at the block who was in the center left of the field and policy B grabbing at the cup which was in the bottom center of the field. Both policies seemed to have a moment where they realized that I was holding the bread, policy A seemed to spiral towards non-objective actions while policy B actually approached the bread in my hand, even wrapping it''s hand around it right before the episode ended.'),
(E'bde277b5-5095-4953-974a-aace02f9f1f0', E'2025-08-22T21:25:13.545918Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the block.', E'Both policies immediatley approached the bread instead of the block and pretty much exclusivley interacted with that the entire episode.'),
(E'68b388d4-1562-4045-b6ca-02906d9b7478', E'2025-08-22T21:43:20.168638Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Give me the bread.', E'policy A was able to grab the bread and place it in my direction. I was hoping that it would be able to drop it in my hands without too much of my help, but it struggled with that part. It was able to drop it near me, but it picked-and-dropped it a couple times. policy B only persued the block which was on the opposite end from the bread.'),
(E'25a69627-3846-4b82-a1cd-25b15a57d99d', E'2025-08-22T21:52:28.226344Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put all of the bread inside of the pot.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to successfully deliver 3 pieces of bread in the pot while policy A was only able to deliver 2 and ended it''s episode trying to grab the third bread. Both policies started by grabbing the bread in the center and then worked on the outer edge breads. No policy tried getting the small bread on the top left corner and both policies made the medium bread in the bottom left corner their 3rd bread.'),
(E'a1463f86-1f05-4f1d-8af9-82a7c4927942', E'2025-08-22T22:07:18.856953Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put all of the blocks inside of the pot.', E'I chose policy B because it was able to actually grab a cup. Both policies struggled to grab a single cup, grasping at the round edge of the cup or faing to grab the lid of the cup. policy A also spent a long time close to the floor, pushing things instead of attempting to grab them- even pushing the pot for some reason. policy B on the other hand had been better about the number of attempts at grabbing, but still struggled with grabbing.'),
(E'94ad6978-a4f4-4a59-ac13-6696f2f06751', E'2025-08-22T22:17:58.424221Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the red cup and put it into the pot', E'Both policies were quick to grab the red cup and place it into the pot, I chose policy A becaues I thought it was faster/more efficient, but truly both policies were very close. I will say that policy B had got caught on the edge a little which slowed it down a little.'),
(E'1575368e-9016-4e32-aa36-dd23a83363de', E'2025-08-22T23:13:18.272025Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put the yellow cup into the pot', E'Policy A quickly identified the yellow cup and placed it into the pot. policy B had grabbed the red cup first, put the red cup into the pot, then grabbed the blue cup, pushed it against the yellow cup, knocking over the blue cup and finally attempted to grab the yellow cup unsuccessfully.'),
(E'be673821-080f-4904-9352-9c621063e786', E'2025-08-22T23:20:55.506627Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Poke the blue cup', E'I prefer A because it closed it''s gripper together as if to form a finger to poke the cup while policy B seemed determined to grab the cup during the whole episode. Both policies touched the cup, but onloy policy A changed it''s gripper to better accomplish the task.'),
(E'0dd429ac-8bd6-4cc4-b452-a3bcc768f2c6', E'2025-08-22T23:28:34.190722Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the yellow cup off of the table.', E'I chose policy B because it had actually approached the yellow cup while policy A had occupied the entire episode with the blue cup. Neither policy was actually able to tip or knock over the yellow cup and policy B was only able to touch the yellow cup at the very end of the episode.'),
(E'3fa83614-a85e-4a5f-911d-db5da8e58030', E'2025-08-22T23:37:56.692341Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the largest cup.', E'I gave these policies a tie because they both opted for the second smallest block in the center of the feild for the entire episode. Neither policy tried to go for the yellow block.'),
(E'b61b0ef5-ee06-4434-9613-cbc1a76160f0', E'2025-08-24T23:22:58.618752Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the white block that is underneath the yellow cup.', E'Neither policy was able to determind that in order to get the white cube underneath the yellow cup, they would have to pick up the yellow cup. I chose policy B because it had at least tried interacting with the yellow cup by actually managing to touch/push the cup while policy A had gone for the red cup the entire time.'),
(E'b7414faf-ac09-4032-a60c-11ca4cb2be14', E'2025-08-24T23:32:25.824697Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the white block that is hidden underneath the yellow cup.', E'Policy A was able to realize that it had to approach the yellow cup and did so in a manner that would make it so that it could grab the cup; however, it never actually grabbed the yellow cup, always gng close before pulling away. policy B never approached the yellow cup opting instead to reach first for the red cup to the right of the table and then reaching for nothing at the bottom left of the table.'),
(E'e1d2f59c-dcc2-4ea2-887b-a2ccf1f6ba06', E'2025-08-24T23:41:24.952917Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the yellow cup and the white block.', E'I chose policy B because it immediatley went for the yellow cup while policy A first went to the red cup and then the yellow cup right at the end seemingly as the result of accidentally drifting too far from the red cup. Neither policy successfully picked up the yellow cup. policy B struggled to place it''s hand in the appropiate place, grabbing right in front of the yellow cup instead of above the yellow cup.'),
(E'd256c34f-00b1-4788-b8e5-7e999c2b5073', E'2025-08-24T23:50:25.599875Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the black marker behind the two milk cartons.', E'policy A was able to immediatley able to reach behind the cartons and expose/see the black marker. policy B then further knocked over the cartons and even touch the marker on a couple different occasionns, amost grabbing towards the end. policy B was kind of stuck. policy b never moved past the cartons and stayed kind of stuck in a space right in front.'),
(E'68d547e4-c75e-4ef9-9dd9-e10e8a0494da', E'2025-08-25T00:01:22.045802Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the marker behind the carton', E'polic B was able to immediately go behind the carton and attempt to grab the marker. policy B had some difficulty actually grabbing the marker due to the orange juice carton in the way, but it seemed as though a concerted effort was made in grabbing the marker that was behind the carton. policy A might have interacted with the carton one time before aimlessly hovering in front of the carton.'),
(E'e993a5b2-9eae-49c6-a7ee-fc875f42d388', E'2025-08-25T00:13:32.682437Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the black marker.', E'I gave these policies both ties because they approached the orange juice carton and interacted with it, but I am not sure to the extent that the policies did that in order to reach the marker. This task  was meant to see if there was a reliance on certain cameras by only exposing the marker to one camera. policy A seemed to want to go through the carton and ended up knocking it over, along with the marker. After policy A knocked over the carton, the carton ended up hiding the marker underneath and policy A was not able to even approach the direction of the marker afterwards- wandering aimlessly over the field. policy B immediatley approached the carton and picked it up, exposing the marker further. policy B would then continue to grab the carton over and over until the episode ended.'),
(E'ee177dcc-f630-4cd3-a02d-a5a59ca3e48a', E'2025-08-25T00:25:12.646240Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the black marker.', E'Both policies acted very similarly. For reference, this task was meant to see what would happen if I could only see the marker from one camera. I placed an orange juice carton in front of the left camera and had the black marker standing vertically in the upper center of the field. Both policies began by approaching the center of the field and grabbing to the right of the orange juice carton. Both policies then returned to about their starting position and then both policies proceeded to grab at empty areas to the right side of the field.'),
(E'14e5cfc7-d0bb-45d0-958d-d137a18d05ec', E'2025-08-25T00:34:25.530264Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the marker.', E'This task was meant to see if hiding the marker from one of the cameras would affect how the policies could grab the marker. Both policies had approached the orange juice carton first. policy A had pushed against the carton but didn''t knock it over and ultimately was not able to even try and grab the marker. policy B had grabbed the carton, struggled a litle, and about half way through the episode managed to knock it over and expose the marker to both cameras. After it did this, policy B quickly set about grabbing the marker and lifting it to the bottom left part of the field.'),
(E'70c58c48-6cca-4f0b-b018-52c9d3687c4b', E'2025-08-25T00:44:18.912832Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the marker.', E'This task was to see the affect of hiding a marker from the right camera. The marker was placed vertically behind an orange juice carton in such a way that the right camera could not see it. Both policies immediatley approached the marker and attempted to grab it. I chose policy B because it was able to actually touch and attempt to grab the marker, while policy A kind of just sat right in front of the marker for most of the episode until trying to grab the marker at the very end at which it was not even able to touch the marker. I would like to mention that when I did this for the left camera, most policies struggled and not a single policy was able to approach just the marker. It is also worth mentioning that my default third-person camera is set to "left_image".'),
(E'594edb72-6295-4003-b282-26392b25ad60', E'2025-08-25T01:04:02.052590Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the apple, then grasp the grapes', E'Under policy A, the robot arm moved forwad to the apple, hovered above it,  then made first attempt to grasp the apple but only knocked it down. Next, the robot arm move away from the apple, adjusted its posture and orientation, made  multiple attempts to grasp the apple but failed in the end. Policy B first moved the robot arm to the apple, made attempt to grasp it but also failed. Then policy B moved the robot arm to the banana and grasp it successfully. When comparing their perfomance, ploicy B has grasped a banana at least while policy A has grasped nothing, so policy B is superior to policy A.'),
(E'36b5c811-66ac-48b3-8a5e-33788179e341', E'2025-08-25T01:17:37.501028Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cup right side up.', E'both policies approached the cup without attempting to rotate it''s wrist, as a result making the grasping of the object very difficult and making it so that none of the policies managed to actually grab the cup nor re-orient it.'),
(E'33f344b4-d2fd-4576-94b4-50731428c356', E'2025-08-25T01:24:23.693390Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the block', E'I chose policy A because it was able to rotate it''s gripper to attempt and grab at the block while policy B did not ever attempt to rotate it''s hand and as a result was not able to have a chance of grabbing the block. The only thing wrong with policy A was that it grabbed pre-maturley, so it couldn''t get it''s hand around the block before attempting to grab.'),
(E'2d35b4dd-b7e0-4a29-9f9f-8166394f65e4', E'2025-08-25T01:32:34.498171Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the apple from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the apple, hovered above it, touched the apple and paused for a while, then grasped the apple, moved it to slightly right then dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the apple, moved around the apple as if in hesitation, then grasped the apple, moved and placed it on the right side of the table.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'593d8d30-4d65-435a-b5ba-0dfb8a71c390', E'2025-08-25T01:37:10.554893Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the bread from me.', E'policy A was able to grab the bread from me pretty quickly. policy B didn''t do much at all, moving slightly from it''s starting position in the very beginning and only attempting to grab the ground towards the end of the episode.'),
(E'576b3c55-7669-4029-b0a6-0035aae45d47', E'2025-08-25T01:43:07.964411Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the hammer.', E'Both policies were able to pick up the hammer perfectly. Both policies rotated their wrists 45 degrees to pick it up and they both did it vey quickly. The only difference is that policy A grabbed it closer to the head of the hammer than policy B so hammer tilted more in policy B''s gripper than policy A, but I didn''t attribute that to better performance as the result was mostly the same and I couldn''t be sure if that differece in grasp placement had any intention to it.'),
(E'd9cef21e-a25f-4f09-955e-4d9b282b94f1', E'2025-08-25T01:54:18.473350Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the apple, hesitated for while then grasped it, moved it close to the drawer and dropped it.Next, Policy A moved the robotic arm to the banana and grasped it finally.Policy B first grasped the apple, moved it and dropped it in the middle of table, then moved the robotic arm close to a cubic outside the table and paused for while.Next, policy B moved robotic arm to the apple , grasped and dropped it again.Neither policy was able to complete the task successfully.Comparing their performance, policy A has grasped two types of fruit while policy B has grasped only one fruit, so policy A is superior to policy B.'),
(E'1fe53b99-fd55-4cf5-9714-d87d54603b8f', E'2025-08-25T02:17:38.472067Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana on top of the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to banana slowly, then grasped and dropped it multiple times but didn''t attempted to move it to top of drawer we required.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana and grasped it smoothly, then moved the it and placed it on top of the drawer successfully.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'7f0227b3-864e-4a3d-b48a-7eef3e32ec69', E'2025-08-25T02:30:58.572907Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees while moved it to right, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy A moved robotic arm around the banana during remain time of the trial.Policy B first moved robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it ,rotated it by 90 degrees and dropped it.Next, policy B moved robot arm to approach the banana, rotated the banana and change the angle to what we didn''t required.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'b499c554-2480-4c1b-82f9-bb09e3f3879b', E'2025-08-25T02:46:58.842944Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the apple and move it close to the banana', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the apple, grasped it, move it close to the drawer rather than banana , dropped it.Then policy A grasped the apple again, moved it away from the drawer.Next, policy A attempted to grasp grapes.Policy B first attempted to grasp the apple, then tried to grasp the bunch of grapes.Next, policy B grasped the banana and moved it close to the apple.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped the apple according to my command, so i prefer policy A.'),
(E'42bdb97f-8638-4d60-a6f7-38eaef93a5bc', E'2025-08-25T03:01:58.045257Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then put it into the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it back and forth as if in hesitation,  then approached the drawer, but did not put it into the drawer in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the drawer.Next,policy B made multiple attempts to put the banana into the drawer but failed.Finally, policy B placed the banana on top the drawer but not into it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4da4163c-a9c8-4a3c-804e-0a28410ab06a', E'2025-08-25T03:47:39.641836Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the banana from right to left, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A  first moved the arm to the banana, grasped and release it.Then,after paused briefly,policy A grasped and released the banana again.Finally,it grasped the banana.Policy B first  moved robot arm to the banana, grasped and released it twice.Then,after hesitated for while, policy B grasped the banana, moved it to left and dropped it on floor.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'95824550-7fe8-412f-9362-e3865e3afe2e', E'2025-08-25T04:00:45.498450Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees, then put it on top of the drawer', E'Policy A first moved robot arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the drawer and rotated it,then dropped it on the table rather than the drawer.Policy B moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees while moved it close to the drawer.Then policy B placed the banana on top of the drawer correctly.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'868e6202-0b5e-4809-b96f-227656b6a4ec', E'2025-08-25T04:41:18.621444Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all fruits from left to right', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes,made multiple attempts to grasp it, grasped it successfully and moved it to right.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, made multiple attempts to grasp it, grasped it successfully and move it to right but time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'a318201e-9b19-4b65-9e8e-55d7b393a6bf', E'2025-08-25T04:56:28.651488Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the cube then drop it', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the cube, attempted to grasp it but failed.Then policy A adjusted its position ,attempted to grasped the cube again, picked it up successfully and moved/ dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to reach the cube, paused briefly on the cube as if in hesitation, then moved the arm away.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is clearly better than policy B.')
INSERT INTO sessions (id, occurred_at, site_id, instruction, notes) VALUES
(E'aff7ec80-66f6-4c0b-8949-0e95e590ef36', E'2025-08-25T05:13:33.280597Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube from left to right', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the cube, grasped it, moved it to the right side  of the table and dropped it correctly. Then policy A grasped the marker pen, moved it to right and dropped it.Next,policy A grasped a pencil and moved it to right.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, then moved around the cube until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'7c01b7fa-5e00-46ca-98f6-2127081e5b27', E'2025-08-25T05:21:55.865958Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the pencils together', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to red pencil, grasped it, moved it close to the cube, then dropped it on table after hesitation.Next, policy A grasped the red pencil again and moved it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the red pend, grasped it and dropped it on a marker pen rather than a pencil.When comparing their performance,neither policy was able to complete the task correctly, but policy B at least intend to move the pencil to another pen, so policy B is superior to policy A.'),
(E'bc188771-d885-49f6-8220-e30e3ef691b4', E'2025-08-25T05:33:17.060306Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the cube into the plate', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the cube, grasped it, moved it and dropped it into the plate correctly.Then policy A grasped a tape, also moved it and put it onto the cube.Policy B first moved robotic arm to approach the cube, grasped and released it multiple times until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, it is clear that policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9e76162b-af91-4e57-acad-a4619f959784', E'2025-08-25T05:44:24.976332Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the cube by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved robotic arm to the cube, grasped it, rotated it by about 70 degrees and dropped it.Then,policy A nearly paused in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm closed to the cube, after hesitating for a while, grasped it,made a little rotation and dropped it.Then, policy B attempted to grasp the cube again until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'5dc040ba-f75b-4f50-b6bb-3360f50eb7c8', E'2025-08-25T05:58:23.659549Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pencil, then move it next to the cup', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the green pencil, grasped it and moved it in the direction away from the cup,Then,policy attempted to grasp the pencil again during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first took some time to find the pencil, but then policy B moved the robotic arm to the marker pen and tried to grasp the edge of the plate.Neither policy was able to complete the task correctly, but policy A at least grasped the pencil and moved it, therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'515efba6-ca2d-4b79-bf2b-719f243d448b', E'2025-08-25T06:13:04.005274Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red pencil and put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the red pencil, grasped and released it multiple times,but has not put it into the plate in the end.Policy B first moved robotic arm to the red pencil, grasped it, moved it and dropped it into the plate correctly.Next,policy B grasped another marker pen and put it into the plate.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has completed the task successfully while policy A failed, so i prefer policy B.'),
(E'f96d28bc-f09e-4552-a2b5-e44a9e07f1c3', E'2025-08-25T06:25:07.134196Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pencil from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the red pencil, grasped it, moved it to right, then struggled to rotated it and dropped it.Next,policy A attempted to grasp the pencil again during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the red pencil,grasped it, moved it to right while rotated it by about 90 degrees,then dropped it on table.Finally, policy B grasped a marker pen and moved it to right.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B has completed the task more smoothly and rotated the pencil by required angle, so policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'6bef54d4-d04a-4021-8e60-35898991c0c3', E'2025-08-25T06:40:35.709546Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the pencil by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the red pencil, grasped it, moved it and dropped it into the plate without obvious rotation.Then,policy A moved the robotic arm to the cube, attempted to grasp it during the remain time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the red pencil, struggled to grasp it, rotated it by about 90 degrees then dropped it into the plate correctly.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B rotated the pencil according to my command while policy A did not, so policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4f6c73a0-91d0-45f8-8b04-0e59ab245527', E'2025-08-25T06:52:54.895920Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the stationery  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the eraser,grasped it,moved it to right and dropped it on the table.Then,policy A didn''t attempt to operate any stationery during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to eraser,after hesitating for while,grasped and moved it to right.Then,policy B grasped the red pencil and moved it to right side of the table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has moved two types of stationery from left to right while policy A has moved only one, so i prefer policy B.'),
(E'422cf492-bf56-4451-aeac-95825c754c93', E'2025-08-25T07:18:59.156911Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bottle, then grasp the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the can of red bull,and knocked it down.Then,policy A moved the arm to the bottle, grasped and dropped it.Next, policy A move the robotic arm to the red block, grasped and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the can of red bull, grasped and released it multiple times,then moved it and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the required task while policy B failed, so i prefer policy A.'),
(E'8b7d0903-9a2e-43ed-ac64-c97af95ddb57', E'2025-08-25T07:39:23.077100Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bottle from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm  to the red block rather than the bottle,  grasped it and moved it to right.Then,policy A attempted to grasp the blue block.Finally,policy A found the bottle, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Policy B first grasped the bottle, then moved it to right and dropped it smoothly.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task faster without any mistakes, so policy B is superior to policy A.'),
(E'9a9f25ca-e422-4b83-a1c0-8d16d16013f0', E'2025-08-25T07:54:32.734686Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wood blocks together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to a wooden block, grasped it, moved it close to the bottle and drop it.Then,policy A moved the arm to the red block,hovered above the red block until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the blue block,then moved the arm to the bottle.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm back to the blue block again and attempted to grasp it.Finally, policy b moved the robotic arm close to the wood block.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped one wood block while policy B grasped nothing, so i prefer policy A.'),
(E'f40389f1-4a98-4e30-a34e-84dc91099741', E'2025-08-25T08:10:06.068240Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the green block onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the green block,grasped it, moved and dropped it.Then policy A grasped the green block again,moved it and placed it onto the red block correctly.Policy B moved the robotic arm to the green block, grasped it, moved it and placed it onto the red block smoothly.Although both policies have completed the task successfully,policy B is more faster and efficient.Comparing their performance,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'f1bf1954-61c7-4763-9dcf-2d33346b4bfd', E'2025-08-25T08:20:16.313726Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bottle by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, paused briefly on the bottle,then moved away.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm to approach the bottle again, attempted to grasp it but failed in the end.Policy B moved the robotic arm to the bottle, grasped the bottom of the bottle, struggled to rotated it but only rotated it by a small angle.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has grasped and rotated the bottle according to command while policy A was unable to do nothing.So, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'255a369d-07e6-48e8-bdf3-986180720649', E'2025-08-25T08:34:32.958364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the blue block and move it close to the bottle', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the blue block, grasped it, moved it and dropped it near a red block rather than the bottle.Then, policy A moved the robotic arm to the blue block and grasped it again, moved it until time ran out.Policy B moved the robotic arm close to the blue block, after hesitating for while, grasped it moved it slightly and dropped it.Then, policy A attempted to grasp the blue block again in the end.When comparing the performance of the two,both policies have only grasped the blue block but have not move it close to bottle, so i choose tie.'),
(E'4d97b958-5850-40e0-85ed-4ff246d6df1e', E'2025-08-25T08:53:37.012571Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the game controller and put it onto the bottle', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to game controller, grasped it, moved it close the bottle and dropped it on the bottle but slipped off the bottle.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the game controller, made multiple attempts to grasp the game controller, struggled to pick it up but did not intend to put it onto the bottle.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A has tried to complete the task according to the command but policy B has not.So, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'8097a708-c549-4894-b8e8-6f47e38a18de', E'2025-08-25T09:10:04.715054Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bottle from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, grasped it, moved it from left to right and dropped it, but didn''t rotated it according to command.Policy B moved the robotic arm to the bottle,grasped the top of the bottle then dropped it soon.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm to the can of red bull, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the bottle from left to right according to the command while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9b6548df-fbde-42a1-a589-a490903a3c4b', E'2025-08-25T09:26:54.742362Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bottle by 90 degrees, then put it onto the box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bottle,grasped the top of the bottle,attempted to rotated it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the can of red bull, after hesitating for while, made multiple attempts to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped the bottle while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'94769f39-abae-4b2d-a00a-aad548dfa9df', E'2025-08-25T09:41:10.917164Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the blocks onto the box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to one wooden block,grasped it together with the cloth,moved it and put it onto the box successfully.Then,policy A moved the robotic arm to the red block and tried to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B moved the robotic arm to the blue block, grasped it ,moved it and put it onto the box correctly.Then,policy B  grasped the red block, moved it and put it onto the box.Next,policy B attempted to grasp the wooden block until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'abfa853f-621b-4e33-b5f0-8bfbe7a5a262', E'2025-08-25T18:12:11.787996Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the white block inside of the pot.', E'Neither policy was able to grab the block. policy A had approached the block but got one side of it''s gripper on the outside of the pot and then instead of moving the gripper fully inside of the pot began pushing the pot forward. policy B had decided to aimlessly search an empty space to the left of the pot. The layout of this evalution was a white block inside of a pot with a white piece of paper ocovering half of the pot but still leaving a space facing the right camera for the camera to see the white block and insert it''s gripper.'),
(E'c5521817-2366-4f34-a7dc-9e9f232f60ca', E'2025-08-25T18:23:41.948550Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Lift the grey circular thing by pulling on the string it is attached to.', E'Neither policy was able to grab or really identify the string. policy A did not even approach the string or the grey circular thing, but instead moved back and forth in the center of the field. policy B immeditaly approached the grey circular thing but it never attempted to grab the string or successfully grabbed anything. For context, there is a makeshift pulley system where a string is wrapped over an overhanging part of the field, and the string is attaced to the grey circular thing.'),
(E'3ff49e13-9ded-4fa9-98c3-cd0cca384cad', E'2025-08-25T18:37:23.660820Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'pull the string.', E'Both policies were able to grab the string and move it around. I said that policy A was better than policy B because policy A had approached the middle of the string while policy B had approached the grey circular thing and almost seemed to grab the string as a result of attempting to grab at the circular object. For context, string was strune about the field and was attached to a grey circular thing on the middle right of the field.'),
(E'09f6ae7f-1983-4e09-8b18-ec0a2a885109', E'2025-08-25T18:54:33.275793Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the grey circular thing by the string and put it in the pot.', E'Neither policy was able to lift the grey circular thing by the string. For context, there is a pot in the top left of the field, a white block in the bottom left and a grey circular thing on the bottom right with a string loop poking up vertically for the policies to grab. policy A approached the pot and pushed it forward for the entire episode. policy B approached the white block, grabbed it, and then brought it to the grey circular thing and placed it on top of it. I chose policy B because it actually grabbed something and it eventuall approached the block.'),
(E'ce55b466-d0c6-4534-b869-3bc03d0f1d08', E'2025-08-25T19:06:53.197404Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Lift the grey object by the string it is attached to and lift it into the pot.', E'For context there is a pot in the top left of the field, a white block in the bottom left of the field, and a grey circular object with string attached to it for the policies to lift on the bottom right. Neither policy was able to lift the grey circular object. policy A had picked up and interacted with the white block for the entire episode. policy B actually approached the grey circular object and even touched the string. Unfortunatley, policy A knocked the string from standing vertically to lying on the floor so the policy wasn''t able to pick up the object from that point forward. I chose policy B because it was able to actually approach the grey circular object and approach the string.'),
(E'e36018f9-2cc0-4629-84f6-3812c92bd6fb', E'2025-08-25T19:17:51.617604Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the bread.', E'I chose policy A over policy B because even though both policies had grabbed the blade, policy A held it longer, made more progress towards the bread and seemed to have greater control over it. policy A seemed to try and rotate the blade so that the sharp end was facing the ground (it was lying with the blade facing up so that setting it would be easier) by dropping the knife and rotating it''s arm a bit. policy B was only able to approach the blade before shortly dropping it and then kind of drifting towards the bottom left(where neithe the bread nor the knife are).'),
(E'747f95eb-6a52-493e-8f0b-4812bb9f7507', E'2025-08-25T19:28:02.514307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the bread.', E'policy A had begun to approach the knife but nevery actually got close enough to grab the knife, moving towards the knife and then retreating back for a good half of the episode and then attempting to rotate it''s hand in a way that it''s open end would be able to match the orientation of knife. policy B had actually aproached the knife in the correct orientation and even grabbed it. It then dropped the knife, picked it up again and proceeded to press the knife against the ground on the bottom left side of the field for the remainder of the episode. I chose policy B because it was able to actually grab the knife.'),
(E'8b8604bd-4854-4bd2-bbbc-791fa61d9603', E'2025-08-25T19:37:23.188522Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Deliver the bread to the happy face.', E'For context there is a drawing of a sad face on the top left of the feild and a drawing of a happy face on the top right and bread in the middle. policy A had approached the bread and grabbed at it, but it was not able to move it anywhere. policy B had approached the bread and spent the episode picking up the bread and dropping it. I chose policy B because it seemed as though it had begun to move the bread where policy A had not.'),
(E'69e4cfd3-0592-4dc2-922a-0a7962fd14d4', E'2025-08-26T01:10:52.294120Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, dropped it and moved away.Then, policy A moved the robotic arm back to the banana again,grasped it and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana,grasped it ,dropped it.Then,policy B also moved the robotic arm back to the banana, grasped and released it several times.When comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task correctly, both policies have only grasped the banana and their behavior was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'be6da69b-fb70-4d18-95cd-1f54533a399b', E'2025-08-26T05:04:56.872824Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bowl then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the bowl, then moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bowl, then moved the robotic arm back and forth several times, finally grasped the bowl, moved and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has completed the task ultimately while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is superior to policy A.'),
(E'ccd6c1b8-2e39-444e-a05f-673fcb8995de', E'2025-08-26T05:32:08.446411Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the boxes together', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the pincers,grasped it and moved it during the most time of the episode, dropped it down in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it,moved it and place it near the bigger box.Then,policy B grasped the bigger box and moved it onto the small box until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B has completed the task correctly while policy A failed.It is obviously that policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'390907ad-48c4-416d-bd97-eae7b9c8bca4', E'2025-08-26T05:54:52.015187Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bigger white box onto the paper', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the bigger white box,then moved away.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm around aimlessly.Finally,policy A moved the robotic toward a smaller box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box,adjusted its posture and made multiple attempts to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy B at least attempted to grasp a box while policy A didn''t do anything.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'9ce9d92c-f00d-478a-928a-f514052baf4b', E'2025-08-26T06:09:04.557956Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smaller box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the smaller box,pushed its edge to rotated it by about 90 degrees,then moved the robotic away from it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, but then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm as if searching the target in the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A has completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, it is clearly that policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'6a5fa907-9499-4faf-ab71-b880bd9db89b', E'2025-08-26T06:25:22.399210Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box, then move it next to plate', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box,grasped it, moved it slightly and dropped it.Then, policy A moved the robotic arm toward a bigger box until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box,then moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box.Finally,policy B grasped a sheet of paper.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to completed the task,but policy A at least grasp the smaller box.Therefore,i choose A.'),
(E'cf495cd1-99c9-4401-8219-abbee12321ca', E'2025-08-26T06:39:09.351048Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box and put it onto the big box', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the smaller box,grasped it and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box,pushed it, then moved the robotic arm away.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least identified and grasped the smaller box,therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'4ff01977-4d3c-4bea-ad60-e61e498842ab', E'2025-08-26T06:50:08.499387Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the small box from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to bigger box, then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy A grasped the smaller box and moved it slightly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target, then moved the robotic arm toward the bigger and the smaller box one after another until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped the smaller box required.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'50dd8813-790f-4df7-a3a2-aecc19d085c5', E'2025-08-26T07:03:46.268414Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the object,then grasped the bigger box in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box,then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least identified the smaller box and tried to grasp it.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'502a594d-a27d-4f3f-8e2d-c166a0888054', E'2025-08-26T07:17:29.105845Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the boxes from left to right', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the middle size box, grasped it,moved it from left to right then dropped it.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm around randomly until time ran out.Policy B first moved robotic arm toward the biggest box,pause briefly,then pushed the biggest box.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm closed to the smallest box and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least moved one box from left to right while policy B didn''t move any box.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'93c37b85-723d-4fbd-b9d7-c4e4c5bcbb2b', E'2025-08-26T07:43:06.195280Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread, then grasp the blue block', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm close to the blue block, paused briefly, then moved around the blue block but didn''t  grasp it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the blue block, then pushed it.Next, policy B moved the arm aimlessly until time ran out.When comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task and their behavior was similar.Therefore,i choose tie.'),
(E'e8a6305e-5ae8-4ac0-9783-81fcaf49a24a', E'2025-08-26T08:06:14.609747Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the bread ,grasped it, moved it from left to right and dropped it on the table.Policy B first move the robotic to the banana,grasped it,moved it from left to right and dropped it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to the bread and attempted to grasp it.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A has completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore,i choose policy A.'),
(E'661b29ac-6a65-4ef5-bd1f-345a0065ef64', E'2025-08-26T08:16:46.962012Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the wooden block which is not food, grasped it and moved it close to the red block.Policy B first moved robotic arm to the red block,grasped it, moved it and dropped it near the bread.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy has completed the task correctly, but policy B at least dropped the block near the bread which is food.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'7cb578e5-5c9b-4217-b670-ac9b6c6e3ae4', E'2025-08-26T08:32:55.404148Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bread onto the paper', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the bread but then moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it,grasped it and moved it close to the paper,finally moved it away.Policy B first grasped the banana,moved it from left to right meanwhile pushed the bread.Comparing the performance of the two,both policy have grasped the wrong object banana rather than bread,and their behavior was similar.Therefore,i choose tie.'),
(E'752d9703-0ec9-4f32-aeda-1d452cadeeb9', E'2025-08-26T08:46:31.187849Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the banana,grasped it, moved it to right then rotate it by about 60 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana,pushed to rotated it.Then policy B grasped the banana and rotated it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'fd1a943c-cc91-4474-99c1-14444d40880c', E'2025-08-26T09:08:26.812515Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it,moved it and placed it on the paper successfully.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the paper,pushed it then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B grasped the banana, moved it and dropped it on the table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore,policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'36f85925-297f-45d1-984c-1efad382bdca', E'2025-08-26T09:18:58.488608Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the bread,grasped and released it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm back and forth around  the bread several times, but didn''t grasp the bread in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic around the bread, but then grasped the wooden block rather than the bread, moved the wooden block to right and rotated the wooden block.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy has completed the task, but policy B at least did the required movement.Therefore,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'7fd5b390-e60c-458d-9ae3-8ffcbf6da42f', E'2025-08-26T09:36:42.478248Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees, then put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the banana,after hesitating for a while, grasped it, rotated it and dropped it on table rather paper.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the banana,grasped it and rotated it by about 180 degrees.Then policy B moved the banana toward the paper until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B nearly completed the task while policy  A failed.Therefore,i choose policy B.'),
(E'8ef9d9df-4a0a-4358-97aa-c6fb16c84908', E'2025-08-26T09:54:57.953984Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods into the plate', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm closed to the bread and banana,then stopped during the remaining time of trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the bread, pushed it to the plate.Then,policy B moved the robotic arm to a wooden block,grasped it and moved it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy has completed the task correctly,but policy B at least pushed the bread which is food to the plate.Therefore,policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'382cd287-c72c-4c10-9d8b-7e79c7fe082f', E'2025-08-27T01:07:06.735891Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the mobile phone, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, made multiple attempts to grasp it, but failed in the limited time.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, adjusted posture and orientation, but didn''t grasp the mobile phone at last.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'47922ba7-84ca-4281-916e-44c0e0f1d814', E'2025-08-27T01:20:25.127934Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mobile phone from left to right', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm to the paper which is under the mobile phone, grasp the paper, pulled it from left to right together with the mobile phone, then released it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the paper which is under the mobile phone, and pushed the paper, then moved the robotic arm away.Next,the robotic arm stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the task while policy B failed, therefore, policy A is better.'),
(E'51c663e2-30e3-4921-9b98-bca9334154cb', E'2025-08-27T01:29:55.386009Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Deliver the bread to the sad face.', E'For context, the field is set up so that there is a frowny face on the upper left side, a happy face on the upper right side and a bread on the lower middle. policy A had approached empty space on the left of the bread and on the side of the frowny face and kind of wandered that space. policy B had grabbed the bread and began to appraoch the faces. Before policy B could actually reach either the happy or sad face, it dropped the bread- the direction/face it had intended to deliver to is unknown. I chose policy B because it had managed to grab the bread.'),
(E'1aadc629-7148-4af1-a7df-186ceb63de2a', E'2025-08-27T01:35:55.546201Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all electronics products onto the book', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm close to the book, pushed it then moved the robotic arm away and stopped during remaining time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the book, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm around aimlessly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'18038b3b-262f-4f61-8a1e-ea4c090f4813', E'2025-08-27T01:40:38.418230Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Deliver the bread to the happy face.', E'For context the layout of the field is that there is a sad face on the upper left side, a smiley face on the upper right side and bread in the lower middle. policy A had managed to grab the bread, but was unable to make any progress towards the faces. policy B had grabbed the bread and dropped it initially on the rght side where the smiley face was, but it was kind of far. The second time policy B picked up the bread, it placed it somewhat in between the happy and sad face but perhaps closer to the smiley face. After picking up the bread a third time, policy B then spent the rest of the episode alternating between placing it towards the blower end of the feild on the smiley side and the bottom right corner of the paper where the sad face was drawn.'),
(E'891667ac-6940-4801-bb0b-51059eeeab0a', E'2025-08-27T02:11:52.715386Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the mobile phone on top of  the book', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the white computer mouse rather than mobile phone, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, but then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm close to the pencil.Finally,policy B grasped the black computer mouse and move it toward the book until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, although both policy were not able to complete the task,policy B at least grasped and moved  one object toward the book.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'46f5d196-4784-46e8-aec6-21f35adfac60', E'2025-08-27T02:22:42.170011Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the sad face.', E'For context, there are pictures of a sad and smiley face on the uppr left and right side of the field respectivley. It also might be worth mentioning that the default third-person perspective is on the right side. Both policies began by approaching the smiley face on the upper right side of the field. First they touched it with open grippers but then both policies squeeze their grippers together. policy A at some point drifted towards the sad face and right at the very end of the episode it was able to touch the sad face. policy B had continued to approach and touch the smiley face for the duration of the episode.'),
(E'6f7f1a08-d447-4a8a-98bb-33fe6e167fed', E'2025-08-27T02:33:05.323774Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the sad face.', E'For context, there were pictures of a smiley and sad face on the upper right and left of the field respectivley. Both policies eventually moved towards the smiley face. policy A initially approached the smiley face and then stayed their for the duration of the episode- moving up and down, forward and backwards to touch the smiley face. policy B initially moved towards the sad face, but before it could touch it, policy B made a turn towards the smiley face and stayed there for the rest of the episode. It might be worth mentioning that this was done with the left camera, but unexpected preferences for the smiley face were seen when the chosen camera was the right one as well.'),
(E'eb9170cc-8b09-4aa1-bcef-92c960718e58', E'2025-08-27T02:43:14.143904Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the happy face.', E'For context there is a sad face and a happy face on the upper left and right of the field respectivley. policy A approached the right side where the smiley face is but touched and grabbed at the bottom right of the field away from the smiley face. For the remainder of the episode policy A exhibited erratic and strange movments, moving forward/backward and also rotating it''s arm for some reason. policy B started by approaching the smiley face right away and then getting so close it was maybe an inch away from touching the paper. It would do that 3 more times before finally grabbing the paper right at the very end of the episode. Also for some reason, policy B would drift towards the sad face in the latter 2 times of going back and forth before coming back to the smiley face.'),
(E'69b85b75-bd1b-4253-9aec-84908e34fa96', E'2025-08-27T02:54:55.616406Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the happy face.', E'For context there is a frowny face on the top left of the field and a smiley face on the top right of the field. Both policies approached the smiley face, got kind of close, but before touching the paper recoiled. Policy A continued to move back and forth from the smiley face for the rest of teh episode. Policy B got arguably close to the smiley face, but I detracted from it''s score because it then proceeeded to attempt to touch the frowny face for the second half of the episode. For some reason when trying this type of task, almost all policies approached the paper, got really close, and then retracted itself. This happend for when it approached the correct face and when it approached the incorrect face.'),
(E'1818fc9f-762e-4394-8ac5-3a6ed6fb1ca3', E'2025-08-27T02:55:58.288995Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pencil and move it next to mobile phone', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward to the mouse, then moved the arm away.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm close to the pencil,then moved the arm away.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the mobile phone and pushed it, then pushed the paper which is under the mobile phone until time ran out.Although both policy failed, policy A at least found the pencil.Therefore,policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'a217f1aa-dc7e-4d44-8173-a0629696513f', E'2025-08-27T03:08:11.026826Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the marker pen, then place it onto the book', E'Policy A first  moved the robotic arm toward the marker pen, grasped it,moved it toward the book,but then stopped near the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the mobile phone instead of the marker pen, pushed it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm close to the pencil and stopped.Comparing the performance of the two, police A is better than policy B.'),
(E'8f5a12ab-1b83-4f58-841b-0163c0f220bb', E'2025-08-27T03:42:01.498710Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the computer mouse from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the mouse, paused briefly, then moved the robotic arm away. Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out. Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the right side of the mouse, then moved around slightly in the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'ebfb2434-3230-4b43-b63f-96c2c5f78876', E'2025-08-27T03:51:58.790541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, then put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the pencil instead of the marker pen, attempted to grasp it. Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, paused briefly, grasped it and moved it close to the book until time ran out.Policy B first also moved the robotic arm to the pencil, then moved the robotic arm away and stopped.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has grasped and moved the marker pen while policy B did nothing.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'38561507-b9ba-4b8b-894f-c556c054421d', E'2025-08-27T04:03:32.026629Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all pens from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the marker pen, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the pencil, grasped it, moved it to right slightly and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm the marker pen, grasped it, paused briefly as if in hesitation and moved it to right slightly.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'b7bee210-8042-4f0f-ad94-f54e5f2b64de', E'2025-08-27T05:05:54.801586Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pliers then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm around the pliers, then moved the robotic arm toward the plate and pushed it.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the pliers, adjusted posture, attempted to grasp it, then didn''t grasp it but move the robotic arm away.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the pliers while policy A did not do any thing.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'3f6910b0-cc1c-4ab4-bf72-80c9c87d13fb', E'2025-08-27T05:15:37.959740Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the screwdriver from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the screwdriver, grasp it, rotated it and moved it to right slightly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to screwdriver, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has completed the task more smoothly, therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'eee21d7a-ed92-49ad-b3ee-5020bc8bc25f', E'2025-08-27T05:25:59.606660Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the boxes together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, grasped it, moved it and dropped it on the table.Then policy A moved the robotic close to a big box and pushed it until time ran out. Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the screwdriver,pushed it, grasp and released it.Then moved the robotic arm around aimlessly.Comparing the performance of the two, although both failed, policy A at least attempted to approach a box in the end.Therefore i choose policy A.'),
(E'46eccf23-f354-46ae-ade5-a5fd9a9514b4', E'2025-08-27T05:38:19.135946Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the pliers into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, grasp it, moved it and put it on the edge of the plate.Policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly as if didn''t find the object, and moved close to a box in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'675433c3-4cf8-4a6f-bab8-6a107dc26862', E'2025-08-27T05:45:21.590403Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the pliers by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees and dropped it on the table.Policy B just moved the arm back and forth until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A was able to complete the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is distinctly better than policy B.'),
(E'427f7b62-8006-4a40-9bbb-28973baf019e', E'2025-08-27T05:54:25.122285Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smallest box, then move it next to pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box rather than the smaller one, pushed it ,then attempted the grasp a paper.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box, then grasped it and moved it close to the pliers.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped a bigger box and moved it close to the pliers.Therefore policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'76b63513-0a2b-4858-867f-fc3bff676529', E'2025-08-27T06:05:41.856740Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box and put it onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the small box, attempted to grasp it several times but failed, then moved the robotic arm to the bigger box in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the small box, paused briefly, then moved the robotic arm toward the bigger box and pushed it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the smaller box.Therefore, i think policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'79e2d929-3462-4a27-8d11-973e3dfcc291', E'2025-08-27T06:15:16.054994Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pliers from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pliers, pushed it to left, paused briefly,then grasped it and rotated it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book rather than the pliers, pushed it.Then policy B moved the arm aimlessly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'b64f0b73-6b7d-4f52-9911-63d8d0c995ca', E'2025-08-27T06:30:19.722659Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated pliers by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, then pushed it to rotated it slowly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, pushed it to rotate it by about 90 degrees,then attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least rotate the pliers by 90 degrees.Therefore, policy B is slightly than policy A.'),
(E'60e91566-6612-40df-a312-dc2fb2a3dfd9', E'2025-08-27T06:41:17.063196Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the tools from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the screwdriver, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy A attempted to grasp the cloth until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, made multiple attempts to grasp it, but failed in the end.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least moved one type of tools from left to right,while policy B didn''t move any one.Therefore,policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'ee347407-cb9a-4aca-bca6-199cf63b62c9', E'2025-08-27T07:03:30.852209Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block, then grasp the grapes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, grasped it, moved it to left and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm around the green/yellow block rather than red block, then paused until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasp the red block while policy B didn''t grasp any block.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4007400f-e922-49c6-943b-04e899608a88', E'2025-08-27T07:32:27.673649Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bunch of grapes from left to right', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm back and forth several time as if searching the target until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the banana, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on the table.Then policy B moved the robotic arm toward the bunch of grapes, grasped it and moved it to right.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B struggled to completed the task but policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'9d2dc12c-4b02-4807-8ef5-6be8ec21960b', E'2025-08-27T07:42:44.429487Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the fruits together', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm to the green wood block which is not fruit, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the orange, pushed it close to the banana and paused in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the arm close to the orange, attempted to grasp it but pushed it to slip off the table.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to yellow wood block which is not fruit.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved two types of fruits together while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'67c8e060-a18d-4520-8ad0-816f6dbf1b52', E'2025-08-27T07:58:05.654578Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the orange into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the orange, pushed it toward the plate,then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm to the red block, grasped it and moved it close to the plate until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the orange, attempted to grasp it but only pushed it close to the plate.Then policy B moved the robotic arm into the plate, pulled it toward the outside of table so that made the orange slip off the table.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least let the orange stay beside the plate while policy B made the orange slip off the table.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'97b5d2ce-678a-419c-b81c-24513951455e', E'2025-08-27T08:57:00.027982Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the green block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the green block, then pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the arm close to the green block, pushed it to right meanwhile let it rotate by 90 degrees.Comparing the performance of the two,both policies were able to complete the task correctly,but policy A seemed more smoothly.Therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'd90a31e3-b564-4b82-a1c5-9d8442ac2203', E'2025-08-27T09:09:05.436555Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and move it close to the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the plate, then attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, pushed it,paused briefly then  grasped it and released it.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm toward the yellow block.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped the banana while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore,i prefer policy B.'),
(E'0d67134a-d6b5-476b-8aa5-d58ac0a51e3d', E'2025-08-27T09:21:33.301551Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the white block and put it onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the white block, attempted to grasp it but didn''t,then moved the robotic arm close to red block.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B approached the white block and grasped it in the end.Comparing their performance, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped the white block.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'73f7cf62-b42b-432a-a7a8-b481c965b0f5', E'2025-08-27T09:31:39.235602Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the white block from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the white block, then pushed it to make it rotate until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the white block, grasped it,rotated it and moved it to right in the end.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B has completed the task ultimately, but policy A has only rotated the white block.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'ea5fa195-fc40-4467-9ff7-63f9ef403aaf', E'2025-08-27T09:45:22.946214Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees, then put it onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the banana, grasped it, rotated it, moved it close to the red block,then moved it close the yellow block and white on after another.Next,after hesitating for while, policy A moved the robotic arm above the yellow block in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, rotated it,moved it close to the bunch of grapes.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task correctly, but policy B at least moved the banana to the blocks.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'7ad5b306-82e2-4287-a8b7-d77f2204b589', E'2025-08-27T10:02:26.437535Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the red blocks into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the red block, grasped it, moved it then placed into the plate.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the white and red block, then paused above them until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has at least put one red block into the plate while policy B has not.Therefore,policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'5ee27500-d275-4aa9-86dc-f136c44d2e91', E'2025-08-27T18:07:29.058209Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the bread.', E'I wanted to see how policies acted in low ligh condidtions so I kept the light off for this evalution. policy A had aproached the direction of the bread and the spray bottle and quickly knocked over the spray bottle. policy A then went to the ground with it''s gripper, sort of pushing the spray bottle towards the bread. After doing that a bit, policy A changed directions to grab at the yellow cup before coming back to the black spray bottle. policy B was much more reserved with it''s movements. policy B started by approaching the milk carton grabbing at it without making contact and then moving towards the spray bottle. policy B approached the spray bottle but after touching it a little paused for a moment before trying to grab the spray bottle and knocking it down. policy B finished the episode by grabbing at the spray bottle. I gave the policies a tie because neither really progressed more than the other. You could argue that policy A might have been directed more towards the bread, but any argument for intention is uncertain.'),
(E'a1854c1c-211e-4d90-8e61-268b64e989b7', E'2025-08-27T18:19:45.055346Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'grab the yellow cup.', E'I wanted to test the effect of low light condidtions so I dimmed the lights in the room. policy A immediatley approached the yellow cup and made many attempts to grab the cup. policy A found some difficulty in getting it''s entire gripper over the cup as the cup was almost the width of the space in the gripper when it is fully open. Towards the end of the episode, policy A had found some success in grabbing the cup, even lifting it off the ground a little, but it wasn''t able to exercise any command over the cup in the air. policy B had moved towards the cup, but didn''t really try grabbing the cup, instead pushing it forward at the end of the episode.'),
(E'ec723e48-aec1-4951-9558-741f713391b1', E'2025-08-27T18:29:13.782254Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the milk carton.', E'I wanted to see the effect of dimming the lights for this evaluation. policy A had approachd the milk carton and jammed it''s gripper into the ground for the entire episode, even moving the field a little. policy B had grabbed the milk carton from the top, and for some reason re-adjusted it''s grip on the milk carton the entire time- picking up the carton, lifting it less than a centimeter, then dropping the carton to fix it''s grip. Eventually policy B moved the carton laterally to do the exact same thing it was doing but in a new place. policy B ended up knocking the carton over when doing this and wasn''t able to recover.'),
(E'4a6d00e1-9376-499b-a24e-d36bdaa2e16f', E'2025-08-27T18:40:24.985280Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take the cup from me.', E'policy A was able to move itself towards me, but instead of moving its gripper to meet me, it had pushed its gripper into the ground and grabbed at nothing at the space underneath my hand. policy B was actually able to reach my hand and wrap its gripper around the cup and squeeze, but it did not hold onto it after grabbing at it, resulting the cup to fall to the ground.'),
(E'31116d05-b2d7-4eda-a343-fff3eb01ee62', E'2025-08-27T18:51:59.575855Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the cup from me.', E'policy A had approached the cup and tried to wrap its gripper around the cup to grab it. policy A never actually tried to grab the cup despite having its entire gripper over the cup, and after failing to grab it from me, it kind of wandered upwards and to the right of the field and never recovered. policy B approached the cup after a little while longer than policy A and tried to grab the inside of the cup and actually grabbed it. Policy B did not continue to hold on to the cup and let it go after less than a second. policy A then proceeded to wander near the floor for most of the episode before again approaching the level of the cup at the very end of the episode.'),
(E'703503fa-a5cc-4ee8-96a3-99612fbca12e', E'2025-08-27T19:03:41.018379Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the yellow cup and drop it off the table.', E'policy A was only able to approach the cup and grab it around the brim. policy A never lifted or moved the cup. policy B was able to grab the cup, lift and move the cup towards the edge of the table but never completely off of the table.'),
(E'e3f998b7-5703-464f-8074-c64ead3ff106', E'2025-08-27T19:51:23.077533Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move all the cubes to bowl', E'With a variety of things displaying on the table, both policies only succeeded in grasping one (out of 3) cubes and mistakenly picking up other objects like egg, duck, or a half-circle into the bowl. They seemed to reach for the objects on the left hand side first and then gradually moved to the right'),
(E'b1fc99ae-b209-4f7c-9f9e-124510817fd4', E'2025-08-27T20:02:46.680823Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the edible things into bowl', E'Policy A slowly reached for the egg and succesfully placed it in the bowl; it also half-way moved the duck into bowl since the arm was hovering right at the top of the bowl. B on the other hand followed a random pattern since it grasped the cube and duck and placed it on and then left the gripper frozen in the position of the egg while the policy came to an  end soon'),
(E'ca7d301e-d39c-4f9d-b087-9538d8eb90a0', E'2025-08-27T20:29:45.918569Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the marker on the cardboard', E'B is slightly better as it at least headed towards the direction where the marker was placed while A just pointed to another tabletop on the left. B grasped the yellow cube which was located next to the marker.'),
(E'7714c727-bcfe-49ca-9709-5f386e02a3d7', E'2025-08-27T20:42:54.150521Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the writing utensils on cardboard', E'A has disrupted the whole seen as it pushed one of the marker off the table and tried to grasp a yellow eraser right next to it. B seemed to know how to property grasp the marker but it ended up putting it on another tabletop'),
(E'b4cbfd4e-6fe6-46e5-b8d7-444246fd2693', E'2025-08-27T21:00:28.434396Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'move the carrot into plate', E'B is indeed better since it completed the task in first few movements while A struggled to identify the exact location of the carrot and thus randomly grasped the other objects that lied along with it sich as banana and black stick'),
(E'ac8b95f4-b64d-44b4-854b-d24982ed453c', E'2025-08-27T21:11:47.250076Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'start the toaster', E'Policy A and B both reached for the bread in the slots without realizing the only way to start a toaster is sto lower the lever on the right to begin toasting cycles. In both trials, none of the policy has shifted to the right direction of the toaster'),
(E'2aacddcc-d81f-418e-8533-e9cbf6d4bf5a', E'2025-08-27T21:23:50.666172Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape into container', E'B completely placed the tape into the desired location while A struggle to grasp the tape in place despite trying for multiple times'),
(E'10954dc5-f91d-4cc4-8ad2-1381bcd68cb7', E'2025-08-27T21:36:29.034182Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape into drawer and then close it', E'Policy B somewhat performed better as it was able to identify the intended object (tape) to start with but had a hard time grasping it completely in the air. A went off absolutely as it moved the lid and placed it into drawer'),
(E'd585f889-279c-446c-97a3-f8ef02e36f44', E'2025-08-27T21:48:14.115219Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the egg into pot', E'Despite beign asked to placed the egg into pot, both policies had the same pattern since they were very swiftly grasping the egg but then placeed it on the bowl, which has a very similar shape as the pot'),
(E'fde1b3a8-d9ca-4adf-bbba-2e991c7ffe1d', E'2025-08-27T22:01:38.986611Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the scissor on notebook', E'A and B both knew it had something to do with the scissor as the arm reached for this object at the very first move. However, A was unable to grasp it upward while B had that ability to do so but got disrupt due to time constraint'),
(E'4c8f57ba-18c7-435f-99e2-5db7bb18572c', E'2025-08-27T22:14:01.304661Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the blue marker into bin', E'A at least could identify the blue marker after multiple trials of pushing the black marker out of the seen or rotating the scissor. A attempte to grasp it but got the marker further and further away that the arm could not reach for. B instead tried to interact with the black marker and ignore the blue one. None of each marker was placed on the notebook as requested'),
(E'02c526aa-bde6-4572-a65e-4f27eefddb28', E'2025-08-27T22:25:04.264787Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape into the black bowl', E'A was much better since it knows the next orientation after lifting the tape upward. A gradually moved the tape over the blakc bowl but the arm at the same time also pushed the base of the bowl, causing the falling of some objects nearby and the tape was not placed on the bowl at last. B on the other hand failed to identify the blakc bowl on the left as it moved the tape over the black bin next to it'),
(E'2e5d5404-5909-4b73-a4af-b8921781be97', E'2025-08-28T01:03:24.490692Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the table, then stopped on the table during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the drawer,then moved the robot arm close to the pencil, grasped it and moved it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least performed some operation while policy A didn''t.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'a2bf8722-19cf-459c-a0ab-27dc769d36ae', E'2025-08-28T01:19:58.488004Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the round button of the remote controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the remote controller, pushed it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the controller, grasped it, moved it then dropped it on the table.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped the controller several time while policy A just pushed it.Therefore,policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'bd980c68-3649-4afd-9f3a-176b88287d84', E'2025-08-28T01:29:52.144904Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all pencils onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the green pencil, grasped it , moved it slowly to the paper until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the green pencil, grasp it ,move it randomly several times, then placed it near the paper in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'754df106-3274-4eb5-a651-dd7afc168eb7', E'2025-08-28T01:39:39.122451Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the eraser on top of the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the paper rather then the eraser, then moved the robotic arm to the red pencil,grasped it,moved it and place it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the eraser, grasped it , moved it slightly close to the drawer and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and moved the eraser while policy A did not.Therefore,policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'dfa62abb-b549-42a6-8799-25794d646104', E'2025-08-28T01:49:36.086292Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the controller, grasped and released it several times, then paused above the controller in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the controller, touched it, then moved the robotic arm away and moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, although both policies have not obviously rotated the controller,policy A at least grasped the controller while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'd30fec84-96f2-419b-a004-60d0aee68258', E'2025-08-28T02:06:40.381145Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp controller and move it next to the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pencil instead of the controller, then moved away.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the controller, grasped it, moved it toward the marker pen, then placed it near the marker pen.Next,policy B grasped the eraser and moved it close to the marker pen.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B have completed the task correctly while policy A has done nothing relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'd75369ac-7872-4bb5-991c-5e497d28476b', E'2025-08-28T02:27:28.788158Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser, then place it into the pencil box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the eraser, grasped it, moved it then dropped it into the pencil box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the tape, then moved the robotic arm toward the eraser, grasped it, moved it toward the pencil box, but dropped it outside the pencil box.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the task correctly while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'c8481341-51e4-4cfd-956c-2772d26529c4', E'2025-08-28T02:55:48.580306Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the pencil box, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pencil box, then moved around the pencil box during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to a pencil rather than the pencil box, then grasped and released the pencil.Next,policy moved the robotic arm to the pencil box, attempted to close it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, both policies have not complete the task, but policy B at least identified the pencil box and tried to close it while policy A has not done anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'0992beb6-0805-4bab-98c0-8797d0861a11', E'2025-08-28T03:07:36.827461Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm toward the controller, rotated it slightly by pushing its top edge, then moved robotic arm close to the book and push it until time ran out.Policy B first took some time to find the controller, then moved the robotic arm onto the controller and paused during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least rotated the controller while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'85ad731b-1f0f-4921-8cf6-03eababa41bc', E'2025-08-28T03:21:00.897609Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all Stationery from right to left', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pencil box, paused briefly,then pushed pencil box slightly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pencils,then grasped the pencils/marker together, moved them slightly to left then placed them on table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has moved some stationery from right to left slightly while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'6fb23509-494c-46cd-99b0-342124b22be2', E'2025-08-28T03:37:19.776348Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bottle then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, knocked one bottle down, then moved the robotic arm to another bottle and attempted to grasp it but failed in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one bottle, pushed it away,then moved the robotic arm to edge of the table and tried to grasp the edge.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least attempted to grasp a bottle while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd454271a-bc52-4c3e-9430-501bc434e458', E'2025-08-28T03:49:00.259288Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the smaller box from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the middle of two boxes, then paused until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the task successfully, while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'a5671f2c-ac30-4883-a344-81a0d036d46a', E'2025-08-28T05:07:03.309673Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the bottles together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to blue bottle, adjusted posture,pushed it to left slightly, then moved the robotic arm close to the red bottle until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, then stopped during the remaining time of the trial.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least pushed one bottle to left while policy B didn''t do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4a91eebf-db90-4873-b3e6-4e1b0d50fbde', E'2025-08-28T05:17:58.478351Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller box onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, after hesitating for a while, grasped the smaller box, moved it to left, then dropped it on the table.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task correctly, but policy B at least grasped and moved the smaller box while policy A didn''t do anything relevant.Therefore,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'822a1d7f-e29a-40ac-ba80-99360dc25251', E'2025-08-28T05:30:05.147820Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the blue bottle by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red bottle rather than the blue bottle, then grasped the cap of the bottle, attempted to rotated it but failed.Policy B first moved the robotic arm toward the blue bottle, grasped it, rotated it by 90 degrees then placed it on the table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'77bbd9a7-fd72-4748-a22f-bc7202763267', E'2025-08-28T05:45:31.360672Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box, then move it next to the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red bottle, pushed it, after hesitating for while,moved the robotic arm toward the smaller box and pushed it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box, attempted to grasped it but failed, then stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B has found the smaller box faster than policy A.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'e34fa9c3-c78a-477a-982f-d88deab9eb7d', E'2025-08-28T06:44:42.389471Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box and put to the right side of the bottle', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm  back and forth aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved the robotic arm closed to the smaller box, pushed it and made it slip off the table.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least moved the robotic arm to the target box.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'192c7a6f-a796-486f-825a-9cc3cf9dfca3', E'2025-08-28T06:58:05.043517Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bottle from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bottle, grasped the cap of the bottle, rotated it by about 90 degrees while moved it to right slightly.Policy B first moved the arm close to the bottle, grasped the cap of the bottle , rotated it by about 90 degrees while moved it forward slightly.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A has moved the bottle slightly to right while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'f64832ab-305f-4805-b962-95549c11b4ef', E'2025-08-28T07:09:26.911562Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to smaller box, pushed the smaller box to make it rotated by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bigger box, pushed it,then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box but didn''t rotated it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least rotated the smaller box while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'1273e21d-1771-4794-98ef-6cafd83e45ed', E'2025-08-28T07:20:43.393175Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the drinks  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the blue bottle, made multiple attempts to grasp it but failed.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the bottom of the two bottles, pushed the bottles forward until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the red bottle, grasped it, moved it to right slightly, then pushed the red bottle forward until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least grasped one bottle of drinks and moved it to right while police A did not.Therefore, policy B is better.'),
(E'17e0adf7-bfb9-44df-a2b3-3ed3d9c447fc', E'2025-08-28T07:38:21.960711Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread, then grasp the pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to screwdriver, then moved around it during the remaining time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pliers , grasped and released it, then pushed the pliers close to the bread.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped one required object while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'c824a216-8512-4345-ba37-c310913c172b', E'2025-08-28T07:52:28.414025Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, adjusted posture, attempted to grasp the bread, but failed in the limited time.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore,policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'cf89de99-9925-484f-a3c5-db42442e8736', E'2025-08-28T08:01:41.769791Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the bread and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the pliers and pushed it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread, grasped it, moved it close to the boxes which is not food.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least put two types of foods together while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'7fd807d2-750a-4238-a039-b9d0c9f3ca2a', E'2025-08-28T08:14:25.970789Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bread onto the pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bunch of grapes, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm away.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the bottle and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task and both policies have not performed any required operations.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'b7ecd92a-1c94-4b8e-bbfb-4121d928ba1b', E'2025-08-28T08:25:57.917930Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the pencil box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to pencil box, grasped it and dropped it to make it open, then grasped the edge of the pencil box,rotated it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, then moved the robotic arm back and forth  randomly as if searching the target.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A nearly completed the task while policy B didn''t performed any relevant operations.Therefore,policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'132b7c0b-667a-4f2c-8262-1ffc0c727b33', E'2025-08-28T09:05:35.579937Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread and move it close to the screwdriver', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the banana, then moved the robotic arm to the pencil box, grasped it, moved it to the middle of the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread, attempted to grasp it but failed, then policy A moved the robotic arm to the banana and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least attempted to grasp the bread.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b77f38e2-7b67-4e9c-8c41-c8a8618342d7', E'2025-08-28T09:17:51.930402Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes and put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bunch of grapes, grasped it, moved it back and forth, then stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bunch of grapes, grasped it, moved it and placed it on the paper.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'cba0f46f-5f72-47f2-b21d-312b883fab11', E'2025-08-28T09:26:44.170866Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bread, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on the table, but didn''t rotated it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread,pushed it forward and made it rotated by a small angle.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped the bread and moved it to right.Therefore,i prefer policy A.'),
(E'118e3440-6d30-415a-9e64-e1fad7648b09', E'2025-08-28T09:39:04.289847Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bread by 90 degrees, then put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bread, pushed it to make it rotated by a small angle.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the paper and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread, grasped it, moved it to right while rotated it by about 90 degree, but did not put it onto the paper.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped and rotated the bread.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b3f2bc1d-c72c-42fb-83e9-860e1353d1b1', E'2025-08-28T09:49:47.537547Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bread, attempted ti grasp it but failed, then policy A grasp the banana and dropped it.Next, policy A grasped the bread and released it.Policy B first moved the arm to middle of the foods, then stopped there during remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped two types of foods while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'3b1f9dbc-6309-4699-ac3c-2cf75037e749', E'2025-08-28T20:42:17.829670Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put all of the cups inside of each other.', E'Policy A was able to place the red cup inside of the blue cup and then grab both cups in preparation for putting it into the yellow cup. policy B was able to put the blue cup into the yellow cup, but since it was not able to place the yellow cup into the red cup(since it is the smallest) policy B never made the effort to go towards the red cup. policy A had started with the smaller cups, so it didn''t have to move to a different cup in order to make progress- instead simply bringing the smaller cups with it to make the progress.'),
(E'5ec0dd34-d507-4ad9-bd68-4a6646db0148', E'2025-08-28T20:52:18.513180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place all of the cups inside of each other.', E'policy A spent was very slow, only spending the later half of the episode doing ''meaningful'' work- knocking over the large yellow cup that it couldn''t even start with and then attempting to grab it by the outside. poliyc B had started with the red cup, quickly placed it in the blue cup and then for some reason moved to the yellow cup and placed that on top of the red/blue stack. Since the yellow cup was bigger than any of the other cups, it just laid on top.'),
(E'fc65e738-88b9-44d0-937d-ffea5d1da74a', E'2025-08-28T21:11:58.949860Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Knock over the red and yellow cups.', E'policy A had started by going for the red cup but accidentally knocked over the blue cup. After knocking it over, policy A attempted to grab the blue cup before going to the yellow cup and grabbing at iand dropping it for the rest of the episode. policy B actually started by attempting to grab and drop the blue cup in the middle before moving to the yellow cup. policy B would then pick up and drop the yellow cup without knocking it over for the rest of the episode. I chose policy B because policy A had knocked down the only cup it wasn''t supposed to.'),
(E'2d15c027-277f-40c0-bf6b-75fb15015771', E'2025-08-28T21:27:42.255307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Tear the paper.', E'For context there was a paper that was folded in half so that one side was taped to the table and the other one kind of stood up in the air. There was also a pre-tear in the paper that neither policy attempted to use. policy A had gone for the middle of the untapped paper for the entire episode, not able to grab anything since it was like grabbing a flat surface. policy B had created a fold when it grabbed the paper, causing it to wrinkle/fold. This fold was then used to later tear the paper(albiet with me holding down the paper since it was not taped down strong enough).'),
(E'2950936d-bf8c-47ea-9af5-b4ad3d3a86cf', E'2025-08-29T01:36:38.608491Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the apple, then grasp the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the apple, pushed it, then attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, then moved the robotic arm to a banana and push it.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm close to cube again in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least pushed and attempted to grasp the apple while policy B didn''t do any thing relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'b40424db-d807-4a04-9dc4-c2d8e88a7104', E'2025-08-29T01:47:08.594604Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to cube, pushed it forward slightly, then stopped in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block instead of the cube, then moved it to right and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task. Policy B at least  grasped one object and moved it to right according to the command, although grasp the wrong object.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'6373a094-dfdd-4dba-a060-3ebd742db422', E'2025-08-29T02:16:10.212833Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all red blocks onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger red block, attempted to grasp it but failed.Then policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller red block, grasped it, moved it and placed it onto book.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to another red block, grasped it, moved it toward the book but dropped during the process.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has put one red block onto the book while policy A has not put any red block onto the book.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
