(E'5593a820-cc35-4aa7-acb6-49152ea75d19', E'2025-08-29T05:40:00.241028Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smallest box into the bowl', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, grasped it, moved it toward the bowl, pushed the bowl away.Then policy A moved the box away from the bowl and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, grasped it, moved it away from the bowl.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to put the box into the bowl, but policy A at least has moved the box toward the bowl.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'72e1b495-0021-47e4-8928-29206ff038f2', E'2025-08-29T05:51:42.104530Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smallest box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, pushed it to make it rotate about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close the bowl, then moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box,grasped it and rotated it slightly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the task correctly while policy B has not rotated it by the required angle.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'1c9f3cf1-9334-4a02-a798-efb468717126', E'2025-08-29T06:02:57.298497Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the white box, then move it close to the bowl', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to white box, pushed it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the pencil box and grasped it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to white box, then moved the robotic arm to pencil box and attempted to grasp it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e06120a3-2675-4124-936c-86244c5fe3ea', E'2025-08-29T06:14:25.864938Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smallest box, then put it onto the biggest box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the biggest box, pushed it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm back and forth randomly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least identified the smallest box.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'6fd539fe-fb35-408a-8fc4-4fc174b22705', E'2025-08-29T06:27:20.794691Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bigger box from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box, then stopped on top of the bigger box during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, pushed it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to the table until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least identified the bigger box.Therefore, i choose A'),
(E'5d2ccff0-f1f1-4e94-a96d-2e3cddf8b3bb', E'2025-08-29T06:37:20.087634Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it into the bowl', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the paper, grasped it, moved it and dropped.Policy B first moved the robotic to the smaller box, adjusted posture, pushed the smaller box to make it rotate by about 90 degrees.Then attempted to grasp the smaller box until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least rotated the smaller box while policy A did nothing relevant.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'e48cbcaf-6cfe-419c-a493-9858e0e7ab8d', E'2025-08-29T06:58:42.808585Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the tableware  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to plate, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the cup and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved arm close to the plate, pulled it to right.Then policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,both polices have move one tableware to right, but then policy A attempted to move another tableware while policy B did nothing relevant.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'0d3d36f3-f8fd-4440-95e3-cb21dba732ec', E'2025-08-30T02:57:49.590030Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread inside of the pot without touching the paper.', E'For context, there was a piece of paper covering part of the pot. policy A had approached the bread and struggled to grasp it and pick it up for most of the episode, only being able to actually lift it to the opening by the end of the episode. policy A was not able to drop the bread inside the pot. policy B had been able to do eveything perfectly up until it came to placing the bread inside of the pot. For some reason, policy B placed the bread directly onto the paper, not clipped or scraped the paper as it aimed for the gap, but directly on the edge of the paper. As a result, even though policy A had placed the bread into the pot very quickly, it did not recieve full credit since it touched the paper.'),
(E'c7fd747c-8231-4448-a071-2eeced32a98b', E'2025-08-30T03:05:40.912172Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread into the pot without touching the paper.', E'For context, there was a pot with a piece of paper over it and a bun to the left of the pot. Both policies had performed the task very well, picking up the bread and placing it into the pot with no or minimal touching of the paper. Some differences were that policy A had to take 2 attempts before being able to grab the bread while policy B did it on it''s first try and that policy A touched the paper less than policy B. I had actually chosen policy A over policy B because it barley touched the paper while placing the bread inside the pot while policy B had clipped the paper a bit more. Otherwise, both policies did a very good job.'),
(E'85b367b1-d16c-409d-be3e-7033907c5477', E'2025-08-30T03:13:12.166074Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread inside of the pot without touching the paper.', E'For context, there was a pot with a piece of paper on it leaving a gap to put the bread inside, there was a cup to the left of the pot and bread to the right of the pot. Both policies were able to place the bread inside of the pot without needing to make any second attempts at grabbing the bread. policy A had done everything perfectly except it had placed the bread on the paper, causing the paper to fall into the pot. policy B had somehow managed to start the episode by grabbing the bread in such a way that the long side of the bread was parallel with the grippers. This unexpectedly became useful later in the episode as policy B places the bread on the paper but only the edge of the bread. policy B then began moving the bread towards the gap and almost slotted the bread into the gap, resulting in the paper mostly being left untouched. I chose policy B because it was able to place the bread in such a way that did not result in the paper falling into the pot.'),
(E'29e5867c-ac5f-48b5-a8c6-9261fefae2f7', E'2025-08-30T03:23:59.908427Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread inside of the pot without touching the paper.', E'For context, there was a pot, piece of paper on the pot in such a way that there was space to place the bread, bread and a cup. Both policies were able to grab tbe bread and approach the pot without much issue. It is when the policies reach the pot that they differ significantly. policy B was able to do the task flawlessly. policy A when it reached the pot, decided to put the bread on the opposite edge of the gap left by the paper and actually pushed the paper off of the pot along with the bread. policy B then tried to grab at the bread unsuccessfully before moving to the right of the pot, in front of the cup where it spent the rest of the episode.'),
(E'd87f9bb4-3c23-41f0-aa38-f310f1803691', E'2025-08-30T03:32:16.958480Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread inside of the pot.', E'For context, there was a pot with a piece of paper completely covering the whole, a sponge to the left of the pot and the bread on the right side of the pot. I wanted to see if the robot could rationalize that it would need to remove the paper before placing the bread inside of the pot. Both policies began by grabbing the bread and lifting it upwards to about the height of the pot. policy A, upon seeing that there was paper over the pot, dropped the bread before picking it up again, dropping in such a way that it rolled off of the table. policy B had simply kept lifting the bread until it was over the table and just dropped the bread!! I want to mention that dropping something off of the table is not something I have been able to get the robot to do when I explicitly ask for it!! Since policy A at least approached the objective and didn''t drop the bread off the edge on purpose, I gave it the victory.'),
(E'd949ad16-6168-404a-b081-374272e41be0', E'2025-08-30T03:51:04.696983Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Put the bread inside of the pot.', E'For context there was a pot with a piece of paper on it with bread on the left side of the pot and a sponge on the right side of the pot. Both policies grabbed the bread, approached the pot and then paced above and around the pot for the rest of the episode. Policy B might have paced further away from the pot sometimes when compared to policy A, but otherwise both policies acted pretty similar. Because of their similarity, I gave them a tie.'),
(E'712b6796-8b97-4a21-9d98-432c278e9987', E'2025-08-30T17:30:25.117928Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do nothing.', E'To put it simply I evaluated the policies with respect to how much they moved. Policy A moved sporadically in many different directions and orientations throughout the entire episode. policy B had moved to a spot in the upper right of the field near the surface and kind of just stayed there until the episode ended. Since policy B moved less than policy A, I chose policy B.'),
(E'530c3552-abf1-49d8-88db-61bfb992af52', E'2025-08-30T17:37:28.911132Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not move.', E'policy A had almost immediatley fully extended and then stayed in that position for the rest of the episode. policy B had moved slightly from it''s starting position before slowing down to almost a crawl, very slowly drifting downwards and forwards for the rest of the episode. I chose policy B because the amount that it had moved was less than the amount that policy A had moved.'),
(E'4f50e8bb-b736-4e28-b99b-9d967c078008', E'2025-08-30T17:44:06.674149Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cause the cup to go onto the plate without touching the cup. If you touch the sponge, I will move the cup onto the plate for you.', E'Neither policy touched the sponge. Both policies approached the cup but did so in a hesitant way, or in a way that would appear hesitant. policy A had actually retracted it arm to a position between the cup and the sponge and for a moment drifted towards the sponge, but before it could get too far, policy A approached the cup again and then just barley touched it right at the end of the episode. Policy B immediatley went for the cup and ended up pushing it forward for most of the episode, even grabbing at it and wrapping it''s gripper around the cup at the end.'),
(E'b7399902-ef83-4119-859f-38efa5b9f129', E'2025-08-30T18:00:27.854634Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cause the cup to go onto the plate without touching the cup. If you touch the sponge, I will place the cup onto the plate for you.', E'Both policies immediatley went to the cup and grabbed it. policy A spent the whole episode either approaching the cup or grabbing/attempting to grab the cup. Policy B did all of that much quicker, grabbed the cup harder and then lifted it higher. After doing that, policy B spent the rest of the episdoe wandering the left side of the field, somewhat in the direction of the sponge.'),
(E'3299f2c8-d8aa-409e-9b40-979558b3ab12', E'2025-08-30T18:15:06.620716Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Move the cup onto the plate by touching the sponge. If you touch the sponge, I will move the cup to the plate for you.', E'Neither policy approached the sponge and had directly approached the cup instead. I want to say both policies attempted to grab the cup, but only policy A actually succeeded in that endeavor. Policy B pushed the cup towards itself until it knocked the cup over and then spent the rest of the episode wandering the field, eventually extending it''s gripper fully off of the table. Because both policies attampted to grab the cup and neither approached the sponge, I give the policies a tie.'),
(E'52010a97-84a5-4c9d-b3d5-0a4209cab365', E'2025-08-30T18:25:30.835462Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Lift the blue cup and the white cube underneath the blue cup.', E'Policy A had spent the entire time, approaching and grabbing the cup. policy A had successfully lifted the cup off of the white block, but it never made any attempts at picking it up. policy B had not even managed to grab the cup, instead inching closer to it for the entire episode.'),
(E'c94e8519-e9ba-43a6-8a97-2d2925cda12e', E'2025-08-30T18:39:37.161348Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Lift the blue cup and the white cube underneath the blue cup.', E'Both policies were unable to grab the cup but struggled to pick it up in different ways. policy A had gotten low and close to the cup and would grab at the edge of the cup, kind of squeezing it away but never actually grabbing it. policy B had gone higher and tried to drop down on the cup to grab it but was never close enough to do so.'),
(E'12b3b3fa-b5c6-419f-9436-b2567fd88217', E'2025-08-30T18:46:08.865914Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the sponge and pick up the bread.', E'For context, the policies had to touch the sponge first to reveal the bread that would be placed down by me. policy A was able to barely touch the sponge, but never attempted to grab the bread. policy B had kind of stayed in the same general area that it started and didn''t touch anything on the field.'),
(E'050cb1db-a515-437b-8c4a-66d466f27d60', E'2025-08-30T18:53:56.637923Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the sponge and pick up the bread.', E'For context, after touching the bread, I would place the bread down to the right of the sponge. Only policy A was able to touch the bread, policy B didn''t move much or touch aything at all, although it did approach the sponge. policy A was also beginning to move towards the bread near the end of the episode. In conclusion, I chose policy A because it had actually touched the sponge.'),
(E'7cf85d7d-2763-4a22-89ed-8400cddf63a4', E'2025-08-30T19:01:41.206019Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Drop the bread off of the table.', E'Policy A had approached the bread, placed its gripper right up against the bread, but didn''t grab the bread. policy B spent the entire episode picking up and dropping the bread, but never moving anywhere with the bread. I chose policy B because it was able to actually grab the bread and lift it while policy A could not even do that.'),
(E'19d8c605-49dc-4901-98d4-ed6bca6bcef9', E'2025-09-01T01:13:55.492438Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pliers, then grasp the white computer mouse', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the screwdriver instead of the pliers, grasped it, moved it close to the pliers, then dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the black mouse, then moved the robotic arm to the screw driver, grasped it and placed it close to the pliers.Comparing the performance of the two, both policies have grasped the screwdriver instead of the pliers, and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'6571a875-88ca-4278-a37a-9288ada5a30f', E'2025-09-01T01:26:18.246322Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mobile phone from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, put the gripper on it and moved slightly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile, pause briefly, then moved the robotic arm away.Next,policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Comparing  the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task. Both policies have identified the mobile phone, but only policy A attempted to move the mobile phone while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'e2e5b99f-f11b-44e9-b6aa-9a477394ae33', E'2025-09-01T01:40:18.438943Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the electronics products together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pliers which is not electronics product, then pushed it until time ran out.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm to the pliers, then policy B grasped a controller and dropped it. Next, policy B grasped the pliers and moved it close to the white computer mouse.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped one electronic product while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'50f76b50-52cf-440d-a315-3fd60821e93e', E'2025-09-01T01:53:04.465929Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put one mouse onto the pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the screwdriver rather than mouse, grasped it, then moved it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the black mouse, after hesitating for while, grasped it, moved it close to the pliers, then dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is clearly better than policy A.'),
(E'd246380e-19ea-4bf0-937e-10a6727c5fb3', E'2025-09-01T02:03:33.853070Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the computer mouse by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, grasp it, rotated it by about 70 degrees, then dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, grasped it and released it multiple times, but didn''t rotated it in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has performed the operations according to my command although the rotation angle did not reach 90 degrees, while policy B has not rotated the mouse at all.Therefore policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'9b83f39d-ea16-4efe-ab97-83165afc3c3d', E'2025-09-01T02:44:42.530491Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Move your hand in a circle around the cup.', E'Neither policy was able to go around the circle and both policies decided to go directly for the cup and grab it. One difference was that policy A had spent the entire episode with it''s gipper grabbing/inside the cup while policy B had retracted it''s arm a couple times and had grabbed the cup much less. That being said, since the max progress achieved by the policies were the same, I would call this a tie.'),
(E'1841b95b-91bf-4a04-87c8-f1c150ba3beb', E'2025-09-01T02:52:51.641836Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Do not grab the cup, but grab the bread.', E'I tied these policies because they both went for the cup and ignored the bread, achieving the same max result. Some differences were that policy A had been much more hesitant, still grabbing the cup, but later retracting it''s gripper from the cup and remaining above it for the rest of the episode. policy B had grabbed and then lifted the cup repeatedly throughout the episode.'),
(E'e1600abd-61ed-4b5b-8b86-e44e929de8d7', E'2025-09-01T02:54:24.209549Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the screwdriver and move it close to the mobile phone', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to screwdriver,  then sopped above the screwdriver in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse rather than the screwdriver, then grasped it and released it .Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least identified the screwdriver while policy B did not.There policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'736963ac-44fd-4773-b121-1f95fe6a82b2', E'2025-09-01T02:59:55.203483Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the small bread and the cup.', E'I chose policy B because while grabbing the bread, policy B was also able to approach the cup. policy A had immediatley approached the correct bread and picked it up. Policy A would then spend the rest of the episode grabbing and pushing the bread. Policy B started by approaching the small bread and then quickly rushing past it and grabbing it barley before dropping it. policy B then pushed the mini bread closer to the cup and eventually grabbed the bread. After grabbing the bread, policy B began approaching the cup with the bread in hand when the episode ended.'),
(E'eb735632-c6ec-408a-9278-b67cfca099ef', E'2025-09-01T03:08:39.027866Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the small bread and grab the cup.', E'I placed a big loaf of bread and a small loaf of bread near the center of the field and then a cup in the upper center area of the field. policy A had gone for the big bread for at least half of the episode before even beginning to approach the small bread, and it was never actually able to grab and lift the small bread, only get it''s gripper around it by the time the episode ended. policy B had immediatley gone for the small bread and then managed to pick it up on the second attempt. policy B would then spend the rest of the time grabbing and picking up the small bread.'),
(E'6a95869d-5d38-4b61-b75a-a6498ec1f9f2', E'2025-09-01T03:09:42.581034Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the black mouse and put it onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the white mouse rather then the black mouse, grasped it and put it beside the paper.Then policy A pushed the white mouse slightly in the remaining time of the episode.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm close the white mouse, after hesitating for a while, grasped, moved the white mouse close to the black mouse.Comparing the performance of the two, although both policies grasped the wrong object, policy A at least moved it in the right direction which is toward the paper while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'c49f3a0c-c652-4ebb-a109-6679c876e1b9', E'2025-09-01T03:18:28.347454Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the smaller bread and grab the cup.', E'For context there was a long piece of bread and a small piece of bread near the bottom center of the field while a cup was near the upper center of the field. Policy A had approached the long bread slowly for the entire episode but never grabbed the bread. policy B started by approaching the big bread before pivoting to the small bread. While at the small bread it spent a very long time with the gripper resting over the bread but not grabbing it. Eventually, policy B did grab the small bread and even managed to lift it before the end of the episode.'),
(E'1886063f-ca22-411c-9988-c1dda4cd7810', E'2025-09-01T03:28:33.023007Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the controller from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the controller, grasped it,rotated it while moved it to right slightly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the controller, pushed it to make it rotated, then grasped it and moved it right.According to my command, the robotic arm should first move the controller to right, then rotate it.But both policies has rotated the controller before moving it to right.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B moved the controller to right more obviously than policy A did.Therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'31102074-214e-43c3-944e-bda1e8128a4b', E'2025-09-01T03:36:37.076043Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the blue object.', E'Unfortunatley I made the task too easy, so both policies were able to complete the task without any major error. The major difference between the two policies were that policy A was much slower and more reserved- slowly approaching the cup before dropping it. policy B had rushed to the cup and then grabbed it, carrying it around the field.'),
(E'41c959da-0f5a-47e0-b24e-0feff67fd425', E'2025-09-01T03:42:35.356257Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Drop the cup near the smaller bread.', E'I placed a blue cup in front of a large loaf and a small loaf. policy A approached the cup, grab the cup and then immediatley dropped it. policy A did that the entire episode. policy B had approached the smaller bread instead. policy B placed it''s gripper over the bread, grabbed it, let go and then began pushing it into the table for the rest of the episode. I chose policy A because it had approached the cup which was the correct object to start with.'),
(E'9de65caf-7ed8-447b-889b-1b204098955f', E'2025-09-01T03:44:41.928384Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees, then put it onto the box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the controller, grasped it, rotated it, but did not put it onto the box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, adjusted posture, grasped and release the controller several time to make it rotate slightly.Both policy have only rotated the controller but have not put it onto the box according to my command.Comparing their performance, policy A rotated the controller more obviously than policy B did.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'56021e73-b8a4-42cf-b6c9-a3560f2be1d9', E'2025-09-01T04:07:49.213983Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the tools into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the plate, pushed it to left, then stopped above the plate during the remaining time of  episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the drawer, pushed it, then policy B moved the robotic arm to the plate and pushed it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies only pushed the plate but didn''t put any tools in it.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'cddfb67c-f579-4e9a-a1e7-351bf5ae8102', E'2025-09-01T05:07:10.389762Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the PCB, then moved slightly around the PCB during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm close to the PCB, pushed it, then almost stopped during the remaining time.It seems that both policies can''t find the book,and they all approached the wrong object PCB. As the performance of the two policies is similar, i choose tie.'),
(E'3ad38369-aef3-4b69-ae4c-e7820b44d62d', E'2025-09-01T05:38:31.741017Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the smaller PCB from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm back and forth as if finding the target, then policy A moved the robotic arm to a cube and attempted to grasp until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller PCB, attempted to grasp it but failed, only squeezed it and made it slip away backward.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least found the required object and attempted to moved it while policy A did nothing relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy'),
(E'3ed08336-5f2f-46d2-887b-3852bd15c8ee', E'2025-09-01T06:51:50.264853Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the PCB together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the bigger PCB, then almost stopped above the bigger PCB during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller PCB , then moved slightly around it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, and both polices only moved the robotic arm close to one PCB without taking further actions.As their performance is similar, i choose tie.'),
(E'45d5ca7f-d403-42fe-9ceb-3afd06efb9c8', E'2025-09-01T07:06:53.958664Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller PCB onto the  paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger PCB rather than the smaller one, grasped the bigger PCB, moved it, then put it under the paper. Policy B first moved the robotic arm above the smaller PCB, but then moved away .Next, policy B moved the robotic arm close to the bigger PCB, attempted to grasp but failed in the end.Both policies have not identified the smaller PCB and attempted to grasp the bigger PCB.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped one PCB and moved it toward the paper while policy B did not.Therefore policy A is slightly than policy B.'),
(E'4d74d62a-0249-4866-95db-2c4e55ad6b80', E'2025-09-01T07:19:20.051785Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smaller PCB by 90 degrees', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger PCB, then moved around the bigger PCB for a while.Next, policy B approached the bigger PCB and attempted to grasp it in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped one wrong PCB while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'482b540d-4b44-4b04-b312-d13146add3d5', E'2025-09-01T07:32:29.904505Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller PCB, then move it next to the book', E'Policy A attempted to search the target in the most time of the episode, and grasped the bigger PCB in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, then also approached bigger PCB, grasped and release it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies have only grasped the bigger PCB rather than the smaller one, and didn''t move it to the book according to my command.As their performance is similar, i choose tie.'),
(E'9c4442dd-b968-47eb-8c0c-026fe92e206a', E'2025-09-01T07:49:53.722982Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller PCB and put it onto the bigger PCB', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller PCB, then moved the robotic arm around it slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller PCB, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'a26850bc-6648-406a-ab4b-9f82acc5f25f', E'2025-09-01T07:58:05.260559Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bigger PCB from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm back and forth slightly without taking any actions during the entire trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger PCB, then moved around it slowly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, Policy B at least identified the bigger PCB and approached it while policy A didn''t perform any relevant operations.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'18adf3a8-5dea-4966-927c-559bbf4f402c', E'2025-09-01T08:10:57.890756Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the bigger PCB by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book rather than the bigger PCB, attempted to grasp the book, then moved the robotic arm away.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to bigger PCB, after hesitating for a while, moved the robotic arm close to the smaller PCB, then moved slightly around the smaller PCB until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least identified PCB and moved around them while policy A did not.Therefore,i choose B'),
(E'50faa897-be56-47fd-9ef3-e8f7b2bf55c4', E'2025-09-01T08:21:45.360687Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the PCB from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to bigger PCB, pushed it forward.Then pushed the smaller PCB slightly.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger PCB and pushed it forward.Then policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A has moved two PCB while policy B moved only one.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'c9bd5c80-3d1f-408d-83c4-30112ae5a210', E'2025-09-01T08:36:42.340292Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread, then grasp the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, pushed it forward, grasped its corner and released.Then policy A move the robotic arm close to a wooden block until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, pushed it,then moved around it during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy A at least grasped the bread while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'9e1a72b1-4961-4bd3-a17d-bf7d7159729d', E'2025-09-01T08:47:13.754498Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to bread, after hesitating for a while, attempted to grasp it, causing it to move to right slightly.Policy B first moved to the red block rather than the bread, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the bread slightly while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'11004fa2-03e6-422a-afcd-84da7660b99b', E'2025-09-01T08:58:09.419314Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow block which is not food, pushed the yellow block for a while, then stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread, then moved slightly above the bread until time ran out.Neither policy was not able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the banana which is food and intend to move it while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'1fac75f6-8396-4c3a-a5fa-3845c46b6275', E'2025-09-01T09:08:38.425477Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bread onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow block, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm around  the yellow block during  the most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bread, pushed it forward, pause briefly, then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least found the bread and attempted to grasp it while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'123b3881-9ba2-4e96-8a89-ac5acd7049b6', E'2025-09-01T09:18:32.555747Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bread by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, then pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, pushed it forward, then moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task correctly while policy B failed.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'b2b338c6-63ee-4c57-8fad-8ea04b12a44a', E'2025-09-01T09:27:12.633372Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bread and move it close to the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, then moved away.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm close to the bread, stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic close to the bread and moved away quickly, then policy B moved the robotic arm to a wooden block, grasped and released it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least identified the bread and intended to move it while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'ec48e59b-dea7-47fd-a97d-37f8930948b7', E'2025-09-01T09:38:33.408838Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block and put it onto the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, moved the gripper slightly around it for while, then moved away.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm to push the cloth during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bread as if intended to grasped it, then moved robotic arm around the bread during most remaining time of trial.Comparing the performance of the two, both policy failed, but it seemed that policy A found the red block while policy B did not.Therefore ,policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'2f4b3d6c-ea6e-4c74-bba8-972cd5180c6e', E'2025-09-01T09:51:52.858776Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bread from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, grasped it, then moved it to right while rotate it by about 90 degrees, dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, pushed it forward,after hesitating for while,  pushed the bread again until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'5f7a3256-09a3-42c9-aa8c-bf9cdd580c5d', E'2025-09-01T10:00:42.772204Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the bread by 90 degrees, then put it onto the box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bread, grasped it , moved it toward the box slightly, rotated it by about 60 degrees, then dropped it on table.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm around the bread during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the box, pushed it, then policy B moved the robotic arm close to the bread. Next, policy B moved robotic arm slowly around the bread  until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A almost complete the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'7ec9d5e9-948b-4ce5-81cf-381161b16c46', E'2025-09-01T10:22:14.750899Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to bread, pushed it forward for a while, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, push it to left, then stopped during the most remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy at least identified one typed of food and moved it while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'671147b8-1988-41b0-8c46-f9dc91f8f931', E'2025-09-01T14:38:42.776180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Spray the plant.', E'policy A had attempted to grab the bottle by the back of the bottle and ended up knockin the bottle over. From that point onward, policy A would attempt to grab the bottle, barley lift it, and then immediatley drop it- repeating those steps for the remainder of the episode. policy B had also tried to grab the bottle by the back part of the spray bottle head, but unlike policy A, policy B was not able to knock the bottle over. policy B then attempted to grab the bottle from the top but had froze for some reason above the bottle- not moving an inch for the rest of the episode. I chose policy A over policy B because policy A was able to grab the spray bottle while policy B could not.'),
(E'1bd22753-ad40-44d8-b84d-6ef6fd9f608f', E'2025-09-01T14:58:53.243423Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Spray the plant.', E'policy A had approached the bottle and tried grabbing it from the top, but approached the bottle from the wrong angle so when it moved it''s gripper down over the bottle, it had instead pushed it away. As a result both the bottle and gripper were oriented horizontally. policy A then spent the rest of the episode almost rubbing the bottle up and down seemingly trying to get above the bottle to grab it but never being able to due to the orientation. policy B had changed the orientation of it''s gripper, grabbed the bottle and even approached the plant a little before dropping it near the plant. policy B ended the episode grabbing the bottle near the plant. It is worth mentioning that the angle of the bottle almost seems like it could spray the plant, but I don''t really count it since it isn''t fully picking the bottle off the ground. I chose policy B because it was able to change it''s orientation(something policies find pretty difficult at times) and grab/move the bottle towards the plant.'),
(E'f86b46d3-d3b0-43e5-b35a-c92cc40074db', E'2025-09-01T15:14:05.866401Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Draw on the whiteboard.', E'policy A was able to take the marker and push it against the white board(but not enough to stain the board). policy A didn''t really rotate it''s gripper, instead rotating the marker with it''s whole arm and approaching the white board with the pointy side pointed in the air. Policy B had rotated it''s gripper and grabbed the marker better than policy A but, for some reason, policy B would drop the marker right after lifting it in the air.'),
(E'5a5d2254-221e-4a45-837b-a191f2b16934', E'2025-09-01T15:22:12.875536Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Draw on the whiteboard.', E'Policy A had grabbed at the marker with some difficulty rotating its gripper. When it did grab the marker it lifted it slightly before immediatley dropping it. After dropping the marker, policy A would make its way to the whiteboard and begin pushing against the whiteboard with it''s gripper until the end of the episode. policy B had an easier time rotating it''s gripper and even oriented the pointy end of the marker towards the whiteboard by grabbing the marker and lifting it. That being said, policy B was pretty slow so it was only able to attempt a grab at the marker one more time before the episode ended. I chose policy B because it was able to correctly orient the marker towards the whiteboard and hold the marker longer as in to approach the whiteboard as well.'),
(E'709164c8-ad01-446d-94e1-1b911167e735', E'2025-09-01T15:32:57.477774Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the blue cup over the white cube.', E'policy A had continuously picked up and dropped the blue cup for the entire episode. policy B had approached the blue cup, grabbed at it, and then for some reason started to extend it''s arm with the gripper pointed towards the blue cup for almost the entire rest of the episode. I chose policy A because it was able to fully grab the blue cup while policy B was not.'),
(E'e55a6d6a-2941-48a9-9b70-2de3cab0b242', E'2025-09-01T15:40:07.244863Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the blue cup over the white cube.', E'policy A had inched towards the cup but never actually got close enough to touch the blue cup. policy B had been able to approach the cup and had grabbed at it, but never fully got its hand around the cup enough to actually grab and lift it up. I chose policy B because it was actually able to touch the blue cup while policy A could not.'),
(E'd6d88a23-c30e-416c-aa61-fe01ff942349', E'2025-09-02T01:15:00.228490Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the  orange, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the orange, then made multiple attempts to grasp it but failed and made the orange fall off from the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the orange, pushed it, then stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least made multiple attempts to grasp the orange while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'b792bcd7-ea34-434f-9487-06e64d871458', E'2025-09-02T03:10:20.542382Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it to left,then move the robotic arm slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped onto the table.Then policy B moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least moved a banana to right and identified the marker pen in the end while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'80965425-c19e-4cd7-a95c-d2d5301ee9ca', E'2025-09-02T03:23:22.686689Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it and placed it onto the paper.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the orange, made multiple attempts to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it and placed it on the paper.Then policy B attempted to grasp a pencil which is not fruit.Comparing the performance of the two,both policies have moved the banana onto the paper, but then policy A attempted to grasp another fruit while policy B tried to grasp a pencil rather than fruit.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'bfcbe3b3-ebfc-4003-8d14-db8eab2bf7d5', E'2025-09-02T03:34:56.801659Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the cube onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, grasped it and released it several times,then almost stopped beside the cube during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, grasped it, moved it toward the book then dropped it on the table.Next, policy B grasped the marker pen and moved it close to the book.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies have grasped the cube but only policy B intended to moved it toward the book.Therefore,i choose policy B.'),
(E'd391fb9e-a5a3-494b-b4d0-3dde38f35500', E'2025-09-02T03:45:23.683501Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to orange rather than the marker pen, pushed it.Then policy A move the robotic arm to the marker pen, grasped it and rotated it by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the marker pen,grasped it and rotated it by about 90 degrees.Both policies have completed the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B identified the marker pen more quickly than policy A.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'975e5f13-d352-4778-a5c6-a7ab9e622198', E'2025-09-02T03:55:01.337833Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pencil and move it next to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen rather than the pencil, then grasped the marker pen,moved it close to the banana.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the pencil, grasped it, moved it closed to the banana, then dropped on table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'25d018c5-01e4-4a51-99a1-9bc9830ffcf8', E'2025-09-02T04:04:06.538821Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser, then place it onto the paper', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the paper rather than the eraser, pushed the paper, then moved the robotic arm close to the banana in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the eraser, grasped it and released it, then stopped beside the eraser during the remaining time of episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task.when comparing their performance, policy B at least identified the eraser while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'b583ffb7-eb90-4619-b3b5-a32b998c45c7', E'2025-09-02T05:04:10.088022Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from right to left, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the marker pen, grasped it, moved it to left, then rotated it by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, after hesitating for a while, grasped the marker pen then released it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A has completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'c1ac45f8-5563-4c4f-b845-befcf902871e', E'2025-09-02T05:12:54.744291Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, pushed it to move it toward the book, then grasped it and placed it on the book, but didn''t rotate it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only half-done the task.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'b6f6cded-7f7b-4545-8a0b-c830c82e29d1', E'2025-09-02T05:23:45.508776Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all Stationery from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a bottle of water which is not stationery, then attempted to grasp a controller beside the water until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it,moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy B moved the robotic arm close to a banana.Comparing the  performance of the two, policy B has at least moved one stationery to right while policy A has not .Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'c0f5ec41-2c20-4296-a8d9-613ea8ffb4be', E'2025-09-02T05:35:47.281409Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the tape then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to tape, grasped it, moved it then dropped it on the table in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the one box rather than the tape, grasp the box, moved it and dropped it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to the tape, attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore,policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
