(E'7c3b490d-1dc6-47f5-89e9-e51dcacaca06', E'2025-09-02T07:05:20.440570Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, then pushed it slightly but almost did not rotate it.Policy B moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified and pushed the smaller box while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'b86c25a2-82ef-4ec0-bda3-8cd25cfb37ed', E'2025-09-02T07:27:36.256021Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the tableware  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, pushed it to left during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, pushed it to top left.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies have only pushed the plate in wrong direction.Therefore,i choose tie.'),
(E'2bf9a580-23d3-4474-bbb4-0b778d9d9e9f', E'2025-09-02T08:07:28.876068Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the mobile phone, then grasp the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to mobile phone but did not grasp it, then moved the robotic arm close to the red block, grasped and released the red block.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the black mouse, pushed it, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, comparing their performance, policy A at least grasped one required object while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'26e59117-d132-4cdb-965a-89cd02d435e5', E'2025-09-02T08:16:29.634250Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mobile phone from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a yellow block, pushed it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to a black mouse, attempted to grasp it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone,pushed it forward, after hesitating for a while , attempted to grasp the white mouse beside the mobile phone.Neither policy was not able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the mobile phone and pushed it while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4443c309-a58c-44e8-9917-2ea4d3c6d8ce', E'2025-09-02T08:30:10.555758Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the red blocks together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, pushed it toward another red block slightly, then moved the robotic arm close to another red block, attempted to grasp it. Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one red block,pushed it, then attempted to grasp a cube near the red block.Neither policy was not able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified and moved two red blocks while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is clearly better than policy B.'),
(E'27c259d7-a303-487e-87fc-615d16caa7ae', E'2025-09-02T08:45:14.992536Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put one red block onto the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, pushed it forward, then moved the robotic arm close to anther red block, pushed it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, grasped it, moved it close to the cube and placed it on the cube successfully.Then policy B grasped another red block and moved it close to the cube until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B completed the task correctly while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5e63d072-d5bb-4cbe-833b-b65b03148bba', E'2025-09-02T08:54:22.421870Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the mobile phone by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, grasped its top side, rotated it by about 45 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to mobile phone, pushed it, then grasped and released it in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A rotated the mobile phone by about 45 degrees while policy B almost did not rotate it.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'7734f313-c422-418e-b9de-4ff6e81a7905', E'2025-09-02T09:02:44.802649Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the mouse and move it close to the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to red block rather than the mouse, pushed it then moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm around the red block during most time of the episode and touched the red block in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have not found the mouse but only move around the red block.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'dad21eb1-6bb5-4f31-a514-7a4538badc35', E'2025-09-02T09:25:46.428373Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block and put it onto the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to red block, attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, made multiple attempts to grasp it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies took similar actions.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'bafdd42a-d903-4483-a756-0a0943b83ffe', E'2025-09-02T09:36:06.860710Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mobile phone  from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to mobile phone and the mouse,then moved the robotic arm to the cube and pushed it.Next, policy moved the robotic arm to the mouse and pushed it in the end.Policy B moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly during entire time of the trial.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least slightly moved the phone while policy B did nothing relevant.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'2ba16ebc-335c-45d8-8493-f59ede538b95', E'2025-09-02T09:48:44.049268Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the yellow block by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the edge of the table, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow block, grasped it, moved it close to the book, then dropped it on the table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least grasped and moved the yellow block while policy A did nothing relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'26054ee4-8ed2-46b1-9c77-db3a55858f85', E'2025-09-02T09:59:36.936576Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the red blocks on the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow block rather than the red block, then attempted to grasp it during most time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, grasped it, moved it toward the book then dropped it on the table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least moved one red block close to the book while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'ca6d07b4-154e-4caa-91af-16f11ab38685', E'2025-09-03T01:01:21.163102Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the blue cup on the white block.', E'Neither policy had actually managed to touch anything. Both policies kind of stayed in the air without making substantial progress. Policy A might have spent more time closer to the blue cup, but in terms of max progress, both policies had achieved about the same- resulting in a tie.'),
(E'746d1acb-4690-4cb4-9f0b-5b212499b6a2', E'2025-09-03T01:08:15.116266Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the blue cup and place it on the white block.', E'policy A had started by approaching the red cup, grabbed it before moving to the blue cup. When at the blue cup, policy A was able to grab the blue cup and lift it before the episode ended. Policy B becgan by approaching the blue cup, grabbing the cup and even managing to bring the blue cup very close to the white block before dropping it. Unfortunatley, policy B didn''t quite get the blue cup entirly over the white block so the blue cup fell to the ground and policy B spent the rest of the episode trying to pick up the cup. I chose policy B over policy A because it was able to bring the cup all the way to the block while policy A could only manage to grab the blue cup after initially picking up the red cup.'),
(E'56cdcbb3-027f-4111-b497-fe022588e41d', E'2025-09-03T01:19:56.889000Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the red cup and place it over the white cup.', E'Neither policy was able to move to the left enough to fully place its gripper over the red cup and was not able to grab the cup as a result. Both policies pushed up against the red cup, attempted to grab at the red cup, and move the cup a little bit from it''s starting spot but not too much. Since both policies did about the same, they tied.'),
(E'968a2abe-4c4c-4228-92eb-a61e3f0520cc', E'2025-09-03T01:40:27.249430Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the red cup and place it on top of the white block.', E'Policy A had paced between the two cups for the entire episode without touching either. Policy B had immediately approached the cup, readjusted it''s grip until successfully grabbing the cup, and finally approached the white cup with the cup in hand. Even though policy B had approached the white block, for some reason it ended up dropping the red cup near the blue cup instead of the white block. Because policy B was able to actually manipulate the cup, policy B did better than policy A.'),
(E'01652078-e5ce-4cf1-a22a-e3fab9d6c074', E'2025-09-03T01:58:59.501912Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Play the red note with the red marker.', E'For context there was a red marker and a black marker placed in front of a xylophone. policy A had attempted to grab the red marker but never could get left enough and ended up squeezing and pushing the red marker away as a result. policy B had successfully grabbed the marker on the second attempt and then dropped it twice- once on the yellow tile and once on the red tile. I chose policy B because it was actually able to generate a sound from the red tile while policy A could not.'),
(E'4bf7ed6d-eb73-4da4-b91d-15c99790b630', E'2025-09-03T02:43:11.370021Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a pencil, grasped it and released it twice,  then moved the robotic arm close to another pencil until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to a  marker pen, grasped it and released it several times until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped one pencil required while policy B only grasped a wrong object.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'174a6d22-6ce1-4677-932f-c220c3faea8d', E'2025-09-03T02:55:03.446735Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes rather than the marker pen, grasped and released the grapes.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A complete the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'866f686d-b52c-439d-8682-8496cafe23e8', E'2025-09-03T03:02:08.906206Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits together', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes,  pushed it slightly. Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the edge of the table, then moved the arm aimlessly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least pushed the grapes while policy B did nothing relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.')
INSERT INTO sessions (id, occurred_at, site_id, instruction, notes) VALUES
(E'cc23c804-3155-41f4-828a-4b84c82dc4a9', E'2025-09-03T03:14:16.494162Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana on top of drawer', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm close to the grapes rather than the banana, grasped and released it.Then policy A move the robotic arm around the grapes until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the banana, grasped an released it, then moved the robotic arm close to the grapes until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the banana while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'd7d2fa04-e674-4c6a-8140-c386a2120fc7', E'2025-09-03T03:22:25.334311Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, then rotated it by small angle until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, after hesitating for a while, pushed the slightly but did not rotated it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A rotated the marker pen by a small angle while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'fa01e9ba-7670-45e8-a1bd-2f66984b468d', E'2025-09-03T03:36:18.294463Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the marker pen and move it next to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana rather the marker pen, after hesitating for a while, pushed it,then moved the robotic arm back and forth until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least pushed the banana while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'2266d349-a4d1-48a6-bba2-99dbb743691b', E'2025-09-03T03:46:06.706858Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pencil, then place it onto grapes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table,then moved slightly on top of the table during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes, pushed it slightly,then almost stopped.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least pushed the grapes while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose policy B.'),
(E'd3d8d8d9-efcc-4171-817c-a41e7a933fec', E'2025-09-03T04:01:48.844540Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen  from left  to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, moved it to right while rotated it by about 180 degrees, then dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes, then moved the robotic arm slightly during most time of the episode.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'e42ee4cf-3229-4bc4-8e9a-075743333326', E'2025-09-03T05:07:00.945159Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, then put it onto the grapes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, then stopped during the remaining time of episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 180 degrees, then moved it to left.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least rotated the marker pen while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'2c9e9a71-6ca8-4fbf-86aa-b875a6a51c78', E'2025-09-03T05:16:21.576478Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the fruits from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen which is not fruit, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to right,then placed it on table.Next, policy B approached the grapes and attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B has moved one fruit to right while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'958b29fd-2acc-4288-bd54-d79797503a39', E'2025-09-03T05:42:27.520598Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the plate then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, pushed the black cloth, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, after hesitating for a while, grasped and released the plate several times.Comparing their performance, policy B complete the task while policy A failed, therefore policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'4ad42cc0-b70c-4d25-8f23-3e8e17a052db', E'2025-09-03T05:50:35.109632Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the biggest  box from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, pushed it, then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the biggest box, pushed it to left.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the biggest box, pushed it to left slightly, then policy B moved the robotic arm to a cup and knock it down.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies have only approached the biggest box and pushed it to left not right.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e1e3ea31-b9aa-4df2-8df9-589ac012dade', E'2025-09-03T06:00:50.878797Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the boxes together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to smaller box, grasped it, moved it toward the bigger box, but dropped it on table where is a bit far from the bigger box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost complete the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'e6d7e1d0-df9e-4dd8-a7dc-b4776b4f4437', E'2025-09-03T06:10:38.801427Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller white box into the bowl', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table, pushed the cloth,then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, pushed it slightly until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy B at least pushed the smaller box while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'b3f73f2c-0180-4bfa-9528-78556bf7445e', E'2025-09-03T06:20:59.204165Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smaller box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to bigger box, pushed it slightly, then grasped and released the plate.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm the smaller box, pushed it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box, moved the arm slightly above the bigger box until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two, both policies only pushed the smaller box without rotating it.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'64681d3d-bb8d-4a29-a684-28c9b7f5d3b9', E'2025-09-03T06:35:33.598396Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box, then move it next to plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, attempted to grasp it several times but failed.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to the plate, pushed it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, moved it close to the plate and dropped it.But then policy B grasped the box again, and moved it away from the plate.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost complete the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'c5a9e01b-a00d-4116-9a38-1b46825c9950', E'2025-09-03T06:47:55.478131Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box and put it onto the big box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, moved it onto the bigger box then dropped it, but the smaller box slipped off the bigger box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, pushed it forward, then grasped it, moved it close to a plate and dropped it.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost complete the task while policy B moved the smaller box to a wrong target.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'001abedf-36c5-4601-beb5-f2ee4a164edd', E'2025-09-03T07:10:25.613360Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the small box from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the small box, grasped it, moved it to right, then policy A moved the robotic arm close to a plate, pushed it.Next, policy A approached the small box until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the small box to right  while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'4562b51c-8f43-42f6-898c-0e532b5e35f2', E'2025-09-03T07:20:43.110166Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slowly on the surface of the table slowly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, then grasped it while rotated it by about 90 degrees.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B grasped and rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'ee07355b-c766-4f9f-ab00-a0c6b7cb4c52', E'2025-09-03T07:32:06.157048Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the boxes from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box,  attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the small box, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy B almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, both policies have moved one box to right, but then policy A attempted to grasp another box while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'664140c5-30cf-4db1-9991-152ba3f566a8', E'2025-09-03T07:45:54.475722Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then grasp the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, attempted to grasped it but failed.Then policy A approached a red block, grasped and released it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to peach, grasped and release it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped the peach while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'40d7c8eb-4ef3-4012-ac17-d03e2d5bfd54', E'2025-09-03T08:00:04.238437Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the peach  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, attempted to grasp it but only pushed it to left.Then policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, grasped it and release it, then grasped a yellow block and moved it to right.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least grasped the peach while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'ff20dabb-dd0e-4641-8bbc-7b2f80874b41', E'2025-09-03T08:09:45.764452Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to red block, grasped and released it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to another red block until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the blocks, grasped a wooden block, put it onto a red block.Although both policies mistook the wooden blocks for foods, policy B put two blocks together while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'e0ef413f-6e37-4881-ac6d-4dc47a5b3ee7', E'2025-09-03T08:26:45.765220Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the grapes onto the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the green block, grasped it, moved it close to the yellow block and dropped the green block onto the yellow block, but fell off.Policy B first moved the robotic arm back and forth as if searching the object, then policy B grasped the bunch of  grapes, moved  it toward the yellow block.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least found the right object while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'c5e0cc92-4149-4f8c-a405-1a7b827443c5', E'2025-09-03T08:38:25.758512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it and rotated it by about 90 degrees, then dropped it on a yellow block.But then policy moved the robotic arm to the banana, pushed it to make it rotate back to the origin angle.Policy B moved slightly during the entire trial and did not performed any operations.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'40a1635c-deda-4d62-a1ac-7cb8feb3e067', E'2025-09-03T08:53:58.953855Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and move it close to the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, then moved the robotic arm around it during the remaining time as if attempting to grasp it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it toward the red block, then dropped it beside the red block.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task while policy A failed, therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'be221c4a-d090-4215-9a0f-bb7acc686f00', E'2025-09-03T09:04:41.846944Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and put it onto the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to banana, grasped it and released it, after hesitating for a while, grasped the banana again and moved it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table and pushed the cloth, then almost stopped during remaining time of the trial.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped and moved the banana while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'6fd6e8e2-8eba-4472-91fd-d063bcde1638', E'2025-09-03T09:15:02.246704Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the green block  from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to green block, grasped it, moved it to right while rotated it by about 90 degrees.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table, pushed the cloth, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'f1efb71d-659a-415b-9cf7-1626d64dfaf0', E'2025-09-03T09:24:08.970758Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees, then put it onto the red block', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm slightly during the entire trial and did not perform any operations.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block,  then moved the robotic arm back and forth until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the red block while policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'afc13060-e6c8-4b9f-afe2-a3d143ce42ff', E'2025-09-03T09:49:18.404838Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a small box which is not food, grasped it, moved it close to the plate and dropped it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during the remaining time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the silver cloth, attempted to grasp it, then grasped the corner of the cloth in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least grasped one wrong object and moved it close to the plate while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'a2900fb8-6a00-48cf-ac0d-599c4ddc536d', E'2025-09-03T20:18:42.715727Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'add ketchup to the bread', E'Policy A and B both reaches for the ketchup among the two bottles but A outperformed since it led the arm in upright position and tried to squeeze it out of nowhere. The ending position is off the bread by a few centimeters. B just grasped the cap of the ketchup bottle and did nothing else afterwards.'),
(E'8d8526b5-3b43-497a-a146-83f77f3be31f', E'2025-09-03T20:45:41.120747Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the waterbottle from the bin and put it on the cloth', E'A is slightly better than B. Both epsides were seen that the bottle was no longer within the black bin but A has moved it over the left, which is the place stated in the command (cloth). B however moved it to the right and got terminated while the arm seemed to grasp the bin as well'),
(E'090b5170-e232-4ce3-88b5-e9eb7996d453', E'2025-09-03T20:56:04.832869Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'use the scoop to move the orange to the tray', E'Both policies had just grasped the handle of the scoop and gradually shifted the scoop to the left. They did not make any progress scooping the orange which was amongst many object on the left. The scoop was eventually dropped and picked up and remained within the tray for the rest of the two episodes'),
(E'9fe70d36-3727-4de8-9f07-5ff0e6fd8888', E'2025-09-03T21:07:19.796606Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'place the duck next to the brush', E'Both policies has done the very first steps of the task as they both shifted to the tray where the duck was placed onto. However, due to the fact that there were a ton of object within the tray, it was unable to detect which and which the duck was exactly at and thus in A the arm was just hovering around the tray while in B, the arm picked one yellow up which was irrelevant'),
(E'60d5b89e-bd7b-4221-8621-f58231683544', E'2025-09-03T21:19:57.350437Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkely'), E'move the feather duster on the cloth', E'Both policies seemed to not recognize the look of afeather duster as they both reached for the another object (sticker note) left on the tray while the duster was clearly located on the right'),
(E'0c78bf88-655c-42e4-bd5b-6eb37fa3c448', E'2025-09-03T21:29:18.846776Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the donut into cup', E'Policy A was able to grasp the donut but it shifted the arm to the left while the cup was located on the right side of the table. B just disrupted the entire seen as it flipped over the cloth where the donut was placed on and just landed the cloth on the tray'),
(E'cc6117ff-c0ee-4b5f-8608-0a1e6c4988fe', E'2025-09-03T21:42:59.436716Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the bowl using white lid', E'Both A and B has just grasped the lid in place but A ended it significantly towards the bowl while B just kept on picking it and dropping it. A tried to push the bread to make space for the lid but it did not seem to level it upward to match the height of the bowl'),
(E'732fb57f-0eec-4618-bf40-acccc2037bdf', E'2025-09-03T21:59:26.208163Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'pour the water into cup', E'The arm was successfully grasping the cap of the bottle in both episodes but the bottle was not significantly getting closer to the cup. The arm supposed to move the bottle in a upright position above the cup but in A, it just lied horizontally next to the bowl and in B it moved slightly to the left'),
(E'61501b03-fb4f-421a-8e94-41af01f04ce8', E'2025-09-03T22:11:48.238742Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the donut into bowl', E'A just tried to wander around the waterbottle without knowing the donut placing right next to it. It also pushed the cup and having it lying down on the tray. The donut was not even touched in this trial. In B, the arm was making little progress on grasping the donut but it still remained in its initial place; the gripper hereafter grasped the entire tray upwards but was fortunately terminted'),
(E'04feeb28-ddef-4904-b3f6-9cb34c2d1b48', E'2025-09-03T22:26:08.024372Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the toothbrush into cup', E'A initially pointed towards the brush but the gripper was not precisely touching the edge of the brush and thus it was grasping the air, moving over the cup and got ended due to time limit. B on the other hand was able to hold the brush in place but it landed the object on the corner of the tray but not anywhere near the interior of the cup'),
(E'4b31f259-3163-4042-a37f-40298daba791', E'2025-09-03T22:39:31.468842Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the brush to the brown bin', E'A at least reached for the brush initially but then it tried to push off the bin and came back hovering around the brush. B on the other hand just tried to reach and graso the other object (scoop) and kept the arm in touch with this the entire time'),
(E'ab7e65da-445e-450c-97e5-c9aa16c7760f', E'2025-09-03T23:24:11.914663Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the black marker and play the yellow key.', E'Policy A had managed to approach the marker, pick it up, and even bring it to the xylophone. After bringing it to the xylophone, policy A ended up dropping it on the right edge of the xylophone caus(the marker) to fall off the table. After the marker fell off the table, policy A began to start pressing into the xylophone with its hands and inching towards the left of the xylophone. policy B had taken a long time to get to a point where it could grab the black marker and when it was, it ended up grabbing the outside of the marker, pushing it just out of the way. Instead of adjusting it''s posititon to grab the marker, policy B just opened and closed its gripper where the marker was for the rest of the episode. Since policy A was able to bring the marker all the way to the xylophone, and policy B was not, I placed policy A above policy B.'),
(E'37780edc-25d7-4347-92d9-ca1273bc5986', E'2025-09-03T23:36:19.308308Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the black marker and play the yellow tile.', E'Policy A had spent the entire episode picking up and grabbing the red marker instead of the black marker. policy B had grabbed the black marker and dropped it on the blue tile in one, mostly continuous, motion. After dropping the black marker, policy B had opted to grab the red marker, which it was able to do right at the very end of the episode. I chose policy A because it had grabbed the correct marker and dropped it on the xylophone while policy A chose the wrong marker and never brought it to the xylophone.'),
(E'0195696d-1ae1-460a-9505-11ff3736f29d', E'2025-09-03T23:52:36.691912Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Give me the sprite.', E'Both policies were able to grab the Sprite. policy A had first approached the coke can tried and failed to grab it, and then pivoted to the sprite can. policy A would then grab and drop the sprite can for the rest of the episode. policy B had started by approaching the sprite can, but retreating before it could grab it. It would then drift around above the air before approaching the sprite again where it then would grab the sprite at the very end of the episode- but not lift it. I chose policy A because it was able to lift the sprite while policy B could only grab it.'),
(E'63cb7ce0-3567-43d7-b9b1-1b2dc28f508b', E'2025-09-04T00:02:40.856115Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the sprite and give it to me.', E'policy A had approached the sprite, grabbed it with some adjustments, and then droppped it almost immediatley. After dropping it, policy A did not go back to the sprite, but instead had gone back to the reset position, stayed there for a second, and then actually began to approach the coke can- even managing to wrap its gripper around the can by the end of the episode. policy B had managed to go to the sprite can, grabbed it after an attempt or two, and then actually began approaching me with the sprite in its gripper. Policy B would drop the sprite before it reached my hand and for some reason began to move its gripper off the table for some reason. I chose policy B because it was able to begin moving the sprite in my direction while policy A had only managed to grab the sprite.'),
(E'71a03087-3b27-445f-afe7-c2f5137716c3', E'2025-09-04T00:16:00.250968Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Bring me the coke can.', E'policy A had attempted to grab everything except for the coke can. First it tried grabbing the red cup, then it tried grabbing the sprite can, and then sort of bounced back and forth between those for almost the entire episode. At the very end, policy A had quickly moved to the reset position which was kind of near the coke can, but I can not tell if that was an attempt to grab it at the last second or not. policy B had basically grabbed the sprite can in a very deep grasp(the base of the hand touched the top of the can) and then let go without lifting the coke can. policy B proceeded to do this for the entire episode.'),
(E'912845f8-a2e4-40ab-ba02-e582c37e69af', E'2025-09-04T01:21:04.640313Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'Close the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table, then moved slightly on the table during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then also moved slightly above the table during most time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task,and their behaviors is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'c4e9ed05-c58c-4374-83c1-3cd3af6fed6c', E'2025-09-04T01:34:12.187698Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the red button of the remote controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a marker pen, grasped it ,moved it and dropped it on table.Then policy A approach the remote controller, hovered above it, touched it, as if attempted to press the button until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pressed one white button, then grasped the controller and released it.Next,policy B grasped a mouse and dropped it.Neither policy was able to press the red button, but policy B at least press a white button while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'1aa06028-bbd5-4c74-bd6f-9cba034e24c7', E'2025-09-04T01:59:33.108715Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the pencils together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one pencil, grasped it and dropped it several times.Then policy A approached another pencil, attempted to grasp it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to one pencil, pushed it away, then moved slightly on the table during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy A at least moved the two pencils while policy B only pushed one pencil.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'e211154f-a306-4242-b59d-981f46ad4990', E'2025-09-04T02:13:46.000590Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the tape on top of the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the tape, pushed it slightly.Then policy A approached the mouse, attempted to grasp it.Next,policy A moved the robotic arm close to the tape again in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the tape, pushed it close to the drawer, attempted to grasped but failed in the end.Neither policy was not able to complete the task, but policy B at least pushed the tape to the drawer while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'd2b30185-f546-4707-9868-055b5384e598', E'2025-09-04T02:24:58.365285Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table, then moved slightly on the table until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pushed it to make it rotate by about 45 degrees.Then policy moved the robotic arm close to the drawer in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'9ed3ea7f-f5d6-40f2-86f7-a7e28f03721c', E'2025-09-04T03:26:38.836305Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the controller and move it next to the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table,then  moved slightly on the table during the most time of the episode, finally, policy A moved the robotic arm close to the controller.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm back and forth.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing their performance, policy B identified the controller faster than policy A.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'15a8b4c9-8ad9-4e10-b451-75bea27b7864', E'2025-09-04T03:38:01.958296Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the tape then place it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the tape, grasped it, then moved it to the book and placed it on the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the most time of the trial, then approached the tape and pushed it in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'0bc3725f-4e33-4512-9fa1-7d639bd83eba', E'2025-09-04T10:07:24.597105Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the controller from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to controller, pushed it to left, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least pushed the controller.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'a729d869-6f1c-42b8-a2c7-938aafddbb96', E'2025-09-04T10:15:19.875439Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped it,rotated it by  about 160 degrees, then dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped it and released it, then policy B moved the robotic arm randomly during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least rotated the controller while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'34ca8a98-419e-407a-a8a9-52844f00bc7b', E'2025-09-04T11:57:17.730889Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all Stationery from right to left', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved slightly on the table until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm aimlessly during most time of the episode, then moved the robotic arm close to the pencil, attempted to grasp it in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the pencil whiled policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'a6a51c82-fb47-448d-9ae3-dd5416bde81b', E'2025-09-05T00:59:27.543191Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Bring me the coke.', E'policy A had spent the episode positioning it''s hand around the can, grabbing it, and letting go before it could really lift the can too high. polilcy B had spent the episode pushing down on the can with its gripper and trying to grab the can, but not being in a good position to grab the can, because it would push itself away from the can. I chose policy A because it had actually managed to grab the can and it even brought it to me a little.'),
(E'a91a2256-9da8-4f65-bf0b-f89ee313dcea', E'2025-09-05T01:07:45.581513Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the blocks on each other.', E'Both policies had grabbed a singular block, picked it up and dropped it for the duration of the episode. The only reason that I chose policy A was because I belive that it demonstrated that it was better at grasping than policy B. policy A was able to quickly approach the block, pick it up and drop it, and repeat that multiple times. policy B was very slow to the block, had a somewhat difficult time rotating its gripper to properly grab the block, and was only able to pick it up and drop it twice. For those reasons, I say that policy A did better than policy B.'),
(E'1f7d8445-d7c0-4263-8f6d-056598f3a5e1', E'2025-09-05T01:20:44.707729Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the block closest to the bread and drop it on the bread.', E'For context, there were 5 blocks placed around the field and a bun placed right next to a piece of bread on the upper left side. policy A had started by grabbing the block that was closest to it, dropping it somewhere near the bread, grabbing the bread, and then dropping that on the correct block near the end of the episode. policy B had started by moving towards the correct block before recoiling to the starting position, almost as if to observe the field better. policy B then proceeds to also grab a block that was close to it, and place that on the far right corner of the field- a place that is completely away from the block. policy B then finished by grabbing the block that policy A had grabbed and began moving it to the same place that policy A had moved it(near the bread). I chose policy A because it had actually dropped something near the bread, and had actually got the bread to touch the correct block(albiet in the wrong way) while policy B was not able to do that.'),
(E'2d2aa917-af2e-4074-a6fe-8e2a0a538c17', E'2025-09-05T01:29:47.627329Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bottle then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close the bottle, attempted to grasp it but failed, only pushed it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, pushed it away as if attempting to grasp it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies only pushed the bottle.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'43c3a93e-51ed-4218-ba23-597a502eb453', E'2025-09-05T01:41:06.383574Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the blocks on top of each other.', E'Both policies had mangaed to grab the block and approach another block as their maximum progress, but they did it in different ways. policy A had grabbed a block very quickly, but when it started to approach a block, it didn''t stop and instead dropped of the block near the far right side of the field for some reason. policy A would never get any closer to acomplishing the task. policy B had not managed to grab a block until very late in the episode, trying to grab a block on the far right, but not having its gripper in the right place. once policy B did grab the block, it approached another block, but before it could place the block in its gripper, the episode ended.'),
(E'b711ca74-1780-49a8-9342-ad58ee42fcd9', E'2025-09-05T01:50:13.200307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the block closest to the bread and put it into the cup.', E'Neither policy was able to grab the block that was closest to the bread. policy A had actually grabbed the bread, dropped it by the other block, and then proceeded to try and grab said block. While policy A was trying to grab that block, it didn''t rotate its gripper in a proper orientation, so it was never able to fit the block inside of it''s gripper. policy B was very slow. policy B had only been able to grab the bread and then try to grab the block nearest the bread(also in the wrong orientation), before the episode ended. Also, I think it is worth mentioning that their grippers were actually aligned the worst way possible, in the sense that their gripper was parallel with the long side of the block making it impossible to grab the block. Finally, the reason that I chose policy B over policy A was that policy B had actually attempted to grab the correct block.'),
(E'35418fb5-2f24-4275-a9e1-23601f96a163', E'2025-09-05T01:50:51.865228Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the smaller box from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on table.Policy B only moved the robotic arm slightly during entire time of the trial.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'4301c81e-1853-4140-acee-ba4b790e2046', E'2025-09-05T02:00:51.362014Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the block closest to the bread and put it inside of the cup.', E'Policy A had started by going for the wrong block before spending the rest of the episode meandering near the bread and eventually trying to grab it. policy B for some reason decided to make a b-line for the corner of the table, fully extended itself and even moved the right camera. I chose policy A because policy B did not even seem to care about any objective and had acted very erratically.'),
(E'25583e5a-79f7-4271-9327-4f840fcaac13', E'2025-09-05T02:13:36.438419Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller box onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, then moved it close to the bigger box, but did not put it onto the bigger box in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box, pushed it close to the bigger box, then policy B moved the robotic arm to a bottle, pushed it during the remaining time of the trial.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the smaller box and attempted to put it onto the bigger box while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'720b2878-b602-4481-a200-aac661e843f0', E'2025-09-05T02:24:55.673697Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the blue bottle by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bottle, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then placed it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, pushed it slightly, then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm close to the bottle again in the end.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'161ec0a2-38d7-446b-ada3-3fb9e495f38e', E'2025-09-05T03:15:17.784206Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box, then move it next to the blue bottle', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it and released,  then grasped it again, moved it close to the blue bottle and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the smaller box, grasped it moved it to the blue bottle, and dropped it beside the bottle.Both policies have completed the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B moved the box more closer to the bottle than policy A did.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'f45657e4-83bd-496f-af31-6e14d97d8943', E'2025-09-05T03:27:51.687177Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the smaller box, then put it to the right side of the bottle', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bottle, grasped it and dropped it several times, then grasped it again in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bottle, grasped it, rotated it, then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies only grasped the bottle rather than the smaller box.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'2541c562-155e-4f8c-9163-df3a4b5c4a4c', E'2025-09-05T03:37:04.334477Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bottle from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm aimlessly during entire time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the white box, attempted to grasp it, then moved the robotic arm  close to the bottle, pushed it to make it rotated by about 45 degrees.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least rotated the bottle while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'7dfada37-d1a2-4588-937d-270bd9f0cd63', E'2025-09-05T03:46:09.553375Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotated the smaller box by 90 degrees, then put it onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, then pushed it to make it rotate by a small angle.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, rotated it by about 70 degrees, then dropped it on table.Next, policy B stopped during the remaining time.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B rotated the box by about 70 degrees while policy A only rotated it by a very small angle.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'121881cd-51b2-4150-b3e1-de5aba282338', E'2025-09-05T03:56:30.762816Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the drinks  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bottles of drinks, pushed them to left, then moved the robotic arm back and forth until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse rather than the drinks, pushed the mouse, then grasped a box, moved it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the drinks while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'16b2b6d1-a484-49d4-9042-da05b69701c1', E'2025-09-05T05:07:46.036233Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the PCB, then grasp the pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm slightly during most time of the episode, then approached the screwdriver and grasped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the PCB, pushed it slightly.Then policy B approached the pliers and also pushed it.Comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy B at least identified the required objects whiled policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'ce5a692e-1e90-45bd-811f-ca905c3510dc', E'2025-09-05T05:19:34.217111Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the PCB from right to left', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the PCB, after hesitating for while, pushed it to right a bit, then moved the robotic arm away in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the pliers rather than the PCB, grasped the pliers, moved it backward, then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing their performance, policy A at least identified and pushed the target while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'803cb78c-1248-4450-8751-a63b6cef651e', E'2025-09-05T05:29:52.035985Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the screwdrivers together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pliers rather than the screwdriver, grasped the pliers and release it several times.Then policy A approached one screwdriver and pushed it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red screwdriver, pushed it.Then policy B grasped a controller, moved it until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing their performance, both policies only pushed one screwdriver and grasped another wrong object.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'c94ba341-224b-433c-9996-8537e4c0b0dc', E'2025-09-05T05:40:58.106190Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the mouse onto the pliers', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, grasped it, moved it close to the pliers, then dropped it beside the pliers.Next, policy A grasped a screwdriver and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, pushed it forward,then grasped it, moved it to the pliers, put it down tight against the pliers.Next, policy B also grasped the screwdriver.Both policies have moved the mouse close to the pliers, when comparing their performance, policy B put the mouse more closer to the pliers than policy A did.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'2aafcaee-b70e-470d-a722-c1711730ac0b', E'2025-09-05T05:56:15.706121Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the yellow screwdriver by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow screwdriver, grasped it, rotate it by about 160 degrees,then put it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the yellow screwdriver, grasped it, rotated it by about 180 degrees,, then dropped it on table.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have rotated the yellow pliers by a similar angle.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'50e2fbaf-f526-4b2f-8ab1-7815c86cc33f', E'2025-09-05T06:14:18.268820Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the PCB and move it close to the screwdriver', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a pliers rather than the PCB, pushed the pliers, then pushed the mouse.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the screwdriver, moved it to right while rotated it by about 90 degrees, then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance, policy B at least moved one relevant object while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'e6e753ba-b3fc-455d-9ea3-940dce82906f', E'2025-09-05T06:35:59.871125Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to mouse, grasped it, then moved it close to the book, and dropped it beside the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, then adjusted posture, attempted to grasp it but failed in the end.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task, while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'6bbc1f4d-392b-48e3-bc59-a0fc1363fc92', E'2025-09-05T06:46:15.295023Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pliers from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to pliers, grasped it and released it.Then policy A almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the pliers,  after hesitating for a while, grasped and released it.Comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only grasped an released the pliers, their behavior is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'97a4e322-82f4-46bf-9cd7-cd4a29e219c4', E'2025-09-05T06:58:48.334916Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the pliers by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to mouse rather than the pliers, then pushed the mouse during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the mouse, grasped it, moved it close to the book, rotated it and put it on the edge of the book.Then policy B approached the pliers grasped it, moved it toward the book while rotated it slightly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and rotated the required object while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4aff9e7e-7730-43ed-96f3-40674e7c1d8a', E'2025-09-05T07:15:17.013497Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the tools onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the screwdriver and pliers, pushed them slightly during most time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, pushed it until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing their performance, policy A at least identified the tools while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'86be5abf-e13c-4c92-a8ff-911237be1016', E'2025-09-05T07:33:11.065786Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then grasp the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, attempted to grasp it but failed, only pushed it slightly.Then policy A approached the red block grasped it and dropped it several times.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana rather than the peach, then moved aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B have not done anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'440d2b70-a6b3-4236-9cc6-5ec1bf74c81a', E'2025-09-05T07:44:10.831473Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the peach  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on table.Next,policy A grasped a red block and moved it to right.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, made several attempts to grasp it but failed, only pushed it backward slightly.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, i choose policy A.'),
(E'92c7531e-6080-4915-ac88-439934227c0e', E'2025-09-05T07:53:18.989045Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the foods together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to a red wooden block which is not food,grasped it, moved it and dropped it beside a banana.Then policy A grasped the banana and moved it until time run out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes as if attempted to grasp it, after hesitating for a while, moved the robotic arm close to the red block in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped one type of food while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'a7f55e59-d53b-4721-9859-b0939ed51a39', E'2025-09-05T08:14:27.559887Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the grapes onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the green block rather than the grapes, then grasped the green block, moved it and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana rather than the grapes, grasped the banana, moved it onto the red block until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, comparing the performance of the two, policy B mistook the banana for grapes but policy B completed required movement, while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b9b13ec0-ba1c-4172-aab9-2499e29489e9', E'2025-09-05T08:29:12.265401Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, after hesitating for while, moved the robotic arm to the grapes, pushed it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, rotated it by a small angle and dropped it on table.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and rotated the banana while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e550b0bd-2379-4845-ba19-ca54cdf25a88', E'2025-09-05T08:45:40.443410Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and move it close to the yellow block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the peach rather than the yellow block, then dropped it on table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the green block, pushed it slightly, then moved the robotic arm close to the grapes in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the banana while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'cfd772c3-9f57-441c-bde2-92da6ba72e3e', E'2025-09-05T08:57:48.255543Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and put it onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it toward the red block, then put it onto the red block in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, then pushed it backward.Comparing the performance  of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'6669fa0f-a5a4-4781-a67f-a72ae11453d8', E'2025-09-05T09:25:40.988032Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the yellow block  from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes rather than the yellow block,grasped it and released it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it and released it.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes, attempted to grasp it.Then moved the robotic arm away.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies did not find the required object, it seems that they all mistook the grape for yellow block.Since their behavior is similar,i choose tie.'),
(E'b97abce2-bf9a-4d09-ae85-d8bcc575402f', E'2025-09-05T09:40:59.623403Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, then grasped and released it several times during most time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the  banana, pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees, then grasped and dropped it, caused it to rotate to origin angle.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least rotated the banana while policy A did not do the required movement.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4ce9f65a-54e8-429d-b861-0670e3b9a6cb', E'2025-09-05T10:01:18.268854Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the fruits into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it, grasped it, then moved it to the plate and put it into the plate.Next, policy A attempted to grasp a red wooden block which is not fruit.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it,as if attempted to grasp it,but failed in the end.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least put one type of fruit into the plate while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'fe21cfd9-8af6-41aa-9856-87db6fd42994', E'2025-09-06T01:50:33.883308Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Give me the milk.', E'Neither policy was able to even grab the milk, but policy B was able to approach the milk while policy A had sort of wandered near the orange juice. That being said, for some reason, policy B hadst of the episode almost reaching past the milk and fully extending its arm. The reason that I had chosen B was because in between extending its arm, it approached the milk.'),
(E'461a28e0-b21a-4ea8-a03c-57b176488e60', E'2025-09-06T01:59:16.539413Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Bring me the orange carton.', E'policy A had started by grabbing the milk carton and while moving to the orange carton had knocked it over while trying to grab it too early. policy A had ended with trying to grab the orange carton. policy B had started by making its way to the orange carton and grabbing on its second attempt. After grabbing the carton, policy B was able to bring the orange carton in my direction slowly at first and then more in my direction a little quicker. For some reason after the second movement towards me, policy B brough the carton closer to the right camera and then dropped it. I chose policy B because it was able to grab and carry the carton while policy A could not.'),
(E'5a45ee7f-e22a-446d-801f-00664f21e88a', E'2025-09-06T02:19:09.444471Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the bush.', E'policy A had spent almost the entire time grabbing the bush before eventually approaching the knife and attempting to grab it right at the very end of the episode. policy B had only spent the episode grabbing the bush and had actually dropped the bush as a result. The reason I chose policy A as mentioned before is that while policy B was only able to grab at the bush, policy A was able to approach and attempt to grab the knife.'),
(E'15776a8d-8ec3-4be3-8fe5-482d189e600f', E'2025-09-06T02:28:45.866950Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the plant.', E'Both policies recieved a tie because they both did nothing but grab at the plant for the entire episode. There are some differences, policy A had moslty grabbed from the top and never dropped the plant while policy B had almost completely extended it''s arm and pushed the plant while grabbing at it. policy A also had grabbed the plant more than policy B.'),
(E'3bc7885f-3fb8-4eb6-9817-6680f035c850', E'2025-09-06T02:37:46.288426Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Draw on the white board.', E'Both policies were able to grab the marker and begin approaching the white board a little, but there were some key distinctions. policy A had managed to approach the marker and slowly orient itself to be in the correct orientation to grab the marker. For some reason policy A grabbed the marker in a strange way, almost scooping the marker and causing the gripper tongs to not be parallel with each other.  policy A would then soon drop the marker causing it to roll near the corner of the table and perhaps out of view. policy A then began to push the white board and finished the episode pushing the ground. policy B had done a pretty good job at approaching the marker, picking it up, and approaching the whiteboard(albiet not quick enough to actually touch the whiteboard). the only issues that policy B had were that it would grab too soon, causing it to grab before being in a place where it could grab the marker. policy B''s final grasp was actually not a very sturdy grasp, barley grabbing enough of the outside to properly hold it. policy B also did not directly approach the white board, but had gone in a diagonal movement that was part ways towards the camera and part ways towards the white boad. With this in mind, I chose policy B because it had made much more progress than policy A.'),
(E'd66649ee-ca7d-41ae-833e-2003b954b417', E'2025-09-06T02:53:46.005544Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Draw on the white board.', E'policy A had been able to grab the marker and bring it to the whiteboard but it didn''t attempt to re-orient the marker, and so the buisness end of the marker was pointed the wrong way. policy B had not even managed to grab the marker. policy B had spent much time re-orienting itself but never actually moved close enough to grab the marker. Then, for some reason policy B had decided to grab at the white board for the rest of the episode. In conclusion, I chose policy A because, while it was oriented incorrectly, it still made much more progress than policy B.'),
(E'53e59a7e-e555-4956-b67e-13b85b325357', E'2025-09-07T00:42:30.094482Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and put in the holder.', E'policy A was able to grab the marker, but instead of approaching the holder directly, it approached to the left of the holder and dropped the marker. After dropping the marker, policy A tried grabbing the marker but ended up pushing the marker with the outside of its hand, knocking it off the table. policy B was actually able to pick up and drop the marker 3 times before the end of the episode. The first time policy B had grabbed the marker, it actually approached the holder with the correct orientation(marker in the vertical position) but it didn''t raise the marker high enough to actually place the marker inside of the holder. The second time policy B approached the holder, it actually placed the marker on top of the holder, and finally the third time it did it policy B had simply brought the marker to the holder. I chose policy B because it was able to pick up the marker many more times than policy A and it was able to get much farther.'),
(E'494b5472-6279-4439-a154-98686ba0b715', E'2025-09-07T01:07:32.158282Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and place it into the marker holder.', E'Both policies were able to grab the marker and even re-orient it in a somewhat vertical position. policy A had gotten stuck at that step and ended up dropping the marker once it was almost completely vertical. policy B had slightly tilted the marker but was also able to bring it all the way to the marker holder before dropping it on top of the holder. After dropping the marker, policy B did not approach the marker again and begun to push itself into the ground towards the end of the episode. I chose policy B because it was able to actually bring the marker towards the holder and drop it on the holder while policy A could not even bring the marker to the holder.'),
(E'b5f8d245-8565-42df-b4b2-29a775ccd05c', E'2025-09-07T01:18:41.984581Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the objects you can eat.', E'I chose policy B because it was actually able to grab a bread. policy A was only able to approach the breads a little, but had a very tough time choosing between the bread and sort of paced between the two bread on the table. policy B had first immediatley grabbed the bread before quickly going to the wooden block and trying to grab that.'),
(E'e84e06d6-0838-44ef-aa17-0f072b519dd7', E'2025-09-07T01:34:55.232352Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the edible objects.', E'Both policies were able to grab the left most bread and pick it up. policy A was not able to pick up the other bread and had instead opted to pick up the first bread again. policy B was able to pick up both breads, and won as a result.'),
(E'feff75ec-08cf-479a-b222-7038b35ac2fe', E'2025-09-07T01:59:08.744035Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the wooden shapes into the holder through the holes.', E'Both policies ended up grabbing the wooden holder, not the blocks. Perhaps this is because the blocks were colorful while the wooden holder was wood colored. In any case, both policies recieved a tie csince they did about the same.'),
(E'68d0abfd-11a1-435e-a385-095c65f1f32a', E'2025-09-07T02:14:23.414604Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the ball into the red cup.', E'policy A had picked up the red ball and placed it into the blue cup. policy A then picked up the blue cup by pressing the inside of the cup with the outside of its gripper. It was almost as if policy A had stuck the ball into the blue cup and then got its hand stuck into the blue cup. policy A then let go of the ball, removed its gripper from the cup and ended the episode with its hand in empty space. I chose policy B because it did everything perfectly and efficiently- quickly picking up the ball and placing it into the cup.'),
(E'37ccf19f-b96b-461e-96ff-8549640e4ffc', E'2025-09-07T02:24:43.539695Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the ball in the red cup.', E'Policy A had attempted to place the red ball into the blue cup, but knocked over the blue cup while transporting the ball. policy A then spent the rest of the episode trying to put the ball into the blue cup and failing. policy B had successfully managed to place the ball into the blue cup and then pushed the red cup a little before ending the episode. I chose policy B because not only was it able to actually place the ball into a cup while policy A couldn''t, it also approached the red cup while policy A couldn''t.'),
(E'c5352789-78ad-4592-9a45-24f5520d6f1a', E'2025-09-07T02:39:05.110826Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the ball into the blue cup.', E'policy A took the whole period to just place the ball into the red cup- moving in slow, staggered steps towards the cup until finally getting to the opening. policy B grabbed the ball rather quickly but while making its way to the blue cup, it dropped the ball and proceeded to touch the blue cup without the ball. After touching the blue cup, it went back to the ball and finished dropping the ball into the blue cup.'),
(E'0a058232-bb7d-41d5-b747-d7aa3e9daf75', E'2025-09-07T02:55:10.965804Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the ball into the blue cup.', E'policy A, after a very long time, was able to place the ball into the blue cup while policy B, after a very long time, was able to place it into the red cup. policy A started by quickly grabbing the ball and bringing it into the space in between the blue and red cup. It would then bring it towards the blue cup and drop it again. Finally, towards the end of the episode, policy A was able to grab the ball and inch it towards the blue cup. policy B had started by grabbing the ball and bringing it towards the red cup. Only towards the end of the episode was policy B able to finally drop the ball and retract a little from the red cup. Since policy A was actually able to do the task while policy B could not, I gave policy A the victory.'),
(E'a26f1251-c54b-4b53-94bd-87a0f037783d', E'2025-09-07T16:57:16.324377Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Knock over the red cup?', E'I gave both policies a tie since the most amount of progress either accomplished was picking at the clear cup in the center of the field. There were some differences worth mentioning: policy A was much more agressive than policy B. policy A would immediatley go to the cup and begin picking it up and letting it go throughout the whole episode while policy B really didn''t grab much if at all. policy B actually spent a non-negligible amount of time standing completely still until the end of the episode.'),
(E'd49e4739-b41a-48a5-abea-2e9ba784c5e1', E'2025-09-07T17:06:21.666144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Knock over the red cup.', E'policy A approached the red cup, grabbed it, and then retreated to a spot above the cup. After retreating, policy A spent the rest of the time standing absolutley still. policy B had approached the clear cup in the center of the field and got right up against it before staying completely still for like 10-20 seconds. It broke the stillness by pushing itself further into the clear cup(which was cracked at the time) and then retracting its hand with the clear cup still stuck on it. policy B finished the episode by touching the space in between the blue cup and the red cup with the clear cup and then raising its hand with the clear cup still stuck. I chose policy A because it actually approached the red cup while policy B approached the clear cup.'),
(E'5c4c029c-e74d-4700-83d7-b593863b73bb', E'2025-09-07T17:17:03.168586Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'poke the blue cup.', E'policy A had spent the entire episode either moving/pushing the clear cup into the ground, grabbing the cup while standing still, or moving back to later move back in to grab the cup. policy B had gstarted by moving towards the blue cup and had pretty much interacted with the blue cup the entire episode(grabbing, lifting, pushing, etc.). What I really wanted to see from policy B was for it to squeeze its gripper before touching the cup, almost like creating a finger for which to do the poking, but since I didn''t specify that behavior, policy B still recieved almost a perfect score. Because policy B had identified the right cup while policy A did not, I gave policy B the victory.'),
(E'0ba384be-17cb-451c-8714-aa068171e106', E'2025-09-07T17:27:20.639241Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Poke the blue cup with your gripper squeezed.', E'policy A was almost violent- smashing the clear cup into the table before grabbing it and migrating to the red cup. policy A would then drop the clear the cup and use the red cup to push the blue cup a little. For some reason policy A had sat there for 5-10 seconds before pushing the blue cup a little more to end the episode. policy B also grabbed the clear cup before using the clear cup to push into the blue cup. policy B then dropped the clear cup, moved back a little before going back to touch the blue cup right at the end of the episode. I chose policy B because it actually approached and intended to touch the blue cup while policy B was only able to push the blue cup with another cup.'),
(E'2adb4a2b-51dd-419f-ada4-949f186eba0f', E'2025-09-07T17:41:58.258634Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'pick up the clear cup.', E'policy A spent most of the episode grabbing anything but the clear cup- starting with the blue cup, then moving to grab the red cup twice, and then finally jamming it''s hand into the clear cup. policy B had basically spent the entire time interacting with the blue cup(grabbing, lifting, etc.) Something I think is worth mentioning is that the blue cup is in the center of the field and might have influenced the policies in picking it. In the end, I chose policy A because it was eventually able to interact with the clear cup- even if it was the very last thing it interacted with.'),
(E'6aa5a205-2164-4dfd-9481-5a7640a481bb', E'2025-09-08T01:46:50.881107Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes, then grasp the controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm aimlessly during most time of the episode, then moved the robotic arm to table in the end.Policy B also moved the robotic arm aimlessly during most time of the episode, then moved the robotic arm close to the table in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, the behaviors of both policies is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'7105e0d3-425f-4914-8911-13af952e59f4', E'2025-09-08T02:00:43.047144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, after hesitating for a while,attempted to grasp the marker pen but failed.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, paused briefly above the marker pen,then grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Comparing the performance of the two,policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'7c9625c3-2229-45a7-9a30-3b92ba73d690', E'2025-09-08T02:17:36.313498Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the grapes, grasped it, moved it to the book and place it on the book.Then policy A grasped the grapes again, moved to to right and dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, touched it.Then policy B approached the grapes, pushed it slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least put one type of fruit onto the book while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'6f02a852-d155-4f12-a374-b1c8b8d7d2f4', E'2025-09-08T02:27:55.557002Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the tape onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to tape, but then moved away as if could not find the object.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table,then moved slightly on the table during most time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least approached the tape while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'847dea2e-6d65-4983-b22f-ccfd819a6cc4', E'2025-09-08T02:38:26.736813Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, after hesitating for while, grasped and released the marker pen in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees , then moved it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B complete the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'02abc7b9-7c1b-47c1-b37b-399d2d7ff191', E'2025-09-08T02:50:51.294991Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the tape and move it next to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the tape, grasped it and released it.Then policy A grasped the taped again, moved it to the banana and placed it on the banana.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved the robotic arm close to the grapes and moved around the grapes during the remaining time.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'194480f3-66a2-435c-94ab-dabc5263a622', E'2025-09-08T03:06:13.384381Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then place it onto the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped it and released it, then pushed the towel slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach,touched it, but did not grasp it, then moved the robotic arm away.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached and touched the peach while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'ad81042b-621f-47a7-8e2f-55cd65f3b19a', E'2025-09-08T03:19:30.669682Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the knife  from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm back and forth aimlessly, then approached the book and grasped it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the knife, pushed it to make it rotated by about 45 degrees, then grasped it, moved it to right until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously than policy A.'),
(E'4c8e9521-17cc-472f-9b4d-462d9f67fdb0', E'2025-09-08T03:31:11.655364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the knife by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm slightly during entire time of the episode,  but did not take obvious actions.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the close to the book, then touched it as if attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least touched the related object while policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'fd823bd1-8d23-483d-b286-d4b5f62a3b5b', E'2025-09-08T03:44:35.144446Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the fruits from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on floor.Then policy A moved the robotic arm close to the grapes.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, pushed it slightly to left.Then policy B approached the grapes and pushed it forward sightly.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved one type of fruit to right while policy B did not, Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'807586b7-edeb-4537-9a9e-a56b5f34da91', E'2025-09-08T03:59:19.863178Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, pushed it,but did not grasped it,  then policy A approached  the white box and pushed it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the edge of the towel, pushed it, then policy A grasped the towel and released it, without lifting the towel.Next, policy A approached a white box and grasped it.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and released the towel while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'ff52b67d-227d-4059-a743-49b04acd545f', E'2025-09-08T04:16:06.227048Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the towel from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm randomly until time ran out.Policy B first grasped the white box, moved it slightly, then dropped it on table and pushed it to left.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'8aa2db08-c68e-45f0-bedd-0fde6c1d84d4', E'2025-09-08T05:06:58.787172Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the box together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, grasped it and released it.Then policy A pushed the smallest box close to the white box.Next, policy A pushed the white box to make it slip off the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, pushed it several times to make it fall off the table.Neither policy was able to complete the task,but policy A at least moved the smallest box toward the white box whiled policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'1f43e9c2-0557-45de-9717-8c7efbc6c6e2', E'2025-09-08T05:34:00.675033Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pull out the tissues', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table, moved up and down several times, then approached the tissues in the end.Policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the entire trial as if could not find the target.Comparing the performance of the two,neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least approached the tissues while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'a61c34ea-5f4b-41da-b8f5-56d57b80515f', E'2025-09-08T05:44:53.301659Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smallest box by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smallest box, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to table, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore,policy A is obviously than policy B.'),
(E'bc9947c1-8e4b-44b8-a594-841ab86946c6', E'2025-09-08T05:52:27.773524Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'wipe the table with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved on the table during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the table,moved on the table for a while, then moved the robotic arm close to the towel, pushed it until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least pushed the towel while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'b43acbb0-8671-4229-b8ad-77ab3ee5566b', E'2025-09-08T06:37:12.119945Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'fold the towel in half', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the right edge of the towel, grasped and released it several times.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the top right corner of the towel, adjusted posture,pushed the edge of the towel to make it fold in about 1/5.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B folded the towel in about 1/5 while policy A almost did not fold the towel.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4ae7b456-b09b-443e-9ede-b8598d5746dd', E'2025-09-08T06:53:30.411299Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the book from  left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slightly above the table until time ran out.Policy B did not response to my command and did not  perform any operations at all.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the robotic arm while policy B did not respond.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'de5e35b7-e936-47b6-8274-7877af05e404', E'2025-09-08T07:07:24.081618Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pull out a tissue, then put it on the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the tissues,pushed the pack of tissues close to the book, then pushed it tight against the book in the end.Policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during entire trial.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least moved the tissues toward the book while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'1ba7a299-e5ba-41b2-944a-065068713b84', E'2025-09-08T07:20:35.307821Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all tissues from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one tissue, pushed it, then grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm close to another tissue until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one tissue, pushed it slightly, then grasped it and moved it to right until time ran out.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A has moved one tissue to right, dropped it and approached another tissue, while policy B has only moved a tissue to right slightly but did not dropped it.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'b6035864-a9a2-4fed-b33d-745c6b36eec3', E'2025-09-08T07:50:36.692845Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp one screw, then lift it up', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block rather than the screw, grasped the red block, then dropped it on table.Next, policy moved the robotic arm away.Policy B also first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, grasped it then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only grasped the red block rather than the screw and their behaviors is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'5419f022-ebe6-4706-b01b-a4b632654b32', E'2025-09-08T08:00:30.580957Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the dinner fork  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then pushed the black cloth to left during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to table, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the black cloth together with the fork while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'2574fc38-1d08-4f64-b711-7a683166eb16', E'2025-09-08T08:13:39.575496Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden color blocks together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm away and almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to a small plate, grasped it, moved it, then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the wooden blocked and pushed it while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'6910abdd-2ece-4149-a15e-7938d2c59f12', E'2025-09-08T08:29:09.588336Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the the block in the shape of the number 8, then put it on the blue block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the blue block, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm randomly, then pushed the black cloth.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy A at least pushed one related object while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'701c56b3-fdb3-4063-9012-b5311a2332db', E'2025-09-08T08:39:20.243450Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the red block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, pushed it to make it rotate by 90 degrees.Then policy A stopped during the remaining time.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved aimlessly as if could not find the target.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'4f82bb1f-e20a-40fb-8c7b-45bd65037232', E'2025-09-08T09:04:24.059954Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the cup and move it close to the blue block', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the wooden block, grasped and released it.Then policy A approached the cup and knocked it down.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the blue block, then pushed another wooden block.Next policy B grasped the book and moved it.Finally, policy B approached the cup and knocked it down.Neither policy was able to complete the task, and both policies only knocked the cup down but did not grasp it.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'b1ea547c-9e79-4180-9ed0-0717b270b4d4', E'2025-09-08T09:19:52.419406Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the blue  block, then put it into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cup, pushed it slightly, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arms close to the blue block, made multiple times to grasp it but failed in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the blue block while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'fddee531-b50c-454b-8366-b5462c36cf2b', E'2025-09-08T09:36:38.008807Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the controller from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped it , moved it to right, then dropped it on the table, but did not rotate it.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm slightly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved aimlessly and rotated the gripper until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the controller to right while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'3a61004d-c552-460b-b346-07d7073f5b09', E'2025-09-08T09:46:59.972228Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the cup by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cup, pushed it toward the book, causing the cup to rotate by about 80 degrees and roll away from the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm aimlessly as if could not find the target until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least rotated the cup while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'8e850252-dd8c-4b55-b019-cdd105e01ace', E'2025-09-08T10:01:27.762177Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all wooden blocks into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block, grasped it, moved it close to the cup, then adjusted posture, made multiple attempts to put it into the cup but failed in the limited time.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one block, grasped it, then moved it away from the cup in the end.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have grasped one block, but policy A attempted to put it into cup while policy B moved it away.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'7e741fbd-02b4-41b4-b70f-69169137c38e', E'2025-09-08T17:20:18.335584Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Enter a space using the keyboard in front of you.', E'policy A was able to approach the keyboard, squeeze its gripper into a single contact point and press sort of close to the keyboard after its second attempt. policy B had spent the entire episode pressing its gripper into and empty space on the table to the bottom right of the keyboard. I chose policy A because it was able to execute the steps needed to precisley target the space bar while policy B did not even seem to know that it should be interacting with the keyboard. The only failure for policy A was that it didn''t have the fine-grain manipulation skills to precisily touch the space bar- otherwise it was almost perfect.'),
(E'3b70d782-c58a-4d8a-8742-0dbf74efce6f', E'2025-09-08T17:29:17.184295Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Enter a space using the keyboard.', E'policy A had made a very good attempt at touching the space bar- getting within milimeters of presssing it. One thing to note was that poilcy A did not ever actuate its gripper, something that might have been desirable for the task given that a squeeze gripper would constrain the action to a sinlg point to touch the space bar with; instead, policy A ended up touching the keyboard in two places at a time. policy B had made a much less concerted effort to touch the space bar- only having touched the keyboard maybe twice and never getting particularly close to the space bar. For these reasons, I gave policy A the victory.'),
(E'e9a8c1ab-9b9a-4746-9ebc-b6986bf2a00c', E'2025-09-08T17:43:27.973228Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'There is a piece of bread in the middle of the table. Please grab the other object instead of the bread.', E'I gave both policies a tie because they spent the entire episode interacting with the bread even though I asked them not to do that.'),
(E'b53ff097-731a-4273-bc5c-a5e34093a1c2', E'2025-09-08T17:57:46.954600Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the block.', E'policy A had started by approaching the block, and descending upon it without changin the orientationn of it''s gripper. As a result, policy A wasn''t able to grab the block. For the rest of the episode, policy A would stay sort of to the right of the block sort of grabbing and interacting with the empty space next to the block. policy B litterally just fully extended its arm for no reason and started grabing at nothing. Since policy A was able to at least somewhat decently attempt to grab the block, I gave it the victory.'),
(E'34aad4f5-8b13-44b6-af85-4cb7c8c11458', E'2025-09-08T18:06:16.945795Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the block.', E'policy A had started by re-orienting its gripper in the proper way so that it could grab the block and then began to approach, but before it could actually made contact, policy A retracted its gripper. For the rest of the episode, policy A sort of stayed above the block, seeminlgy analyzing where to grab. policy B was very different, it began by immediatley smashing its gripper into the block but without re-orienting it first. policy B was much more active, getting closer to the block than policy A and even touching it again before the end of the episode. That being said, even though policy B touched the block while policy A did not, I chose policy A because I believe that re-orienting the hand was greater progress than simply touching the block. The block was placed so that it would be impossible for the policy to grab the block without changing the orientation of its hand; this was done so that I could test the policy''s ability to fully utilize the gripper rotation as part of its action space.'),
(E'9454fb51-2af9-4cca-a1d6-30f3157e9af7', E'2025-09-08T18:17:19.012041Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Bring me the marker.', E'policy A began by approaching the marker but placing its gripper a little to far to the right and failing to pick it up. For at almost the entire rest of the episode policy A would then explore the upper right space of the field for seemingly no reason before making one last attempt to grab the marker. policy A was able to get its entire gripper around the marker but didn''t grab it and ended up ending the episode sort of hovering in space. policy B had spent the episode sort of grabbing and dropping the marker. policy B never moved the marker anywhere, simply grabbed it and sometimes would pick it up before dropping it. I chose policy B because it was able to actually grab the marker while policy A could not.'),
(E'1068ca88-77e9-43c9-958f-367421b31135', E'2025-09-09T01:08:57.953203Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the orange, then grasp the mobile phone', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana rather than the orange, grasped the banana, moved it close to the orange, then dropped it on table.Then policy A pushed the orange to make it fall off the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the orange, made several attempts to grasp it bu failed,then policy B moved the robotic arm to a controller, pushed it.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the orange while policy A did not.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'7c400b46-d951-4f16-aade-6960c9e85dab', E'2025-09-09T01:23:59.032417Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mobile phone from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, after hesitating for while, grasped and released it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target, then pushed silver cloth during the remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the mobile phone while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'c290df87-cab5-4f00-8620-07ce267cb689', E'2025-09-09T01:34:15.612195Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all fruits onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, grasped it, moved it toward the book, then dropped it on the table, causing the peach to scroll away from the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, made multiple attempts to grasp it, but only made the peach scroll close to the book.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least succeed in grasping the peach while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'80e8e7ee-19a7-4c7b-af16-eb9d3e6ccd1e', E'2025-09-09T01:52:07.191692Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the blue controller onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the blue controller, grasped and release it,then slightly moved the robotic arm above the blue controller until time run out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the blue controller, grasped and released it several times, then grasped it, moved it and put it onto the book in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'166a784b-185a-4a7d-8af9-69decbe84c79', E'2025-09-09T02:09:41.569870Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the red controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller,grasped it and release it several times until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, pushed it to make it rotate by about 60 degrees. My requirement is to rotate the red controller by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A only grasped and released the red controller but did not rotated it while policy B rotated it by about 60 degrees.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'54ed20c6-99f0-4336-9f3d-736e1bc9162f', E'2025-09-09T02:23:38.794471Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the mobile phone, then move it next to the blue controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone, pushed it slightly, then moved the robotic  arm close to the red controller and moved around it during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, pushed it away, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to pick up the mobile phone and move it next to the blue block, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the mobile phone and pushed it while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly than policy B.'),
(E'84154421-194f-4262-96d7-7dfee45c1235', E'2025-09-09T02:37:15.643735Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then place it onto the mobile phone', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, pushed it slightly, then policy A approached the banana, grasped and released it several times until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, pushed it, grasped it and released it, then moved around it during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the peach and put it onto the mobile phone, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the peach while policy A only grasped the wrong object banana.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'774f7db1-e749-465f-a7c9-d9220610c394', E'2025-09-09T02:51:48.268005Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the red controller  from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees, then moved the robotic arm around it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, grasped it, moved it forward rather than to right.Then pushed it to make it rotated by about 90 degrees in the end.My requirement is to moved the red controller to right and rotate it by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have rotated the red controller, but only policy B grasped and moved the red controller (in wrong direction). Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'c6c57906-3b50-4f6a-a458-e2ceb0a27d0a', E'2025-09-09T03:07:50.972059Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the mobile phone  by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to book, touched it, then almost stopped on it during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mobile phone,pushed it slightly, but did not rotate it.Then policy B approached the book, pushed it until time ran out.My requirement is to rotate the mobile phone and put it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the mobile phone while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'636aa34e-bb42-49bd-9d28-0fcdd7825a5f', E'2025-09-09T03:19:29.555945Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the electronics products from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controllers,pushed one blue controller to top right.Then pushed another white controller to top left.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the white controller, pushed it to right slowly until time ran out.My requirement is to move all the electronics products to right, there are two electronics products on table which is two controllers,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only pushed one controller to right, but after that, policy A pushed another controller in wrong direction.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'b2f4a6f4-5ec2-45fd-8a9f-ed1e11471c0e', E'2025-09-09T03:40:32.787975Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the towel then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped it together with the tissues, lifted them up, and dropped them on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped it, lifted it up, moved it then dropped it on table.Next, policy B grasped and dropped the towel twice until time ran out.Both policies have completed the task successfully, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B performed the operations more smoothly and accurately than policy A.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'070dd9f5-5cf5-4f4e-adc4-d1856a619d70', E'2025-09-09T03:53:53.242406Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the towel, then move the towel from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped it, moved it a white box, dropped it on the box,but pulled it back to left. Then policy A grasped the towel,  moved it to right and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on the table.Both policies have completed the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B succeed in the first attempt while policy A succeed in the second attempt.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'0cce6aee-92ce-4942-84b2-2b948c2cf114', E'2025-09-09T05:08:42.623072Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the boxes together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it and release it several times, then moved it slightly and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close the smaller box, grasped it, moved it slightly then dropped it on the table.My requirement is to put all the boxes together and there are two boxes in total, that is to say, the task is to put the two boxes together.Neither policy was able to complete the task, both policies have only grasped one box but have not moved it to another box.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'0ef0f98d-d3f8-422b-8bb6-f3df63299dc9', E'2025-09-09T05:21:56.841208Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pull out the tissues from the pack', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pack of tissues, grasped one tissue, pulled it out from the pack, moved it,  then dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the pack of tissues, grasped the tissue together with the pack, then moved them to right and dropped them on table.Next, policy B attempted to grasp a towel until time ran out.Comparing the performance of the two, since my requirement is to pull out the tissues from the pack, policy A have completed the task correctly while policy B have not pull out the tissue, only grasped the tissue together with the pack.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'd9781c6c-6f3e-4af6-894e-87ff41821677', E'2025-09-09T05:37:17.907442Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the cola by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees.Then policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then put it on table.Both policies have completed the task successfully, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A have completed the required task more quickly than policy B did.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'662b182f-b3ad-43e1-a567-307f68e94534', E'2025-09-09T05:56:31.685799Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the towel, then wipe the book with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped and release it several times, then moved the robotic arm away in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, then approached a smaller box.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm back to the towel again, grasped it, moved it to the book,pushed the book.My requirement is to wipe the book with the towel, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A only grasped the towel while policy B grasped the towel then moved it to the book,almost completed the task.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e0644ab2-35ed-46f1-b6bf-8efa3f099a7b', E'2025-09-09T06:28:33.650864Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'fold the towel in half', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped its bottom left corner, moved the corner to right, then put it close to the middle right edge of the towel.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then grasped the silver cloth rather than the towel, then released it.My requirement is to fold the towel in half, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'7c173737-2d64-4aa3-b650-f4f9eff7883e', E'2025-09-09T06:45:27.507662Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mouse from  left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, grasped it, moved it to right, then put it on table.Next, policy A moved gripper above the the mouse until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, hovered above it for a while, then grasped it and moved it to right in the end.My requirement is to move the mouse from left to right then rotate it by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only moved the mouse to right but did not rotate it.But policy A used less time to complete the first step (which is to move the mouse to right)  than policy B did.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'd4412797-e00c-49fe-a579-51166de98ea2', E'2025-09-09T07:01:44.904256Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pull out a tissue, then put it on the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pack of tissue, grasped the pack, after hesitating for a while,then moved it to the book,and put it on the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the robotic arm close to the pack of tissues, grasped the pack of the tissues, moved it close to the book,then dropped it beside the book.My requirement is to pull out the tissue then put it on the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task except pulling out the tissue, but policy B only grasped the pack and moved it close to the book.Therefore, policy A is obviously than policy B.'),
(E'cde84f8d-d94d-4dde-9d9f-dad9b8f8dcb3', E'2025-09-09T07:15:06.972048Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all tissues from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the one tissue, grasped it, moved it and released it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm to another tissue, grasped and released.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one tissue, grasped and released it.Then policy B moved the robotic arm to the book in the end. My command is to move all the tissues to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A grasped two tissues while policy B only grasped one tissue, but both policies did not move the tissues to right obviously.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd3333b2f-a15c-44da-acfc-a4ca8b8b9773', E'2025-09-09T07:33:17.422728Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the lid of the cola, then lift it up', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, knocked it down,then moved the robotic arm to the towel, grasped it, moved it and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, then moved the robotic arm close to a book, pushed it.My requirement it to grasp the lid of the cola then lift it up, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the cola and approached the cola while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'ae89ea52-215d-4208-871e-fe21ccc3d475', E'2025-09-09T07:46:09.988344Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube backward', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller beside the cube,grasped and released the controller.Then moved the robotic arm to approach the cola.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, after hesitating for while, grasped and released the controller several times.My requirement is to move the cube backward, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only grasped the wrong object controller, and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'c7d74067-c5fe-441e-9586-c2e929115006', E'2025-09-09T07:58:26.766675Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden blocks together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, pushed it to make it fall off the table.Then policy A approached one wooden block and pushed it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block,  then hovered above the block and moved slightly.My requirement is to put all the wooden blocks together, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least pushed and moved one block while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'44bdc5fd-431e-4154-a378-396167050084', E'2025-09-09T08:25:59.699121Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the wooden  block,  then put it on the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped and dropped it.Then policy A grasped and dropped the controller.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the wooden block, grasped and released it.Then policy B almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the wooden block and put it onto the cube, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least identified and grasped the wooden block while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b81f774c-6af5-48d3-a876-0e50f0ea86c1', E'2025-09-09T08:56:52.736221Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, moved slightly on the table for a while, then almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close the banana, pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees, then moved the robotic arm away.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed, therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'330ab2cb-c426-4573-a5b9-1b249febad8d', E'2025-09-09T09:05:09.735453Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and move it close to the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, then pushed the book.Next, policy A stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the  table, then moved slowly on the table for a while.Next, policy B approached the knife, grasped and release it.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least pushed one related object book while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'8b6f97dd-68d6-4e7f-8dc4-990bf0be66d1', E'2025-09-09T09:15:07.495391Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book,pushed it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the drawer rather than the book, then dropped it beside the drawer.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least grasped the banana while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'eb232d2d-8ad9-4abf-97df-f55fed582f67', E'2025-09-09T09:26:01.071409Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the controller from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped it, rotated it by a small angle, then dropped it on the table.Then policy A pushed the controller to make it rotated and move to right a bit.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slowly on the table during most time of the episode.Comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'9ed29436-f28d-47c5-b738-37f40db66cc1', E'2025-09-09T09:36:41.007366Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the red controller by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, then stopped above it during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red controller, pushed  it to make it rotate, then grasped and released it.My requirement is to rotate the red controller by 90 degrees then put it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least rotated and grasped the red controller while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'5361542c-c6bd-4716-996e-6e78785f2339', E'2025-09-09T09:49:35.617459Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden blocks into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block, grasped it, moved it to the plated and put it into the plate.Then policy A grasped and released the edge of the plate several times until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the one wooden block, grasped it, moved it to the plate and put it into the plate.Then policy B grasped another wooden block, put it into the plate.My requirement is to put all the wooden blocks into the plate, there are two blocks in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A only put one block into the plate while policy B put all the two blocks into the plate.That is to say, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'15cfa0f8-4c71-417f-8b11-3b5ab49a5c31', E'2025-09-10T00:07:26.383982Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Give me the marker.', E'policy A had a somewhat hard time to grab the marker but it was able to pick up the marker and drop it. policy A might have spent half of the time interacting with the marker and had definently spent less time than policy B. policy B had a much easier time grabbing the marker and actually held it for much of the episode, even bringing it within 3-4 inches of my hand. I chose policy B because while both policies could grab the marker, only policy B had brought the marker somewhat close to me.'),
(E'a068aa16-1276-41c9-b32f-81b102281736', E'2025-09-10T00:15:27.138627Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Bring me the marker.', E'I gave both of these policies the same score because their maximum progress was the same. Both policies had managed to grab the marker and neither policy was able to even begin bringing me the marker.'),
(E'c6902e4a-f0e2-43cd-ad19-9446dcdf6178', E'2025-09-10T00:29:06.431164Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Stir the pot with the ladel.', E'policy A had approached the ladel before pausing slightly above the ladel, maybe 3-4 inches above the ladel. Policy A would then stay paused for the remainder of the episode. policy B had spent the entire episode grabbing the ladel. I am not sure if it was due to the weight of the ladel, but policy B was never able to lift the ladel very high, only lifting it once maybe a few mm off of the ground. That beign said, policy B did immediatley approach the ladel and was able to grab at the ladel for most of the episode even if it didn''t really lift it. Since policy B was able to actually grab the ladel, I gave policy B the victory.'),
(E'50dee03f-601d-43ed-af49-7a949ad8f2a7', E'2025-09-10T00:39:45.509411Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Stir the pot with the ladel.', E'policy A had spent most of the time grabbing the handle end of the ladel and was even able to lift that side upwards about 10-20 cm albiet not completely off the ground(the other side stayed on the ground). policy B had actually spent the entire time trying to grab near-er to the buisness end of the ladel, almost by its neck. policy B was not able to actually pick up the ladel and becuase of that, and because policy A could pick it up and at an arguably more advantageous position, I gave policy A the victory.'),
(E'fd130bc0-e90e-4c8f-9d56-d3ff0ae96ad8', E'2025-09-10T00:50:45.908321Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the marker in the wine cup and take the paper off of the wine cup.', E'Unfortunatley, when I said to remove the paper from the cup, I didn''t consider the possibility of accomplishing that by simply knocking over the cup! Both policies decided to knock over the cup but at different times. policy A immedialty knocked over the cup and spent the rest of the time trying to grab the paper while it was on the floor. policy B had started by attempting to grab the marker and had even gotten pretty close before deciding to switch tactics and simply knocked over the wine cup. Interestingly enough, policy B then interacted with the wine cup. While I don''t want to suppose what the model was thinking but after knocking the cup away from its field of view, policy B then seemed to change tactics again and begun interacting with the marker(albiet very clumsily) for the remainder of the episode. By interacting, I mean policy B put its gripper over the marker and the block that was holding the marker but didn''t grab. With all that in mind, since policy B had made more progress on the marker aspect than policy A and seemed to try engage in more of the objective than getting caught up on the paper, I gave policy B the victory.'),
(E'18aa0b46-c300-4fd3-9595-ab3ae5e67704', E'2025-09-10T01:14:39.064505Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the carrot, then drop it ', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table, then moved on the table during the entire trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then approached the controller beside the carrot until time ran out.My requirement is to grasp the carrot then drop it,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least moved the robotic arm close to the carrot while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'528102e1-b8d8-4989-926f-17d1af75a5b0', E'2025-09-10T01:25:09.246517Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the carrot from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, pushed it, grasped it, moved it to right then dropped it on table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy B grasped and released the carrot again.Both policies have completed the task successfully, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B grasped the carrot more smoothly than policy A did.Therefore,i prefer policy B.'),
(E'7c70445f-f0fd-42e0-b7bf-803750a9281b', E'2025-09-10T01:41:25.368275Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all vegetables onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to carrot, grasped it and released it, then moved the robotic arm around the carrot during most time of the episode, and grasped / released the carrot again in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, let the gripper grasp in the air, then moved the gripper onto the book until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped one type of vegetable while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'db63017c-ba5f-458c-8231-d06205355fab', E'2025-09-10T01:55:05.608370Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the bell pepper onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book, then moved the robotic arm slightly around the book during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bell pepper, pushed it, then attempted to grasped but failed.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm close to the book.Neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least pushed and attempted to grasp the bell pepper while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'1c14ddcb-4f73-4946-9786-6a427c0380f0', E'2025-09-10T02:06:04.971824Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees then dropped it on the table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm away and almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 160 degrees, then dropped it on the table.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have rotated the marker pen, but policy A rotated the marker pen by the required angle 90 degrees while policy B rotated it by 160 degrees.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'0a9aa81e-66eb-4287-a1d3-1765a32c4c59', E'2025-09-10T02:16:15.934304Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the carrot and move it next to the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to carrot, pushed it.Then policy A approached the bell pepper.Next, policy A moved away from the bell pepper and moved near the edge of table until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, pushed the book and the cube.Then policy B moved the robotic aimlessly during most remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least approached and pushed the carrot while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'4ca70c81-4dc0-4135-aef1-a0f7a9aee303', E'2025-09-10T02:29:21.043786Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the eraser, then place it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table,then moved the gripper around the edge of the table during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, it seems that both policies could not find the eraser.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least pushed one related object book while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e4a506c5-0740-4a79-8ced-c710e8293849', E'2025-09-10T02:41:57.944280Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the carrot  from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slowly around the edge of the table during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees while moved the carrot to right, then dropped the carrot beside the book.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'9fe879c5-e926-4ec1-a6c4-2dd8d6f960b8', E'2025-09-10T02:51:49.343577Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved aimlessly on the table during most time of the episode.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen and pushed it to make it rotate by about 45 degrees in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped and released it, causing it to rotate by a small angle.Then policy B almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task,both policies have only rotated the marker pen by a small angle but have not put it onto the book.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A have rotated the marker pen by bigger angle than policy B did.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'13ba38df-1173-4bd1-aa59-173462d001bf', E'2025-09-10T03:13:14.946196Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all vegetables from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to carrot, grasped it , moved it to right, then dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, moved it to right, then put it on table.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to move all vegetables to right, there two vegetables in total.Both policies have only moved one type of vegetable to right, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B took less time to find and move the carrot to right than policy A did.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'ac33e216-a890-4470-a252-f2bf32b52708', E'2025-09-10T03:30:01.931866Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the biggest button of the controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped and release it several times,then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped and released it several time,then pressed the biggest button in the end.My requirement is to press the biggest button of the control, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'd73f102b-6312-4cbf-86d4-29d47ee922ec', E'2025-09-10T03:39:25.996728Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the smaller controller  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to left side of the table, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have not done anything relevant.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'f9dfeb7e-2221-43a3-aa0b-15f0b1501a68', E'2025-09-10T03:50:04.655679Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the cups together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one cup, pushed it away, after hesitating for while, attempted to grasp the cup but failed in the end. Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one cup, knocked it down,then attempted to grasp it but failed.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm back and forth until time ran out.My requirement is to put all cups together, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both polices have attempted to grasp one cup but failed, only knocked the cup down.Since the behaviors of the two policies is similar, i choose tie.'),
(E'83db1d41-564d-425f-8a8c-ca0f8f469b7c', E'2025-09-10T06:52:02.844409Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the potato  into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm to the table, then moved on the table during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close  to the potato, made multiple attempts to grasp it, then picked it up,  moved it close to the plate and put it into the plate.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5c58f6a5-1a35-4c16-a755-5c3379455bdb', E'2025-09-10T07:18:53.852697Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the smaller controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger controller, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees then dropped it on table.Next, policy A grasped and released the controller several times until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm to the bigger controller, pushed it.Then policy B approached the smaller controller pushed it to make it rotate by about 90 degrees.Next, policy B pushed the bigger again to make it rotate.My requirement is to rotate the smaller controller by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B rotated both controllers while policy A only rotated the wrong controller. That is to say, policy B completed the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'd9e78d79-a03a-47f2-a737-4cdf13d53964', E'2025-09-10T07:32:03.426407Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel, then cover the potato with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to towel, grasped and released it several times, then pushed the towel until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, adjusted posture,grasped the towel, lift is up,moved it then dropped it on table.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two,policy A only grasped the towel but did not lift it up, while policy B grasped the towel and lifted it up.Since my requirement is to cover the potato with towel, the behaviors of policy B is more suitable to my requirement.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'2fb731da-13c3-421f-bac8-f58ec4b04c2c', E'2025-09-10T07:48:27.758513Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel, then cover the controller with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the edge of the table, then grasped the edge during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped and released it several times, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the towel while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'360eb1c1-64da-4c8c-86ee-d4049afb6dd7', E'2025-09-10T08:04:07.747864Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the game controller from left to right and rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved the gripper on the table during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the game controller, touch it slightly, then almost stopped during most remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least touched the game controller while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'04cac11b-c766-4cb5-b1d6-f4f6106d687d', E'2025-09-10T08:20:00.097038Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate  the white box by 90 degrees, then put it on the plastic bag', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the white box, pressed the top of the white box while rotated the gripper, causing the white box rotated by a small angle.Then policy A attempted to grasp the white box until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the white box, pushed it, as if attempting to grasp it.Then policy B approached the plastic bag, grasped it, moved it until time ran out.My requirement is to rotate the box then put it on the plastic bag, neither policy wax able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least rotated the white box by a small angle while policy B only pushed the box forward.Therefore, policy A is sightly better than policy B.'),
(E'8c1d0630-cec4-4c48-b108-35b5633b1270', E'2025-09-10T08:36:54.587242Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the boxes  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved the gripper on the table for a while.Next, policy A approached one box, attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one box, grasped it,moved it to right, then put it on table.Next,policy B approached another box, pushed it until time ran out.My requirement is to move all the boxes to right, there are two boxes in total.Neither policy was able to complete the task. When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved one box to right while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'fbc5d280-7441-4b13-bb4c-4669a7536a11', E'2025-09-10T08:50:44.426280Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the plastic bag, then cover the red block with the plastic bag', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to plastic bag, grasped it, moved it slightly to left and dropped it on table.Then policy A grasped and dropped the plastic bag again.Finally, policy A approached the red block in the end.Policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the entire trial, it seems that policy B could not find the target.My requirement is to grasp the plastic bag and cover the red block with it, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the plastic bag while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'1d25f316-624c-4061-9ffb-490717691a91', E'2025-09-10T09:22:12.776180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the PCB from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the PCB, touched it slightly, then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic to the table, attempted to grasp the black cloth, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at  least touched the PCB while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'ee00b675-b9ed-4339-a16c-c74547e4fdff', E'2025-09-10T09:34:52.302449Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden blocks onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block, grasped it,  moved it to right, dropped it on table.Then policy A grasped the wooden block again, moved it until time ran out.Policy B first move the robotic arm close to one wooden block, pushed it, then policy B pushed the book.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm to the wooden block again, almost stopped above the block during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to put all the wooden blocks onto the book, there two wooden blocks in total.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped one wooden block while policy B only pushed one block.Therefore, policy A is slightly than policy B.'),
(E'6370554f-80da-4303-828b-7d49d29f19be', E'2025-09-10T09:48:38.120140Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two wooden blocks', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book rather than the wooden block, pushed the book.Then policy A approached one wooden block, pushed it slightly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one wooden block, grasped and dropped it several times until time ran out.My requirement is to stack up the two wooden blocks, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least grasped one wooden block while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'229339f6-8a4d-45b6-b108-837494119530', E'2025-09-10T10:00:50.066454Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two white boxes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one white box,made multiple attempts to grasp it but failed in the end, only pushed it slightly.Policy B first took some time to find the target,then approached one white box, pushed it as if attempting to grasp it, but did not succeed.My requirement is to stack up the two white boxes, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only pushed one white box, but policy A has found the target more quickly than policy B did.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'114b3dee-d068-464e-8a63-6489c71ebfd8', E'2025-09-10T20:19:53.503029Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the egg to the to-go container', E'Both A and B knew it had to manipulate something around the bowl which contained the egg. A arm position was too high thus it grasped nothing after directly point to the bowl and thus the arm did not bring anything to the container. B on the other hand decided to bring the entire bowl into the container which hypothetically completed the task with the egg but it was better to bring just the egg'),
(E'b3580eb4-b812-41e5-a7b5-ff5bba7236f3', E'2025-09-10T20:30:54.864048Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the wooden bowl into the highest stack of bowls', E'Both policies A and B swiftly reached for the wooden bowl and rotated to the stack of blue bowls which is the highest amongst the two stacks. A performed quite a bit of unecessary moves after finishing thing up as it grasp the whole stack up in the air but got terminated due to time'),
(E'd9d58f3b-14de-420b-a214-73420cdf3e63', E'2025-09-10T20:40:50.646875Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the red marker into paper cup', E'B was good at pointing to where the red marker was initially located at but the arm was haivng difficulty rotating in the exact place to grab the marker. A did the same thing as B but i pushed the pen holder off the table and knocked the marker on the surface of the table; it was able to grasp the pen but ended up loosening it and dropping eventually.'),
(E'e19de1e1-dd2c-4a50-8230-dc452b181ac7', E'2025-09-10T20:50:58.890816Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the blue tape on the notebook', E'A was pointing to the direction where the tape was placed on but it hovered for too long, parhaps consider which tape to select since there were two types of tape on the table. B on the other hand quickly located the blue tape and put it on the table. The arm also shifted to the left side where something having the same color was involved'),
(E'496abd92-cbe1-4e37-9332-2a2bc2ce36f2', E'2025-09-10T21:01:01.307819Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'finish making the sandwiches', E'A was searching something in the left side in which the dish contained just the writing utensils and cubes. A was totally going off the task here. B was doing a little bit better since it shifted towards one of the bread slice on the other table after pushing the cup off. Both did not do so well since the point of this task is to move the slice on bread on the green filling'),
(E'a145a0af-6318-4bad-a6cd-5277a4699960', E'2025-09-10T21:11:40.198551Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'sprinkle the sugar onto bread', E'A was going off the point here as it grabbed the pen and manupulating around the bread for this episode. B was a little bit better since the arm at some point went to the direction where the red bottle which contained sugar but the arm was grabbing nothing and moving to the bread'),
(E'8ef1eda2-7183-4948-9393-aa040ce99bf9', E'2025-09-10T21:22:26.274709Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'make a breakfast by sandwiching the green filling', E'A went straight grabbing the small cup which was irrelevant while B was sort of being on point. B recognized the bread location but it failed to do the task correctly step by step. The other slice of bread still remained on the table since B was trying to pull the slice on the plate out'),
(E'97be2505-44f6-4677-a2fe-2c2a18555f69', E'2025-09-10T21:37:01.321367Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'use the feather duster to clean up the table', E'Policy b was hovering in front of the duster and wasnt sure what to do next while A was decisive into this task as it grabbed the duster and performed a swiping motion thus pushed up the paper cluster off the table.'),
(E'c8a79fa2-e343-4484-8707-76410b0111cb', E'2025-09-10T21:48:03.037517Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'cook the corn and close the lid', E'A was indeed better since it did not disrupt the seen like in B. Both were able to grasp the corn first but it succesfully placed it on the pot and erwards it had a hard time adjusting the gripper to get the lid. The gripper should precisely grab the litle handle of the pot. B was pushing the pot at first and it grabed the corn up mid air, which was pointless since the pot was off seen'),
(E'97746aae-fc9f-48b4-b87b-d039dbb6ca32', E'2025-09-10T22:00:27.049079Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the pen onto notebook', E'B was hovering above the pen without knowing the next steps for this command while A completely nailed the movement in the first half of the episode. The arm hereafter got rested after placing the pen on notebook'),
(E'b7854c36-e8fc-4a34-b40e-39857ab1c298', E'2025-09-10T22:10:31.467078Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'complete the purple puzzle', E'Both policies recognized it had to do something with the purple cubes as they both neatly grasped it and lifted it up air but in both cases the arm was not sure where it should put it on eventually and it kept dropping the cubes consequently until the arm decided to push the other cubes closer to us'),
(E'e5ec41ca-72b5-4fb6-b5e8-a0b45a91707e', E'2025-09-10T22:29:59.854619Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'pour water from the small cup to orange one', E'B completely disregarded the order of the task since it tried to reach for the orange cup and further pushed it off the table. A initially reached for the smaller cup in purple but wasnt sure what to do next as it hovered after pointing towards the small cup'),
(E'a8ad69bb-5e00-4aaa-9335-eaf0b08c4bd6', E'2025-09-10T22:38:23.270907Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the screw driver into cup', E'both policies did not do so well as they seemed to not recognize the look of a screw driver and in both trials, they tended to reach for the paper clipper or pushing the cup further away from the seen'),
(E'c22d009e-c0ce-4424-ae78-506259ac9d4e', E'2025-09-10T22:54:10.808130Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the paper clipper into bowl', E'BOth policies were not able to locate the clipper which was placed in a tricky location on top of a sticker note. A grabbed the wooden bowl while B grabbed the screw driver and moving them around the seen'),
(E'a4586881-dfe7-41f0-95bb-798e3cb9400e', E'2025-09-11T00:21:57.848222Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and place it in the wine glass.', E'policy A grabbed the block holding the marker and held it for almost the entire episode, only releasing it right at the end. policy B had overshot the marker and gradually moved its gripper up the field towards the wine cup until it knocked it over. After knocking the wine cup over, policy B sort of wandered around there for the rest of the episode. I chose policy A because it had attempted to grab at something and it had gotten closer to the marker than policy B.'),
(E'3779ccbb-eecc-4d6c-8909-b310433c52ff', E'2025-09-11T00:31:17.786968Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and place it in the wine cup.', E'policy A for some reason approached the cup towards the thin handle part and inadvertently knocked the cup over. After knocking the cup over, policy A tried grabbing the cup once or twice but never approached the marker. policy B had gone for the marker, but ended up grabbing both and then grabbing the hole the marker was in before lifting it in the air somewhat towards the cup. I chose policy B because it had actually managed to lift the marker(albiet in addition to the block) and move it towards the wine cup.'),
(E'1fcda35f-1cdf-4763-aba4-27a31aed63cf', E'2025-09-11T00:43:17.755686Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the marker into the left hole.', E'policy A had tried grabbing the marker but pushed a little too hard and sort of pushed past the marker. After that solid attempt at grabbing the marker, policy A would push against the block holding the marker and try grabbing at that for the rest of the episode. policy B for some reason started by placing its hand to the far right of the field and drifting to a point where it was almost fully extending its arm. policy A would move back towards the block eventually, but it never really tried grabbing the marker. the best it was able to do was sort of hit the marker before going to grab at the block. Becaause policy A was able to actually grab at the marker, I gave policy A the victory.'),
(E'09135972-56b5-4911-92da-88d7967b9df2', E'2025-09-11T00:58:17.376699Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread inside of the pot.', E'Both policies were able to grab and place 2 pieces of bread inside of the pot but they did it somewhat differently. Both policies started with the bun on the bottom right of the field. After placing the bread inside of the pot policy A retracted its hand, paused for a moment and then grabbed the bread on the bottom left and placed it in the pot. After placing that last piece of bread inside of the pot, policy A retracted its hand again but instead of approaching the loaf to the left of the pot, policy A sort of cocked its hand back as if to survey the area and ended up not even approaching the last loaf. policy B after placing the bun inside the pot had moved its gripper above the pot and paused for about 5-10 seconds before going for the loaf that was close to the pot and placing it into the pot. After policy B placed the loaf into the pot it was actually able to approach the last bun twice before the episode ended. Because policy B was able to place 2 breads in the pot while also being able to approach the last bread while policy A could only place the 2 breads, I chose policy B to be the victor.'),
(E'7a78f8f8-5a1e-461c-938f-d99523474d27', E'2025-09-11T01:11:24.408434Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes, then grasp the potato', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the potato, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm  close to the potato, then almost stopped beside the potato during the remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the grapes then grasp the potato, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least pushed the potato while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'85937980-c47f-4ddd-8766-9c8ea858e598', E'2025-09-11T01:14:21.274574Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the bread into the pot.', E'Both policies started by grabbing the middle loaf and placing that into the pot. For some reason policy A then extended its hand as if it were looking for bread behind the pot and began drifting its gripper forward until it was off of the table where it would end the episode. After policy B placed the first loaf into the pot, it went around the pot to grab the top most loaf and place that into the pot. policy A wouldn''t go for the last bread- instead actually reaching into the pot before retracting its hand having grabbed nothing before ending the episode. In short, because policy B was able to grab 2 bread while policy A could only grab 1, I chose policy B.'),
(E'e6ff247b-4329-4dd3-93df-e9f5de4fb398', E'2025-09-11T01:21:38.201719Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bell pepper from left to right', E'Policy A first took some time to find the target,then moved the robotic arm close to the bell pepper, made several attempts  to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first took some time to find the target,then moved the robotic arm close to the bell pepper, pushed it forward as if attempting to grasp it during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to move the bell pepper to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,both policies have not move the bell pepper to right, only attempted to grasp the bell pepper but failed.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'af9c41f4-bfcd-4a32-854b-f4a074d34c62', E'2025-09-11T01:25:00.770216Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Poke the foam with the pen.', E'Policy had little difficulty grabbing the pen and spent most of its time holding it, and pressing it into the floor(which in this case is made out of foam) while completely ignoring the foam block to the top right of the field. policy B was much quicker at picking up the pen than policy A, but grabbed it in a scooping fashion that made the grasp over the pen unstable. Both policies had completed a maximum progress that was very similar to each other, but the reason that I chose policy B was that it had actually started to move the pen in the direction of the foam block(abliet only a little bit).'),
(E'824cbbcd-6c39-4639-8516-d1961a641ab1', E'2025-09-11T01:41:19.771256Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all  the fruits onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the book, then put it on the book.Then policy A approached the grapes, attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to the book, and put the banana on the book.Then policy B moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task,when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have put one fruit on the book,but then policy A attempted to grasp another fruit while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'66f7734f-a8a2-4cc7-819b-f0ba750b581b', E'2025-09-11T01:54:06.273909Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana onto the grapes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, then moved it to the book and put it on the book rather than the grapes.Then policy A moved the robotic arm slightly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it close to the grapes, then adjusted posture, put the banana onto the grapes.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'1af94875-9c64-452f-9c57-c0fa6cf5f8d4', E'2025-09-11T02:23:23.993959Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the carrot and move it next to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, moved it close to the banana, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy B grasped the carrot again,moved it to banana but moved the carrot away in the end.Comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully, while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'6e5aa39c-34b1-4d03-a52b-c31074b0f267', E'2025-09-11T02:33:26.708294Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the potato, then place it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to potato, pushed it to the edge of the table as if attempting to grasp it, then moved the robotic arm close to the plate in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, then pushed it during most time of the episode.My requirement is to put the potato into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least pushed the potato while policy did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9513a04e-cadc-48f3-8744-5b897651a084', E'2025-09-11T02:51:55.104526Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the bunch of grapes from right to left, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then moved it to right rather than left slightly and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes, pushed it to left slightly, but did not rotate the bunch of  grapes in the end.My requirement is to move the grapes to left then rotate it by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least rotated the bunch of grapes by 90 degrees correctly while policy B only pushed the grapes to left a bit.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'8635101e-2204-407f-bb60-d01b8b684d56', E'2025-09-11T03:22:34.583304Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the carrot by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book  rather than the carrot, pushed the book.Then policy A approached the carrot, and pushed it to make it rotate while fall off the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, pushed it to the edge of table, but did not obviously rotated.Then policy A approached the grapes until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least obviously rotated the carrot while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'7499b4f4-361a-4a30-8878-18be81655cc6', E'2025-09-11T03:43:55.982549Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the vegetables from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot , grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy A grasped the carrot again and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A approached the bell pepper in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy B grasped and released the carrot several times until moved the robotic arm away.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have moved one vegetable to right, but then policy A attempted to grasp another vegetable while policy B did not.Terefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'72a13a97-9416-4010-a804-a00ed8c1dee0', E'2025-09-11T03:57:53.086558Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the charger then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the charger, then moved around the cable of the charger during most remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cable of the charger, grasped it, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy B grasped the cable again in the end.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and dropped the cable of the charger while policy A did not grasp anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'7da42593-91e4-4e54-b890-ca039c505205', E'2025-09-11T04:09:19.000174Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the mouse from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, then moved the robotic arm close to the charger.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm to the middle of the two, grasped and released their cable.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cable of the charger, then moved around the cable during most time of the trial.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the cable of the mouse while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'a309965d-c386-4807-a378-96e6befb4a79', E'2025-09-11T05:13:09.126445Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the  cups together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target, during entire time of the trial.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the one cup, grasped it, then moved it slightly toward another cup.My requirement is to put all the cups together, there are two cups in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A failed.Therefore,policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'a7b2463d-5f9a-4ca8-8965-ea4bd990392b', E'2025-09-11T05:30:25.855650Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the black mouse  onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm randomly during most time of the episode, then stopped near the edge of the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, then moved away.Next, policy B approached the mouse, grasped it, moved it close to the book, and placed it on the table near the book in the end.My requirement is to put the black mouse onto the book, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5944e49b-8e18-484a-8695-093651ff6410', E'2025-09-11T05:50:21.122581Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the left button of the mouse', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, pressed the right button of the mouse several times, then grasped and release the mouse.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, pressed the middle of the mouse several times.My requirement is to press the left button of the mouse, neither policy was able to complete the task. When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least press the wrong button while policy B only pressed the middle of  the mouse.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'2d976863-a4f5-4f7c-993a-1d1bc724f1e0', E'2025-09-11T06:37:26.497057Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book, adjusted posture, put the gripper under the cover of the book, then pushed it, attempted to close it during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, adjusted posture, then pushed the book while turned the pages of the book.My requirement is to close the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least turned the pages of the book while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'a1be3fba-567b-4ac1-95a0-891f4ac89255', E'2025-09-11T06:53:31.663274Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the book, put the gripper to edge of book, then turned the pages of the book, but the pages closed again when the gripper moved away.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, then moved the gripper on top of the book for a while, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'2ae2bda5-bdb6-4558-a525-d44c1ca934a8', E'2025-09-11T07:05:59.138486Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick a grape from the bunch of grapes', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes, grasped and dropped them.Then policy B attempted to grasp the grape several times, and grasped one grape in the end.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'95a35fe6-55cd-41fe-97f8-8802340e1690', E'2025-09-11T07:18:23.771257Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the mouse  by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to mouse, grasped it, moved it to the plate, then put it into the plate.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the right side of the table, then touched the plate.Next,policy B moved aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least put the mouse into the plate (although did not rotated it) while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd624e8d6-b9f6-41a7-8038-bb439fbfac2d', E'2025-09-11T07:30:13.443247Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the mice  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one mouse, grasped its cable, moved it to right, then released it.Next, policy B moved the robotic aimlessly, but did not attempt to move another mouse.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one mouse, grasped it, moved it to right, then released it.Next, policy B move the robotic arm slightly during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only moved one mouse to right and did not attempt to move another mouse.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'63b278a6-eb6d-465f-a4e4-2f04059b2d54', E'2025-09-11T07:50:02.514749Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'knock over the cola', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, pushed it to knock over it.Then policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the entire time of the trial.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'9c0ea73d-53a9-4fc5-b82e-f52eb35343a2', E'2025-09-11T07:59:18.417323Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the smaller box from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to smaller box, pressed the top of the smaller box, then pushed it to right slightly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, then moved it to right.Then policy B moved the robotic arm randomly during remaining time of the episode.Both policies have completed the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B moved the box further to right than policy A did.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'0c968e1d-07e1-4490-91c9-ea4e83c680ad', E'2025-09-11T08:09:08.031709Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the boxes together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the white box, pushed it forward.Then policy A approach the controller, grasped it, moved it to the red box and put it on the table close to the red box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the white box, grasped it, moved it toward the red box, then placed it near the red box.My requirement is to put all boxes together, there are two boxes in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'c6c32ae5-459a-4f2a-bde6-998a857d61b7', E'2025-09-11T08:21:31.255709Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the smaller white box onto the bigger box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, pushed it as if attempting to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bigger box rather then the smaller box, pushed it.Then policy B approached the smaller box, pushed it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only pushed the smaller box but did not put it onto the big box.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'572624c6-f5c0-4c0b-a61b-a44df961c40b', E'2025-09-11T08:34:19.163879Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'turn the smaller box over', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, pressed its edge, attempted to turn it over but failed.Then policy A moved the robotic arm away and stopped during remaining time of episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the smaller box, grasped it, rotated and  dropped it, attempted to turn it over but failed.Then policy B also press the edge of the smaller box, tried to turn it over, also failed.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B have tried two different method to turn over the box while policy A only tried one.Therefore, i choose B.'),
(E'27ba66c9-1858-4f0b-a279-9f9336efdf41', E'2025-09-11T08:51:20.826493Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the lid of the cola', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, grasped the body of the cola and released it.Then policy A pushed a box beside the cola.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, grasped the lid of the cola, then released it.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least grasped the lid of the cola while policy A only grasped the body of cola.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'666add10-958a-47f8-bd00-c025faeab771', E'2025-09-11T09:07:28.533343Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the box and put it onto the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the box, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy A moved the the robotic arm randomly until approached the box in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified and pushed the box while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.')
INSERT INTO sessions (id, occurred_at, site_id, instruction, notes) VALUES
(E'5c0e028b-6c63-49e7-a7d4-434facc4c98a', E'2025-09-11T09:18:27.146774Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'fold the towel in half', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to edge of the towel, grasped the bottom left edge of the towel, moved the it to right.Then policy A fold the towel again.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, put the gripper near its bottom right corner, pushed it slightly until time ran out.My requirement is to fold the towel in half, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost complete the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'044eabe7-85e3-4dbf-85b5-3c3980a470c1', E'2025-09-11T09:32:11.162752Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the power plug by 90 degrees, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm randomly for a while, then pushed the plate close to the power plug in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, grasped and released it.Then policy B moved slightly around  the edge of the plate.My requirement is to rotate the power plug by 90 degrees and put it into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the plate close to the power plug while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'41ff6461-d530-4c7c-be44-69d69385fcce', E'2025-09-11T09:55:51.648878Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel, then wipe the table with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table,  after hesitating for a while, approached the towel in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, after hesitating for while, approached the towel, grasped it, then moved it slightly on table as if wiping the table.My requirement is to grasp the towel then wipe the table with it, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'36ac6f58-daf9-4632-b529-80230183cfbf', E'2025-09-12T00:09:44.679405Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cup on the mini coat hanger.', E'policy A was only able to pace back and forth above the cup and wasn''t actually able to do anything. policy B had actually been able to touch the cup but in an awkward fashion pretty quickly but for some reason then retracted its gripper a lot(almost across the table and greater than 2ft above the table) while holding the strange hand configuration. Policy B would then do that one more time before ending the episdoe with its hand in a weird position in the air. With this in mind, I chose policy B because it was able to actually touch the cup while policy A could not.'),
(E'0c9ad02b-46cd-4ce7-9b6b-54094c2c1680', E'2025-09-12T00:23:07.937180Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cup on the mini coat hanger.', E'Both policies were able to grab the cup, but they went about it differently. policy A had grabbed at the cup quite a bit and even lifed/moved the cup before the end of the episode. policy B was very slow, spending most of its time hovering with its gripper around the cup but never grabbing the cup. Througout the entire episode, policy B only grabbed the cup once or twice and never moved the cup. It''s for this reason that I chose policy A over policy B.'),
(E'825a207d-9fd8-4895-a576-4c07d28aa597', E'2025-09-12T00:31:20.684946Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove everything from the plate.', E'policy A managed to remove the red cup off of the plate and the proceeded to grab the top of the cup for the rest of the episode. policy B had managed to remove all but one object from the plate(albiet with some difficulty with placing its hand right on the target object. policy B started with the red cup and had toppled it over causing it to roll to the edge of the table. With the red cup so far away, policy B quickly switched focus to the green wooden block and after some struggling managed to pick it up and remove it from the table. policy B would end by grabbing the white block-after, yet again, some more difficulty. In all, I chose policy B because it had accomplished much more than policy A.'),
(E'943b9692-b06c-4863-a737-bafa960d8e09', E'2025-09-12T00:40:51.668543Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove everything from the plate.', E'If I had to characterize the policies, I would call policy A quick but unsteady while policy B was slow and clumsy/inaccurate. policy A started with the red cup and pretty quickly removed it from the plate. policy A then moved to the green block and managed to grab it very quickly but never ended up doing anything with it. policy A would pick up the green block once or twice more before ending with the green block in its hand over past the plates. policy B started with the red cup, try it once and then moved to the white block. policy B continued grabbing things once before moving on(including the plate) until it grabbed the green block and moved it away from the plate to end the episode. I chose policy A because it simply did more than policy B.'),
(E'd5baae55-cedb-4ce8-8418-7af625b5f99c', E'2025-09-12T00:50:06.795720Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove everything from the table.', E'policy A didn''t really do anything that really stood out, it just took a while to grab the red cup, remove the red cup, and then attempt to grab the green block but never end up removing it from the table. Policy B was very efficient at removing things from the table, removing both the cup and the white cube in almost a semi-continuous movement. The one thing that policy B did poorly was that after it placed the cube away from the plate, it would keep trying to grab it and in the end policy B was not able to tear itself away from the white block. I chose policy B because it was able to remove 2 things while policy A could only remove 1 thing.'),
(E'eba182ee-52eb-491f-b50c-8aa77e516a94', E'2025-09-12T01:12:22.493432Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the orange, then grasp the pencil', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen, grasped it and released it several times, then moved the robotic arm away in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the orange, pushed it several times as if attempting to grasp it, then grasped the cloth near the orange.My requirement is to grasp the orange then grasp the pencil, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the orange and attempted to grasp it while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'87194280-3756-4913-8af1-5ab8f9972179', E'2025-09-12T01:23:35.282856Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to cloth, pushed the cloth, then grasped and released the cloth.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, attempted to grasp it but  failed,then policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to move the cube from left to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified and attempted to grasp the cube while policy A did not do anything relevant Therefore,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4ac24aaf-91a0-4f13-9e9d-083b2b169b5d', E'2025-09-12T01:34:27.525284Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the fruits onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller rather than fruit, grasped the controller, moved it to right.Then policy A moved the gripper onto the book until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it toward the book, then grasped the banana and put it near the book.Next, policy A grasped the banana again and moved it onto the book in the end.My requirement is to put all the fruits onto the book, there are two fruits in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved one fruit onto the book while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'5908d966-8d97-4cf6-88fd-8c56de0a24e4', E'2025-09-12T02:15:42.665214Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel, then cover the banana with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, then grasped and release it several times until time run out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel, grasped it and release it, after hesitating for while, grasped and moved the towel to right in the end.My requirement is to grasp the towel then cover the banana with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only grasped the towel but have not covered the banana with it.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'0f8ddf55-3e9f-4ea0-99ed-0575569374e8', E'2025-09-12T02:29:18.338790Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'touch the right side of the small wheel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the small wheel, pushed it forward, adjust posture,then touched the right side of the wheel.Next, policy A almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the small wheel, touched the top left side of it, then moved the robotic arm away.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm randomly until grasped a banana in the end.Comparing the performance of the two,policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'12bf823b-1ef3-4174-94ab-3522fb3472ce', E'2025-09-12T03:23:14.915560Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the small wheel close to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm back and forth, then approached the small wheel, grasped and release it twice until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the small wheel, after hesitating for a while, pushed the small wheel forward slightly.My requirement is to move the small wheel close to the banana,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A grasped the wheel while policy B pushed the wheel forward, but both policies have not moved the wheel close to the banana.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'9c4e7e99-5413-4427-a4a8-2a956c124c52', E'2025-09-12T03:35:43.870264Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then put it on the wheel', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana,then grasped and release it several times until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped and released it.After hesitating for while, then policy B approach ed the banana again in the end.My requirement is to grasp the banana, then put it on the wheel,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,both policies have grasped the banana but have not put it on the wheel.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'c97c93f1-aa9e-4060-a751-d28d544877e4', E'2025-09-12T03:48:12.823317Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cola from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, grasped it, moved it to right, then put on table.Next, policy A almost stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, grasped it , moved it to right while rotated it by about 90 degrees, then dropped it on table.But the cola scrolled off the table.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A only moved the cola but did not rotate the cola.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'72215ecf-92e0-4510-af79-56fb2d435e91', E'2025-09-12T03:58:01.939285Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the  cube  by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table, then moved on the table during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, pressed its edge to make rotate.Then policy B moved the robotic arm away and approached the book.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least rotated the cube while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e44eed60-f381-43c4-a000-d08762e9febd', E'2025-09-12T04:06:53.883242Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'turn over the controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slightly above the table until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the edge of the table, then moved around the edge during remaining time of the episode.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies only moved the robotic arm randomly but did not identified the controller.Therefor, i choose tie.'),
(E'f2c7ead1-b164-4170-8a11-649a76a45b16', E'2025-09-12T05:20:43.561174Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'knock the blue block over', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to book rather than the blue block, then moved away, after hesitating for while, approached the book again.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the blue block, pushed it, then grasped it, rotated and moved it as if attempting to turn over it, then put it on the table but failed to turn over the blue block.My requirement is to turn the blue block over, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B almost completed the task while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'76a1121f-5d88-44a9-a7e2-9c033bea7826', E'2025-09-12T05:36:23.832536Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the red blocks from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then move on the table during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, grasped it, moved it to right and dropped it on table.Then policy B grasped the red block and moved it to right again.My requirement is to move all the red blocks to right, there are two red blocks in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved one red block to right while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'8f1a3999-16aa-4af7-8956-99f0a7ddfbe1', E'2025-09-12T05:47:38.724477Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the vegetables together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, pushed it away, then grasped the controller, moved it and put it on the book.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the carrot, grasped it, then moved it back and forth until time ran out.My requirement is to put all the vegetables together, there are two vegetables in total.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped and moved one vegetable while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'4f37b919-c3f6-4ade-bf82-65d4a7535945', E'2025-09-12T05:59:54.476961Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the small wheel into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the small wheel, knocked it over,then moved the robotic arm away and stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the plate, then approached the small wheel, knocked it over.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm aimlessly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two,both policies have only knocked the smaller wheel over but did not put it into the plate.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e7389510-7fd7-429c-bcd3-d99703b00f25', E'2025-09-12T06:11:04.386414Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the yellow block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, touched it, then approached the yellow block, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees and dropped it on table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block,  grasped  and released it several time.My requirement is to rotate the yellow block by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'c8e303e7-ce12-44e6-9479-7b469bd87011', E'2025-09-12T06:24:25.969121Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the stem of the apple', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during entire time of the episode as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table,  then approached the apple, pushed it slightly.Next, policy B stopped during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the stem of the apple, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached and pushed the apple while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'93e88085-1cda-474d-a1b0-e26df2a607f3', E'2025-09-13T01:42:15.464974Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bunch of grapes, then grasp the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes, grasped it, moved it, then put it near the banana.Next, policy A grasped and released the banana.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved slightly during the remaining time of the episode.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'00432039-22a4-40a6-9547-5a55125b25c1', E'2025-09-13T01:55:00.714944Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the marker pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to marker pen, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on table.Next, policy A grasped and release the marker pen again in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, pushed it, grasped it and dropped it on table.Then policy B approached the marker pen, grasped it until time ran out.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B only grasped the marker pen but did not move it to right.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'330882a2-aaac-4ea2-80fe-1dff682a82d0', E'2025-09-13T02:05:58.269393Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the fruits into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it toward the plate, then dropped it tight against  the plate.Next, policy A approached the bunch of grapes, attempted to grasp it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to the plate and put it into the plate.Then policy B approached the grapes, grasped it, moved it to the plate, placed it into the plate.My requirement is to put all the fruits into the plate, there are two fruits in total.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A only moved one fruit to the plate while policy B completed the task successfully,Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5a45818e-bbdb-4c86-9baf-42be0ac60388', E'2025-09-13T02:17:41.961500Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table, after hesitating for a while, approached the banana, grasped it and released it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped it, moved it back and forth, then put it onto a red block rather then the book.My requirement is to put the banana onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A only grasped the banana while policy B grasped and put banana onto the red block(although it was wrong ). Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'f69149a2-7e1a-49ce-980b-52a2df9b21ba', E'2025-09-13T02:29:03.036846Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the bunch of grapes rather than the marker pen, pushed the grapes.Then policy A moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, then rotated it a bit during remaining time of the episode.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'a1b658bf-d65a-489f-8c86-e1f93a9e246d', E'2025-09-13T03:47:46.133471Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the marker pen and mit close to the banana', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to banana, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the marker pen, grasped it, moved it close to the banana then moved away, put the marker on the table where was far from the banana.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost complete the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'a2bde0ed-311f-4f5b-96f2-7c174ac8d394', E'2025-09-13T05:22:18.537474Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the red block, then place it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, grasped it, moved it toward the book, then placed it near the book.Next, policy A grasped the banana, moved it back and forth until put it onto the book in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red block, grasped it ,lifted it up and dropped it.Then policy B grasped the red block again and move it slightly until time ran out.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, both policies have grasped the red block, but only policy A have put the red block close to book while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
