(E'afb31873-8e97-4303-8935-a3a0e897268c', E'2025-09-14T06:22:37.583656Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the controller onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, grasped it, moved it to right, then dropped it on the table.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm randomly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bell pepper, pushed it, then approached the controller, grasped it, moved it to the book and put it onto the book.My requirement is to put the controller onto the book, when comparing the performance of the two,policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'f47fb19a-3c3d-4988-a2a7-5c648e1a8c28', E'2025-09-14T06:39:11.196188Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to book, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pressed it, then moved slightly above the controller until time ran out.My requirement is to rotate the controller by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified and pressed the controller while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'8a268b15-eb74-406a-8d3f-63eb3333d217', E'2025-09-14T07:00:34.129818Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the pencil, then put it onto the controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pushed it,then approached the banana until time ran out.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, pushed it, then approached the pencil, grasped it, moved it toward the controller, stopped above the controller in the end.My requirement is to grasp the pencil then put it onto the controller, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'bd430b21-06d9-41c0-8257-c42cc80d13df', E'2025-09-14T07:10:29.376511Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then place it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, grasped and released it, then pushed it to left slightly.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the peach, pushed it slightly as if attempting to grasp it, then approached a plate, pushed it until time ran out.My requirement is to grasp the peach then place it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the peach while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd71d6d3b-607a-40ff-a1bf-8179eb5b05c1', E'2025-09-14T07:32:18.759396Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the controller  from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to controller, grasped and released it, then grasped it again, moved it to right and dropped it on the table.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the controller, pushed it slightly to left, then grasped a pencil rather than the controller and rotated the pencil.My requirement is to move the controller  from left to right then rotate it by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the controller and moved it to right while policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4d994c5a-1dcf-4cea-913b-a256068a534e', E'2025-09-14T07:56:26.858069Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana  by 90 degrees, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the banana, grasped and released it to make it rotate by a small angle, then moved the robotic arm away and stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the book, after hesitating for a while, then touched the book.My requirement is to rotate the banana  by 90 degrees then put it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped the banana and made it rotated by a small angle while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'995204f1-a10b-4d3c-80ea-06fe278c7466', E'2025-09-14T08:20:15.812693Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move all the electronics products from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, then moved around it during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, then moved aimlessly until time ran out.My requirement is to move all the electronics products from left to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, it seems that policy A identified the mouse which is electronics product while policy B could not find the target.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'ca5f670e-a1c3-4af1-afa5-df0ed2f41577', E'2025-09-14T08:43:30.676403Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the lid of the cola, then lift it up', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cola, pushed it, knocked it over.Then policy A moved robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table, then moved on the table until time ran out.My requirement is to grasp the lid of the cola then lift it up, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified and pushed the cola while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'cf74d6b4-20ee-4e23-8040-a713451f44ff', E'2025-09-14T09:03:46.423026Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube backward', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, touched it, then put the gripper on the cube until time ran out, as if attempting to grasp it.My requirement is to move the cube backward, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified and pushed the cube while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e443080c-99fe-40e4-b843-df3e98007f7f', E'2025-09-14T09:14:14.564186Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the red  blocks together', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to one red block, grasped it and dropped it.Then policy A grasped the red block again, moved it slightly and dropped it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the one red block, turned it over, then approached another red block, pushed it slightly toward the first red block.My requirement is to put all the red  blocks together, there are two red blocks in total.When comparing the performance of the two, neither policy was able to complete the task, but policy B at least identified two red blocks and tried to move them together while policy A only identified one red block.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'3e419514-b58d-4763-b953-009ec2a1eff9', E'2025-09-14T09:26:05.666971Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the wooden  block,  then put it on the cube', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to wooden block, after hesitating for while, pushed the wooden block forward, then moved the robotic arm away.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the wooden block, then approached the cube and stopped during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the wooden  block then put it on the cube, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least pushed the wooden block while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'2f9a555b-b06f-481a-be2b-53ebde02fca6', E'2025-09-14T09:48:16.042364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the wooden block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm back and forth as if searching the target, then approached the wooden block but did not rotated it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the wooden block, touched it, then pushed it to make it rotate by a small angle.My requirement is to rotate the wooden block by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least rotated the wooden block by a small angle while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'020b9224-1f74-41e5-a552-0878d5811566', E'2025-09-15T19:13:26.283734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove everything from the plate.', E'Policy A for the first half would grab in front of the red cup, close it''s grippers, retract it''s hand, and open it''s grippers again- almost as if it were dispensing the red cup even though it never actually grabbed the red cup. For the second half, policy A had pressed up against the red cup and began grabbing/pressing(not enough to thuroughly push the plate) until the end of the episode. Policy B had actually managed the grab the white block and moved it off of the plate. policy A began by pushing up against he cup and actually pushing the plate forward. After not making any progress with that, policy B then stopped pushing the plate a little and began focusing on the white block instead- grabbing it and moving it with litle haste hiccups. Policy B would retrun to the red cup, doing much the same as policy A - pushing against the cup while grabbing- until the end of the episode. In conclusion, I chose policy B simply becuse it was able to remove something from the bad list while policy B could not.'),
(E'91285b4a-de45-42f1-beab-3fdef62dd8b8', E'2025-09-15T19:26:51.450126Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Remove everything from the plate.', E'I prefer policy A over policy B because policy A was actually able to remove something from the plate. policy A stareted by going for the red cup-pushing and grabbing at it; however, only after retracting could it see an available white block to go and grab. Policy B started by pushing agants the red cup and grabbing at it for almost the whole episode. A couple times it had gottne really close(the closest I''ve seen after running one other trial today) to actually picking up the cup(grabbing it successfully at the end of the episode but not removing it). Neither policy acknowledged the green slab and neither policy could remove more than one object, but at least policy A could remove an object while policy B could not.'),
(E'd3c90b0a-763b-4a28-9e79-bf39b86a63bb', E'2025-09-15T20:01:51.541442Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cups inside of each other.', E'Both policies had gone for the middle purple cup first. policy A took the purple cup to the smaller cup and, upon seeing that it was unable to place the larger purple cup into the smaller red cup, it sort of stood there unable to do anything. policy B had done the opposite with the purple cup and took it to the larger yellow cup and successfully placed the purple cup inside the yellow cup. After stacking the first 2 cups, policy B grabbed the stack and began moving to the small red cup, but when it realized that it would not be able to place the stack inside the smaller red cup, policy B began wandering aimlessly with the stack in its hand. In short, I chose policy B because it was able to actually stack a cup while policy A could not.'),
(E'a0f4fcb3-467e-4721-8900-20233dbec79c', E'2025-09-15T20:10:43.990264Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cups inside of each other.', E'policy A started with the small red cup on the left side and placed it into the middle blue cup. While initiallly looking like the very first policy to place all 3 cups inside of each other, due to some miscoordination, policy A was not able to grab the stack it had just made and ended up moving randomly until eventually picking up the yellow cup and placing it on the stack to end the episode. Policy B had grabbed the blue cup and half hazardly placed it onto the yellow cup before wandering the field for the remainder of the episode. With this in mind, I chose policy A because it was able to get a clean stack while policy B could only sort of get one cup into the other and didn''t even make an effort towards the other cup.'),
(E'fbb05a61-651c-4279-a537-3856f2c27d2a', E'2025-09-15T20:18:19.682065Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the small cup behind the orange juice and place it into the pot.', E'Unfortunatley my eval was not as challenging as I would have hoped!! Based on max performance, both policies did the same(although I argue policy A did it faster) in that they completely nailed it. The only difference being that policy B struggled a little more to put it into the pot than policy A. That being said, since their maximum completion was the same, I gave them the same score and thus they tied.'),
(E'3d0a39c9-883c-478d-b29d-de5519843dd6', E'2025-09-15T20:31:57.949869Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take the cup out of the pot and put it behind the orange juice.', E'Policy A started right away with grabbing the cup inside of the pot, but ended up crushing it for the most part because it would grab the cup from the outside. policy A was only able to grab the cup and take it out of the pot near the end of the episode.Policy B had the same issue except that it was much more pronounced when it inserted and retracted its gripper to grab the cup and it was much more violent with the cup - crushing it completely as it took it out of the pot ruthlessly and placed it on the ground behind the orange juice. I gave policy B the victory because it was actually able to let go of the cup in a place that was behind the orange juice and also close to the orange juice while policy A could only grab the cup by the very end of the episode.'),
(E'b76cd4be-3d77-4fc2-849b-748c3df47a8b', E'2025-09-16T16:55:44.516902Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the cup that is behind the orange juice into the pot.', E'policy A moved slow and confused, unable to see the cup that was occluded from the 3rd person view, it sort of wandered around the starting posision, not doing anything. Policy B on the other hand immediatly moved to the cup, knocked over the orange juice. After the cup was now in plain view of the 3rd person camera, policy B had no problem going to the cup and grabbing it to place it into the pot. Because policy B was able to make progress towards the cup while policy A could not, I give policy B the win.'),
(E'29051af1-1777-449a-8bbe-8aebe8ca7dfd', E'2025-09-16T17:03:34.438144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the cup from inside the pot and place it behind the orange juice.', E'policy A started by quickly picking up the cup and placing it behind the orange juice. Policy B was also able to place the cup behind the orange juice, but it struggled much more than policy A to grab the cup(about 1-2 more attempts) and also knocked over the orange juice when placing the cup. policy B did place the cup closer to the orange juice than policy A did, but I am unsure if that warrants more praise or not. In the end I chose policy A because it did the task much quicker and with much less issue than policy B.'),
(E'a14b4f1e-2ab2-4909-b678-a738bc3dc3fb', E'2025-09-16T17:15:25.318317Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'play the yellow note with the tool in front of you.', E'policy A seemed to be reaching for the far right of the scene for no particular reason. Reaching back and forth in the beginning, but eventually shifting to only fully extending its arm for the rest of the episode. Policy B slowly went for the tool but struggled to grasp it- only grabing it for the first time near the 1/3 or 1/2 way mark and only lifting it a little bit once by the end of the episode. Despite not being able to do much, I give policy B the win because policy A was not able to do anything at all and was acting very strange the whole episode.'),
(E'06f997ee-517d-4731-8d54-9a46adc127ab', E'2025-09-16T17:22:57.846968Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Play the yellow key with the tool in front of you.', E'policy A had decided that it would spend the episode grabbing the orange tile(which is close to the yellow tile). First, policy A approached the xylophone and touched it with its gripper. It was able to touch the yellow gripper with its hand open, but it would also close its hand around the orange tile. Eventualy policy A would freeze on that orange tile for the rest of the episode. policy B had grabbed at the space in between the xylophone and the tool to start the episode, moved towards the tiles but didn''t touch anything and then ended the episode by placing its gripper around the tool. In the end, even though I thought it would be interesting to consider playing the yellow tile with your hand a form of progress, policy B was the only one between the 2 to make actual progress towards the objective, even if it was at the very end. Because of this, i give policy B the win.'),
(E'7178b650-4ef8-418b-81ff-045b28bd1c21', E'2025-09-16T17:32:58.169169Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Play a sound', E'policy A managed, near the halfway point, to begin touching the xylophone. by the 3/4 way mark policy A had attempted to grab the tool but failed and actually made a noticable sound in the process with the quick return of its gripper tongs to their reset posision after the attempted grab. Policy B had spent the entire episode just grabbing at the xylophone, but while I was turned away for a moment I did hear the clink of the xylophone. Because I was able to actually here something from the xylophone, I give policy B the win, even if it did ignore the tool the whole time.'),
(E'765cf528-9008-4e4d-a490-1d8bea5392d5', E'2025-09-16T17:54:51.782842Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Touch the green tile with the screw driver.', E'policy A began by immediatley trying to grab the xylophone and spent the rest of the episode sort of hovering back and forth with its gripper close, amost as if it wanted to touch the green tile. Policy B began the episode by approaching the tool but didn''t grab it, instead sort of moving up and down above it with its gripper around the screwdriver but never grabbing it. About halfway through the episode, policy B gave up tyring to grab the screwdriver and begun approaching the xylophone itself- rotating its gripper and ending the episode with one fingertong over the xylophone and the other over the table surface. I chose policy B because it was able to attempt to grab the tool(somewhat) while policy A could not.'),
(E'a86eae6a-8cbe-47c8-a96d-f88ad05b8ba0', E'2025-09-17T01:35:17.930812Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'close the laptop', E'Policy A seemed to have understood the task, which was to close the lid of the laptop. It correctly positioned its gripper above and behind the laptop lid, and tried to execute a downward motion to close the lid. It wasn''t super smooth, nor did the policy succeed on the first try, but after a few tries it succeeded at closing the laptop lid, which is positive. The 2nd policy (policy B) however did not seem to understand the task, and actually ended up increasing the angle of the laptop screen, eventually reaching an unsafe pose, after which I had to terminate the episode.'),
(E'7393bed9-e49c-49d8-ae64-078dc676c54d', E'2025-09-17T02:18:14.429738Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put all three trays into one stack', E'Both policies were very comparable, policy A just edged out. Policy A spent most of the episode trying to pick up the tray, but grasping at the center of the tray instead of the edge. Thus it was unable to pick up the tray. However at the end of the episode it managed to pick up the tray by the corner, but immedietaly dropped it. The final state was that all three trays were roughly in their same starting position. Policy B understood the task, but always early grasped. Thus it was never able to pick up any of the trays.'),
(E'd1bcc2c2-8bec-4675-b14f-76d0c045936c', E'2025-09-17T20:19:43.167455Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the spoon in the white pot', E'B just started the focus on two of the colored blocks in the center of the table and moved them to the greyish pot. A did a little bit better since it moved towards the spoon but the arm could not move close enough to reach and grasp it'),
(E'b3cd7254-b4a7-4eb5-b13b-ce78cd108e7d', E'2025-09-17T20:30:17.687437Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the green sponge on the whiteboard', E'BOth policies have been good at the point that they recognized the main object of the task (sponge) and tried to grasp it despite many drops and fail of grasping; the sponge did not move significantly from its initial position'),
(E'd41de4e0-a847-4166-8d8f-009c4a737bd0', E'2025-09-17T20:43:03.571513Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stir the cup of coffee', E'Both polciies has disruptively  interuptted the set up as in A, the arm was pushing the cup away off the table and in B, the arm did a little alignment with the task since it tried to grasp the spoon but the cup was also attached along with it'),
(E'ad78b853-01d3-49fe-a739-c872cd3ef22f', E'2025-09-17T20:53:32.952528Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'scoop the cube into cup', E'Two policies did not do so well since both were unable to recognite the task must involve with the stainless steel scooper on the side. A has attempted at least grasping the yellow cup and shifted the position upright to place into the cup but unfortunately the cup has collasped previously. B was just hovering around the scooper and the cup and did not try to do anything'),
(E'8e100551-2a67-4fde-867f-7064e21332bb', E'2025-09-17T21:05:55.979840Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the lid of the donut bowl', E'Policy A only attempted to grasp the scooper despite being asked to manipulate an action with the lid. Policy B briefly touched the lid and push the small seen a little bit away from the view but after that it also reached for the scooper on the left'),
(E'67440f61-0c96-482c-b5d1-4d109dbd8aae', E'2025-09-17T21:23:40.016489Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the tape on the sponge', E'A at least at one point has succesfully grasp the tape up in the air but it laid it down on the edge of the sponge not in the surface. B has reached for the cup the entire time despite having a better light condition'),
(E'0a9d0a6f-ebbf-4516-b189-547a21a96810', E'2025-09-17T21:34:32.953864Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the two bananas altogether', E'A technically moved the two bananas in one place but the approach was quite off the rubric.It must moved only the banana but in this case it moved the entire bowl which contained the banana and place on the other bowl. B has iniitially attempted the grasp one of the banana out but ended up dropping it on the surface'),
(E'77c87eee-64dd-471d-9481-1a33d2627bfb', E'2025-09-17T22:06:43.817873Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeleuy'), E'put the pen next to the scissors', E'B did way better since it accomplished the task within a very short time while A was completely off the point as it reached for cup on the edge of the scene'),
(E'a320c345-99a8-47a5-a6a7-cbba17c5d1bd', E'2025-09-17T23:50:54.446427Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place half of the marshmellows into each bowl.', E'policy A stareted by approaching the cups themselves instead of the marshmellows. policy A would then, over the course of the episode, drift to the far right of the field, fully extending its gripper for no reason. policy A ended the episode with it''s arm still fully extended but also raised to about a 45 degree anlge. Policy B was very slow for the entire episode. Policy B started by grabbing a marshmellow, bringing it all the way to the cup on the far right, and then fumbling it right before dropping it into the cup. After fumbling the marshmellow, policy B would spend the rest of its time either approaching the group of marshmellows or being amongst the marshmellows but never getting close enough to grab any. With this in mind, I give policy B the victory because it was at least able to grab the marshmellow while policy A could not.'),
(E'86ecdd35-f003-411c-a4ae-79871334bfbf', E'2025-09-18T00:02:15.624971Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Split the marshmellows between the two bowls.', E'policy A started by bringin its gripper to the bowl on the right before grabbing a marshmellow on the top right and placing it in said bowl. policy A would then grab the red bowl before placing its hand where the bowl used to be for no good reason. policy B was just very slow. policy B started by taking almost half the episode to grab a marshmellow just to drop it almost immediatley. While policy B was able to grab the marshmellow again, it sort of held on to it for the duration of the episode and was never able to place it into a bowl- although it did try to place it into the bowl on the left. In the end I chose policy A as the winner because, even though it was a little excentric, it was still able to place a marshmellow into a bowl while policy B could not.'),
(E'5175c884-9bff-4a5d-935a-532f206eb65a', E'2025-09-18T00:13:01.308815Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place half of the marshmellows into each of the bowls.', E'policy A started by extending its gripper over the red bowl and then freezing for like 10-20 seconds. After unfreezing near the end of the episode, policy A extended its hand as far as it could for pretty much the rest of the episode in between the two bowls. policy B started by going for the top left marshmellow and trying to place it in the red bowl but couldn''t since it got stuck on its gripper when it tried letting go. After sort of wandering around with the marshmellow in its grasp, policy B ended the episode having finally freeing itself from that marshmellow and had begun moving around again(albiet somewhat aimlessly). In the end I chose policy B since it was actually able to grab a marshmellow while policy A could not.'),
(E'086060c0-8979-46cc-92f2-a19a9dd30d04', E'2025-09-18T00:24:07.335631Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Hide the red ball.', E'Policy A approached the red cup and tried grabbing it but had difficulty getting it''s hand in the right position- often being to far to grab it fully, too high, or having its grippers be misaligned. In the end, policy A was unable to grab the cup and it is uncertain if it knew what to do with it afterwards. Policy B also approached the cup but was much less agressive with the grabbing, only attempting to grab it once the entire episode. In the end I chose policy A because I sincerely thought it made more progress in grabbing than policy B.'),
(E'b0252ca5-4eb6-43dc-9285-049cb843d6ed', E'2025-09-18T00:41:24.496269Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Hide the red ball.', E'policy A started by attempting to grab the red ball somewhat unsuccessfully- grabbing it too far away from it and pushing it away as a result. policy A was only able to grab the ball near the end of the episode and only grabbed it once. policy B also went for the ball but had an easier time grabbing it - placing its hand fully around the ball before grabbing. Policy B was able to grab the ball over 4 times by the end of the episode. policy B also ended up raising its arm up high for no reason at the end of the episode. I chose policy B since it was simply better at doing what both policies decided to do- picking up the ball.'),
(E'8c7767ba-671c-4ecd-9cbd-bca3439538e5', E'2025-09-18T00:49:18.210578Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Hide the red ball using the blue cup.', E'policy A very quickly grabbed the cup but immediatley dropped it. After that first attempt, policy A didn''t really make much more progress, only grabbing one more time at the very end of the episode. policy B, to start, grabbed the red ball very quickly and dropped it near the blue cup. policy B would later slowly approach the blue cup but only try grabbing it once before the end of the episode and failing at that attempt. I chose policy A because it was able to at least attempt to grab the blue cup while policy B did not.'),
(E'cd59be9a-1993-414a-8419-a69cbe5e7faf', E'2025-09-18T02:26:16.587612Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the bottle, then drop it', E'Policy A first took some time to search the target, then moved the robotic arm close to the bottle, touched it, but did not grasp it in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close the bottle, pushed it to make it scroll off from the table.My requirement is to grasp the bottle then drop it, Neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only pushed the bottle, but policy B made the bottle fall off the table while policy A did not.Therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'58e8fc0b-b509-4740-ab4f-1b649daf9f61', E'2025-09-18T03:29:40.677358Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the mouse, then move it  from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the table,  then approached the mouse, as if attempting to grasp it but did not succeed.Next, policy A moved the robotic arm aimlessly during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the mouse, touched it, then moved the robotic arm away and almost stopped during remaining time of the trial.My requirement is to grasp the mouse then move it  from left to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, it seems that policy A at least attempted to grasp the mouse but policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'0381b1f8-e013-4221-b643-33683c0346f0', E'2025-09-18T03:47:08.902789Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the green block onto the box', E'Policy A first took some time to search the target, then moved the robotic arm close to the green block, pushed it, then moved the robotic arm above the green block in the end, as if attempting to grasp it.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the green block,  adjusted posture, grasped it, then moved it toward the book and put it on the book.My requirement is to put the green block onto the box, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5ec15b54-4df7-44e6-88c4-765a56e9ba7e', E'2025-09-18T05:15:51.193666Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the red bottle onto the box', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to table,  then approached the red bottle, moved it toward the box, finally put it onto the box, but the red bottle fell off the box.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the red bottle, grasped and released it several times, but did not lift it up in the end.My requirement is to put the red bottle onto the box, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'66a6418c-b483-4797-b5af-1f93f4ae6312', E'2025-09-18T07:25:34.293362Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the red bottle by 90 degrees', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the bottle, pushed it to make it scroll away.Then policy B approached the box, pushed it.My requirement is to rotate the red bottle by 90 degrees,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least pushed the red bottle while policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'41d49be9-6753-4b0e-bc85-2e626261504f', E'2025-09-18T07:40:26.127794Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pen and move it next to the controller', E'Policy A first moved the robotic arm close to the pen, pushed it to left, then approached the controller, grasped it, moved it toward the pen and put it near the pen.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the pen, grasped it, moved it toward the controller, pushed the controller away, then put the pen on the table close to the controller in the end.My requirement is to grasp the pen and move it next to the controller, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully while policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'28fbfea3-5d83-4a44-95c9-7fab6f0b3d63', E'2025-09-18T08:38:04.222019Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the green block, then put it into the cup', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the green block, grasped and release it several times.Then policy A almost stopped above the green block during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the green block then put it into the cup,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasp the green block while policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'cbb851ae-594a-4f5d-8681-978d4c548e07', E'2025-09-18T08:48:57.069074Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pen from left to right, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the table,  moved slightly above the table during most time of the trial, then approach the edge of the table in the end.My requirement is to move the pen from left to right then rotate it by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the robotic arm while policy A did not show any response.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'663df041-25ae-4342-8d53-ead433306e80', E'2025-09-18T23:20:29.157305Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Make the cup upright', E'Policy A was able to pick up the cup while Policy B was unable to pick up the cup and only attempted to approuch the cup. Both policies were unable to make the cup upright.'),
(E'c6a185c8-fccb-49ea-8263-350b7f0b9f55', E'2025-09-18T23:33:26.633281Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the cup in the dishwasher', E'Policy A picked up the cup but only briefly and let it go, after that it struggled to replicate picking up the cup again. Policy B was able to pick up the cup and attempted to carry it over to the dishwasher. However, when moving towards the dishwasher, the Policy didn''t lift the cup high enough and just dropped the cup to the table. Ultimately, Policy B did better than the Policy A.'),
(E'5edc6bd9-341f-47a6-b1a4-0b839c794b12', E'2025-09-18T23:45:31.200422Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put the coffee bag on the plate', E'Policy A did better than Policy B. Policy A approuched the coffee bag and attempted to pick it up but was unable to. However, after approuching to pick up the coffee bag, the policy gave up and went to pick up the cup and put that into the plate. Policy B did not approuch the coffee bag at all which makes it not bettethan Policy A and the policy approuched the fork, putting that into the plate. Policy A attempted the instructions provided while Policy B ignored it and put something different on the plate, not showing any signs of approuching the coffee bag.'),
(E'84203798-763e-4072-94dd-527a8930257c', E'2025-09-19T00:13:06.305335Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape in the container.', E'Policy B did better than Policy A. Both polices picked up the tape and tried to put the tape into the container. However, the difference is that Policy B dropped of the tape closer to the container whereas Policy A dropped the tape off much further away when both policies attemped to put the tape in the container. Thus, Policy B did marginally better!'),
(E'8b101bde-8b74-4b5c-85cc-f44e808481de', E'2025-09-19T00:24:49.071805Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the tape off the paper it is currently on.', E'\\Policy A did better than Policyttemped to pick up the tape and was approuching it but unsuccessful in picking it up and putting it on the table. However, Policy B did not at any point go near the tape and the policy was going towards other objects, ignoring to pick up the given task to pick up the tape. Thus, Policy A did better than Policy B as it attempted to pick up the tape whereas Policy B ignored it.'),
(E'309b427e-8652-493d-b4e4-fa0feea96292', E'2025-09-19T00:39:02.379630Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'Put the stapler inside the container', E'Policy A did signficantly better than Policy B. Policy A was able to pick up the stapler and attempted it to put it into the container. However, Policy B only approuched to the stapler but was unsuccessful in picking it up at all. Thus, Policy B was able to almost do the full task, whereas, Policy A was unable to even pick up the stapler.'),
(E'a01141b5-5429-49ca-8a26-0690b0de896c', E'2025-09-19T20:43:22.546878Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and place it into the cup.', E'For some reason policy A approached the cup first knocking and then sort of erratically moved around the field afterwards till the end episode. policy B also approached the cup and sort of lingered near it, opening and closing its gripper. Since both policies made about the same amount of progress(only approaching the cup) I gave them a tie.'),
(E'6701e266-bb3b-4d4e-856d-c456bf0ff542', E'2025-09-19T22:14:06.276993Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the marker inside of the holder into the red cup.', E'policy A started by immediatley attacking the red cup and knocking it over. After doing that, policy A raised its arm, bent its gripper inwards at a 45 degree angle and froze there for the duration of the episode. policy B was pretty much frozen the entire time. Because policy A was at least able to move, I chose policy A.'),
(E'f669968f-01a6-4a41-af2b-2cb4cd80ce4b', E'2025-09-19T22:24:32.074898Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and place into the cup', E'policy A started by quickly overshooting the marker and trying to grab. Policy A would then stay near the marker and try to grab it for the rest of the episode, making contact and getting pretty close to a solid grasp, but never stabilizing at one. I would say policy A was very quick and might have had difficulty grabbing as a result. Policy B on the other hand was very slow, taking a fourth of the time, just to grab in the center of the field. After that, policy B spent most the episode gently pushing/rubbing against the red cup, almost as if it were pushing it off the table, before opening/ raising its gripper to end the episode. In the end I chose policy A because it was able to try and grab the marker while policy B did not.'),
(E'2e7396e4-d94c-486d-a459-03ce80ca8765', E'2025-09-19T22:36:53.486610Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'pick up the smaller bread and place it on the plate.', E'policy A started by grabbing the biggest bread and placing that on the plate before very quickly switching to the small bread and placing that on the late at about 66% done. policy A would then retract its hand and end the episode in a somewhat neutral position near the reset position. policy B moved a little in the beginning of the episode but then didn''t do anything else for the rest of the episode. Since policy A was actually able to make progress towards the objective, I chose policy A.'),
(E'31e16d47-b0e1-4d2a-a137-9f3201da8abb', E'2025-09-19T22:43:26.899700Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the smallest bread and place it on the plate.', E'policy A started by calmly grabbing the small bread and placing it onto the plate without issue. For the rest of the episode, policy A sort of pushed the plate a litte bit forward before returning back to a starting position. policy B started by slowly grabbing the large bread a little before sort of hovering above it and opening/closing its gripper. Policy B would spend the rest of the time occupying the time in between the large bread and the plate, occasionally grabbing at nothing or just sort of slowly drifting around in the space.  In the end I chose policy A because it accomplished the task without any issue while policy B could not.'),
(E'9612b5bb-e334-4759-adb0-87e2dec06fd7', E'2025-09-19T22:52:18.279418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the largest bread and place it onto the plate.', E'policy A moved forwards a little before freezing for the rest of the episode. policy B started by grabbing the smallest bread (which was in the bottom left corner closest to the robot) before spend of the rest of the time randomly grabbing at the empty space on the right side of the plate for the rest of the episode. In the end I chose policy B because it was able to do something while policy A could not.'),
(E'3610ff4d-43bd-4c98-af69-32369d1ca258', E'2025-09-19T23:05:31.456208Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the largest bread and put it on the plate.', E'policy A started by grabbing the largest bread and putting on the plate without issue. After doing that, policy A sort of sporadically moved around the scene, not seeming to know what to do with itself after doing the task. policy B also grabbed the big bread but then dropped it before bringing it to the plate. After dropping the big bread, policy B would change to the small bread and end the episode by dropping the small bread onto the place. In the end I chose policy A because it was able to do the whole task without issue while policy B could not finish the task.'),
(E'bc8e3cd3-416a-45b1-9d33-cf07527752dd', E'2025-09-19T23:16:10.973632Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the small bread and place it onto the plate.', E'policy A started by picking up the big bread and placing it onto the plate and then, by the end of the episode, placed the small bread onto the plate. policy B pretty much did the exact same thing, so I gave them a tie.'),
(E'2489b752-ce2b-4698-9987-1d993e7ef576', E'2025-09-19T23:31:25.365392Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'pick up the cookies', E'policy A knocked down the orange juice in attempts to grab before going to the poky sticks and grabbing those. policy B had sort of manuevered its hand around the cookies but never really got close to grabbing them or anything. policy A moved around a lot, even knocking over the poky sticks and would angle its hand in weird ways that pointed to the cookies. In the end, I chose policy A because it was able to grab something, and it had gotten just as close to the cookies as policy B.'),
(E'8d2bb4d4-5a69-4364-bf31-0540a9e03d28', E'2025-09-19T23:57:24.202225Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the cookies.', E'policy A started by approaching th orange juice and poky sticks and knocked over the poky sticks. After knocking the poky sticks, policy A spent the rest of the episode picking it up, droping it and trying to pick it up again. Policy B had very slowly moved to the poky sticks and, without dropping it, grabbed and lifted the poky sticks. Policy A would then spend the rest of the episode trying to grab the poky sticks. With that being said, I chose to give the policies a tie because they both did the same amount of progress, although in different ways.'),
(E'22a7f350-a7c6-4bd6-9e25-ad9e026f50c8', E'2025-09-20T00:10:43.398838Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'grab the orange juice', E'policy A started by ignoring the orange juice and grabbing the poky sticks which were in the center of the field and then continued grabbing at it for the rest of the episode. policy B started by going to the orange juice but then pivoted towards the poky sticks. After going to the poky sticks, policy B pressed on the cookies and somehow rotated the entire field leaving only the orange juice up right. Finally, policy B approached the direction of the orange juice and the poky sticks and, while pressing on the poky sticks, would touch the orange juice right at the end of the episode. In the end, I chose policy B because it was able to start moving in the direction of the orange juice and even touch it while policy A could not.'),
(E'37333cd6-bfb8-4486-a37c-502256fc7503', E'2025-09-20T00:18:30.251672Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'grab the poky sticks that are behind the orange juice and the cookies.', E'policy A sort of inched its gripper towards itself for less than half of the episode before doing nothing for the rest of the episode. policy B started by grabbing the cookes and then almost angled it towards the right camera(which was the default 3rd perspective camera). After doing that, policy B sort of fully extended its arm at a 45 degree angle while bending its gripper towards the robot at a 20 degree angle and holding it there for the rest of the episode. In the end I chose policy B because it was able to do something while policy A did nothing.'),
(E'3288af0d-014d-4fae-a744-d9a3e45ee504', E'2025-09-20T00:26:21.690596Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Grab the orange juice.', E'policy A started by knocking over the cookies before placing its gripper behind the orange juice(from the perspective of the 3rd person camera) and began to grab. After failing to grab anything, policy A left the orange juice and began grabbing at the box of cookies for the rest of the episode. policy B started by trying to grab the orange juice, but ended up pushing it over instead. For the rest of the episode, policy B would inch in the dirction of the orange juice, but never get close enough to actually grab the orange juice- almost as if there was an invisible wall between the gripper and the orange juice. In the end I chose policy B for the victory since it did touch the orange juice and seemed to approach the orange juice entire time while policy A spent a long time going for the cookies.'),
(E'2dff40a0-18a4-4125-a3b3-b0e087ae48d1', E'2025-09-20T00:36:45.080650Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'topple all of the boxes and pick up the coke can.', E'policy A began the episode by knocking over the poky''s box, then the cookies box before getting really close to grabbing the coke can. policy A was not able to grab the coke can then, but after some time and some meandering, it finally could right towards the end of the episode. policy B started  by pressing on the orange juice and eventually pushed everything, including the coke can, in one fell swoop. After knocking everything over, policy B grabbed at the can for the rest of the episode. I chose policy B because it was able to do everything while policy A was able to do everything but knock over the orange juice.'),
(E'87215abf-cd9e-43d8-ab79-84752bb9fe92', E'2025-09-20T00:46:06.467059Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Knock over all of the boxes and pick up the coke can.', E'policy A started by moving back and forth before grabbing at the orange juice, knocking it over in the process. policy A would then grab at the orange juice for most of the rest of episode, seemingly going to do that for the rest of the episode. Then, somehow miraculously, policy A touched the can and inadvertently knocked over both of the other boxes. Having exposed the can, policy A was able to then end the episode with its gripper around the can about to grab. policy B pushed down against the orange juice and the poky sticks to knock both of them over. Then about halfway through the episode, policy B would knock over the cookies and the cup, getting as far as it would for the remainder of the episode. In the end I would chose policy A because while being able to knock over all of the boxes, policy A was also able to start grabbing the coke can while policy B was not even able to approach the coke can.'),
(E'4ad791c3-957f-41a1-856f-628be60e3883', E'2025-09-20T00:56:07.151407Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the tree.', E'policy A started by going to the  upper right and pressing down on the table while grabbing. policy would do this for a little over half the episode before approaching he knife, but, even after approaching the knife, policy A would sort of pace up and down above the knife and would never grab the knife. policy B started by grabbing the plant and carrying it around. policy B would meander around the left half of the field for over half of the episode before dropping the plant and then starting again. Policy B would finish the episode with the plant in its hand. I chose policy A because even though it was erratic and going weird places, it was able to identify the tool needed to cut the plant and make an attempt at grabbing it.'),
(E'4c093637-08bb-4a6a-af4e-702c6cb05348', E'2025-09-20T01:03:47.440445Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Cut the plant with the knife.', E'policy A started by grabbbing the blade of the knife and lifting it. After droping the knife, policy A would spend much of its time sort of hovering above the knife, trying to grab. policy A only grabbed the knife one more time before the end of the episode and was not able to lift it. Policy B very quickly grabbed the knife by the handle and moved it to the bottom left of the field. While policy B would not be able to do anything more than grab the knife(which it was able to do successfully), because it was able to grab the knife in a more reasonable place and actually move the knife, I gave policy B the win.'),
(E'1126ae49-ace9-482b-8cb4-2f864f3ff700', E'2025-09-20T04:55:34.295507Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the box, then grasp controller', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the box, pressed its edge to made it turn over.Then policy A approached the controller, grasped and dropped it.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the controller, touched it, then moved slightly around the controller until rime ran out, as if attempting to grasp it, but did not grasp in the end.My requirement is to grasp the box then grasp controller, neither policy was able to complete the full task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped one required object whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'23356920-8b1e-4712-8510-2a52ac3a334c', E'2025-09-20T05:19:52.166715Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to pen, grasped it, moved it to right, then put it on the table.Next, policy A almost stopped near the edge of the table during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the table, then approached the pen, grasped it, moved it slowly to right until time ran out.My requirement is to move the pen from left to right, both policies have completed the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A performed the operations more smoothly than policy B did.Therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'7ddd90c3-5203-401b-ba1d-405ccf365483', E'2025-09-20T05:34:06.746281Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden blocks onto the big box', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to one wooden block, grasped it, moved it toward the big box, then put it onto the box.Next, policy A pushed the box,moved the gripper around the box until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper to the box, pushed it, then moved the gripper aimlessly during most remaining time of the trial.My requirement is to put all the wooden blocks onto the big box, there are two wooden blocks in total.Neither policy was able to complete the task, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least put one wooden block onto the box whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9f4c7a3f-67e4-40e3-8cc4-829eb41cc54f', E'2025-09-20T05:56:45.810009Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two boxes', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not performed any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the table, moved on the table slightly, then almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to stack up the two boxes, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the gripper whereas policy A did not take any action.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'faf27b00-c7c9-442c-9832-9bdf22f53576', E'2025-09-20T06:11:59.566647Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the pen, grasped it, then slowly rotated it by about 270 degrees until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the pen, grasped it, then rotated it by about 180 degrees during remaining time of the trial.My requirement is to rotate the pen by 90 degrees,neither policies has rotated the pen by the correct angle.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A rotated the pen by 270 degrees which is equal to -90 degrees, whereas policy B rotated the pen by 180 degrees.Therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'deb3c5ab-4f95-4453-b943-0accda701640', E'2025-09-20T06:49:25.993246Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pen and move it next to the controller', E'Policy A first took some time to find the target, then moved the gripper close to the pen as if attempting to grasp it, but did not grasp it in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the controller, pushed it, then moved the gripper back and stopped during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the pen and move it next to the controller, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the pen and attempted to grasp the pen, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'e3b388d9-5539-4f7c-a5d4-f31b2be87911', E'2025-09-20T21:34:46.644105Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the coke onto the sponge and take the sprite off of the sponge.', E'policy A started by grabbing the coke can and lifting it very slightly. policy A never lifted the coke can high enough to actually place it onto the sponge, so it would push the can forward almost in an attempt to place it onto the sponge. Policy A would pick move back and forth to pick up the sponge a couple times, but never make any more progress than what was already mentioned. policy B also started with the coke can but moved much slower and grabbed it in a much less stable grasp. Despite all of this, policy B was actually able to lift the can higher than policy A(greater than 4 cm), and, because of this, I give policy B the victory.'),
(E'5e30cc33-018e-465c-8925-31ce0d816ad7', E'2025-09-20T21:51:12.542793Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place the coke onto the sponge and remove the sprite from the top of the sponge.', E'policy A started by grabbing the can lifting it on its second attempt and then sort of lifting it around, moving it to the bottom left and the middle right before dropping it and nearly having it roll of the table. At the end of the episode, policy A was also able to knock off the sprite from the sponge that, while not quite what I was intending, is technically correct.policy B started by slowly grabbing the coke can. At some point after repeatedly trying to grab at the coke can with mixed success, policy A grabbed the coke can and lifted it in a way that tilted the sponge knocking the sprite off. policy A would then end the episode by going to grab the sprite. Since policy A was able to actually lift the coke can a reasonable height and move it around, I give policy A the victory.'),
(E'a19d6a44-944e-4e6f-9099-05e3595ba3e4', E'2025-09-20T22:01:33.834765Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place both of the cans onto the sponge.', E'policy A started with the coke can and barely picked it up. Policy A would continue to pick up and drop the coke can for the duration of the episode, getting pretty close to placing the coke can onto the sponge on its second attempt but not raising it high enough to do it. policy B started by quickly brushing past the sprite and then quickly brushing past the coke can, causing them to both be knocked over. policy B would then move pretty erratically for the remainder of the episode, and even begin pushing the foam tiles that everything was sitting on top of off the table. In the end, since policy A was able to at least start picking stuff up, I chose to give policy A the victory.'),
(E'c70a770f-8ca3-4f62-bae1-5fadc7c57102', E'2025-09-20T22:08:13.246617Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Place both cans onto the sponge.', E'policy A started by slowly moving towards the coke can and putting it onto the edge of the sponge, but, since it didn''t fully put it on the sponge, it fell off. Despite that, policy A was able to be the first policy I have seen place a can onto the sponge by grabbing the fallen coke can and placing it horizontally on the sponge. Policy A was even able to begin grabbing the sprite can but wasn''t able to get a good grasp since one of its fingers would get stuck on the brim of the can as it lowered its hand over the can. policy B started by approaching the coke can and sort of pushing up against it, but not grabbing it. After trying once with the coke can, policy B moved onto the sprite can and pushed it into the sponge, eventually knocking it over. After knocking it over, policy B would move back and forth over the sprite can but never pick it up. With that in mind, I chose policy A because it was able to actually place a can onto the sponge, something I have never seen before in 4 trials of placing cans onto sponges!'),
(E'16b03b15-1970-4fc3-961f-389dd185fc4b', E'2025-09-20T22:16:35.537212Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Type a space.', E'policy A started by sort of pressing down on the bottom right of the tile and would sort of stay their for most of the episode, only moving around slightly at the end. policy B pretty much did the same thing, but instead was near the bottom center of the feild and moved up and down much more. Policy B also would press its fingers together and push on the table towards the end of the episode. Because policy B was able to get a little closer to the space bar and bring its gripper into a closed formation(better for pressing a key), I will give it the victory- even if it was only by an extra 5% completion.'),
(E'a2b9dbe1-326e-4fad-805d-95889983a2cc', E'2025-09-20T22:23:22.569471Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Type a space on the keyboard with your gippers closed.', E'policy A approached the keyboard and when it got close closed its gripper. When it did this the first time, it would move sort of to the bottom right of the keyboard, and slowly drift towards the center near the end of the episode. The closest policy A ever got was that it was abot 3-4 inches above the space bar with its gripper closed. Policy A was never able to press a key on the keyboard. policy B for some reason moved towards the bottom left(towards me and my keyboard) before quickly moving to the opposite side. Policy B would then move erratically for the rest of the episode. Because policy A was actually able to approach the keyboard, I gave policy A the victory.'),
(E'dbbc9911-c3e4-4573-8c03-5622b51eb6a5', E'2025-09-20T22:29:27.424187Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Press the space bar on the keyboard.', E'policy A started by quickly pressing its fingers onto the arrow keys before moving to other parts of the keyboard. policy A would eventually press the space bar in sort of rubbing its closed fingers along the keys of the keyboard. policy B started by pressing onto the tile near the bottom right corner of the keyboard. policy B would then press the arrow keys once before sort of meandering around the field for the remainder of the episode. Since policy A was actuallly able to do the task, I give policy A the victory.'),
(E'733f65c6-f8aa-4f7c-8bac-7945420b0cf2', E'2025-09-20T22:37:43.067876Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Take the marker out of the holder and put it into the red cup.', E'policy A kind of just did nothing. policy B started by approaching the marker and holder and sort of grabbing near the marker, but mostly grabbing the holder. After not being able to grab the marker, policy B sort of closed its gripper and then moved over the cup with its gripper angled towards itself. Since policy B wa able to do something, I give policy B the victory.'),
(E'7b8e7b96-77b1-43c0-b4ab-5dc12c142dad', E'2025-09-20T22:46:21.669138Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the marker and put it into the red cup.', E'policy A sort of moved its gripper to the far right for no particular reason. policy A would keep it there for over half of the episode before closing its gripper and pacing up and down above the cup. policy B sort of did nothing for the entire episode. Because policy A was able to do something, I give policy A the victory.'),
(E'3e096519-c704-4b02-923b-0ec2386ac72a', E'2025-09-20T22:51:40.377847Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the sponge until it touches the white block.', E'policy A started by pressing on the top of the sponge and moving it. policy A would then move its hand back a little and then approach the sponge from the front, pushing the sponge against the white block. For the rest of the episode, policy A would kind of push the block forward from the top. policy B would press directly on top of the block without moving the sponge for almost half the episode before approaching the sponge from the front and pushing it to the white block near the end of the episode. While policy A was able to complete the objective much faster than policy B, since they did the same amount of progress by the end of the episode, I must give them the tie.'),
(E'95369811-9a57-4969-ab57-107537a64e15', E'2025-09-22T01:06:32.717014Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pen, then grasp wooden block', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the cable of of camera, after hesitating for while, grasped the cable in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the pen, grasped and released it.Then policy B approached the table and stopped on the table during remaining time of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the pen then grasp wooden block,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped one required object whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'50e0b610-1c7d-4c82-b424-e105d19ab44b', E'2025-09-22T01:18:40.890978Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the pen from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the pen, pushed it, grasped it, then moved it to right and put it on the table in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper to the pen, pushed it to left,then policy B moved the gripper away, and stopped near the edge of the table during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to move the pen from left to right, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully while policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'4fc0ff37-6524-49cd-ac07-fbd3b784abfa', E'2025-09-22T01:55:38.141666Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the wooden blocks onto the big box', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to one wooden block, grasped it,  moved it to the big box, put it onto the big box.Then policy A approached another wooden block, picked it up, moved it to the big box and put it onto the big box.Policy B first moved the gripper near one wooden block, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to put all the wooden blocks onto the big box, there are two wooden blocks in total. When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the full task successfully whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'6771f719-2650-4d02-8628-9cbe1d292f83', E'2025-09-22T02:22:10.613981Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two wooden blocks', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to one wooden block, pushed it, then grasped and released it.Next, policy A approached another wooden block until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the table, after hesitating for while, approached and picked up one wooden block, then dropped it on the table in the end.My instruction is to stack up the two wooden blocks, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only grasped one wooden block, but it seems that policy A identified the two wooden blocks whereas policy B only identified one wooden block.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'39ebf83a-80dd-443c-9ac9-1b8716e19816', E'2025-09-22T02:33:46.847525Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the wooden block by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the wooden block, grasped and dropped it, then grasped it  again, rotated it by about 180 degrees until time ran out.Policy B first paused for a while, then approached the table, closed and opened the gripper several times during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to rotate the wooden block by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'fe913c4b-1ef4-4c20-a986-b1f0b396e7ca', E'2025-09-22T02:46:37.760202Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pen and move it close to the controller', E'Policy A first moved the gripper randomly as if searching the target, then approached a wooden block rather than the pen.Policy B first took some time to find the target,  moved the gripper close to the pen, then moved away, after hesitating for while,approached the controller and pushed it.My instruction is to grasp the pen and move it close to the controller,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the pen and the controller whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'9c3ad887-b3b6-426a-a9f7-72fe68b99d91', E'2025-09-22T02:59:14.025308Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the wooden block,  then place it onto the controller', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the table, after hesitating for a while, approached the controller and pushed it.Then policy A moved slightly near the edge of the table until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper back and forth as if searching the target, then touched the controller.Next, policy B moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to grasp the wooden block then place it onto the controller, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only pushed or touched the controller, their performance is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'c4f31c3c-e9e5-4185-937e-e08742a59123', E'2025-09-22T07:01:56.124144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the marker pen, grasped it, then rotated it by a small angle, dropped it on the table, causing it to fall off the table.My instruction is to rotate the marker pen by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'f0cb79ff-f0a8-41a6-8d95-f84d97c368a0', E'2025-09-22T07:17:38.880895Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put all the fruits to the right side of the table', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the banana, then moved the gripper back and forth during remaining time of the episode, as if searching the target.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to put all the fruits to the right side of the table, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not respond at all.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'7923b042-641a-43ad-8847-ad12d1c0655c', E'2025-09-22T07:27:02.134562Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the cube then drop it', E'Policy A first took some time to find the target, then moved the gripper close to cube, grasped it, moved it,and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the trial, as if could not find the target.My requirement is to grasp the cube then drop it, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully whereas policy B failed.Therefore,policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'6e7fe569-9422-454d-84d8-6ff00e3f0086', E'2025-09-22T07:48:21.207271Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the cube from left side to right side of the table', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the cube, attempted to grasp it, but caused it to fall off the table.Then policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the cube, pushed it, grasped and released it.Then policy B moved the gripper away  and grasped the curtains.My requirement is to move the cube from left side to right side of the table, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the cube whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e4fb8d5f-f11f-4a1f-8291-8314351bb461', E'2025-09-22T08:03:26.580279Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the all the fruits together', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the robotic arm randomly as if searching the target, then approached the peach, attempted to grasped it, but caused it to fall off the table.My instruction is to put the all the fruits together, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the peach whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'8de12a6b-c513-4bf7-bd35-8ce73e61c5bd', E'2025-09-22T08:15:37.647036Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana onto the white box', E'Policy A first moved the gripper slightly, then stopped during the remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the edge of the table, then moved the gripper randomly, as if could not find the target.My requirement is to put the banana onto the white box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the gripper whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'15c6eb45-d79e-4367-8488-298cd5397630', E'2025-09-22T08:36:57.851380Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana  by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to banana, pushed it to make it rotate, then grasped it, rotated it by about 90 degrees, put it on the table.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it, then slowly rotated it by a small angle until time ran out.My instruction is to rotate the banana  by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two,policy A completed the task successfully whereas policy B did not rotate the banana by required angle.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'57546b0e-a833-4413-9aee-171881d7c18d', E'2025-09-22T09:14:16.988765Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the white box, then drop it on floor', E'Policy A moved the gripper randomly during most time of the trial,then stopped in the end, as if could not find the target.Policy B also moved the robotic arm aimlessly during entire time  of the episode.My requirement is to grasp the white box then drop it on floor, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have only moved the gripper randomly but did not do anything relevant.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'f5c7635a-9a82-4be3-af38-0fb6cfeaf411', E'2025-09-22T09:24:00.042481Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana and put it onto the  box', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to left, then dropped it on floor.My instruction is to grasp the banana and put it onto the  box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the banana whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'b194b1f6-f74f-4fe6-bfde-462acf2bc7da', E'2025-09-22T09:37:16.025184Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the towel, then wipe the table with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the towel, touched it, after hesitating for while, grasped and released the towel several times.Policy B first moved the robotic arm close to the towel grasped it, moved it, and dropped on floor.Then policy B moved the gripper aimlessly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to grasp the towel then wipe the table with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B grasped and moved the towel whereas policy A only grasped the towel.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'fb83e3d1-24c9-4d04-81fe-5b69e8388a99', E'2025-09-22T09:49:34.782150Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the curtain,then moved the gripper aimlessly during most time of the episode.Next, policy A moved the gripper toward the banana as if found the target, but time ran out.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to grasp the banana then put it into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the robotic arm whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'8b5c905b-62f9-4a8c-9527-70738af0cbe6', E'2025-09-22T10:08:22.555748Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the white power adapter into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the curtains, then moved the gripper aimlessly during most time of the trial, and grasped a controller in the end.Policy B first moved the robotic arm randomly, then approached the curtains, as if attempted to grasp it until time ran out.My requirement is to put the white power adapter into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasped a wrong object while policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'0ae0a1cc-7808-48ab-979b-874ea20f5665', E'2025-09-22T17:45:38.959798Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'dispense handsanitizer.', E'policy A slowly approached the hand sanitizer and proceeded to grab it. While grabbing and releasing for the entire episode, it was able to dispense hand sanitizer by pressing down slightly while grabbing the sanitizer, completing the task. For the remainder of the episode, the hand sanitizer got stuck to the gripper and policy A sort of drifted in space while grabbing and releasing its gripper. policy B approached the side of of the hand santizer and sort of rubbed it for a while in a top-down motion. Eventually the rubbing stopped and policy B just decided to push the hand sanitizer bottle off the table. In the end I chose policy A as it was able to actually dispense some sanitizer.'),
(E'33ce131e-a1d3-425f-a620-ab6e2a8b7471', E'2025-09-22T17:54:49.580179Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the white cube into the sponge without causing the cube to fall off the sponge.', E'policy A did nothing. policy B started by moving towards the white cube and back again. The rest of the episode can be characterized by policy B quickly moving forward, back, and upwards repeatedly while occasionally pushing the white cube. It is also worth mentioning that policy B was very close to pushing the cube off of the sponge since it applied an uneven force with a singular tong of its gripper.'),
(E'b224da9b-f28a-476b-a953-4b706d623150', E'2025-09-22T18:02:04.803723Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the white cube to the red cup.', E'policy A started by trying to grab the white cube. After this, it would repeate a cycle of drifting forwards, pulling back, and approaching the block. policy A was not able to make any real progress only touching the block 2-3 times and not moving it more than an inch. policy B moved much slower to the the block and decided to grab and lift it to the cup, actually going so far as to put it inside of the cup. Later policy B would grab the cup as well and end up dropping it off the side of the table. In the end I am going to give policy A the victory. I do this because policy A seemed to actually try and push the block while policy B had grabbed it instead. This is important because the spirit of this evaluation was trying to see how well the policies did actions other than simply grabbing things, to which I believe policy A did a better job.'),
(E'b010eece-0eb1-47cb-af11-19965f504548', E'2025-09-22T18:11:08.484533Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Push the white block to the red cup.', E'policy A started by grabbing the cup. After grabbing the cup policy A drifted very slowly to the white cube and dropped it into the cup near the end of the episode. policy B did the exact same thing except it didn''t even bother grabbing the cup and was able to drop the white cube into the cup much faster than policy A. That being said, the spirit of this evaluation was to see how well the policies could do tasks that did not involve grasping, and since both polices decided to grab the cube and place it into the cup, I am giving them a tie.'),
(E'467e6cae-e9fb-4980-8064-36ae5b5d98c3', E'2025-09-22T18:19:16.815152Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'grab the cup by the handle and give it to me', E'policy A was very slow and spent most of its time grasping the lid of the cup, lifting it slightly, or drifting around the lid in order to grab it. policy A never moved the cup towards me.Policy B did much the same as policy A- grasping the lid of the cup, lifting it slightly, or drifting around the lid in order to grab it- but policy B actually managed to bring the cup towards me a little, and, because of that, I give policy B the victory.'),
(E'f1c70a58-cc1c-42ad-9d46-8500ac1b0232', E'2025-09-22T18:28:13.830559Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'put the trash onto the plate.', E'policy A started by going for the k-cup and then drifting a bit forward. policy A would then start drifiting forward and to the right for the rest of the episode, ending the episode near the far right corner of the table. policy B did nothing. Since policy A could actually touch one of the items of trash, I give policy A the victory.'),
(E'c1501346-7f51-48ad-8581-a93716664582', E'2025-09-22T18:40:14.459961Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the trash and place it onto the plate', E'policy A started by grabbing the plastic bag and bringing it to the plastic bottle. policy A would then interact with the bag and bottle for the rest of the episode - kind of pushing on them grabbing at them but not really moving them, all while ignoring the plate entirley. policy B had attempted to grab the plastic bottle, but couldn''t get its gripper around the bottle and kind of fumbled at it as a result. After fumbling around, policy B actually ended up pushing the bottle off the table and would then keep its arm fully extended an pointed to the far right for the rest of the episode. Since policy A was actually able to grab at trash and make contact with two pieces of trash, I gave the victory to policy A.'),
(E'58a51d7d-b7a7-4507-9502-ab95db621387', E'2025-09-22T18:51:38.300854Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Pick up the trash and place it onto the plate.', E'policy A started by attempting to grab the small aluminum lid. It would take about half of the episode for it to grab the small aluminum lid(likely due to its size) and then it would take the other half to drop it onto the plate. I suppose this is because policy A moved very slowly and wasn''t able to move the lid to the plate on its first attempt, but takeing a second attempt after the first successfull lift attempt to do the whole motion successfully. policy B also grabbed the small aluminum lid but did it pretty quick and with one fell swoop. policy B was then able to quickly grab the plastic bag and deposit that as well in one fell swoop. policy B would then move its hand back to the reset position to end the episode. With that in mind, I chose policy B becuase it was able to do so much more than policy A.'),
(E'b8f5e8b4-b378-4884-8e9a-9abf119063cb', E'2025-09-22T19:01:21.649430Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Topple the sponge with the screwdriver.', E'policy A started by grabbing the corner of the sponge and eventually knocking it over. policy A would then spend the rest of the time, pacing back and forth between the center of the field and the sponge, but also never grabbing the sponge again. policy B also went for the sponge, but instead grabbed it by the center. At some point halfway through the episode- after policy B was done grabbing the sponge- policy B approached the screwdriver, grabbed it, and actually begun pushing the screwdriver against the sponge near the end of the episode. Since policy B was actually able to grab the screwdriver and press it against the sponge, I give policy B the victory.'),
(E'10c81c85-25c4-4a44-bfc6-6aa7de64e95a', E'2025-09-22T19:08:53.899358Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UT Austin'), E'Topple the sponge with the screwdriver.', E'policy A decided to extend its hand to the far left of the field and grab. After this, policy A would raise its gripper almost 2 feet off the ground and begin to approach the sponge, but, since it was too high, policy A didn''t end up doing anything. policy A ended with its gripper above the sponge by about 6-7 inches. policy B started by grabbing the screw driver and was able to lift it on its first try and even move it-albiet to the right. For the rest of the episode policy B would try grabbing the screw driver, succeeding occasionally but usually in a way that would lead to it dropping the screwdriver. By the end of the episode policy B probably moved the screw driver a max of 3 inches from where it dropped it after that first successful grasp attempt. Despite its troubles, I gave policy B the victory because it was able to grab the screw driver while policy A could not.'),
(E'bf4f3b7d-2e4e-442d-b694-d8683e5cdba7', E'2025-09-22T20:07:58.436850Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'pour the water into bowl', E'Policy b somewhat do an orientation that is relevant to the task; it reach for the bowl and tried to hold it up air. Policy A just remained unchanged from the initial position while being asked to pour the water from one of the plastic cup to bowl'),
(E'e4b971a9-1d0a-444a-b315-f38bfdd60548', E'2025-09-22T20:16:33.849480Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'make a bowl of watermelon slices for dessert', E'A did much better sin ce it completed the task within the time interval and the efficiency is much better as policy took longer to execute but the watermelon still lied on the table; it was moved from the right to left'),
(E'a9acb1e2-2b1d-4614-b1d9-9a9e56d06b2c', E'2025-09-22T20:28:53.192318Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'wipe out the water spill', E'Both policies has succesfully performed wipng motion on the area of the water spill but the water was not completely cleaned up. There is still area where a little drop of water has not been touched'),
(E'58787e54-e2ea-4fb5-bdba-06e90564f764', E'2025-09-22T20:36:54.605750Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'flip the bowl upside down to cover the fruit', E'Policy A has done the flipping motion on the bowl but the final destination was quite off since the bowl was just covered nothing and sitting next to the straeberry. Policy B just pushed the bowl inwards and forwards from the camera view  without having focus to the strawberry position'),
(E'a0f81c44-45a0-488e-bc88-489dc79249ba', E'2025-09-22T20:52:39.488698Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the canned beans lid', E'BOth policies failed to reach for the lid which was placed at the center view in the seen. Policy A has pushed the canned food to the left while interacting with the strawberry alongside, making it contained in the bowl at the end. Policy B also pushed the canned beans forwards but it eventually reached for the lid at the very end - the arm has not yet been in touch with the lid'),
(E'17919042-74ed-4dd7-a7e4-1dd2a5eef285', E'2025-09-22T21:00:36.383137Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the kidney bean next to the strawberry', E'Both policies has not even close interpreting the task correctly. A reached for the purple bowl at times and ignored the beans which was placed inside the can. B similarly follow the off-track movement as it reached for the textbook at the edge'),
(E'85e17c30-4b77-4eea-a172-11dcbe734d00', E'2025-09-22T21:11:18.186449Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'open the textbook', E'BOth policies has correctly turned pages to pages of the book but policy A just touched on the cover and the first page so it would not count as a opened book; policy B did better since it turned over a few pages along with the cover'),
(E'89e88768-80be-49d6-9ab2-1a6d408ee75f', E'2025-09-22T21:21:23.977923Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'push the tape towards the waterbottle', E'A has just perfected the movement as it completed the task in one chain of orientation. Policy B on the other hand has grasped the tape in the air and kept loosening and dropping it eventually. The tape in B was not even close to the postion of the bottle'),
(E'eb0f8683-0276-43e5-b37a-15198598ef46', E'2025-09-22T21:34:43.047066Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'pour water to the cup from waterbottle', E'Policy A failed to address the first orientation which should be surrounded the waterbottle; A just kept grinding over the cup slowly and gradually froze mid air. B on the other slightly understood it had to reach for the bottle first as it has done correctly but it ended up grasping nothing and moved the arm in the upright position (as for the pouring required) and the arm was not placed on top of the cup'),
(E'6b80587d-94c0-4683-85c1-672286dbbfa1', E'2025-09-22T21:46:47.748517Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'hide the stapler in the bin', E'Both policies has not done well since they both shifted to the eraser which has similar shape as the stapler. A grasped eraser and moved it closer to the bin while B has just grasped it for a few second a ran out of time'),
(E'2f5710ac-5058-4a63-954d-27c398e66e51', E'2025-09-22T21:55:47.789418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put all the stationery items on the notebook', E'B simple opened and closed the gripper at times and gradually moved towards the tape without significantly grasped anything with it. A slightly did better since it picked up botj the tape and eraser at some points but the arm lost motion with them as it dropped them right away; these two stationery still remained initially where they were before'),
(E'8b32154c-5bc0-46f3-a589-dcbec1dfb53b', E'2025-09-22T22:06:23.772732Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'right click the mouse', E'Policy B has somewhat moved towards the right of the mouse but the arm was not able to gently hit the button or reached closer to it. A was completely off-track as the arm kept bending its length inwards the base of the robot without doing anything relevant to the task'),
(E'b6b8db96-b561-4a26-aa85-01287c2b0bfe', E'2025-09-22T22:17:13.290924Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'squeeze the waterbottle 3 times', E'A just reached the bottle and then froze afterwards. B did better as it was able to squeeze/ touched a waterbottle with a significant force then lifted it upwards, thus dropping it as it reached the edge of the table'),
(E'41621ac2-f5ef-43dd-88bc-eb8c16e735b4', E'2025-09-22T22:33:13.856041Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'hide the cube from my sight', E'Both policies have done badly but each has a different approach to this problem. A remained frozen as the arm did not move at all. B shifted its focus to the cup which was not what should be intended to manipulate with.'),
(E'd1310acc-c1dd-4334-9197-baf5647008e9', E'2025-09-23T01:09:06.478356Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the door of the refrigerator', E'Policy A first moved the gripper randomly as if searching the target,then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to open the door of the refrigerator, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is slightly better than policy B.'),
(E'937a0b05-1a3c-4cbd-8cb4-0ccadfc91ddf', E'2025-09-23T01:27:36.109330Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the door of the refrigerator', E'Policy A first moved the gripper slightly forward, paused briefly, moved the gripper toward the door of the refrigerator but then moved away.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to open the door of the refrigerator, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd9f79145-489f-47ed-b08f-45b712920cd5', E'2025-09-23T02:22:10.556289Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'move the shoes from left to right', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the curtains, closed and opened the griper several times, as if attempting to grasp it, then approached the refrigerator in the end.Policy B first the gripper close to the shoes, then moved slowly above the shoes during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to move the shoes from left to right, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the shoes whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'9fb977db-be2b-47cd-acd4-a812421ed219', E'2025-09-23T02:32:48.357360Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the shoes, then drop it on floor', E'Policy A moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the episode,as if searching the target.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to grasp the shoes, then drop it on floor, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not do anything .Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'098e14ff-8b77-4aa3-ac75-57ca6c20cee8', E'2025-09-23T06:32:27.624997Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the controller by 90 degrees', E'Policy A did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations.Policy B first also showed no response to my command and did not take any actions.My instruction is to rotate the controller by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies showed no response to my command.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e6a91826-6ec7-44d2-b815-90ba7f1fd973', E'2025-09-23T07:00:04.591446Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the controller, then rotate it by 90 degrees', E'Policy A moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the episode,  as if could not find the target.Policy B first took some time to find the target, then approached the controller, grasped and released it, caused it to rotate by a small angle.My instruction is to grasp the controller then rotate it by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'94ef66d4-7645-42bc-92cc-69294f273d76', E'2025-09-23T07:11:19.211183Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the banana, then put it into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it, moved it to the plate, then put it into the plate.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it , moved it to the plate, then put it into the plate.Next, policy B almost stopped during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to grasp the banana then put it into the plate, both policies was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, after finishing the task, policy A still moved the gripper randomly whereas policy almost stopped.Therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'fcd4c3bb-2979-421c-b387-caf7f7e4894d', E'2025-09-23T07:23:26.194737Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the marker pen, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper aimlessly for a while, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B moved the gripper back and forth  during entire time of the trial, as if searching the target.My instruction is to grasp the marker pen then put it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A stopped during most time of the episode whereas policy B at least attempted to search the target.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'bf24b833-6be4-4a68-a904-8f64bc323e7e', E'2025-09-23T07:33:53.103235Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the peach, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper back and forth as if searching the target, then approached and touched the book.Next, policy A moved the gripper away in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the peach, attempted to grasp it, but pushed it to make it fall off from the table.Then, policy B moved the gripper around the book during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to grasp the peach then put it onto the book,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified and attempted to grasp the peach whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'88902f0b-600e-4cb7-8856-9735c48c25e3', E'2025-09-23T07:46:22.681494Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pencil, then put it onto the book', E'Policy A moved the gripper back and forth during entire time of the trial, as if searching the target.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to grasp the pencil then put it onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4fb1a469-1cc7-4a6f-898c-5ba472a533b6', E'2025-09-23T07:56:28.647954Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the book, then adjusted posture, pushed the book, attempted to close the book but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper aimlessly, then moved the gripper under the table during remaining time of the episode, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to close the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to close the book whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd2fa4b99-1d44-4efa-a8f4-d92845f819a7', E'2025-09-23T08:10:11.700349Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pull out one tissue from the pack', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the tissue, grasped the pack of the tissues, lift it up, moved it, then dropped it.Next, policy A approach the tissues and attempted to grasp it, but time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the pack of the tissues, grasped and released the pack twice, then grasp one tissue, attempted to pull it out until time ran out.My instruction is to pull out one tissue from the pack, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B almost completed the task while policy A only grasped the pack of the tissue.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e1fa9a32-5739-41dc-af20-f033150c2d4f', E'2025-09-23T08:35:24.442566Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the  cola  from the refrigerator', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the refrigerator, approached the cola, then closed and opened the gripper several times, as if attempting to grasped the cola,but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper back and forth as if searching the target, then approached the curtain and attempted to grasp it.My instruction is to grasp the  cola  from the refrigerator, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified the cola and attempted to grasp it whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'9d624264-9b1d-44ea-be27-a3923c597abf', E'2025-09-23T08:48:35.154452Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the  cola  from the refrigerator', E'Policy A first moved the gripper back and forth during the most time of the episode, as if searching the target, then stopped in the end.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to pick up the  cola  from the refrigerator, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'ef90e038-977d-4dba-b544-4b2eff67a6e8', E'2025-09-23T08:59:09.049507Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the refrigerator door', E'Policy A  moved the gripper aimlessly during entire time of the trial, as if could not find the target.Policy B also moved the gripper back and forth during the entire time of the of the episode.My instruction is to close the refrigerator door,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, it seems that both policies could not find the target, and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'81c80e7f-59aa-4fe6-a9e3-e4cc8e7f60c4', E'2025-09-23T09:08:52.237222Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the fridge door', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the fridge, then moved away.Next, policy B moved the robotic arm randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to close the fridge door, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the fridge whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'16cb7d00-e90c-4f04-8ec5-ab232436b0a8', E'2025-09-23T09:26:25.475431Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the curtains on your left', E'Policy A moved the gripper back and forth during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper randomly for a while, then approached the curtains and attempted to grasp it but did not succeed.Next, policy B moved the gripper away in the end.My instruction is to open the curtains on your left, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the curtains while policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'9f2b7f02-2a74-4752-8fc5-02eddd48f097', E'2025-09-23T09:38:16.749772Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the curtains ', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the curtains ,touched the curtains, adjusted posture, then pushed the curtains to make it open a bit.My instruction is to open the curtains, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B opened the curtains a bit while policy A did not do anything .Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'91f77c94-e588-40e0-ab5c-1073f527e3d5', E'2025-09-23T09:52:11.925713Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the shoes on the floor', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the shoes, attempted to grasp them, but did not succeed.Then policy A moved the gripper away.Policy B first took some time to find the target, moved the gripper toward the shoes, then moved away.My instruction is to pick up the shoes on the floor, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the shoes whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'1c628e03-77c3-46c2-a481-4c5f701ecd5c', E'2025-09-23T10:10:43.921608Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the cola from the fridge', E'Policy A moved the robotic arm randomly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the fridge, then moved the gripper toward the cola, but moved away after hesitating for a while.My instruction is to pick up the cola from the fridge, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, it seems that policy B at least identified the cola whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'e8a0a2fc-094a-4c77-8f6e-2662e9453728', E'2025-09-24T20:20:01.305674Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'put spoon in the correct location of dish rack', E'A has approached the spoon briefly right after the episode started and graudually moved it over the dish rack. The spoon was placed into a bowl which should not be the intended location of eating utensils - there is a utensil holder hanging on it. B just got to the point that it reached for the spoon and holded it for a few seconds before dropping it on the ground'),
(E'8515445b-312b-469e-b8f2-b026f72ec287', E'2025-09-24T20:43:04.207541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'type franka', E'Both policies succesfully headed towards the keyboard to perform typing work but in both cases, the correct word has never been typed up as A head for the first row of the keyboard and B just sticked to the enter key'),
(E'71db64eb-b819-4980-bced-b5bb3ce938ec', E'2025-09-24T20:52:39.872826Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'left click the mouse', E'Both episodes we saw the arm just reached for the mouse without doing anything relevant to the pressing success. A pushed the mouse further away from the seen and B was hovering up after tap in the middle of the mouse. It should slighly shift left to press it'),
(E'83d07777-2bec-44ad-921b-55db9df45415', E'2025-09-24T21:08:07.126179Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'prepare breakfast with bread and donut in the tray', E'In both episodes, the arm just sticked to the bread which was already placed in the tray. The arm should reach for the donut on the right side; thus the corn should be removed from the tray as it was not a part of the portion mentioned in the task'),
(E'e44fbff1-9459-4dd0-926b-8e941206111a', E'2025-09-24T21:28:36.821120Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put vegetables in the bag', E'A was going off point since it headed towards the dish rack on the left while the tray of vegetables were placed in the center of the seen. B was not doing any better since it grasped the grape (which is not a kind of vegetable) to the left while the bag was seen on the right. Both were not doing wuite well since it was unable to recongnize the very first orientation towards the tray'),
(E'9a7e2d95-4dc6-4b0a-b6ca-867b8da6120d', E'2025-09-24T21:40:00.887037Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move he feather duster into bag', E'Both policies has briefly moved the duster towards the bag but the arm position after grasping was different. A tended to be much sliding in a lower point as compared to the height of the bag; it then loosen the gripper on the side of the bag. B on the other hand was doing slightly better since the arm was gearing up to a significant height compared to the bag but it went exceeded the surface of the table and ended up dropping it on the ground'),
(E'e9bb73ea-28af-4772-a90f-de5e9422d5a1', E'2025-09-24T21:54:57.761959Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'use the hand fan to create a breeze', E'A just tapped the fan and moved on to the left and hovering there for a while. B started off frozen but then started to behave aggressively by twisting the arm and lower joint alll over the place; it did end up at the fan at some point but was able to grasp it due to time'),
(E'c7979568-6f67-471e-b699-983604b59e7e', E'2025-09-24T22:04:59.748578Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move all the toys into drawer', E'Policy A was succeed in moving one of the toy into drawer but then it tried to grasp the entire drawer shifted down-left form its initial position. B in the other hand completely ignored the first orientation with the toys and just picked up the drawer and drove it away from the table'),
(E'74e4e048-2cff-4d3a-9373-7b21c75623ac', E'2025-09-24T22:15:56.675475Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'sort all the lids into plate', E'Both policies has just shifted the arm towards the plate without recognizing it had to first reach for the two lids on the right and move it over to the plate. Both had equal score of success'),
(E'a8145292-e4b5-4851-a1e8-d290ec2d1ff1', E'2025-09-24T22:39:11.295575Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the tapes', E'Both policies at some point almost finished the stacked tape. A after finishing stacking the arm has pushed the drawer towards the two tapes and thus the stacked was fell down. B has just finished stacking but it then moved the other tape away and hovered there for a while'),
(E'62c8e396-5d68-4d40-b38c-e6931deb823f', E'2025-09-25T01:42:01.906449Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the shoes, then drop it', E'Policy A first moved the gripper  above the shoes, seemingly observing it, then moved the gripper slightly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close the shoes, then  grasped one shoe and dropped it twice until time ran out.My instruction is to grasp the shoes then drop it, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully whereas policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better then policy A.'),
(E'b4ec017f-ac10-4f1c-9770-4042f18b7a99', E'2025-09-25T01:59:20.021118Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'untie the shoelaces of the shoe in front of you', E'Policy A moved the gripper  back and forth during entire time of the trial,  as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the curtains, then grasped it, pull it, release it.Next, policy B moved the gripper randomly until time ran out.My instruction is to untie the shoelaces of the shoe in front of you, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped the wrong object and pull it whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'e09f322b-950d-4e01-a9ab-98c42c8526c2', E'2025-09-25T02:14:12.581426Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the shoelaces and pull it', E'Policy A moved the gripper  randomly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B also moved the gripper randomly during the whole trial, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to grasp the shoelaces and pull it, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, it seems that both policies could not found the shoelace, and their behaviors was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
