(E'7750012e-0eee-4bf8-b295-b3b658471a61', E'2025-10-01T21:36:47.155315Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the tape into drawer', E'both policies seemed to be distracted by the dense set up. A reached for the black arm on the right of the table although the tape we were looking for was located in the left.  B also pointed toward the right and tried to pick the sticker note'),
(E'0c72b75c-b89c-4b4a-a38b-51735db19a4b', E'2025-10-01T21:48:38.344430Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the notes from drawer', E'Both policies recognized the very first step is to reach for the drawer. A performed gripping motion around the edge of the drawer without going through the interior of it. B did slightly better since it was able to get in the drawer and searched for the notes; however, the note still remained inside there'),
(E'e7a20c5d-4125-4004-b3f6-4847395f0dcf', E'2025-10-01T21:56:45.220932Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'stack the plate into a bigger stack of plates on the left', E'policy B indeed completed the task in one turn of grasping and after that, it moved very aggressively by twisting and turning the joint of the arm. A on the other hand got thee single plate over the right side although the instruction already specified the direction'),
(E'4003f259-1d2c-49ba-b06b-8e2c4eea5eef', E'2025-10-01T22:06:34.714888Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the stainless lid over the plate', E'bpoth policies has got to the point that it reached for the stainless steel lid and trying to grasp it; however due to the small nature of the handle, the gripper had difficulty to pick it up entirely as in both turns the arm struglled to grasp it and kept dropping it'),
(E'e7597633-2c13-463d-b55d-dc4070581241', E'2025-10-01T22:20:04.241072Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the toothbrush to the plate in which contains the carrot', E'Policy A reached for the toothbrush but then the arm grasped the air which the distance between the gripper and brush wasq quite far, and it should move closer to perform proper grasping motion. The arm in A then moved over the plate with nothing in hand. B repeated the same pattern but after moving nothing over the plate, it tried to grasped the entire stack of plates which is unfavorable'),
(E'ab5f0ba7-d1af-4847-b92d-50fa32bd662e', E'2025-10-01T22:50:37.802572Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'use the orange lid to cover the wooden bowl', E'Policy A tended to reach for something on the left side while the lid clearly laid on the right. B did half way of the job but then after grasping the lid very carefully, it ended up dropping it back again and shifted the arm over the wooden bowl as if it still hold that lid in place.'),
(E'410f4f0a-83ca-41e7-b4c2-bca484d45c7e', E'2025-10-06T20:53:53.789153Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'Berkeley'), E'help me make a corn and carrot soup', E'A has firstly reached the corn and then shifted to the bowl containing the carrot with nothing in hand; it then grasped the entire bow;, showing the ability to recognize the pattern of the task. However, it should have the corn in hand and kept it to the bowl. B just froze the entire time'),
(E'ea6c8df7-9a30-4abc-8e34-fa25226d81fa', E'2025-10-06T21:02:45.047804Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'squeeze the ketchup into bread', E'Both policies did relatively bad since they seemed to be distracted by other objects. A just tried to grasped the carrot while B was finding something underneath the table top'),
(E'b16afc5d-65d2-4c85-8bb8-9fc838a755d4', E'2025-10-06T21:16:35.465268Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move only grocery items into bag', E'Both policies did not move towards any of the grocery items on the table (carrot, ketchup, etc) A at least did something relevant since it searched around the bag  without having anything to move over. B simply did not move in this episode'),
(E'c5a09c7e-d6c0-499d-a1b1-325bedbe87c8', E'2025-10-06T21:38:12.580585Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the tape on the whiteboard', E'A moved towards the package which the tape indeed not located there while B was considering between the bread and the tape for a while and tended to lean towards the tape at the end since the gripper moved closer trying to grasp; howverarm was too far apart to the surface of the tape'),
(E'5a9b5a04-b4b6-4d4c-ae7a-d97fcf31fb72', E'2025-10-06T21:53:40.882581Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'use to spoon to stir up the pot', E'Although the two polciies both scored 0, I prefer policy A since it at least performed a movement around the end point of the task (pot) while B just remained idle from its initial position'),
(E'19222a27-4f3c-47df-abf5-8be70fd54988', E'2025-10-06T22:03:26.281738Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the pot over dish rack', E'Policy A was able to detect the location of the pot and then tried to pick it up but then failed at the very last orientation; the arm dropped it at the edge of the rack. B on the other hand just slightly touched upon the pot but then shifted over the spoon on the right and pushed it away from our seen.'),
(E'3f69ea24-dc0a-44ad-96c6-ccd1fcf27046', E'2025-10-06T22:17:40.629328Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the red plate over dish rack', E'A was taking very a while to choose between red plate and yellow. It first reached the red but then shifted the gripper onto the yellow plate. B did a little better since it was able tp pick up the red plate and move over the table; however the final  should be the rack'),
(E'8608ea16-729d-4055-8d8f-73b8555f0436', E'2025-10-06T22:33:24.388722Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the grape into drawer', E'A froze the entire time with the arm pointing inwards the base of the robot. B at least moved around the dish rack and search for a suitable object to manipulate. It stops in front of the grape but at a very far distance'),
(E'142c1576-b0a8-448f-8a1a-0970fbdc38dc', E'2025-10-06T22:52:28.398707Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the orange into drawer', E'Policy B remained idle the entire time while A at least tried to reach for one kind of fruit (grapes) while being asked to move the orange around'),
(E'5322e188-c7db-4889-98ce-a13732c275f7', E'2025-10-06T23:03:41.770510Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the scooper into reusable bag', E'A performed a little off since it sticked to the surrounding of the scooper while B is more focused on the actual object (scooper) but it failed to grasp it peroperly. It also tried to pull the tray contained everything off the table'),
(E'758a51d0-c71f-434a-8a41-970082ddf56b', E'2025-10-08T09:25:58.730493Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'KAIST'), E'move the fruits from the box to the pot', E'policy A succeeded to grab one toy fruit, and place it well in the pot. policy B also succeeded to grab one toy fruit, but it failed to place it in the pot.'),
(E'334932c5-3e6b-4389-a136-a1a2cb35882c', E'2025-10-08T20:48:41.009350Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'throw the ketchup into the red bin', E'Policy A moved very closely towards the ketchup but it did not move close enough to touch upon the rear of the ketchup and grasp it. The arm then pretended that it picked up something (indeed nothing is hold) and moved over the red bin. B Just headed upwards to the rear of the table and arm tended to moved inwards the base of the robot. B obviously did not do any progress related to the task'),
(E'73788b94-9800-4338-b2c6-6f6bb38a4ab9', E'2025-10-08T21:01:01.811933Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'serve the bread in the plate', E'Both policies were able to move to the bread but the gripper did not align very well to the edge of the bread. Both failed to grasp it'),
(E'bf1a4fa0-05ef-4429-b28c-5ed03dca7a65', E'2025-10-08T21:11:47.532785Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'make toast using the machine', E'Policy A and B both followed the same approach. It first reached the toaster while having nothing in hand. It should first grasp the bread with just laying next to the machine and move over the machine it self. At least they did something relavant to the toasting'),
(E'564530ff-c1d8-41fe-a93b-7ee6976ed655', E'2025-10-08T21:27:00.787151Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeeley'), E'move the toothbrush next to scooper', E'Policy A completely ignored the instruction and just tried to reach something on the left while the toothbrush placed on the right. B at least pointed towards the tooth brush but at the same time, object surrounding was terribly disrupted and the arm still did not grasp the brush nicely'),
(E'8a4ff094-c294-4920-943a-741a8d71bc0b', E'2025-10-08T21:38:25.010760Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'make mushroom soup', E'Policy A moved around the left area and only shifted back to the right (where we found the mushroom) at the very end. B succesfully grasped the mushroom but it ended up on the table while we needed it be on the pot. The arm in B then reached for the cup and hold it up - which is also irrelevant'),
(E'6dde0a43-6c2c-4ba0-832a-c14508379254', E'2025-10-08T21:51:51.591126Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'close the lid pot', E'Both policies significantly distrupted many objects in the scene. A lifted the entire tray upwards the moved towards the lid at the very end. The tray somehow alway fell off the table. B first reached for the pot and then threw it off the seen. The lid remained untouched in this episode but it showed it could possibly approach the task without disrupting the surrounding'),
(E'4d7f19f8-6bc2-4cec-bc64-2a47ce013439', E'2025-10-09T01:30:32.639474Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the plastic bag, then throw it into the trash can', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to trash can, then grasped and released the edge of the trash can several times during most time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the plastic bag, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it randomly for while and dropped it on floor.My instruction is to grasp the plastic bag then throw it into the trash can, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at lest picked up and moved the plastic bag whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'0d5dda62-e58b-41f5-a276-20317f187cc0', E'2025-10-09T01:43:29.957473Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'throw the banana into the trash can', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to banana, then made multiple attempts to grasped it during remaining time of the episode, but did not succeed.Policy B moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the trial, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to throw the banana into the trash can, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the banana whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'449b50fc-32fe-4f01-88c5-5d264a8fa3d5', E'2025-10-09T02:03:10.581751Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the pomelo', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the pomelo, made multiple attempts to grasp it but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the pomelo, touched it, then moved the gripper away and moved randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to pick up the pomelo, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp to pomelo during the whole trial whereas policy B did not.Thererfore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'4081707a-6b76-4ae2-895b-55240035ab93', E'2025-10-09T02:14:25.089830Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the plate and put it into the plate.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor.My instruction is to put the banana into the plate, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'172ad111-9bff-4943-ba24-6ecf32b507bb', E'2025-10-09T02:23:38.880851Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the shoulder bag', E'Policy A first moved the gripper randomly for a while, then approached the shoulder bag, adjusted posture, grasped the zipper side of the shoulder bag as if attempting to open it, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B moved the gripper slightly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to open the shoulder bag, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least identified and attempted to open the shoulder bag whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'26f9e933-82e6-4a9c-b691-5b1bd699c580', E'2025-10-09T02:43:54.369757Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the shoulder bag with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped and released it,  then picked it up, moved it to left, then dropped it on floor in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up,then  moved it and dropped it into the trash can.My instruction is to cover the shoulder bag with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only picked up the towel but did not cover the shoulder bag with the towel, and their behaviors is similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e07bc36c-129e-4fbb-8cea-d472f34fc4e3', E'2025-10-09T03:02:09.153802Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the pillow with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it randomly for a while and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A picked the towel up again in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the pillow and dropped it near the pillow.Next, policy B picked the towel up again, put it tight against the pillow.My instruction is to cover the pillow with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least put the towel close to the pillow whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'fef51514-8505-4023-968a-a4e64dc504e6', E'2025-10-09T03:21:14.087436Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the controller onto the pillow', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B did not respond to my command and did not take any actions at all.My instruction is to put the controller onto the pillow, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies did not respond to my instruction.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'6c0074c1-b266-4a46-b54e-8253515197c4', E'2025-10-09T03:30:58.543508Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the controller onto the pillow', E'Policy A stopped during most time of the episode, then moved slightly in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the controller, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy B moved the gripper back and forth until time ran out.My instruction is to put the controller onto the pillow, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least identified the controller and attempted to grasp it whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'e312162b-5f7f-4ea6-bdbf-c96e02566814', E'2025-10-09T05:16:18.245771Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the cube onto the pillow', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the cube, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor.Policy B showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to put the cube onto the pillow, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up and moved the cube whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'b88dcd39-39ab-476b-8f20-f7f67cc109bd', E'2025-10-09T05:47:28.855932Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the cube onto the pillow', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the cube, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A approached the cube again during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the cube, grasped it,picked it up, then moved it and dropped it near the pillow, causing it to fall off from the sofa to floor.Next, policy B moved the gripper randomly until time ran out.My instruction is to put the cube onto the pillow, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies have picked up the cube, but policy B dropped the cube near the pillow whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'a7eccc7d-405f-47a3-8597-a6c41a87eb22', E'2025-10-09T06:08:32.612566Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'grasp the pillow, then lift it up', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to pillow, grasped it, lifted it up, then dropped it on sofa.Next, policy A grasped the pillow again in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the edge of the sofa rather than the pillow, attempted to grasped the sofa, then almost stopped at the edge of the sofa during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to grasp the pillow then lift it up, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'160ff122-29b3-43cf-9629-8438f2688d65', E'2025-10-09T06:33:39.899693Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'touch the English words on the book', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the book, then moved the gripper away and moved randomly during most time of the episode.Next, policy B approached the book again in the end.My instruction is to touch the English words on the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the book whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'be66cf08-55df-4e71-bfda-0ce627afa068', E'2025-10-09T06:50:46.115307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'write in the book with the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the marker pen, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it near the book and dropped it on floor.Policy B moved the gripper back and forth during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to write in the book with the marker pen,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up the marker pen whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
