(E'ff463f88-1298-45da-b6d3-e00004b696b4', E'2025-10-29T08:34:56.634109Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'poke the banana with the fork', E'Policy A first moved the gripper slightly, then stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the banana, but moved away soon, then approached the fork,but also moved away soon.Next, policy B moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to poke the banana with the fork, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy B at least approached the target, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'0aa15926-e963-4429-8e90-dd7ecfb9e8f2', E'2025-10-29T08:47:29.634965Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two cups', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to one cup, knocked it over, then attempted to grasp it several times, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to one cup,grasped it, but the cup slipped while being lifted, then policy B moved the gripper toward another cup and moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to stack up the two cups, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least grasped one cup, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd1763253-73d4-41c8-8726-07dfcecd51c0', E'2025-10-29T09:15:48.298212Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'wash the plate  with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the plate, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and put it on the sofa.Next,policy A moved the gripper away and moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper back and forth during most time of the episode,then approached the plate in the end.My instruction is to wash the plate  with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two,policy A at least grasped the plate, whereas policy B only approached the plate.Therefore, policy A is slight better than policy B.'),
(E'faf35f95-0356-4dd0-916b-9b8b60d754b6', E'2025-10-29T09:24:21.485990Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'wipe the plate withe towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the plate and dropped it on floor.Next,policy A stopped during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the towel, attempted to grasp it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor in the end.My instruction is to wipe the plate withe towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies picked up the towel, but policy A obviously moved the towel toward the plate while policy B did not.Therefore, i choose A.'),
(E'6204faa9-b34e-44bf-8f08-902ea835a48d', E'2025-10-29T20:58:23.707742Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move all the vegetables into bowl', E'Policy remained freeze in the entire episode although it seemed to responded to the command for the first few seconds. B at least was able to grasp the corn (among all 3 vegetables) into the plate while the plate is indeed not what we aasked to stimulate into'),
(E'ea7d7e53-5ce5-425f-a83c-c441591248d3', E'2025-10-29T21:08:24.293725Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'sort all the cubes on the plastic container', E'Policy first approached the green cubes and moved it over the edge of the table as it amlmost dropped out; then the arm shifted focus to the plastic container and tried to grasp it. This action repeated a few times before the arm tried to approach the blue cube but then it stopped midway due to time. Policy B succesfully moved to blue to the desired place but then the arm kept handling and dropping the cubes on and off over a few times; we did not see it approaching the green one'),
(E'f64ee994-4450-4a0d-abb5-62ebd8b4d507', E'2025-10-29T21:19:03.127344Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'prepare the slice of bread on my plastic lunch box', E'Policy A tended to ignore the bread and went on to the other on the table (strawberry) and tried to grasp it; the grasping success is low since it was not able to keep the object tightly. B at least reached for the bread but it got stuck the the middle of the session as the arm did not move'),
(E'6101ad13-2604-4e54-ba8b-a52c35441196', E'2025-10-29T21:27:51.251909Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the mushroom onto bread', E'Policy A moved to the direction where we found the mushroom but then it grasped the carrot instead and then dropped it instantly; the arm then twisted and turn in a very strange position that blocked the view of the right camera and trigger a red light, which wa dangerous to proceed. Policy B also went to the direction of the mushroom but then it got the marker in hand and dropped it out of nowhere (off the table)'),
(E'f524073d-1e99-4e17-a6d4-2afc718a3019', E'2025-10-29T21:39:33.992368Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the canned food into pot', E'B at least did somethign relevant to the task (moved towards the pot at the very beginning) while A tended to focus on the plate contained all the vegetable which was on the other side of the seen'),
(E'74a7c406-02e5-492e-9f3f-911905ccc922', E'2025-10-29T21:51:08.702632Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the canned food over the green cup holder', E'policy a was trying the grasp the pot which was quite irrelevant; the score is marked as 10 since the arm might shift a little bit over the canner food but it is not clear since it is in the middle of the seen. B grasped the entire plastic bowl which contained the pot; the pot was pushed off the ground and the arm was moving over the canned food but again the intention was to fail off the can horizontally and grasp on the wider surface area but the time was up as the gripper touched the lying canned'),
(E'e1c3b178-d034-4b94-a7b8-0951d3cf9549', E'2025-10-29T22:06:02.019068Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the pencil over the cup', E'Policy A and B did relatively bad since they did irrelevant action over the two observations. A tried to grasp the plate while B tried to get the carrot on the plate. The pencil size is tiny compared to other objects so that might explain it'),
(E'c0e15ace-fe93-44e6-8a0a-174b88b89506', E'2025-10-29T22:22:17.318079Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the brush next to the carrot', E'both policies did not ever touch the brush which was designed specifically for animal grooming. A reached for the cup while B attempted to grasp the strawberry'),
(E'73c0a2ff-6439-41a9-ac00-e1f270b691ae', E'2025-10-29T22:35:41.336896Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'fold the cloth in half', E'Policy A got the cloth in place but then it hang it over to the left without being folded in half. B decided to go completely off since it tried to grasp the plate'),
(E'423c644f-a1bf-4ccb-8c67-1c36b152c95b', E'2025-10-29T22:44:13.751345Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'place pot onto the cloth', E'B did not move from its intial position after interpret the task while A had the intention to push off everything in the seen; it first approached the cup and knocked it down, then hovered over to the plate and push it off the table'),
(E'af496ae0-74d7-4310-ab82-1724993af6c8', E'2025-10-30T01:10:01.312307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the towel into the plate', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the plate,  hover above the plate for a while, then moved the gripper above the towel in the end.My instruction is to put the towel into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the gripper above the target, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd9a7a8bf-8a9c-44ff-86ca-767408115808', E'2025-10-30T01:20:22.839853Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the towel into the plate', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the towel, then attempted to grasp it several times during remaining time of the episode, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to put the towel into the plate, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the towel, whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'e6aab3dd-966c-4f04-a966-6e1728493eb0', E'2025-10-30T01:32:33.632314Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'touch the yellow button of the remote control', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the remote control, closed the gripper as if attempting to touch the remote control, then moved the gripper away and moved randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the remote control, closed the gripper, approached the yellow button as if attempting to touched it.Then policy B moved the gripper away and moved randomly until time ran out.My instruction is to touch the yellow button of the remote control, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies approached the remote control, but policy B moved the gripper above the yellow button while policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'8b006fcd-f7a1-4588-919c-5a48c07905d8', E'2025-10-30T01:47:26.106921Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the controller with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to plate, grasped it and released it, then moved the gripper away and moved randomly for a while.Next, policy A approached the towel, grasped and released it in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the controller during remaining time of the episode, but did not cover the controller with towel in then end.My instruction is cover the controller with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least picked up the towel and moved it toward the controller, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'2b24711f-6af4-4c07-b6ee-e29e8d494cc3', E'2025-10-30T01:59:39.173644Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the pliers', E'Policy A first took some time to find the target, moved the gripper close to pliers, attempted to grasped it several times, then grasped one side of the pliers, picked it up, moved it and dropped it on sofa, but did not close the pliers.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the pliers, after hesitating for a while, grasped one side of the pliers , picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor, but also did not close the pliers.My instruction is to close the pliers, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only grasped one side of the pliers and picked it up,but did not close the pliers.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'51402d86-0701-4064-bff8-ac36c4ad6549', E'2025-10-30T02:17:56.960151Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the lid of the white box', E'Policy A first rotated the gripper, then moved the gripper randomly during most time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Next, policy A approached the book in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the book, approached the edge of the book, pushed it several times, as if attempting to open the book.My instruction is to open the lid of the white box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least mistook the book for the box and attempted to open it,whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'795af3d7-1677-4e18-8801-9d0a6075e299', E'2025-10-30T02:41:51.686249Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'squash the white box', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the white box, hovered above the box for a while, then moved the gripper away, moved back and forth during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the sofa, approached the edge of the sofa,  then approached the pliers, picked it up and released it.My instruction is to squash the white box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least approached the white box, whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'f0d1c16f-d1a8-4053-9066-b37cc87401dc', E'2025-10-30T02:51:28.237628Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'tap the cube with the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the cube, grasped and released it, then picked it up, moved it and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A approached the cube again in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the marker pen,  made multiple attempts to grasp it, then picked it up, moved it and dropped it on sofa.Next, policy B attempted to grasp the marker pen again in the end.My instruction is to tap the cube with the marker pen,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least picked up the marker pen, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd49a23a7-42fa-4689-b2e2-381f53ba14b3', E'2025-10-30T03:28:52.380400Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'take off the cap from the marker pen', E'Policy A  first moved the gripper toward the marker pen, grasped and released the cap of the marker pen, then moved the gripper away and moved slightly until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the marker pen but moved away soon, then approached the cube, grasped it, picked it up and dropped it on sofa in the end.My instruction is to take off the cap from the marker pen, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least grasp the cap of the marker pen, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'71120a64-c491-4014-99e4-ac23e231b6ac', E'2025-10-30T03:41:31.815326Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the zipper of the shoulder bag', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the shoulder bag, approached the tab of the zipper, then,after hesitating for a while, attempted to grasp the tab until time ran out, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the shoulder bag, approached one zipper, attempted to grasp it, touched the zipper.Then policy B approached another zipper of shoulder bag, attempted to grasp the tab of the zipper, but did not succeed in the end.My instruction is to open the zipper of the shoulder bag, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B find two zippers of the bag and attempted to open them, whereas policy A only attempted to open one zipper.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'50c3f046-5023-47ff-8fab-7705c21958ec', E'2025-10-30T05:16:15.171288Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the book', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to close the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the gripper, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'495f8fc6-8b2a-4e78-b36a-074cbdf8229b', E'2025-10-30T05:25:16.473916Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the book, adjusted posture, but moved away soon, then policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B moved the gripper back and forth during the whole trial, as if could not find the target.My instruction is to close the book,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least moved the gripper toward the book, whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'bc608440-83ee-41ed-a27f-175c0103d065', E'2025-10-30T07:15:13.377209Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'write a letter o in the book with the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to marker pen, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it for a while as if writing something in the air, and dropped the marker pen on floor in the end.Policy B showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to write a letter o in the book with the marker pen, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up the marker pen and moved it, whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.')
