(E'eb5aad4e-f93d-4d9f-b801-94421b978bba', E'2025-11-12T08:52:50.115432Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'remove the towel, then pick up the cube under the towel', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the towel, grasped it, picked it up, moved it and dropped it on the cube, causing the cube to be covered again.Then policy picked up the towel again and moved it until time ran out.My instruction is to remove the towel then pick up the cube under the towel,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least removed the towel, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'af5a6e34-c6ae-4e1f-82ee-348a41472ce2', E'2025-11-12T09:06:05.875474Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the upper drawer', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the drawer, approached the pull handle of the draw, but moved away soon.Then policy B moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to open the upper drawer,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the drawer, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'7d0f76b3-73d3-434d-931f-ba97bb249a4e', E'2025-11-12T09:15:17.834165Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the drawer', E'Policy A first closed the gripper, then moved the gripper back and forth for a while, approached the drawer, but moved away soon.Policy B showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to close the drawer,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least approached the drawer,whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'480efc7c-535d-4fdd-9afb-3c183c325847', E'2025-11-12T09:33:16.034535Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the marker pen into the drawer', E'Policy A first moved the gripper close to the marker pen, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the drawer and dropped it into the drawer.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.My instruction is to put the marker pen into the drawer, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B did not do anything.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'644603e4-929f-4e8c-be4e-267b15c9d7d1', E'2025-11-12T09:47:19.027435Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the drawer', E'Policy A showed no response to my command and did not perform any operations at all.Policy B first moved the gripper close to the edge of table,attempted to grasp it, then moved slowly, closed and opened the gripper several times during remaining time of the episode, as if could not find the drawer.My instruction is to close the drawer, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least moved the gripper, whereas policy A did not do anything.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'69fabaa1-957c-4f5e-ac44-b063ff8ee4fb', E'2025-11-12T20:15:46.337276Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'put the red marker into cup', E'PoliCcy B approached the two markers without actually grasping anything in place; it wandered between the red and green marker for a while and decided to focuus on the green on which is not what I asked. PoliCy A succeeded in grasping the maker but it rotated over the empty space on the table and dropped it down. It shifted over to the green one but again rotating it upwards and failed to reach over the cup'),
(E'd7213327-93b4-4484-adcb-5b859bd93790', E'2025-11-12T20:28:20.937796Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'place red marker on the note', E'Policy A reached for the green marker despite being asked to manipulate with the red marker. Policy B did a little better (not sure if this by chance since the two are very close to each other); the arm then tried to hold it but it kept loosened and fell off the table'),
(E'ec06d97e-ace5-4b2b-a9a1-2e5b25798fe1', E'2025-11-12T20:43:32.871355Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'fold the cloth in half', E'A did better since it reached for the small cloth and tried to fold the edge of it inwards; it then pushed the cloth further away from each reach (forwards to the  top part of table), the cloth remained unfold at the end. Policy B only tried to pick up the cloth and moved it over the big black curtain on the right; it then aggressively teared off the black curtain which led to termination'),
(E'9876b96f-ff84-4a87-aec2-7c895e6f76e8', E'2025-11-12T21:10:36.051732Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the red bottle over the stainless steel scoop', E'POliCy A at least reached for the red bottle while B did not respond at all after executing the command'),
(E'1f508558-0adb-4ab8-84e3-ec946123b62b', E'2025-11-12T21:26:39.573122Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'remove the tape from the bowl', E'Both policies did relatively well since the complexity of the seen and objects are decreased and the command was simple. They reached the tape very swiftly and moved it to the right'),
(E'f40cf78d-30de-4da6-a297-46bf0c222407', E'2025-11-12T21:48:26.194631Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'berkeley'), E'move the green sponge onto bigger bowl', E'policy A completely went off since it picked the spponge to the pink, smaller bowl. B did a little bit better since the direction was onto the big bowl but it stopped right in front of the surface of it due to time limit.'),
