(E'9f924ee8-09f7-410f-a56b-7f878caedc2b', E'2026-02-03T12:52:28.017858Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'KAIST'), E'pick up the carrot and place it on the purple plate', E'policy A reaches to the carrot while policy B fails to reach to the carrot'),
(E'ea2db95c-1038-4607-bc81-bc7b981f76b6', E'2026-02-03T12:57:47.321850Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'KAIST'), E'pick up the brush and put it in the pink bin', E'policy A did not reach to the correct object or pick up anything. policy B did not reach to the correct object but at least pick up something'),
(E'8ce7a98b-73fc-4e07-92d1-f97a908e0212', E'2026-02-03T16:39:48.101035Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Toss the crumpled paper into the bin', E'Policy A was able to reach, grasp and pick up the crumpled paper. However, it was not able to bring the paper above the bin to put it in. Policy B was able to complete the task successfully by putting the crumpled paper into the bin. Therefore, policy B is the preferred one.'),
(E'38f7c842-032d-460b-8cb0-663339031d2d', E'2026-02-03T16:58:20.343661Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'put the can in the bin', E'Both Policy A and Policy B were only able to reach the can but not grasp it successfully. However, Policy A continued to try to grasp the can after it knocked it over while Policy B went on to grasp a completely different object (crumpled paper). Therefore, Policy A had the more desirable behaviour.'),
(E'bf38904c-1d4f-4d6d-a81a-5e1efaf3b34a', E'2026-02-03T17:10:04.815691Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'take the lid off of the pitcher', E'Policy A was able to successfully grasp the lid and take it off the pitcher. However it did knock down the pitcher while it was doing it. Policy B was not able grasp the lid and then did not retry successfully.'),
(E'26496f65-b2b1-448e-9596-4fe41911f032', E'2026-02-03T17:20:24.615645Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'place the cutlery items to the side of the plate', E'Policy A grabbed both the cutlery items simultaneously and was able to move them to the side of the plate. However it did not get the spoon properly off the plate. Policy B reached for the knife but was not able to successfully grasp it; after which, it moved on to grasp the cloth.'),
(E'71c57281-b7da-43ca-847a-ee731244311c', E'2026-02-03T17:45:14.158958Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'close the book', E'Both policy A and policy B tried to grasp the edge of the book to close it, but were not able to successfully grab all the pages. Both policies lifted some of the pages and tried to flip them.'),
(E'd305443b-40d9-41a2-8599-676ae5e2efab', E'2026-02-03T17:58:52.736759Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'remove the inedible item from the plate and put it on the table', E'Both policies incorrectly grabbed the wrong item at first. Policy A did however reach for the tennis ball after removing the orange from the plate. Policy B did not even grasp the tennis ball.'),
(E'9d9e15e6-5a85-4fe9-b109-4ace32228bf6', E'2026-02-03T18:20:22.918561Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'put the yellow chain in the box', E'Policy A did not move at all. Policy B grasped the chain and brought it to the box, but was not able to put it inside the box correctly.'),
(E'84a75da7-2a56-49f1-8d1b-a2543082fccb', E'2026-02-04T01:52:17.468354Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the red can on the grey cylinder', E'A managed to grab the can, B did not. Also A brought it to the correct location, but dropped it rather than placing it properly.'),
(E'36431785-fecf-45d6-931f-5c14e7939370', E'2026-02-04T02:05:49.215166Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the green ball in the white cup', E'A did not identify the green ball properly, confusing the pear and baseball with it. B grabbed the ball, and even brought it to the white cup properly. However, it did not properly predict the height of the cup, pushing the cup across the table rather than centering the ball above it and dropping it.'),
(E'8a87ab39-3623-4619-9c8c-e39803efab38', E'2026-02-04T02:22:46.305227Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the blue cube onto the red cube', E'A did not even manage to pick up the blue cube. B was successful, identifying the correct destination cube and even correcting itself.'),
(E'8969268e-4ed1-4146-8503-767de6680b64', E'2026-02-04T02:49:21.402556Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the black tape on the blue plate', E'A was successful, B put the tape on the wrong plate.'),
(E'cc655f86-507d-4058-8b21-18210190c8f0', E'2026-02-04T02:57:31.629516Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the black pen in the white cup', E'Both went for the wrong item. A tried to put the wrong item in the wrong destination object.'),
(E'b1b45f8b-802b-47a3-a8b0-43fad2256efb', E'2026-02-04T03:03:23.970554Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pour the pink mug into the green plate', E'A was successful, but awkward in its execution. Took much longer, and one screw fell out. B was fast, smooth, and got all screws into the plate.'),
(E'e99f3865-aec2-482a-8365-e41f87dbe7df', E'2026-02-04T03:13:25.642318Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pick up the bread from the green plate and place it into the toaster', E'A picked up the bread, and ran out of time before placing the bread in the toaster. B did not manage to pick up the bread.'),
(E'0cffe184-1602-4534-8094-b057fd414964', E'2026-02-04T03:23:51.794705Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the lime in the blue cup', E'Both did badly. A put the lemon in the blue cup and then timed out. B did the same but had time remaining to touch the lime. The fact that B touched the lime is the deciding factor.'),
(E'aec10dc7-b425-4b6f-9e11-b103ce78d688', E'2026-02-04T03:24:14.851891Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it to the cup, dropped it on the edge of the cup, causing the banana to fall off to sofa.Next, policy A picked up the banana again, knocked the cup over, moved slowly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, attempted to grasp it, then picked it up, moved it toward the cup, dropped it near the cup.My instruction is to put the banana into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least dropped the banana on the edge of the cup, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'94cbc60b-3f5e-40e9-a620-a54d6a4f35a0', E'2026-02-04T03:35:40.096077Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it to the cup, dropped it on the edge of the cup, causing the banana to fall off to sofa.Next, policy A attempted to grasp the banana again during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it , rotated it, dropped it on sofa.Next, policy B picked up the banana again, moved it until time ran out.My instruction is to put the banana into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least dropped the banana on the edge of the cup, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'76c593b2-57e0-4b09-bc1e-4a6723993ad1', E'2026-02-04T03:44:31.580624Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the skittles in the red bowl', E'A was successful. B put the skittles in the wrong bowl.'),
(E'a004c699-0166-41e3-b245-a301cbd90701', E'2026-02-04T03:47:27.552451Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, touched it, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then  policy A moved the gripper around the banana during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped and released it, then, after hesitating for a while, policy B picked up the banana, rotated it by about 90 degrees, dropped it on floor.My instruction is to rotate the banana by 90 degrees, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully, whereas policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5f16ea6c-38c1-4656-b1c7-d1c8e1c80a5c', E'2026-02-04T03:57:45.427556Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two cups', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the left cup, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the right cup, moved around the right cup during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the left cup, knocked it over, pushed it, causing the left cup to roll toward the right cup.My instruction is to stack up the two cups, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up and moved the left cup to the right cup, whereas policy B did not even grasp the cup.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'7b63585e-2a67-4bf0-a835-56bc4b5a10c7', E'2026-02-04T06:22:56.428865Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'knock over the left cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the right cup, then moved back and forth during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the left cup, attempted to grasp it, then moved the gripper away and moved randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to knock over the left cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached and attempted to grasp the left cup, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd493d600-2524-4c54-ace8-6b89fd91815d', E'2026-02-04T06:31:35.609342Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the red block into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the red block,grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the cup, dropped it, causing the red block to fall off to sofa.Next, policy A attempted to grasp the red block again during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the red block,attempted to grasp it several times, then picked it up, moved it, dropped it.My instruction is to put the red block into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies picked up the red block, but policy A moved the red block close to the cup, while policy B did not.Therefore,policy A is better then policy B.'),
(E'eeabf0f3-4bc6-4c8f-b079-234d715b8e7c', E'2026-02-04T06:51:44.998700Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the wooden block into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the wooden block, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it to the cup, dropped it into the cup.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the red block rather than the wooden block,  then approached the wooden block, attempted to grasp it.Next, policy B attempted to grasp the red block.My instruction is to put the wooden block into the cup, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'c7e6cdb5-bdaa-44aa-8b36-fc8bc428b32e', E'2026-02-04T07:00:21.951224Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the cup onto the red block', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the cup, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the cup, grasp it, picked it up, then moved it above the red block, dropped it on the red block, causing the cup the fall off to floor.Next, policy B moved the gripper slowly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to put the cup onto the red block, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least dropped the cup on the red block, whereas policy A only moved the cup.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'fb83d79b-4d43-49f9-8675-b4ef89b24f3d', E'2026-02-04T08:11:24.038307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the yellow button of the controller', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the controller, closed the gripper, approached the yellow button,press the gray button beside the yellow button.Then policy A grasped and released the controller.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the controller,closed the gripper, touched the blank area of the controller, then pressed the gray button near the yellow button.My instruction is to press the yellow button of the controller, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only pressed the gray button near the yellow button.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'e0366542-86f7-47be-bf8b-30c51ced4e95', E'2026-02-04T08:21:11.370544Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'press the round button of the controller', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the controller, closed the gripper, but moved away soon.Then policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the controller, closed the gripper, pressed the rectangle button near the round button,then policy B hovered above the controller during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to press the round button of the controller, neither policy was able to complete task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least pressed the rectangle button near the round button, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'2c0da81e-8158-4a40-8bcf-0cb1f70e3637', E'2026-02-04T08:30:46.691759Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the fruit', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, moved it and dropped it on floor.Then policy A approached the carrot, attempted to grasp it, but did not succeed.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, touched it, then moved the gripper back and forth during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to pick up the fruit, there is only one fruit which is the banana.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'bf803d3b-a1fd-4971-95fa-3be929c68ea7', E'2026-02-04T08:40:27.757740Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the carrot by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the carrot, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it, dropped it, made the carrot rotate by about 70 degrees.Then policy A attempted to grasp the banana, pushed the carrot.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it, rotated it, dropped it on floor.My instruction is to rotate the carrot by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least rotated the carrot by about 70 degrees, whereas policy B rotated the wrong object.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'11a1a0f1-6b77-4317-8dc3-c6da408b8538', E'2026-02-04T09:20:21.131052Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the banana with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the towel, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy A approached the carrot, attempted to grasp it.Next, policy A approached the towel again in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the carrot, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy B hovered above the carrot during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to cover the banana with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the towel, whereas policy B did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'c0ce0bf1-1eb4-4076-934b-8951e8622e48', E'2026-02-04T15:42:16.916512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Put all of the blocks into the container', E'Policy A tried to grab some blocks, but failed to pick up any. Policy B confidently and swiftly picked up a bunch of blocks, however it failed to put them into the container.'),
(E'c02631b8-42d5-4505-a265-a7eac099af7c', E'2026-02-04T16:25:11.054817Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Take the chain out of the cup and place it on the table', E'Policy A failed to even grab the chain and did not take any of it out of the cup. Policy B managed to bump into the chain in such a way that resulted in the chaing partially hanging out of the cup. Policy B then managed to grab a chunk of the chain and pull it out onto the table. However still more than half of the chain remained inside the cup. Policy B is preferred, as it seems it might have carried out the task succesfully if it was given a longer time.'),
(E'cec4e001-dfdd-4002-8807-c65883ff9dbd', E'2026-02-04T17:20:21.244921Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Spoon the vegetables out of the blue bowl with the spoon', E'Both A and B removed the carrot piece with the gripper, not the spoon.'),
(E'30298b84-d00a-4bf0-b101-147618b4100e', E'2026-02-04T17:21:01.821008Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the tape measure into the basket', E'Policy B quickly picked up the tape measure and placed it into the basket as desired. Policy A was not as good since it grabbed a marker and placed it into the basket, while also making lots of unnecessary movements during the rollout. Since policy B fully accomplished the task it is the winner.'),
(E'c49328f2-3918-4d57-a6bc-3407dbde9010', E'2026-02-04T17:21:52.837590Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Take all fruits and vegetables out of the pan', E'Policy A tried to grab one of the fruits in the pan (an orange), but failed to do so. Policy B struggled with grabbing, but ultimately managed to grab and lift an apple.'),
(E'177a0897-297f-4d01-a41b-d9422c7507ad', E'2026-02-04T17:38:14.026420Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Put the orange into the pan', E'Policy A confidently picked up incorrect fruit (a peach) and placed it in the pan. Then it tried to put the apple into the pan as well, but failed to lift it. Overall Policy A made no attempt to put the correct fruit (an apple) into the pan and only interacted with the wrong fruits. Policy B was somewhat hesitant and slow, however it moved directly to the correct fruit, lifted it and dropped it in the pan. While Policy A moved faster and more confidently, it did not recognize the correct fruit. Policy B is the winner, because while it moved slower, it did not get confused with other objects.'),
(E'84e8b914-8b2b-4d21-8931-135f20c353bc', E'2026-02-04T17:47:42.399938Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pick up the dish brush and use it to scrub the tray', E'Policy B is preferred since it grabbed the brush and scrubbed the table. Policy A was not as good since it struggled to grab the brush, and when it did have it in its grasp it let go of it, without ever doing a scrubbing motion. Since policy B was able to pick up the brush and make a scrubbing motion, it is preferred.'),
(E'8545ad5c-ca8b-4102-8c14-85af2babb213', E'2026-02-04T18:20:30.058977Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the croissant in the basket', E'B put the baguette on the basket incorrectly. A did not pick up anything.'),
(E'30a17d5f-5bee-40d3-bf08-8cc837c0ceed', E'2026-02-04T18:23:19.758585Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Throw the can into the bin', E'Policy A approched the can, tried to grab it from a bad gripper pose and did not manage to even pick it up. Policy B managed to grab and pick up the can, but immediately dropped it. Policy B then tried to pick it up again, but failed to do so. Policy B wins by a narrow margin as it at least picked the can up, but none of the policies succesfully completed the task.'),
(E'd3504f70-3618-4577-8b07-fc63be427d58', E'2026-02-04T18:25:26.315355Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the shoe on the top shelf', E'Policy B was unable to pick up the shoe. Policy A picked up the shoe, searched for the top shelf, but ultimately dropped the shoe behind the shelves rather than onto the top shelf. Since Policy A was able to pick up the shoe and made an attempt at placing it onto the shelf, it is preferred.'),
(E'9e63b865-d340-4a33-8f73-6c93f1c68c03', E'2026-02-04T18:26:46.808371Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the tapes', E'A stacked one tape successfully, but did not manage to pick up the other tape. B tried to stack one tape, but it fell off.'),
(E'beae2721-fa1e-4f5f-a455-59fe74f553d9', E'2026-02-04T18:34:16.337737Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Throw the can into the trash bin.', E'Policy A tried to grab the can, but failed to pick it up. Policy B successfully picked up the can and started moving it towards the trash bin, however it did not lift it up enough to be above the bin. Policy B was then terminated, because it was slowly pushing the bin off the table. Policy B is the winner as it picked up the can, but neither policy completed the task.'),
(E'0779012d-40bb-4725-9e91-c11b07a09ab3', E'2026-02-04T18:36:30.249108Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove an item from the bottom shelf', E'Policy A reached for the correct shelf, but was not successful in picking up an item. Policy B removed an item, but from the wrong shelf. Policy A is preferable for its understanding of reaching for the bottom shelf, even if it did not remove an item.'),
(E'8b951630-efc3-4e68-8095-2e8145d1a915', E'2026-02-04T18:44:59.830579Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the teapot on the hot plate', E'Policy A was able to pick up the teapot, and half-place it onto the hot plate such that it was still touching the table. Policy B was on target for the teapot but did not pick up. Since policy A was able to pick up the teapot and somewhat place it onto the hotplate, it is the the winner.'),
(E'695c6661-7c41-4b2c-9f04-38516a7e8f03', E'2026-02-04T18:47:27.073495Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'hang the gauze on the tripod', E'Policy A knocked over the tripod and picked up the gauze but never placed it. Policy B attempted to pick up the tripod, similarly causing it to fall, and picked up the gauze also. Policy B placed the gauze on the fallen tripod, making it the better outcome of the two policies.'),
(E'9cf2dba9-f281-4803-ba29-79ff26f69b57', E'2026-02-04T18:50:15.333762Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Throw the apple into the trash can.', E'Policy A picked up the apple and lifted it, then dropped it back on the table. Policy A then tried to lift up the apple a couple more times, but did not really succeed. Policy B picked up the apple and lifted it even a bit less than Policy A, then dropped it. The apple then rolled away maybe almost out of the view of cameras. Policy B then tried to lift the can of chips, but did not succeed. While Policy A managed to lift the apple slightly higher during its run, both policies failed the task at approximately the same stage of the process.'),
(E'eb5d7e8f-c756-4ffd-8ca4-61c4bdd045ff', E'2026-02-04T18:55:46.976529Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'depress the stapler', E'Both policies immediately picked up the stapler and moved it such that the paper could no longer be stapled. Policy A used a closed gripper and made the depress motion but pressed onto the table. Policy B used a closed gripper and depressed the stapler itself, but did not use enough force to activate the stapler. Since policy B was able to use its closed gripper to slightly depress the stapler, it is preferred over policy A which did not press the stapler.'),
(E'49caa8fd-a86d-4b27-8704-982b3e11f3de', E'2026-02-04T19:19:45.001233Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Use the spatula to stir the fruits in the pan.', E'Policy A grabbed the spatula by its handle, but then dropped it. Subsequently it grabbed the spatula almost by the flat stirring part of it and somewhat stirred the fruit in the pan. I consider that a somewhat successfull run, as it did use the spatula to stir the pan, however it didn''t hold the spatula by its handle and the stirring was not very good (it resembled poking rather than stirring). Policy B failed to identify the spatula and grabbed the handle of the pan instead. Policy B then kept slightly lifting and wiggling the pan. Policy A was therefore better, as it identified the correct tool to use, even though its handling of the tool wasn''t very good.'),
(E'746c0e26-e311-44ca-8fed-347cedd82faa', E'2026-02-04T19:30:09.848582Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pick up the orange sponge and scrub the plate', E'Both policies accomplished the same amount of the task. They both got the gripper around the orange sponge, but the two policies never picked up the sponge. No policy is preferred over the other for this case, since they both did not accomplish much, and made very similar motions.'),
(E'c4e5272e-93db-4601-93fa-b7b57f7ad489', E'2026-02-04T19:30:47.101072Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the baseball on the glove', E'Both policies reached for the whiffle ball rather than the baseball initially. Policy A finally reached for the baseball near timeout. Policy B nearly crashed the arm into itself at one point, and only reached for the whiffle ball.'),
(E'34143ad9-01e4-496d-bbc7-d38fb64c58da', E'2026-02-04T19:34:02.303047Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'CIIRC, CTU in Prague'), E'Unfold the blue tablecloth and spread it on top of the table.', E'Policy A did not manage to grab the tablecloth and did not unfold it at all. Policy B managed to pinch the tablecloth once, however it did not unfold it at all as well.'),
(E'7671c98e-0279-4a9e-9c2e-f7727542ee5d', E'2026-02-04T21:32:31.256259Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'match the objects to the corresponding bowl', E'B was half successful. A put the object in the wrong destination.'),
(E'd67e6424-3f98-4c82-a6fb-9c5bbe417775', E'2026-02-04T21:37:48.211255Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pick up the children''s book and place on the table', E'Policy A reached for the notebooks rather than the children''s book. Policy B attempted to grab the children''s book and did not reach for the distractor objects. Both policies unintentionally pushed the book stand away when reaching for the items.'),
(E'65b87dc6-c2b2-461f-844d-a2161e4e00c7', E'2026-02-04T21:42:08.845152Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove all bread from the basket', E'Policy B was preferred since it was able to pick up and remove one piece of bread from the basket. Policy A was unable to grab any bread. Clearly policy B performed the task better so it is preferred.'),
(E'626ecec4-8254-46be-a502-0714a03dce29', E'2026-02-05T00:55:45.749499Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Assemble the Burger', E'A picked up the bun and was very close to placing it on the burger before ultimately timing out. B just picked up the cheese and lettuce.'),
(E'53d46a80-c90d-4aad-824b-f16292e79e3d', E'2026-02-05T01:08:05.538012Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the red cube in the tape, then stack the other cubes on top of the red cube', E'Both models tried to grab the red cube, failed, then tried to grab the tape and failed.'),
(E'149fc641-cc78-46be-bf21-430dd4d5068b', E'2026-02-05T01:16:40.143541Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Complete the castle with the remaining 2 cups', E'Both failed to place the rest of the cups in a castle-like fashion.'),
(E'340189b5-7f08-4653-998a-6143779e49cc', E'2026-02-05T19:17:43.565769Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the tapes', E'A did not let go of the blue tape. B let go and placed it better than A.'),
(E'72055674-bb58-4ac4-a0f3-ca85b3ccec16', E'2026-02-05T19:33:20.262231Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the lime into the blue bowl', E'A went for the right object, but B did not. Neither picked up anything.'),
(E'69d12137-236e-4aed-9239-b652019b233e', E'2026-02-05T19:37:24.650136Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pick up the kitchen utensil and place it in the open drawer', E'Policy A is preferred since it quickly picked up the spoon and held onto it. policy B struggled greatly to pick up the spoon when compared to policy A. Neither policy was able to get the spoon to the drawer. Since policy A was able to quickly grab and hold onto the spoon, it is preffered.'),
(E'd99d4172-3503-4b28-91fb-beea69b65e2a', E'2026-02-06T01:11:23.407662Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Move the pear to the blue bowl', E'Neither picked up the pear, or poured the green bowl into the blue one.'),
(E'0c73bbf1-17a3-403c-8cbc-ad6d5a131a67', E'2026-02-06T05:35:07.714400Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the green toy onto orange plate', E'A is extremely fast, smooth and determined, looks like a TAMP system, and can stay at origin position after rollout. B runs also really fast, but it is more random and behaves like an animal, typical VLA behavior to try. B don''t stay in orgin position after task finish'),
(E'd1586d59-4f68-487e-942e-47a0774692d4', E'2026-02-06T05:42:07.792524Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'open the upper drawer', E'A initially went towards bookshelf instead of drawer, and then knock the right cabinet. B intially go towards caibinet handle than set back, then go knock the cabinet several times, both policies do not recognize the ''upper drawer'' and cannot find where is the handle'),
(E'e66a58c1-7bc1-48f4-b151-81bb9ffdf67f', E'2026-02-06T06:03:57.916284Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'put the toy into middle of the plates', E'A failed to understand the task (A put toy into one of the plates instead of in the middle of two plates). B somewhat try to randomly put the toy in between of the plates, but not completely, and once tried to carry the tone of the plates instead. B end position is closer to in the middle.'),
(E'48201ad6-674b-4c07-9407-362a8855a199', E'2026-02-06T08:01:27.138826Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the carrot onto the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the carrot, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the towel, dropped it on the towel.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it, dropped it on floor.Next, policy B approached the carrot, picked it up, moved it until time ran out.My instruction is to put the carrot onto the towel, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'bff20ea5-8fc4-42c0-84fb-818d3e266713', E'2026-02-06T08:30:30.088461Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the controller with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the towel, then attempted to grasped several times, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the towel, then attempted to grasp it several times, but did not succeed in the end.My instruction is to cover the controller with the towel,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of he two, both policies only attempted to grasp the towel but did not succeed.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'961d323e-c6be-4a88-9947-1e60bf1ea76f', E'2026-02-06T09:02:38.211909Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the controller with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it, dropped it.Next, policy A picked up the towel again, dropped it on floor.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the towel, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy B moved the gripper away.My instruction is to cover the controller with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up and moved the towel, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'0e2ba7a7-25e6-4530-84d9-fc4ec89fe308', E'2026-02-06T09:15:08.751451Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'write a letter o on the book with the marker pen', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the marker pen,attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy A approached the book, attempted to grasp.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the book, attempted to grasp it, touched it, then moved around the book during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to write a letter o on the book with the marker pen, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the marker pen, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'db543e07-f291-421f-a494-064b0d1627f0', E'2026-02-06T09:26:54.645452Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'close the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper back and forth for a while, then moved the gripper toward the floor, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper randomly for a while, then approached the book, but moved away soon.My instruction is to close the book,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the book, whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore,policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'581d9630-e289-4e30-b52a-abc88690f1eb', E'2026-02-06T09:36:57.099959Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'open the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the book, approached the edge of the book,adjusted posture, then moved slightly during remaining time of the episode, attempted to grasp the book but did not succeed.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the book, approached the edge of the book, adjusted posture, touched it, then moved the gripper as if attempted to pushed edge of the book.My instruction is to open the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least reached the book and attempted to pushed the edge of the book, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'95e5d7cf-86af-4c8b-9737-76d4d722a4b5', E'2026-02-06T19:25:07.043987Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Move the red grapes to the right of the bowl and the green grapes to the left', E'A made substantial progress towards completing the task and would likely have with more time whereas B was hesitant to act'),
(E'670d746a-642d-4848-aa59-7041d8744072', E'2026-02-06T19:45:00.528420Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the small bowls in the big bowl', E'B was able to complete the task whereas A fixated on the distractor after completing the first half of the task. B showed better language following in this case.'),
(E'b585e778-41e7-45b0-addd-f59b8748ff6d', E'2026-02-06T23:09:00.818522Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'shake the bowl of grapes', E'Both policies were able to grab the bowl containing grapes, but policy B did it quicker, and lifted the bowl off the table faster than policy A. Policy B had a better ''shaking'' motion than Policy A, and made more motions while holding the bowl than policy A. Since policy B had a smoother pickup and more aggressive shaking motion, it is preferred.'),
(E'76f87822-89b7-4c90-82dd-fb8b8f7e72fb', E'2026-02-06T23:27:12.844252Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'erase the whiteboard using the black eraser', E'Policy A took a few tries to pick up the eraser, and ended up just dropping it onto the whiteboard, with nothing getting erased. Policy B quickly picked up the eraser, moved the eraser to the whiteboard and made the erasing motion. Policy B did not fully erase all of the whiteboard, but got a majority of it. Because policy B made better grabs and actually erased some content from the whiteboard, it is preferred.'),
(E'ac010073-f19a-4386-95a2-47abb003b7d3', E'2026-02-06T23:52:02.068008Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'stir the cup', E'policy A picked the cup up fully, and dropped it onto its side. Policy B only tried grabbing the stirrer, and never tipped the cup over. While both policies failed to grab the stirrer and use it, policy B was less destructive and was closer to the desired outcome of only stirring the cup without tipping it.'),
(E'f973552c-8f84-40ee-a70a-2c68757a8605', E'2026-02-07T00:32:49.683857Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the blue marker in the blue bowl', E'Both policies, interestingly, put a domino in the bowl before reaching for the marker but while Policy A reached for the marker eventually, Policy B actually almost placed in the small blue bowlhen the deposit was not successful it tried to correct its deposit angle.'),
(E'58322cb3-b5e9-4ef4-82b1-7b5b0f5879fd', E'2026-02-07T00:57:44.125382Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the marker on top of the drawer', E'A hesitated to grasp the marker but did reach for it, ended up lifting the marker and its enclosure (tape wheel). Policy B was able to pick up the marker, it dropped it on the table instead of progressing towards the drawer. Appeared to try to correct after as well.'),
(E'30c41c8a-1006-4dbb-9ca1-4d686d658f0b', E'2026-02-08T05:05:53.844913Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'GeorgiaTech'), E'pick up bowl', E'A approaches the bowl with hesitation and fail to perform grasping. B tilt to different angles and fail to grasp, but also put the bowl out of the table. A is better.'),
(E'5feecc33-4ca2-4be4-8a5a-3f6e1b73c5e6', E'2026-02-09T17:42:10.872221Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pick up the dominoes and place them in the blue bowl', E'Policy A was able to pick up 1 domino and place it into the bowl successfully. Policy B was only able to pick up 1 domino, and did not get it into the bowl before timeout occured. Since policy A was able to complete more of the task in the time frame, it is preferred.'),
(E'a383e59a-c5d4-4817-9b99-d467d6172c9c', E'2026-02-09T18:31:01.791831Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Move the yellow roll of tape onto the blue roll of tape', E'Policy B picked up the yellow tape roll, and moved it onto the top of the blue roll. It did not release the yellow tape roll, it made 1 attempt at releasing but quickly grabbed it again. Policy A was only able get on target for the yellow tape, and was unable to pick it up entirely. Policy B is preferred since it accomplished much more of the task and was very close to fully completing it.'),
(E'db93d157-ddca-469b-8e43-046603482b0b', E'2026-02-09T19:09:50.172388Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the red blocks in the box', E'Policy A was preferable because it placed both red blocks into the box on its first attempt. Policy B missed placing the second block, dropping it in front of the box. Policy B corrected and placed it correctly on the second attempt, but the poor placement on its first attempt gives Policy A a slight edge.'),
(E'4e4e9b11-f6a4-4879-8543-39fad2f37c69', E'2026-02-09T19:12:32.692533Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the crown on the head', E'Policy A was able to pick up the crown, but did not move it towards the head. Policy B was on target for the crown, but was unable to pick it up. Since policy A accomplished more of the task than policy B it is preferred.'),
(E'fe2132a6-cb14-4e6e-9e27-faa783e9731e', E'2026-02-09T19:16:22.974908Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the balloon on the green plate', E'Policy A completed the task, without touching distractor items. Policy B grasped at the orange before finally picking up the balloon toward the end of the run. Policy A was more successful'),
(E'b5492c65-aabb-47d2-8883-3d47ec01cc92', E'2026-02-09T19:23:10.501073Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pick up the grey cylinder and place it in the green tape', E'Policy B picked up the cylinder with the first grasp, whereas Policy A made multiple attempts to grasp the cylinder before picking it up. Additionally, Policy B was the only policy to place the cylinder inside the tape.'),
(E'f91b0fb4-f166-4fd4-9553-9c6aeb3ceed1', E'2026-02-09T19:28:42.543264Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Place the dark blue cup into the cup holder', E'Policy A was able to pick up the cup, but placed it inside of a cup already in the cup-holder rather than putting the cup in its own slot. Policy B made erratic movements and was never on target for the cup. Since policy A made much smoother motions and partially accomplished the task, it is preferred.'),
(E'6f551c1d-242d-410a-9b2c-6c5416f0e5b6', E'2026-02-09T19:39:06.882148Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'use the towel to cover the pyramid', E'Policy A picked up then dropped the towel about 3 times, and policy B was able to fully accomplish the task. Because policy B picked up the towle and used it to cover the pyramid versus policy A which only picked up the towel, policy B is preferred'),
(E'7aa6a6a9-1453-4899-baec-3ad1d03c41d6', E'2026-02-09T19:42:10.609513Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the bread on the red tape', E'A picked up the bread and dropped it onto the tape. B neglected to pick up the bread at all.'),
(E'e0b65fb4-69aa-4dcc-acce-e8f32f7a997d', E'2026-02-09T19:49:49.432520Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Cover the burger with the towel', E'A moved the towel away from the burger. B moved the towel towards the burger until the towel touched the burger. The towel did not cover the burger though.'),
(E'91c143de-9270-468a-a49d-8972fc7de1f9', E'2026-02-09T19:52:54.234552Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put all fruit into the jack''o lantern basket', E'policy A was slightly better since it was able to get an object into the jack''o lantern, compared to policy B which spent the whole rollout trying to pick up the apple. Even though policy A placed a ball into the basket rather than a fruit, this is more than what policy B was able to accomplish, which only was focused on the fruit and could not even pick one up.'),
(E'c2da9ee4-4bbf-4711-9dd1-227bdf39b114', E'2026-02-09T20:14:16.736955Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the green ball in the jack-o-lantern', E'Policy A picked up the ball and attempted to drop it it while Policy B couldn''t pick up the ball in the first place'),
(E'4949ca70-fcbe-4e80-a730-0f1bac1ca399', E'2026-02-09T20:28:52.756335Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place bread in the jack-o-lantern', E'They both did not pick up the bread and instead picked up the bannana. They both failed the task'),
(E'b8a85019-e52e-47a4-8153-699aace9c340', E'2026-02-09T20:32:23.704724Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Drop the grapes into the cup', E'Policy A held the grapes in the cup and did not drop them, it kept adjusting the "drop" of the grapes while inching the grapes inside the cup whereas Policy B moved the grapes adjacent to the cup and pushed it nearly off the table. B showed good correction action but the cup was off table already and so it placed the grapes on the distractor plate. Policy A only took the grapes to the cup and ignored distractors.'),
(E'99cea07e-254c-430d-8804-1e667dcd01a3', E'2026-02-09T20:35:59.264781Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put strawberry in the jack-o-lantern', E'They both went for the apple at first and never corrected to the strawberry to put into the jack-o-lantern'),
(E'68d82940-8b64-41c7-bac2-a641a529d346', E'2026-02-09T20:45:49.383555Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Flip the green bowl upside down to cover the strawberry', E'It showed understand of the task where it picked up the bannana and attempted to flip it upside down. However, they both went for the bowl, but failed to grab the bowl. Policy B meanwhile did at least sttempted to flip the bannana over the apple'),
(E'e2dfdb94-5095-4684-b703-8969acb3c4cb', E'2026-02-09T21:02:38.509734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'drag the bowl towards the bannana', E'They both went for the bannana in different ways. Policy A dragged the bowl towards the bannana although missing a bunch. Policy B grabeed the bowl and went towards the bannana, but it didn''t drag leading to A winning'),
(E'bffff257-6f95-4eb1-b3a7-e94b531d030b', E'2026-02-09T21:03:57.282753Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'deposit the black marker into the pink tape', E'Policy B progressed slowly but very accurately grasped the marker and deposited successfully within the pink tape. Policy A struggled to orient itself originally and dropped the marker/tipped over the cup. Policy B was able to grasp the marker from the limited area presented and inclined angle and deposit the marker where it did not fall out from the tape. Policy A did not move the marker towards the tape after grasping (dropped).'),
(E'd141a901-dac3-42a1-b6f5-5f7e483ab522', E'2026-02-09T22:30:06.389652Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'roll the tape to the back of the table', E'Policy B reached for the tape but very quickly knocked it over onto its side rather than pushing it forward. Policy A failed to identify the tape altogether. While Policy B did not fully follow the action it still was closer to succeeding than Policy A.'),
(E'293a1c9c-89d1-4814-a4a9-1adda07b6900', E'2026-02-09T22:39:12.912592Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove the pegs from the holder', E'Policy A moved erratically and then reached around the object but did not pick up anything. Policy B made more intentional movements and successfully removed one peg and placed it on the table. Policy B also made attempts to grab the second peg, but did not complete in time. Policy B was preferable here.'),
(E'4de2e9ea-4b2b-4591-8b1f-6654cb059114', E'2026-02-09T22:49:02.474324Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the battery in the bag', E'Policy A was successful, althorugh it never really removed itself from the bag after placing the battery. Policy B picked up an incorrect item and dropped it on top of the bag, moving quicker but with less precision. Policy B was better since it managed to correctly identify the battery and place it inside the bag.'),
(E'2323e43f-2cd6-4b3d-90b3-457a73191ca0', E'2026-02-10T00:26:05.836734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'use the blade to pop the balloon', E'Policy A was unable to pick up the blade, even though it was on target for it. Policy B was able to pick up the blade twice, but did not try to pop the balloon with it. Since policy B was able to pick up the blade while policy A could not, B is preferred.'),
(E'b0ba56ef-8b5e-469d-b109-bc880722817e', E'2026-02-10T00:31:07.626128Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the bread on the plate', E'A picked up the banana (wrong obj) and brought it near the plate. B tried to pick up the banana (wrong obj) and failed.'),
(E'ebe1cb0e-f924-4786-928e-92eba5440642', E'2026-02-10T00:34:27.601696Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'transfer the hat onto the other head', E'Both policies completely failed the task, neither picked up the hat. Both policies waved the arm around, searching the scene. Since both policies were equally bad, it is a tie.'),
(E'bc14f466-7f07-46d2-804f-f17a486b184d', E'2026-02-10T00:40:07.815503Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the yellow tape onto the blue tape', E'A was successful. B srtuggled to grasp the object properly. It then gave up and went for the yellow cube.'),
(E'07a690c8-a391-4f2c-8e2a-8eda57267874', E'2026-02-10T00:45:26.405169Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'gather the cables into the bin', E'Policy B is preferred since it was able to get 1 cable into the bin, while policy A was only able to pick up a cable. Policy A struggled to pick up the cable, but policy B was able to grab it and set it in the bin. Since policy B completed more of the task, it is preferred.'),
(E'53f41ab8-210f-4020-bd9e-4c8574a21357', E'2026-02-10T00:46:11.117248Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Drape the cable on the tripod', E'A was almost successful. It draped the cable but it fell off. B did not even go for the cable, choosing to knock the tripod down and pick up the tape.'),
(E'ec2c16e3-20f6-4816-8c78-456fe0c099c5', E'2026-02-10T00:54:29.866512Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'TRI'), E'Put the banana on the plate', E'A was better at retrying and tasking on task. also pretty smooth. B started strong with a one shot pick up but slipped and went off course'),
(E'f1e84827-1c9b-45ff-ab25-b8cf235841f5', E'2026-02-10T00:59:52.247992Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack the coffee cup onto the stack of cups', E'A picked up the coffee cup and tried to bring it to the stack of cups but the cup slipped out of the gripper. B did the task in the opposite manner, trying to bring the stack of cups to the coffee cup, not stacking them.'),
(E'aac94478-c1fa-41c4-a1e5-30d96f75cb74', E'2026-02-10T01:01:14.245947Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'dump the basket of fruit into the orange bowl', E'Neither policy picked up the basket and dumped the fruit into the bowl. Policy A did not grab anything, so it fully failed the task. Policy B grabbed a fruit and placed it into the bowl, so while it did not follow the instructions, it did earn some partial score for transferring the fruit to the bowl. Since policy B was closer to matching its actions to the instructions, as well as actually picking up something, it is slightly preferred.'),
(E'c7c5dee7-3b99-489d-aee1-1597863f125b', E'2026-02-10T01:02:08.349311Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'TRI'), E'Put the cube on the plate', E'Both did the same thing, but A started by interacting with irrelevant objects and doing a random task, B stayed on goal'),
(E'38cc8559-9dfe-4788-8b7d-6c6785ddcaf8', E'2026-02-10T01:13:29.209012Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Clean the bowl with the brush', E'Both picked up the brush, neither went to the bowl to clean it. B was considered worse since it was contorting very awkwardly and jerkily, whereas A did not jerk awkwardly.'),
(E'cfbb6e43-e0e3-412d-9053-f28ddeec4fd0', E'2026-02-10T17:43:59.334751Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'roll the tape out of the black square', E'Policy A correctly targeted the tape in the black square, and made a few pokes at it before finally picking up the roll of tape and timing out. Policy B was distracted by the other rolls of tape, and never went for the tape that needed to be rolled out of the black square. Since policy A was correctly on target and almost made the correct motions, it is preferred.'),
(E'38ad3f75-c8da-438a-a179-d0d9c736e12a', E'2026-02-10T18:19:54.389734Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'use the utensil to knock over the tower', E'Policy A quickly grabbed the spoon, and touched the tower using the spoon, never applying enough force to knock over any part of it. Policy B took time for it to grab the spoon, and when it did it never went near the tower with it. Since policy A accomplished more of the task and was able to touch the tower with the spoon, it is preferred.'),
(E'd3de9f64-8bbd-46ad-87bb-2acf77ce1d6a', E'2026-02-10T18:40:41.141781Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the banana in the yellow tape', E'B got the banana in the tape, but it fell out. A ignored the banana and moved the brush.'),
(E'a7574614-a27e-4a0b-81d5-7f452319ae8e', E'2026-02-10T18:43:41.493376Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the keyboard and mouse into the box', E'Policy A knocked the keyboard onto the table while trying to pick up the mouse, as wella s taking two tries to pick up the mouse. Policy B picked up the mouse instantly and did not knock the keyboard down. Both policies accomplished the same amount of the task, but since B did not impede itself by knocking the keyboard flat on the table, it is preferred.'),
(E'a5206232-f739-433a-871e-88a5e1c104bd', E'2026-02-10T18:55:02.696719Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the brush in the bowl', E'A chose the wrong obj and put it in the correct destination obj. B picked the right obj but mistook the hat for the bowl.'),
(E'12964cf1-eaec-4bda-8ecf-0b2b1cf6c068', E'2026-02-10T19:01:34.628177Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove the roll of gauze from the tin and place it on the green dish', E'Policy A only grabbed the gauze before quickly releasing it back into the tin. Policy B picked up the gauze, and carried it towwards the green dish, but timed out before it could release the gauze. Policy B likely was going to fully complete the task, which makes it preferred compared to policy A which only accomplished a small grab on the gauze.'),
(E'f45d119e-f134-46d4-a65b-8dd24dd52393', E'2026-02-10T19:05:36.055846Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pour the bowl with batteries into the green bowl', E'A grabbed the wrong bowl, and made a slight pouring motion over the green bowl. B grabbed the correct bowl, and poured out the batteries, albeit slightly outside of the green bowl.'),
(E'16447a27-712a-42f4-972d-27b061bfb286', E'2026-02-10T19:12:22.673624Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'exchange position of pineapple and banana', E'A touches two object slightly, tried to grasp but do not pick it up; then A reset to origin position without doing; B wonder around a bit but successfully pickup the pineapple and place to the left of banana, although it is not a perfect position exchange but the do meet the instruction, so we prefer B'),
(E'e4318fd3-87ae-45fd-b204-a32f86975e0e', E'2026-02-10T19:17:19.160447Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the towel in the wooden tray', E'Policy A reached solely for the towel and took multiple attempts but finally picked it up. Policy B did make one attempt at the towel but otherwise reached for the cup. Since Policy A was able to pick up the intended item and was not distracted by other objects, it is more successful here.'),
(E'840398a5-f09b-4cde-af7b-86bf9caff4eb', E'2026-02-10T19:19:08.358029Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'close the lid of the tin box', E'Policy A waved around the scene, and did not touch any objects. Policy B quickly positioned itself to pull the lid closed, and was able to fully complete the task in one motion. Since policy B completed the task and A did not, policy B is preferred.'),
(E'aaec1844-3e1b-47a2-9499-2d76579c5f25', E'2026-02-10T19:21:10.693872Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the red I cube into the purple bowl', E'A firstly go towards the blue P, knock over the red I then tried to touch green 4, it didn;''t do any useful action aligned with tasks; B slowly approaches red I, tried 3 times to pick it up, then slowly place into the purple bowl, however, it keeps trying to pick up the cube in the bowl instead of resetting to origin position. so I gave B -10 progress penalty'),
(E'acda9b0f-4459-4c01-b892-4a53d30399a8', E'2026-02-10T19:28:01.005814Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the banana in the trash can and then close the lid', E'Policy A pushed the trash can away, but managed to pick up the banana and attempted placing it inside the trash can. Policy B did not pick up the banana, immediately trying to close the lid. The motions were intentional to close the lid but it was unsuccessful. Since Policy A completed more of the task, it was more successful.'),
(E'66edd90c-baf7-4a57-aa08-b5bf030cd92f', E'2026-02-10T19:34:00.264699Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove the gauze from the head', E'Policy A was able to grab the gauze, and remove it from the head completely. Policy B never grabbed the gauze, it repeatedly pressed the gripper against the top of the head. Policy A is preferred since it accomplished the task, versus B which did not.'),
(E'c59cde6d-b9ca-4cd1-891e-d1bc07f59f25', E'2026-02-10T19:37:43.890854Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'open the lid of the mailbox', E'Policy A managed to open the mailbox halfway, although it froze in place and did not open it further. Policy B appeared to try opening the mailbox from the hinge side, and was not able to open the lid. Policy B made an attempt, but policy A was slightly more successful in getting to open the lid.'),
(E'2f32d30a-2108-44b5-bdef-d7c2639c589e', E'2026-02-10T19:44:08.352803Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the cube with number on it into the bowl', E'A go on top of number cube green 4 then stuck in the air; B pick up the blue P slowly and place into the purple bowl, so I give B penalty by choosing A'),
(E'4bc7596f-615f-4265-a443-6658c0a51cff', E'2026-02-10T19:59:44.139107Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place only the toy cubes into the bowl', E'A keeps wonder around, touch the stuff but not able to place blocks into the bowl; B wonder around and place red I cube into the bowl, then tried to touch creeper toy, not able to clean the desk'),
(E'd3371466-bb01-433e-afa0-57680984c198', E'2026-02-10T20:13:55.476771Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the turkish fig back in their container', E'Both A and B do not recognize what is the turkish fig and reach the cube, A moves greatly backward while B misplace the cube into the bowl, both are bad practice so tie'),
(E'd130a613-2f93-49d1-81f0-c7b1a39fe7ee', E'2026-02-10T20:20:54.650788Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'fetch the creeper toy on the cabinet and place into the purple bowl', E'Both policy performs badly without seeing the creeper toy on the cabinet; A reach the desk in front of cabinet and stucks; B reaches cabinet too then steps back greatly, wonder around. Both are bad and does not follow instructions;'),
(E'4010f6b5-10a5-47a8-acfe-077e80c1d59e', E'2026-02-10T20:44:59.629129Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'stack the yellow cup in the white cup', E'Policy A was able to complete the task cleanly and smoothly without any errors. It spent little time searching for the correct object and grasped the white cup directly before moving it into the white cup. Policy B, on the other hand, struggled with locating the yellow cup at first and seemed to attempt to grasp the blue cup. It failed in grasping the blue cup and so it returned to its original position. After returning to its position, it was able to accurate ly locate and grab the yellow cup to place into the white cup.'),
(E'7c9f2731-bdd4-4446-9879-0ba8af96480f', E'2026-02-10T20:55:22.481013Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'push closed all the drawers', E'Policy A never got on target for the drawers, compared to policy B which was able to close 1 of the 2 drawers. Policy B did not get on target for the second drawer after it pushed the first one closed. Policy B is preferred due to the fact that it was able to close a drawer, while A did not.'),
(E'87b2343e-4adf-4529-b864-89e2b1e23a19', E'2026-02-10T21:03:53.633300Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'', E'I accidentally pressed enter without writing a prompt. The expected policy in this case should be to do nothing. Instead, I observed that policy A grabbed the white cup ait in the same position. On the other hand, policy B grabbed the orange cup and attempted to place it in the white cup. It was able to place the orange cup into the white cup, but knocked over both cups and this was not the intended task.'),
(E'3b41e0dd-6bfc-43df-bc5f-187587c1fa39', E'2026-02-10T21:10:59.030715Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pour the orange juice into the cup', E'Policy B was able to pick up the orange juice, but kept releasing it from its grip as it moved the juice towards the cup, it never made a pouring motion. Policy A was on target for the juice, but never grabbed it. Because policy B was able to rpick up the juice and moved it towards the glass, it is preferred over policy A.'),
(E'acafd73d-6c39-4c87-b4a8-1d8153a43c23', E'2026-02-10T21:11:25.603228Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the orange cup into the white cup', E'Policy A moved smoothly and almost picked up the orange cup on its first try. However, when it was gripping the cup, it seemed like it did not exert enough physical force to actually lift the cup and caused the robot to not grasp the orange cup. It was then, however, able to lift the orange cup from its side and place it into the white cup, but knocked both cups over. After it completed its task, it started going for and grabbing the yellow cup but did not finish what it was attempting to do. On the other hand, policy B failed because although it was able to recognize and grab the orange cup, it ended up placing it into the yellow cup which is not what I asked the robot to perform as a task.'),
(E'aa8a5569-3252-4cb0-9b4e-3d99ffd83e45', E'2026-02-10T21:28:31.826467Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'use the whisk to whisk the cherries in the pan', E'Policy A picked up a brush rather than the whisk and dropped the brush into the pan. Policy B spent the whole rollout trying to pick up the whisk, and timed out when it finally had a good grab on the whisk. Since policy A did not follow instructions, policy B is preferred for this task.'),
(E'88fb6a88-7b2b-4901-bef6-b3b120a3772d', E'2026-02-10T21:30:56.345407Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue cup into the yellow cup. Then, place the orange cup into the blue cup. The blue cup should already be in the yellow cup.', E'Policy A ran smoothly and was able to grab the blue cup right away. When it placed the blue cup into the yellow cup however, it was not able to let go of both cups and ended up with both cups being stuck to the gripper. It spent the majority of the run trying to become unstuck but did not perform any meaningful actions. Policy B was actually able to place the blue cup into the yellow cup, but ended up knocking both of the cups over. It tried to correct the positions of the two cups, but failed to do so and ended up grabbing the white cup and attempting to use the white cup to adjust the position of the knocked over cups.'),
(E'12ad9a85-2b77-467c-bd12-bf508da61328', E'2026-02-10T21:39:03.802013Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the blue block into the cup', E'Both policies ultimately failed to complete the task. Policy A started by attempting to grab the blue cup and failing. I believe policy A might not have seen the blue block and thought I was referring to the blue cup. When it knocked over the blue cup, it was then able to see the blue block and attempted to grab the blue block but failed. Whereas policy A saw the blue block near the end of its run, policy B failed to see the blue block altogether. It ended up placing the blue cup on the shelf instead of completing the task I provided.'),
(E'7f457511-abbc-4d5a-be3d-96a860d98950', E'2026-02-10T21:42:31.102402Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'slide the tray with the doughnut onto the black square', E'Policy A gently pushed the tray over to the black square, such that about half of the tray was over the black square by the end of the rollout. Policy B made lots of extra movements, and did not push/nudge the tray with any clear intention besides just moving the gripper around the scene. Policy A followed instructions and almost fully completed the task, so it is preferred.'),
(E'1b406547-57fc-4639-aaa4-d10210378a9c', E'2026-02-10T21:47:44.490648Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'move the blue objects to the right side. Move the green objects to the left side.', E'Neither policies were able to grab any of the objects. Policy A moved around the objects and seemed to be scanning them. It seemed like it was unsure of where the blocks it should move were. On the other hand, policy B grabbed the blue cup and attempted to move it to the right, but it ended up moving both of the objects back. Neither policies were able to grab any of the objects. Both actions exhibited fast movements and jolts in some particular areas. The task may have been unspecific about directionality.'),
(E'6006b30c-8b5b-4951-bdc9-26bdbe493fb5', E'2026-02-10T21:54:56.248619Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the block onto the blue cup', E'Policy A didn''t attempt to grab the block at first and didn''t appear sure of its actions. When it did grab the block, it attempted to place it onto the blue cup, but failed. Policy A went straight to the block, but was unable to pick it up.'),
(E'95d7371a-bcbe-4082-8824-375818ae1666', E'2026-02-10T22:03:30.121618Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'depress only the green ''GO'' button', E'Policy A did not ever find the green ''GO'' button, it spent the whole rollout searching the scene. Policy B quickly found the green button, and pressed it with a closed gripper, completing the task. Because policy B completed the task and policy A did not, B is preferred.'),
(E'98df1a0a-b588-4a83-a977-23382ccb6619', E'2026-02-10T22:21:17.348490Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'tear off a page from the notepad', E'Policy A was able to complete the task by tearing off a single page from the notepad. Policy B grabbed the whole notepad and pushed it to the left, never tearing a page off. Since policy A completed the task and policy B did not, policy A is preferred.'),
(E'3ea12f84-5c38-4fb1-9c16-58333a0b2be3', E'2026-02-10T22:41:05.586710Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the orange tape in the bowl', E'A picked up the orange bowl mistakenly and put it in the pan. B didn''t do anything, just idling the whole rollout.'),
(E'a29f0cd7-ff5d-46e5-af4e-83d7bc964463', E'2026-02-10T22:46:28.291729Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'draw on the whiteboard with the marker', E'Policy A waved the arm around the scene, and did not accomplish any of the task. Policy B picked up the marker, set it down next to the board and searched the scene. Policy B is preferred since it was able to pick up and move the marker.'),
(E'060d3e00-24cf-4620-a939-64469b8b1b62', E'2026-02-10T22:49:55.016478Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Stack all the cubes onto the red cylinder', E'A picked up the blue cube, tried to place it on the red cube. Did not try to stack it on the red cylinder. B did not try to stack anything at all. Did not manage to pick up any cubes.'),
(E'd10bf58a-ef2a-4dc6-b83d-d42a24a3eda7', E'2026-02-10T22:55:00.680537Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'draw on the paper using the pencil', E'Policy A waved around lots, and made frantic searching motions without ever getting on target. Policy B was on target for the pencil, but never closed the gripper around it. Both policies completely failed the task, but policy B was less erratic, and closer to actually picking up the pencil. Policy B is preferred since it was on target for the pencil, versus policy A which waved around frantically.'),
(E'7f0383a3-96ab-4e4b-a5db-176f4521b157', E'2026-02-10T22:58:37.876316Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Place the towel on the purple head', E'Both placed the towel and had it fall off. B then decided to pick up the balloon unnecessarily whereas A did not making A seem better.'),
(E'10cb0c22-b55c-49d2-9fbb-4c7eac81236a', E'2026-02-10T23:08:22.858035Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'hang the hanger on the tripod', E'Policy A was unable to grab the hanger at all. Policy B picked up the hanger and touched it agains the tripod, but dropped it before it could hang it up. Since policy B accomplished more of the task it is preferred.'),
(E'dd415d24-3987-435e-933e-76df4882c8c7', E'2026-02-10T23:11:51.903768Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Place the metal tray onto the orange plate', E'A picked up the metal tray and placed it awkwardly onto the orange plate. B did not even manage to pick up the metal tray.'),
(E'246bedc5-4394-453d-a6d9-392f4b7c5c5f', E'2026-02-10T23:19:28.224730Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place a domino on top of the red triangle', E'Both policies were able to pick up a domino and place it on the red triangle. Policy A took a few tries to grab its domino, while policy B grabbed it first try. Policy B was overall quicker to perform the task than policy A, and also had no hesitation in identifying the red triangle; therefore policy B is preferred.'),
(E'59c6c66e-5b97-4856-be26-f7f35c4af477', E'2026-02-10T23:29:24.892137Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pour the blue bowl into the red bowl', E'A was successful, B did not even pick up the blue bowl.'),
(E'ffab093a-6f4c-46f5-bd2d-67d3b790ecdc', E'2026-02-10T23:39:03.411571Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'peel both the sticky notes off of the jack''o lantern', E'Policy A was able to grab 1 sticky note, but did not peel it off. Policy B grabbed at the jack''o lantern, and never got tried to peel a sticky note. Since policy A got furthur into the task than policy B it is preferred.'),
(E'b1efc5c5-cd09-4a8a-9f7e-3edf1752b696', E'2026-02-10T23:43:22.961256Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Place the oranges in the green bowl', E'A somewhat grasped the orange. B didn''t do as good a job of grasping the orange. A did drop it, but B knocked it out of reach.'),
(E'686e78b6-c580-4687-a4de-a534a186af4c', E'2026-02-10T23:49:39.871150Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'bend the straw', E'Policy A grabbed the straw but never got it into a bent shape as desired. Policy B successfully bent the straw, although only at a 45 degree angle which is why it scored 90, rather than a 90 degree bend which would score 100. Since policy B was able to bend the straw it is preferred.'),
(E'd85458be-8cc9-4b49-a03f-66ad08dfd1b0', E'2026-02-10T23:55:07.014760Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Use the blue spatula to put the croissant into the green bowl', E'A picked up the spatula in a way that kept the croissant on the spatula. Its jerky movements knocked the croissant off though. B picked up the spatula in a way that let the croissant fall off.'),
(E'beaf345e-438e-4bde-bc43-bcb6397cd1fb', E'2026-02-11T17:29:06.536401Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'slice the bread with the knife', E'Policy A attempted to pick up the knife, which is the first step to complete the task. Policy B did not reach for the knife, instead picking up the bread and placing it on the plate. Neither policy was able to complete the task, but Policy A was more on track.'),
(E'dc3dca01-dd12-4f67-a4c7-b3eee94eae6a', E'2026-02-11T17:58:18.121864Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the shallot on top of the grey cylinder', E'A completed the task with time to spare. B neglected its task.'),
(E'f15a1adb-cae6-4de1-9c6d-da5f7eeed041', E'2026-02-11T18:07:10.505128Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'withdraw the bread from the oven and place it on plate', E'Both policies were successful, but Policy A grabbed the tray along with the bread, pulling the toaster oven in the process of removing the bread from the oven. Policy B touched only the bread, making it the preferable policy.'),
(E'24c958d3-84eb-461d-985d-073118a553ff', E'2026-02-11T18:10:48.891880Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Pop the ballon with the dart', E'A did not do much, just went towards the balloon with closed grippers. B actively did incorrect actions like going for the distractor item.'),
(E'e6a37be8-9d11-4041-ac78-9e1cc5fd15ed', E'2026-02-11T18:31:58.883418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Put the espresso cup on the blue-lined platform on the coffee machine', E'A was jerky and moving unnecessarily. Tried to grab the cup 2-3 times but aimed the grippers badly. B tried to grip the cup but also aimed badly. It was lethargic, not moving much.'),
(E'201ccb10-86b2-4433-ad89-6009ec9c8bee', E'2026-02-11T18:32:37.569119Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'bake the croissant in the oven', E'Policy A did not touch anything and waved around the scene. Policy B picked up the croissant and moved it toward the oven, although could not maneuver it inside. Policy B was closer to finishing the task, and was more successful than Policy A'),
(E'c82ce60e-8344-4958-abb7-537a70af4b30', E'2026-02-11T18:45:50.593935Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'elevate the mango to the highest platform', E'Policy A picked up the mango and dropped it above an object on the highest platform. While it didn''t successfully place the mango, it recognized the highest shelf. Policy B knocked the mango off of the table while reaching for it, then reached for other objects and pushed the shelf. Policy B was unable to complete the task, making Policy A preferable in this instance.'),
(E'35c39b66-240f-4042-bdc3-b1dfe87b74fc', E'2026-02-11T18:47:23.245368Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Dump the contents of the brown coffee bag onto the table', E'Both were bad. A seemed to move around more and look at the brown bag. B just fixated on the coffee machine. A wins because it it didn''t get "stuck" in one place.'),
(E'24aea56d-d111-421f-b95c-258545635f91', E'2026-02-11T19:06:59.466690Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'drop the glove between the baskets', E'Policy A reached for the glove and then did random actions for the remainder of the time. Policy B reached for the glove for the entirety of the time. Both were unable to pick up the glove in order to drop it, and neither really outperformed the other.'),
(E'5dd3410a-81a9-402b-a83c-a29631d0e536', E'2026-02-11T20:58:24.700194Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Slot the dark-brown espresso puck into the silver portafilter', E'A picked up the wrong puck, and put it in the coffee machine, not the portafilter. B didn''t do anything at all.'),
(E'24066248-a990-4a70-9de4-cc368036305c', E'2026-02-11T21:05:53.876589Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Slot the silver portafilter into the coffee machine', E'Neither model seemed to know what a portafilter is. Both went for the teal coffee puck, which is interesting.'),
(E'da58c887-a0e6-47dc-9bfa-feab448039b9', E'2026-02-11T21:16:22.996876Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Slot the teal cappucino puck into the coffee machine', E'B actually grasped the teal puck, A did not grasp it but went near it.'),
(E'e8980308-b84b-41ae-9828-d367a34d8e3c', E'2026-02-11T21:23:23.159174Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'arrange the blocks in a line', E'Policy A moved one of the blocks next to another block, whereas policy B did not move any block. Policy A was closer to completing the task'),
(E'e139fed9-22b2-46a8-8271-95287c7a7f47', E'2026-02-11T22:36:54.561663Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'save the baby', E'B just tapped the baby doll; A tapped it many times and eventually knocked it out of where it was "trapped" though it was not the best solution.'),
(E'7b41884a-3ffe-4475-ae78-c03a3f2a905a', E'2026-02-11T22:43:38.989765Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the dice from colorful board and place into the yellow cup', E'Policy A grabbed the wrong object and placed it in the yellow cup. B grasped the right object and did succeed at placing it in the cup, but it messed up once and had to go back and retry.'),
(E'3feaf17b-a273-4293-8ba4-39f78af0310d', E'2026-02-11T23:05:10.600018Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'Put the K in the yellow cup', E'A just wonders around, without picking up the cube; B goes towards the board but gets distracted by board, it doesn''t know what to do'),
(E'c8147bb0-d279-4c49-92f9-99e596ef539f', E'2026-02-11T23:11:24.316398Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'place the medicine into the paper cup', E'A stuck in the air and don''t move; B knock over the med and rotate the gripper in weird shape; A is safer so I prefer A'),
(E'f403aea7-c87e-4d8f-9489-61f523856751', E'2026-02-11T23:16:54.729680Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the cube that can complete the word ROBOT', E'A tried to pick up the blue X in the middle, but cannot pick it up; B goes towards blue D and pick up the desk cloth, which is bad. I prefer A because it is safer'),
(E'7ad7b91f-6803-4a33-b710-3aa8685e8bca', E'2026-02-11T23:24:01.956494Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the blue cube and stack on the leeft of ROBO', E'A failed to grab the right object and messed up the whole setup; B grabbed the correct object (successfully but poorly) but timed out before reaching the goal'),
(E'e1ffcd16-6aa8-404f-a41c-9e44c20b9955', E'2026-02-12T17:55:11.514728Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Separate square objects onto the plate', E'B grabbed a square object and tried to place it on the plate, but was unsuccessful. A grabed a round object. B is better because it correctly grabbed a square object.'),
(E'323a1907-3fa0-4280-8b3f-e2fec99d0e31', E'2026-02-12T18:04:40.469237Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Arrange the citrus fruits on the plate', E'Both placed one citrus fruit, however A went for the apple following the first placement and B went for the orange.'),
(E'8f1888ce-f4af-4848-8a12-947caa87de1a', E'2026-02-12T18:28:32.435933Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Transfer the blue cone to the purple cylinder', E'Neither model did much beyond moving around in an idle fashion'),
(E'658af6b8-b6a1-436d-bd0d-2066ebeffba4', E'2026-02-12T18:34:46.776474Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Mount the blue cup onto the grey cylinder', E'A was successful with time to spare. B just moved around for no reason.'),
(E'007e0ab3-f702-4a3d-bbb3-5cca5e6d0ea6', E'2026-02-12T18:44:50.821373Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'Depress the lid on the box', E'A depressed the lid but not fully. B did not contact the lid when trying to depress.'),
(E'e8f7a1a7-e4c5-427f-b99d-61ee8f4dc6f4', E'2026-02-12T18:50:46.781491Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the skittles in the drawer and close the drawer', E'Policy A picked up the cup and waved it around the table, bumping into the drawer but not attempting to place. Policy B picked up the skittles and placed them on top of the open drawer, although the way they were oriented prevented them from being placed fully inside, and then policy B picked up the cup and placed it in the drawer as well. Although neither policy closed the drawer, policy B was able to place items into the drawer, making it preferable.'),
(E'b332500d-2a3d-4bd6-bb8f-4306f7b51ed4', E'2026-02-12T19:06:12.697215Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'dispense the soap onto the plate', E'Policy A grabbed the soap bottle from the caddy and placed it onto the plate. Policy B grabbed the entire tray but reached for the soap toward the end of the timeout. Policy A completed more of the task'),
(E'f961219f-9d0a-4b5c-98aa-8713f557db79', E'2026-02-12T19:17:39.273899Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'return the mayonnaise', E'Policy A picked up a piece of bread. Policy B reached for mustard, which was not the target object but is at least a condiment and also in a bottle. Policy B was slightly preferable'),
(E'1f580069-deb6-4c07-a765-bebe19c20fec', E'2026-02-12T19:35:54.155658Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'organize the condiments inside the tray', E'Policy A moved clumsily and without intention. Policy B picked up one sauce but moved it inside of the black tape rather than the tray. Still, policy B outperformed policy A'),
(E'a959d8c7-d47c-47da-8fd0-1d707cb5dfe4', E'2026-02-12T23:52:25.935617Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'insert the pizza fully into the oven', E'Policy B did not interact with the pizza oven. Policy A angled itself to grab the pizza tray, but instead ended up removing the pizza from the oven. While neither policy was entirely successful, Policy B did not score as well because it only interacted with the plate.'),
(E'd1eb8f35-b3e6-4c60-bbbe-f5ba70ce5b8b', E'2026-02-13T00:25:50.825142Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'place the red cube within the red boundary', E'Both policies picked up the red cube but only Policy B placed it on the paper. The cube was about 80% inside of the red boundary, while policy A never placed the cube. Policy B is preferred.'),
(E'88ab768c-386d-4cc7-bfd1-c083e0768399', E'2026-02-13T00:36:50.331800Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'remove the headphones from the mannequin', E'Policy A did not touch anything. Policy B waved around the scene but then grabbed the headphones and successfully removed them.'),
(E'388480a0-1de3-4185-8fc4-7c4b72226199', E'2026-02-13T00:50:15.053522Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'roll the baseball across the table', E'Policy A picked up a cube and then touched the baseball, but didn''t roll it across the table. Policy B roughly made the motion to roll the baseball, managing to get it about half way across the table. Policy B rolled the baseball further than policy A, so it is preferred.'),
(E'0aeb2473-25aa-4be4-b05a-9c3e645d69e3', E'2026-02-13T01:01:26.189121Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'GeorgiaTech'), E'put the pink cup in the drawer', E''),
(E'0676afd4-9da9-4eab-acc2-8f299aa07712', E'2026-02-13T01:02:46.387464Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'insert the pipe cleaner into the straw', E'While both were unable to identify the pipe cleaner, Policy B interacted with the straw, while Policy A was more distracted.'),
(E'36231395-625b-421e-b6a2-8cb9e87a4f19', E'2026-02-13T01:08:55.767273Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'GeorgiaTech'), E'put the pink cup on the table', E''),
(E'45dfeeaf-ccc4-49e0-86f8-38fa60be4b8a', E'2026-02-13T01:13:45.561680Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'pour from the cup into the empty cup', E'Policy A picked up the full cup and tilted the cup above the empty cup, but not enough to where anything could fall out. Policy B picked up the empty cup and tried pouring it into the full cup, but tilted the cup much further such that items would have fallen out of it if it were the full cup. Since policy A did not tilt the cup enough, and policy B chose the wrong cup to pour, their performance is not clearly distinguishable.'),
(E'a9b4f59a-5b27-49ca-93eb-3aeefecb19f0', E'2026-02-13T01:20:38.077522Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'GeorgiaTech'), E'open the oven', E''),
(E'e0daf8d0-0a9a-42dd-b711-18a0a9b32e22', E'2026-02-13T01:33:33.094701Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'GeorgiaTech'), E'put the cup on the brown plate', E''),
(E'5477a9ec-c907-4bbf-9725-d9b6773e1703', E'2026-02-17T02:38:36.866304Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'pick up the orange', E'Both policy recognize the orange, try to touch it but cannot pick it up. The grasp is not firm, A moves very very slow, B moves back and forth fast, but never grasp it. I say both are bad'),
(E'cf638f95-09e6-4377-a58b-215784ce9ccf', E'2026-02-17T02:46:22.997236Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'UPenn'), E'clean up the table by putting all the orange peals into the cup', E'A tried 3 times to grasp the orange peal, cannot tell if it has firmly picked up, and mis place outside the cup. So I gave a 33 as partial success; B tried to pick up many times but cannot firmly picked up, release the peal in the air; Ais smoothier so I prefer A'),
(E'5ac9042f-e8e3-4c78-8797-98cd37fcc507', E'2026-02-18T16:36:08.063634Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'close the lid of the tin lunch box', E'Both policies moved near the lunch box but did not make contact with the lid or attempt to close the lid.'),
(E'dedc1424-e5dd-4aad-9d46-23ab44283be9', E'2026-02-18T16:45:49.230296Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'insert the toy saw into a hole on the wooden box', E'Policy A reached for the toy saw, although it did not grasp ot pick it up. Policy B however failed to reach for the saw and did not make any progress  in following the language prompt. Policy A was slightly better.'),
(E'2ec7df92-cac5-46c8-a18f-c6f649f24309', E'2026-02-19T16:31:22.022334Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'put the toast on top of the drawer', E'Policy A never interacted with the toast, instead moved the plate. Policy B attempted grabbing the toast once, but was unable to grasp and did not complete any action. Policy B is slightly better in this task'),
(E'217f8f47-4cf0-4ecd-b2cf-05af767a7e1f', E'2026-02-19T16:48:03.257581Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'\\fold the t-shirt', E'Policy A made more realistic folding motions, folding the shirt in half vertically and then in half horizontally, although it was a messy fold. Policy B picked up the shirt from the middle, moved the shirt around and only made one folding motion at the end. Overall, policy A was neater and appeared to fold more intentionally.'),
(E'1dd4a597-48f5-4aaa-aa83-91e9ab5de7ea', E'2026-02-19T17:12:30.839614Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'draw something with the pencil', E'Both policies tried folding the shirt after attempting to pick up the pencil, neither were able to pick up the pencil to draw.'),
(E'35846fed-09f2-41fb-8fc7-066e0e82b3da', E'2026-02-23T16:47:57.724811Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'scoop out the screws from the bowl', E'Policy A touched the spoon but was not able to grasp it. Policy B removed some screws from inside the bowl. While neither policy exactly followed the prompt, policy B completed more of the task and scooped out some screws by picking them up.'),
(E'845c17f7-a397-4cba-a008-5557360ca5b9', E'2026-02-23T16:56:32.465483Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'hook the roll of tape onto the top of the cone', E'Policy A picked up the tape and moved it onto the cone, whereas policy B picked up the tape and placed into the bowl. Since policy A recognized the cone, it was more successful in this task'),
(E'a808c915-e90d-457d-9b24-1911a6900385', E'2026-02-26T16:39:52.065747Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'nvidia'), E'transfer the grapes to the other bowl', E'Policy A only attempted to pick up the apple. Policy B reached inside the bowl with the grapes and then picked up the bowl and tilted it as an attempt to pour the grapes onto the table. While Policy B was not able to pick up the grapes or move them to the other bowl, it more closely followed the goal of the task.'),
(E'917da323-7f56-4bac-8d6c-c2b893b565cd', E'2026-02-27T06:08:03.973295Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the marker pen onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the marker pen, grasped it ,picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the marker pen, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the book, dropped it on the book, causing the marker pen to roll off to the sofa.My instruction is to put the marker pen onto the book, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least dropped the marker onto the book, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'88382e18-da6a-45de-bd31-0c333d00fdae', E'2026-02-27T06:23:01.779364Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the shoe', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the shoe, adjusted posture, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it, put it on sofa.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the shoe, pushed it, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed.Then policy B moved the gripper away and moved slightly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to pick up the shoe, when comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'b9d7451e-e3e9-462f-bdd3-20eb65bc4ecf', E'2026-02-27T06:38:14.626681Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'knock over the shoe', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the shoe, touched it, then policy A moved the gripper away and moved slowly for a while, approached the shoe again, grasped the shoe in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the shoe, grasped it, moved it,then pushed the shoe, causing it to fall off to floor.My instruction is to knock over the shoe, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies grasped the shoe, but policy B pushed the shoe to floor, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is slightly better than policy A.'),
(E'8e27fdb1-4349-4c3d-947a-7d4b2da3e195', E'2026-02-27T08:38:39.426418Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'untie the shoelace', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the shoe, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy A almost stopped on the shoe during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the shoe, then closed and opened the gripper several times near the shoe.My instruction is to untie the shoelace, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least reached the shoe, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'd9e0f036-b839-425a-95e2-444fdd7f4d1e', E'2026-03-02T02:53:58.654227Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the shoe onto the box', E'Policy A moved the gripper slowly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the box, pushed it, then attempted to grasped it several times, but did not succeed in the end.My instruction is to put the shoe onto the box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least approached the box, whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'0bd85371-a834-4763-86ae-0fe264803783', E'2026-03-02T03:03:48.988738Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the shoe onto the box', E'Policy A moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the shoe, touched it, attempted to grasp it but did not succeed, then policy B approached the box, grasped it, picked it up, moved it and dropped it.My instruction is to put the shoe onto the box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least attempted to grasp the shoe, whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'25c4a92f-f7b2-4013-a27e-a62a15dcc4c7', E'2026-03-02T03:13:46.917030Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'rotate the banana by 90 degrees', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana but moved away soon, then policy A moved the gripper back and forth for a while, approached the banana, picked it up, moved it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, rotated it by about 80 degrees, then rotated it to the origin position in the end.My instruction is to rotate the banana by 90 degrees, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least rotated the banana by 80 degrees, whereas policy A did not.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'61c3e526-9aea-4674-9a85-84ab4924ed69', E'2026-03-02T03:25:00.497953Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana onto the white box', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the white box, put it onto the box.Next, policy A picked up the banana again, dropped it on the white box, causing the banana to fall off to sofa.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to put the banana onto the white box, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A almost completed the task, whereas policy B did not move the banana to the white box.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'353ef115-ef9b-4d49-86e7-cbb5c8090267', E'2026-03-02T03:36:10.645128Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the white box with towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the towel, grasped it and released it, then policy A moved the gripper away and moved slowly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the towel, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the white box, put it on the white box.My instruction is to cover the white box with towel, when comparing the performance of the two, policy B completed the task successfully, whereas policy A failed.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'64b58f96-4b4c-4ec2-93a4-5fa01991ef7d', E'2026-03-02T06:48:42.749279Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'stack up the two cups', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the right cup, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the left cup, put it into the left cup.Next, policy A picked up the two cups, moved them and put them on the sofa.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the left cup, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it to the right cup, put it into the right cup.Next, policy B stopped during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to stack up the two cups, both policies completed the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B stopped after finishing the task, whereas policy A did extra unnecessary actions.Therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'226f513b-ac1a-4900-a12a-88d355b39397', E'2026-03-02T07:01:43.889453Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the top cup on sofa', E'Policy A moved the gripper randomly during entire time of the episode, as if could not find the target.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the two cups, knocked the cups over, then attempted to grasp them, but did not succeed in the end.My instruction is to put the top cup on sofa, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least knocked the cups over, whereas policy A did not do anything relevant.Therefore, policy B is better than policy A.'),
(E'd1effdf5-7b78-4bac-8d65-a7c6150b4a84', E'2026-03-02T07:33:42.440019Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'fold the towel in half', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward floor, then approached the towel, grasped the bottom right corner of the towel, moved it to the left side, causing the towel to be folded although not in perfect half.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the towel, grasped the bottom left corner of the towel, moved it to right, causing the towel to be fold a bit.My instruction is to fold the towel in half, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A folded the towel better than policy B did.Therefore, i prefer policy A.'),
(E'1ea3ed4b-75c7-4902-a319-cd45e3f66b2d', E'2026-03-02T08:00:32.199877Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'cover the cup with the towel', E'Policy A first moved the gripper randomly for a while, then approached the towel, grasped it, picked it up, moved it until time ran out.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the cup, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the towel, put it onto the towel.My instruction is to cover the cup with the towel, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least picked up and moved the towel, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
(E'bb04081e-dedb-4dda-ae95-3343fdbe709a', E'2026-03-02T08:14:29.229645Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the potato into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the potato, grasped and released it, then picked it up and dropped it, causing the potato to fall off to floor.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the potato, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped, causing the potato to fall off to floor.My instruction is to put the potato into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies only picked up and dropped the potato, and their performance was similar.Therefore, i choose tie.'),
(E'f988ff9f-6ee7-4f48-a85d-60e6e9c5052a', E'2026-03-02T08:43:29.466307Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'pick up the vegetable', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward bitter melon, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped it on floor.Next, policy A moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana which is not vegetable, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the bitter melon.My instruction is to pick up the vegetable, there is only one vegetable which is bitter melon.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'581c105b-e479-498f-ae8f-c1ef6dc55c32', E'2026-03-02T08:54:06.430976Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the fruit into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the potato which is not fruit, then attempted to grasp it several times, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the cup, put it on the edge of the cup, causing the banana to fall off to sofa.Next, policy B picked up and dropped the bitter melon.My instruction is to put the fruit into the cup, there is only one fruit which is the banana.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least dropped the banana on the edge of the cup, whereas policy A did not even find the fruit.Therefore, policy B is obviously better than policy A.'),
(E'5c611806-fb73-45e2-b65a-0644aa1025bb', E'2026-03-02T09:04:57.627144Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the fruits together', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the apple, put it on the apple.Next, policy A picked up and released the potato.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it for a while, dropped it on floor.Next, policy B picked up and moved the potato.My instruction is to put the fruits together, there are two fruits which are the banana and the apple.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A completed the task successfully, whereas policy B failed.Therefore, policy A is obviously better than policy B.'),
(E'784479f8-7d77-4743-839d-e685cf2ba564', E'2026-03-02T09:26:40.267371Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the carrot into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the carrot, grasped it and released it, then approached the apple, grasped and released it.Next, policy A picked up the banana in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the cup, dropped it into the cup, causing the cup to fall over.Next, policy B moved the gripper randomly during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to put the carrot into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy B at least put the wrong object banana into the cup, whereas policy A seemingly did not get my idea.Therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'd59c6930-11af-4fd1-a2f1-18349853db42', E'2026-03-02T09:37:57.557524Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the banana into the cup', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it toward the cup, dropped it on the edge of the cup, causing the banana to fall off to sofa.Next, policy A knocked the cup over, picked up and dropped the carrot.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the banana, grasped it, picked it up, then moved it and dropped near the apple.Next, policy B picked up the banana again, moved it and dropped it near the cup.My instruction is to put the banana into the cup, neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, both policies dropped the banana near the cup, but then policy A knocked over the cup, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, i prefer policy B.'),
(E'44c33669-2039-4511-8c6e-2bec80b64e32', E'2026-03-03T02:50:04.755237Z', (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE name = E'frodobots'), E'put the remote control onto the book', E'Policy A first moved the gripper toward the remote control, touched it, then attempted to grasped it several times, but did not succeed in the end.Policy B first moved the gripper toward the remote control, then almost stopped near the remote control during remaining time of the episode.My instruction is to put the remote control onto the book,neither policy was able to complete the task.When comparing the performance of the two, policy A at least attempted to grasp the remote control, whereas policy B did not.Therefore, policy A is better than policy B.'),
